{
  "chapter.63A7B1E69BE2C38A.title": "I · A Light Among Ruins",
  "chapter.63A7B1E69BE2C38A.chapter_subtitle": [
    "You wake beside a ruin of Heliodor with empty hands. A compass is waiting for you, and so is an Atlas."
  ],
  "quest.3C1A37141ABD78D8.title": "Waking among ruins",
  "quest.3C1A37141ABD78D8.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Use the pedestal at the heart of the ruin to take the Heliodor Compass, then pick a nearby site with water, wood and room to grow. Quests open with F8 or the book icon in your inventory; confirm once you have read this.",
    "",
    "Tuff cut by machines, copper veins gone dark, gardens that kept growing with nobody to tend them. Whoever lived here left all at once."
  ],
  "quest.3AC9E31D78B2BCB0.title": "Somewhere to begin",
  "quest.3AC9E31D78B2BCB0.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Craft a crafting table. Before spending materials, check a recipe's uses in the recipe viewer.",
    "",
    "The ruin kept its stones, not its tools. Whatever Heliodor knew, you start again from wood."
  ],
  "quest.153F660992CE9BA3.title": "Read the stone",
  "quest.153F660992CE9BA3.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Make a stone pickaxe. Check the block overlay before mining an unfamiliar ore: tool tier matters.",
    "",
    "The ruin's tuff was cut with machines, not chisels. Some day you will need that kind of precision too."
  ],
  "quest.0CA82678D5DFA3E8.title": "A recipe worth keeping",
  "quest.0CA82678D5DFA3E8.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Bookmark a recipe you plan to make next in the recipe viewer (its keys are listed in Controls), remove finished ones so the list stays useful, and confirm.",
    "",
    "A short list of what comes next: that is how Heliodor's workshops started every morning."
  ],
  "quest.2742A6E0D4B75C80.title": "A shelf for tomorrow",
  "quest.2742A6E0D4B75C80.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Make a chest. Keep your next project's materials apart, and try the sorting and matching-deposit controls on ordinary items.",
    "",
    "Among the loose pages, a copper seal with a golden A: 'Council inventory. Everything is recorded.' Somebody here counted everything."
  ],
  "quest.216E7E97E831A00C.title": "Heat with a purpose",
  "quest.216E7E97E831A00C.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Build a furnace and smelt or cook a useful batch; prepare the inputs before lighting it.",
    "",
    "Supply, transform, collect: Heliodor ran whole cities on that pattern, fed by the sun instead of coal."
  ],
  "quest.73220D1B896D7CD9.title": "The edge of the dark",
  "quest.73220D1B896D7CD9.quest_desc": [
    "Shelter by the ruin",
    "",
    "Prepare eight torches and light the path between your entrance, water and workshop before you go underground.",
    "",
    "A loose page carries a blessing, signed with a single letter: 'May the light find you at home. —B.'"
  ],
  "quest.4FC6DEBD8FEED1C0.title": "A return address",
  "quest.4FC6DEBD8FEED1C0.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Place and use a bed once you can get wool safely; keep the respawn space clear and tell your companions where it is. Confirm when done.",
    "",
    "In the ruin, nobody switched the lights off. Whoever lived there meant to come back that same night."
  ],
  "quest.34262755FE4ACAB3.title": "The Atlas listens",
  "quest.34262755FE4ACAB3.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Click the task to open the Atlas, pick The Atlas Awakens and deliver a book and a copper ingot. You get a Living Atlas to come back to it.",
    "",
    "In the Atlas Courtyard the cover warms up. A voice pushes through the static: '…make room for… &kthose&r who… have not arrived.'"
  ],
  "quest.744122ED817C45E5.title": "Carry the river",
  "quest.744122ED817C45E5.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Smelt iron for a bucket and bring water to a small farm beside your shelter.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's gardens still drink from channels nobody tends. Water was the first thing its people learned to move."
  ],
  "quest.4E81EB4CAA1D1D13.title": "The patient part",
  "quest.4E81EB4CAA1D1D13.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Harvest three wheat and replant before you leave; keep seeds apart from food.",
    "",
    "A note in careful green ink: 'Sow extra. Someone hungry always turns up. —J.'"
  ],
  "quest.0DDC984DEA3CAD80.title": "A kitchen tool",
  "quest.0DDC984DEA3CAD80.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Make a flint knife and check its uses: Farmer's Delight knives work on the cutting board and gather certain ingredients.",
    "",
    "The ruin's kitchens were built for crowds. Whoever ran them fed far more people than ever lived here."
  ],
  "quest.1EE8E17F9022A402.title": "A different kind of crafting",
  "quest.1EE8E17F9022A402.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Place a cutting board, put an ingredient on it and use the tool its recipe shows.",
    "",
    "In Heliodor even a kitchen board was a small machine: something goes in, one gesture, something useful comes out."
  ],
  "quest.7CD0636D9B7DDA5E.title": "Four places at the table",
  "quest.7CD0636D9B7DDA5E.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Prepare four bowls. Some meals give the bowl back, so count them when you plan a batch.",
    "",
    "The ruin's tables are laid for more guests than chairs. J. wrote underneath: 'A kitchen is measured by who it can welcome.'"
  ],
  "quest.7022698D6AF61048.title": "Food before distance",
  "quest.7022698D6AF61048.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Bake three bread for a short survey and watch saturation as well as hunger. Keep a reserve at home.",
    "",
    "J.'s packing lists always start with bread, 'for whoever gets lost'."
  ],
  "quest.5E980BB86AE535DF.title": "A table for those returning",
  "quest.5E980BB86AE535DF.quest_desc": [
    "J.'s notes · Garden and table",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas, select A Table for Travellers, check what is missing and choose Deliver.",
    "",
    "J. always kept a place set for strangers. The Atlas answers the delivery with one clear word through the noise: '…welcome.'"
  ],
  "quest.0E2E2C08C06F343B.title": "Metal that remembers weather",
  "quest.0E2E2C08C06F343B.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Smelt four copper ingots and keep them with the glass for the lens.",
    "",
    "Every instrument in the ruin has a copper frame gone green. Someone designed them to be repaired, not replaced."
  ],
  "quest.27B833739C94F3B1.title": "A window small enough to carry",
  "quest.27B833739C94F3B1.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Smelt four glass, taking sand from a small, safe patch rather than undermining your shelter.",
    "",
    "Heliodor built with glass so the light could reach everything. It was what its people loved most."
  ],
  "quest.7D9F3FDD50B52514.title": "A borrowed horizon",
  "quest.7D9F3FDD50B52514.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas, select Assemble the Lens and deliver the listed materials to receive the raw lens once. Keep it for the first signal.",
    "",
    "Beside the sketch, in a small, precise hand: 'Measure before believing. —T.'"
  ],
  "quest.67D63EA89ED72879.title": "Mark the ordinary",
  "quest.67D63EA89ED72879.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Find the map's controls, mark your shelter with a practical name and confirm.",
    "",
    "The Atlas remembers a world that no longer matches yours. Your own map is the one that tells the truth today."
  ],
  "quest.078C1FA519669777.title": "Leave with a question",
  "quest.078C1FA519669777.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Prepare three paper for field notes, and pack food, a pickaxe and light with room left for samples.",
    "",
    "The compass will not send you far. Heliodor's traces are close, if you know how to look."
  ],
  "quest.42845362110B95B7.title": "Two accounts of one place",
  "quest.42845362110B95B7.quest_desc": [
    "T.'s notes · Measure the horizon",
    "",
    "Take a short walk and compare a nearby landmark with your map, then open Field Survey in the Atlas and deliver its materials (paper and an ordinary compass) to receive your survey notes.",
    "",
    "What the villagers remember and what the Atlas remembers do not match. Somebody has to write it down again."
  ],
  "quest.5625EFC0A0C376CF.title": "The expedition ends at home",
  "quest.5625EFC0A0C376CF.quest_desc": [
    "Small useful habits",
    "",
    "Back home, restock food and torches before storing the rest, try matching-deposit and note one material you were missing. Confirm when done.",
    "",
    "Every trip in J.'s notes ends the same way: 'Back home. Nobody lost.'"
  ],
  "quest.762B0B9FB46F552F.title": "One light answers",
  "quest.762B0B9FB46F552F.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Open First Signal in the Atlas and deliver the listed materials. Once, your team receives a signal core and two of Terra's calibration frames: the core builds a survey station, and one frame builds the metallurgic infuser that copies the rest.",
    "",
    "Far away, a light answers. Through the static, a voice: '…can you &khear&r… us? We are still… here.'"
  ],
  "quest.258FF615C9AD9711.title": "A workshop with a destination",
  "quest.258FF615C9AD9711.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "When every project of this act is delivered, choose Advance in the Atlas to open the next one; if it takes too long, choose Refresh before retrying. Confirm to close the act.",
    "",
    "The voice has gone quiet. Once you advance, the compass will turn toward a workshop that sank with its tools inside."
  ],
  "quest.2E22D95F3AC6BE45.title": "A place your compass remembers",
  "quest.2E22D95F3AC6BE45.quest_desc": [
    "A light answers",
    "",
    "Build a survey station from the signal core, copper, smooth stone and glass. Use an ordinary compass on it to mark the spot without spending the compass (it points here within this dimension); an empty hand opens your team's Atlas.",
    "",
    "Heliodor had a station like this in every square. The Heliodor Compass follows the Atlas; this one brings you home."
  ],
  "image.5FA9913813897189.title": "&#E8DCB5Shelter by the ruin",
  "image.59D6720CE929BFC4.title": "&#E8DCB5J.'s notes\\nGarden and table",
  "image.5B66BE95D53E20EF.title": "&#E8DCB5T.'s notes\\nMeasure the horizon",
  "image.0DEB76F601E735E0.title": "&#E8DCB5A light answers",
  "image.64856A838DF0F3F2.title": "I · A Light Among Ruins",
  "chapter.0F7AE2DC86CB6F50.title": "II · The Lost Crafts",
  "chapter.0F7AE2DC86CB6F50.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A workshop the earth swallowed keeps Heliodor's crafts: measuring, powering, growing and feeding. Someone once brought them to one bench."
  ],
  "quest.048D2E6A70144A24.title": "Four benches, one workshop",
  "quest.048D2E6A70144A24.quest_desc": [
    "The Sunken Workshop",
    "",
    "Pick any branch below. Hexagonal tasks open the Atlas, and only a delivery there moves your team's story; the rest are lessons. Confirm when ready.",
    "",
    "The signal led to a workshop the earth swallowed. Four benches, four crafts, and one name scratched into every one: Terra."
  ],
  "quest.1C29DD1E3979A642.title": "Let water do the turning",
  "quest.1C29DD1E3979A642.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Craft a Create water wheel from planks around a shaft, and use its Ponder scene to set it in flowing water.",
    "",
    "Terra's first note starts with a stream, not a furnace: 'Borrow a force before you make one.'"
  ],
  "quest.505AD15489797C5A.title": "An iron ingot, made flat",
  "quest.505AD15489797C5A.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Connect a mechanical press to rotation with a depot under its head, as Ponder shows, and press iron ingots into iron sheets.",
    "",
    "In the Sunken Workshop the presses still stand in a row, rusted mid-stroke."
  ],
  "quest.24DF7B8F88C1FCB9.title": "Read the strain",
  "quest.24DF7B8F88C1FCB9.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Make Engineer's Goggles (glass, string and a gold plate from your press), wear them and compare a machine's speed and stress before adding another.",
    "",
    "Terra crossed out 'make it turn faster' and wrote 'measure first'. Somebody above her kept asking for more."
  ],
  "quest.5C34E7D93BAD4D93.title": "Wire without a factory",
  "quest.5C34E7D93BAD4D93.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "With Immersive Engineering's hammer turn a copper ingot into a plate, then use its wirecutters to make copper wire for your first connections.",
    "",
    "A hand route for when the machines are gone. Terra always left one."
  ],
  "quest.5F676C980602FEFF.title": "A Measure of Iron",
  "quest.5F676C980602FEFF.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Build a Mekanism metallurgic infuser with one frame from First Signal, then infuse a raw lens with redstone to copy the frame. Deliver the copy to Precision Bench in the Atlas and keep the infuser running: every later frame comes from it.",
    "",
    "Terra's standard joins hand tools and machines in one measure. The same frame holds Heliodor's lens in its solar heating plates."
  ],
  "quest.1AF624DC63ABDC33.title": "A small electrical beginning",
  "quest.1AF624DC63ABDC33.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Build an Actually Additions coal generator (iron casings with black quartz, iron and wooden rods) and keep fuel nearby.",
    "",
    "A soot-stained page: 'Coal, for now. Until the sun. —T.'"
  ],
  "quest.4E94D46197FC6BC3.title": "A beam with a job",
  "quest.4E94D46197FC6BC3.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Build an Atomic Reconstructor (iron casing, iron and redstone), power it and test it with one redstone dust where drops are easy to recover.",
    "",
    "Heliodor shaped matter with light long before it tried to shape anything bigger."
  ],
  "quest.5525FEC32B117FD6.title": "Redstone remembers another shape",
  "quest.5525FEC32B117FD6.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Beam redstone dust into ordinary Restonia crystals (40 energy each). Keep two, with an iron casing and two Create andesite alloys, for an energy coupler.",
    "",
    "The crystals hum at the same pitch as the Atlas. Terra noticed too; her margin only says: 'Why?'"
  ],
  "quest.5281CA2BAADED9DF.title": "A Crystal Connection",
  "quest.5281CA2BAADED9DF.quest_desc": [
    "Power with a purpose",
    "",
    "Craft an energy coupler from two Restonia crystals, an iron casing and two andesite alloys, and deliver it to Crystal Grid in the Atlas. Your generator and reconstructor stay installed.",
    "",
    "With the coupler, Heliodor turned rotation into current. Every generator coil it built asks for one."
  ],
  "quest.13D42DB7A4E29182.title": "Write a first working spell",
  "quest.13D42DB7A4E29182.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Make a novice spell book from a book and a spare iron shovel, pickaxe, axe and sword, then try a utility spell somewhere safe.",
    "",
    "Beside Terra's machines, someone kept a quieter shelf of prayers and spells, signed with a single letter: B."
  ],
  "quest.1751AC5350F46D6C.title": "Keep a source-gem reserve",
  "quest.1751AC5350F46D6C.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Make Ars source gems by imbuing amethyst or lapis in an imbuement chamber (archwood planks and gold). The living matrix needs two.",
    "",
    "B. wrote that magic is tended, not squeezed. The workshop's gem beds were never emptied."
  ],
  "quest.0D777B65AE7AD4C0.title": "A crop with workshop uses",
  "quest.0D777B65AE7AD4C0.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "At an Enchanting Apparatus (diamond, gold and sourcestone), a seed with four source gems makes magebloom seeds; the listed Source cost is zero. Grow a bed and craft the blooms into fibers: keep two.",
    "",
    "A flower grown to be woven into machines. Heliodor never quite saw a line between the two."
  ],
  "quest.7A2C3D602817EC20.title": "The living workshop",
  "quest.7A2C3D602817EC20.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Craft a living matrix (two magebloom fibers, two source gems and a new calibration frame) and deliver it to Living Workshop in the Atlas after Precision Bench.",
    "",
    "Terra's measurements drawn over B.'s garden bed: the only page in the workshop signed by both."
  ],
  "quest.60274F8FAAB2F834.title": "The kitchen keeps working",
  "quest.60274F8FAAB2F834.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Build a Farmer's Delight cooking pot (iron, bricks, a water bucket and a wooden shovel), set it over heat and cook a batch from nearby crops.",
    "",
    "J.'s list puts a cooking pot before any second machine. A workshop runs on whoever feeds it."
  ],
  "quest.53F96B4513813835.title": "Use the catch",
  "quest.53F96B4513813835.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Fillet a catch with an Aquaculture knife and cook the fillets on a campfire, in a furnace or in a smoker. Save some for rations.",
    "",
    "The workshop's canal still has fish. J. stocked it himself, the note says, 'for the long shifts'."
  ],
  "quest.7B649EF9ED27AC7F.title": "Pack a real travelling meal",
  "quest.7B649EF9ED27AC7F.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Two vegetable soups and two cooked Aquaculture fish fillets make one pack of Travel Rations; the soup takes carrot, potato, beetroot and leafy-green tags.",
    "",
    "J. packed these for workers who were not allowed to go home. The note does not say who gave that order."
  ],
  "quest.774DD93299251487.title": "The travelling pantry",
  "quest.774DD93299251487.quest_desc": [
    "J. · Provision the journey",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas and deliver one pack of Travel Rations to Travelling Pantry. No pot, rod or other equipment is taken.",
    "",
    "J.'s note ends with a correction: 'Count the people who come back, not the crates that leave.'"
  ],
  "quest.3E9B76FA05037B25.title": "Can the next person repeat it?",
  "quest.3E9B76FA05037B25.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Measure and shape",
    "",
    "Optional: press a second iron ingot, label the press's input and output, and leave a note on what to check if rotation stops. Confirm after trying it.",
    "",
    "Terra wrote every procedure 'for the next one'. She never expected to be the one missing."
  ],
  "quest.453C69E2CF5980E2.title": "Leave the bed ready",
  "quest.453C69E2CF5980E2.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop that grows",
    "",
    "Optional: harvest a small magebloom batch, process some fibers and leave the bed planted, with seeds and spare fibers stored apart. Confirm after trying it.",
    "",
    "B.'s rule for any garden: leave it ready for someone else's hands."
  ],
  "quest.069839E9FD2685EE.title": "The room in the records",
  "quest.069839E9FD2685EE.quest_desc": [
    "The Sunken Workshop",
    "",
    "With the four projects delivered, bring three paper and one copper ingot to the Atlas and deliver Workshop Archive. The Atlas hands you Terra's Arm, which lengthens your reach while worn.",
    "",
    "The Sunken Workshop agrees at last: no craft ever replaced the others. And through the static, for the first time, the voice says its own name: '…&kTe&rrra.'"
  ],
  "quest.3D2B82152F596665.title": "A workshop worth connecting",
  "quest.3D2B82152F596665.quest_desc": [
    "The Sunken Workshop",
    "",
    "Optional: choose one supply worth improving (sheets, crystals, fibers or provisions) and keep the other benches working. When the act is complete, choose Advance in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "Terra's workshop fed routes she never drew. The next pages follow where everything went."
  ],
  "image.03FB4B88054E9EEE.title": "&#E8DCB5Terra\\nMeasure and shape",
  "image.53449E341176BD4D.title": "&#E8DCB5Power with a purpose\\n ",
  "image.7A2F67C2142D529E.title": "&#E8DCB5A workshop that\\ngrows",
  "image.7FA32DD3E4117588.title": "&#E8DCB5J.\\nProvision the\\njourney",
  "image.581C3012B6280B80.title": "II · The Lost Crafts",
  "chapter.778667D17CE889F6.title": "III · Routes of Exchange",
  "chapter.778667D17CE889F6.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Under a broken glass dome a garden still blooms. Heliodor's routes started here and led to a capital no map shows."
  ],
  "quest.37439F67D72711CE.title": "The silence between workshops",
  "quest.37439F67D72711CE.quest_desc": [
    "The Greenhouse Dome",
    "",
    "Five projects below rebuild Heliodor's routes: hexagons open the Atlas, squares teach the materials and circles are optional trials. Confirm when ready.",
    "",
    "Under the Greenhouse Dome, Juan's trees still flower. His ledgers show food leaving here for every city, and above all for one: Solsticio."
  ],
  "quest.6B801E1DFD8835ED.title": "Presses from the fallen sky",
  "quest.6B801E1DFD8835ED.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Break a meteorite's mysterious cube without Silk Touch to get the four AE2 presses (a charged meteorite compass points to one), then print and assemble two logic processors in a powered Inscriber.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's routes spoke a language of circuits. The presses fell from the sky; Terra only learned to read them."
  ],
  "quest.67715DD11D530227.title": "A board takes several benches",
  "quest.67715DD11D530227.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Assemble a PneumaticCraft PCB from an unassembled board, two capacitors and two transistors, following its guide for plastic, UV exposure, etching acid and pressures. The Amadron PCB blueprint costs eight emeralds.",
    "",
    "Every route in Juan's ledgers has a board like this at each end, so either side could repair it."
  ],
  "quest.34E8C304216AA748.title": "A blue signal",
  "quest.34E8C304216AA748.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Beam lapis into ordinary Palis crystals at the Atomic Reconstructor (40 energy each). Two go into a routing matrix, with two logic processors, a PCB and a calibration frame.",
    "",
    "Blue was the colour of Heliodor's routes. On the old maps, every blue line ends at the same blank spot."
  ],
  "quest.3E5FB620D650D35E.title": "Budget the first crystal",
  "quest.3E5FB620D650D35E.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Four inferium around an infusion crystal make one prudentium; the crystal costs a diamond, four prosperity shards and four inferium. Budget eight additional inferium for two prudentium.",
    "",
    "Juan grew essences the way he grew wheat: planted, counted, never all at once."
  ],
  "quest.6FF1C6BDC6CF1D6A.title": "Wax from an ordinary hive",
  "quest.6FF1C6BDC6CF1D6A.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Process ordinary Minecraft honeycomb into wax in a basic Productive Bees centrifuge (iron and a grindstone). Two wax, no special breeding.",
    "",
    "The Greenhouse Dome still hums. Juan's bees outlived everyone who kept them."
  ],
  "quest.7E5DA638A8AF99BA.title": "The old garden contributes",
  "quest.7E5DA638A8AF99BA.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Make another living matrix (a calibration frame, two source gems and two magebloom fibers): the act II one was consumed. With two prudentium and two wax it becomes a propagation core.",
    "",
    "Juan's notes grow into B.'s garden bed: the two of them planned this greenhouse together."
  ],
  "quest.1AAAAA6B2E1E4563.title": "Osmium learns a signal",
  "quest.1AAAAA6B2E1E4563.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Infuse an osmium ingot with 20 redstone infusion in a powered Metallurgic Infuser to make a basic control circuit. A power regulator needs two.",
    "",
    "A small generator is enough. Heliodor spread its power thin on purpose, so no single failure could take everything."
  ],
  "quest.597D8746CE914B5A.title": "Steel without a giant furnace",
  "quest.597D8746CE914B5A.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Hammer a steel ingot into an Immersive Engineering steel plate; Mekanism's carbon infusion (enriched iron, steel dust, then smelting) is an early route to the ingot. Keep two plates.",
    "",
    "The dome's frame is steel under copper. It held the glass up for years after the people were gone."
  ],
  "quest.5D719D69593E262A.title": "A coupling, not a power plant",
  "quest.5D719D69593E262A.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Rebuild an energy coupler (two Restonia crystals, an iron casing and two andesite alloys). With two circuits and two steel plates it makes a power regulator.",
    "",
    "The same coupling Terra drew in the Sunken Workshop, now feeding a whole greenhouse."
  ],
  "quest.16E8D490AF70ABCE.title": "Read the tree before the shelf",
  "quest.16E8D490AF70ABCE.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Squeeze a Menril log for 1000 mB of resin, dry it in a Drying Basin into a crystallized Menril block, and craft the block into nine chunks. Keep two.",
    "",
    "Juan planted Menril along every route, so the roads themselves could keep count."
  ],
  "quest.4D75C5943C18E96B.title": "Bake the logic",
  "quest.4D75C5943C18E96B.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Craft four raw LaserIO logic chips from a quartz block, clay balls, gold nuggets and redstone, and smelt them into finished chips. The sensor needs two.",
    "",
    "Clay and gold, baked like bread. Some of Heliodor's best ideas came out of its kitchens."
  ],
  "quest.601DDFCEB1D5FEA2.title": "A second matrix has a job",
  "quest.601DDFCEB1D5FEA2.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Make another routing matrix (two logic processors, a PCB, two Palis crystals and a calibration frame): the first went to A Shared Language. With two Menril chunks and two finished chips it makes an inventory sensor.",
    "",
    "A route that knows when it is full needs nobody shouting at it. Juan's ledgers say that took years to learn."
  ],
  "quest.7C4CA98F4865E101.title": "Paper tells the hands",
  "quest.7C4CA98F4865E101.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Craft six blank Modular Routers modules from paper, gold nuggets and redstone; keep two for the handling core and configure the rest for real jobs.",
    "",
    "In Heliodor, instructions were written on paper first, and only then given to a machine."
  ],
  "quest.130D7A6D79505C81.title": "Five careful passes",
  "quest.130D7A6D79505C81.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Start a Create precision mechanism with a gold plate, then deploy a small cogwheel, a large cogwheel and an iron nugget in order, five times (deployers need brass hands; see Ponder). The result is probabilistic: keep spare inputs.",
    "",
    "Terra's hand shows in every Heliodor mechanism: patient, repeatable, never quite trusting luck."
  ],
  "quest.4634B9599F78810B.title": "A regulator for the hands",
  "quest.4634B9599F78810B.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Make a second power regulator (two basic circuits, two steel plates and an energy coupler); the first was delivered. With two blank modules and a precision mechanism it makes a handling core.",
    "",
    "Hands that pass a part along and keep their tools: Juan's crews worked that way, from dome to dome."
  ],
  "quest.2BF5828C4002A4BD.title": "Label the destination",
  "quest.2BF5828C4002A4BD.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Optional: pick one workshop input, label its source, destination and spare stock, and send a small batch its receiver can recognise unaided. Confirm after trying it.",
    "",
    "Every crate in Juan's ledgers carries a destination. The ones bound for Solsticio carry a golden seal as well."
  ],
  "quest.2D2C52A913E6718A.title": "Leave another harvest possible",
  "quest.2D2C52A913E6718A.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Optional: harvest one crop batch and one ordinary hive batch, and keep back what each needs to produce again. Confirm after trying it.",
    "",
    "Juan never shipped his last seed. 'The city can wait a week,' he wrote. 'The field cannot wait a year.'"
  ],
  "quest.7601671FE64DE066.title": "Watch a whole batch",
  "quest.7601671FE64DE066.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Optional: run a small infuser batch and compare its energy buffer before and after; keep spare fuel or a second source. Confirm after watching it.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's glass roofs once caught the sun for machines like these. None of them ever ran on a single source."
  ],
  "quest.758AAF75374D9805.title": "Stop before overflow",
  "quest.758AAF75374D9805.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Optional: with Integrated Dynamics and Integrated Tunnels, or LaserIO, read a buffer and stop insertion at a small threshold, then watch it resume. Confirm after observing it.",
    "",
    "Every pipe in the greenhouse has a valve Juan could close by hand. He never trusted a store that could not say 'enough'."
  ],
  "quest.2011CCEBA6EF8242.title": "Thirty-two arrive together",
  "quest.2011CCEBA6EF8242.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Optional: move 32 ordinary items between containers with configured Modular Routers modules or a Create setup, and account for all of them at the other end. Confirm once all 32 arrive.",
    "",
    "Juan counted crews the way he counted crates: everyone who left had to arrive."
  ],
  "quest.17BBD680007901AB.title": "A Shared Language",
  "quest.17BBD680007901AB.quest_desc": [
    "A shared language",
    "",
    "Deliver one routing matrix to A Shared Language in the Atlas. It also gives you an Altar of Peace, which keeps hostile creatures from spawning around it.",
    "",
    "Different benches agree on a destination again. The Atlas voice, clearer now: 'Terra here. If you &kcan&r read this… the routes… still work.'"
  ],
  "quest.075794DD2C2DFAA0.title": "Seeds of Continuity",
  "quest.075794DD2C2DFAA0.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · Supplies that return",
    "",
    "Deliver one propagation core to Seeds of Continuity in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Growth: crops around it grow much faster and yield more.",
    "",
    "Juan designed that altar to feed a Heliodor that never stopped growing. His greenhouse fed multitudes; now it can feed you."
  ],
  "quest.55E5576006404510.title": "Power without a Monolith",
  "quest.55E5576006404510.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · Power in many places",
    "",
    "Deliver one power regulator to Power without a Monolith in the Atlas. Regulators are also what Create's advanced solar heating plates, energisers and motors ask for.",
    "",
    "Terra's drawing leaves room for many small suns instead of one great one. Someone wrote 'inefficient' across it, in gold ink."
  ],
  "quest.27A67154B0D96862.title": "When the Shelf is Full",
  "quest.27A67154B0D96862.quest_desc": [
    "Measure before moving",
    "",
    "Deliver one inventory sensor to When the Shelf is Full in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "A full shelf can warn before it jams. Juan's routes did; the orders from Solsticio never waited for the answer."
  ],
  "quest.6C696AA48D00D512.title": "Small Hands, Large Workshops",
  "quest.6C696AA48D00D512.quest_desc": [
    "A workshop within reach",
    "",
    "Deliver one handling core to Small Hands, Large Workshops in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Levelling, which flattens the ground around it, moving earth without creating any.",
    "",
    "Heliodor levelled its terraces with this altar and planted every one. The fields went on; the people did not."
  ],
  "quest.6542C13CC523B0E9.title": "Routes of Exchange",
  "quest.6542C13CC523B0E9.quest_desc": [
    "The Greenhouse Dome",
    "",
    "After the five projects, deliver three paper and one copper ingot to Exchange Route in the Atlas to close the act.",
    "",
    "Every route ends at Solsticio, the capital, and Solsticio is on no map. Terra's voice: 'Look up. The city &mfell&r… did not fall. It is &kstill&r… here.'"
  ],
  "image.1DB295BCFB482280.title": "&#E8DCB5A shared language\\n ",
  "image.1338180D935C206D.title": "&#E8DCB5Juan\\nSupplies that return",
  "image.6927ADE174034DB6.title": "&#E8DCB5Terra\\nPower in many places",
  "image.7C0FD0C7A3DDAD7A.title": "&#E8DCB5Measure before\\nmoving",
  "image.66F68AD0DC228920.title": "&#E8DCB5A workshop within\\nreach",
  "image.15CF12312DD272BC.title": "III · Routes of Exchange",
  "chapter.5EDFD33D3A393061.title": "IV · Voices of the Atlas",
  "chapter.5EDFD33D3A393061.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From an observatory on a cliff, Heliodor watched the sky. In the Temple of the Sacred Light it tried to seize it. In the Aether, the Sun Spirit stopped it."
  ],
  "quest.4C15458A9B706E5B.title": "The missing witnesses",
  "quest.4C15458A9B706E5B.quest_desc": [
    "The Observatory · The witnesses",
    "",
    "Four routes below lead to this act's Atlas projects, and a fifth ends at the Sun Spirit; arrivals in other worlds are recorded on their own when your team gets there. Confirm when ready.",
    "",
    "The Cliffside Observatory still points at the same patch of sky. Its log ends on a single line: 'The light answered.'"
  ],
  "quest.2D6ECC29EBA13A7E.title": "Aether: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.2D6ECC29EBA13A7E.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach the Aether with anyone on your team; arriving, logging in or respawning there counts, even in an earlier act. Clicking this task does nothing: the server records the journey.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's telescope pointed here. Heliodor went up to ask the sky a question."
  ],
  "quest.7FC45742FF7B3AC7.title": "Twilight Forest: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.7FC45742FF7B3AC7.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach the Twilight Forest with anyone on your team; arriving, logging in or respawning there counts, even in an earlier act. The server records it and there is nothing to deliver.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's gardeners called this forest the rehearsal: a world where the light never quite arrives. Juan kept a sanctuary here."
  ],
  "quest.5F8D676F685B8FCE.title": "Bumblezone: a witnessed arrival",
  "quest.5F8D676F685B8FCE.quest_desc": [
    "Journeys recorded by the team",
    "",
    "Reach the Bumblezone with anyone on your team; arriving, logging in or respawning there counts, even in an earlier act. The server records it and there is nothing to claim.",
    "",
    "Juan's bees came from here. Heliodor signed a treaty with them, and the bees still keep their side."
  ],
  "quest.04C25D07C0D4FB2A.title": "A crystal tuned to listening",
  "quest.04C25D07C0D4FB2A.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Make Spirit Fire (drop datura and light it with flint and steel), turn four diamonds into four spirit-attuned gems in it, and craft the gems 2×2 into one spirit-attuned crystal.",
    "",
    "The Observatory listened as well as looked. Its crystals still catch voices nobody is speaking."
  ],
  "quest.3BF05DF763333CD9.title": "Two fragments of testimony",
  "quest.3BF05DF763333CD9.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Make Malum's crude scythe (three iron ingots, one refined soulstone and two wooden rods) and kill a witch with it for arcane spirits. Keep two for each spectral lens.",
    "",
    "Every spirit the scythe frees carries a scrap of something it saw. Heliodor's scraps all end in the same flash."
  ],
  "quest.470125DBFA02EAFD.title": "A patient shutter",
  "quest.470125DBFA02EAFD.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Prepare one Create precision mechanism for the spectral lens; its assembly can fail, so budget a few attempts.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's shutter opened for one second a night. Terra built it; the order to open it wider came from someone else."
  ],
  "quest.4066B5E1E0D6EF29.title": "The familiar frame",
  "quest.4066B5E1E0D6EF29.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Craft a calibration frame from two iron sheets, two copper wires and a raw lens; the spectral lens consumes it.",
    "",
    "Terra's frame again, the same measure as in the first workshop. She built everything to fit together. That was the problem."
  ],
  "quest.599BBE74166CEC6E.title": "Assemble the spectral lens",
  "quest.599BBE74166CEC6E.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Combine a spirit-attuned crystal, two arcane spirits, a precision mechanism and a calibration frame into one spectral lens. Plan two lenses: the archive takes one and the containment seal another.",
    "",
    "Through the lens the static thins. You can hear several voices now, and one of them is giving orders."
  ],
  "quest.3A81D7FB202BC1EF.title": "A route with a return",
  "quest.3A81D7FB202BC1EF.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Optional: the Aether portal is a glowstone frame lit with water; the Twilight Forest opens when you throw a diamond into a 2×2 pool ringed with flowers (lightning strikes, so stand back). Pack food, mark the way home and confirm.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's charts mark both doors. Heliodor never went through one without a way back."
  ],
  "quest.72D8C6025B573FA7.title": "Light above the clouds",
  "quest.72D8C6025B573FA7.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Mine ambrosium ore in the Aether for two ambrosium shards, and keep them apart from your expedition supplies.",
    "",
    "The Aether's light is not the sun's. Heliodor noticed first, and wanted it."
  ],
  "quest.63A78566481EFF47.title": "A forest worked into metal",
  "quest.63A78566481EFF47.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Craft raw ironwood from liveroot, raw iron and a gold nugget, and smelt it into two ironwood ingots.",
    "",
    "Juan's sanctuary in the forest kept samples of everything, labelled with the place and the date. The last label has no date."
  ],
  "quest.00A91663CFB48B49.title": "Food for the record and the road",
  "quest.00A91663CFB48B49.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Make a spare pack of Travel Rations (two vegetable soups and two cooked fish fillets); the horizon chart consumes one, along with survey notes, which can be crafted again. Bring separate food to eat.",
    "",
    "Juan packed rations for the Observatory's night crews. The last order asked for double, 'for the ceremony'."
  ],
  "quest.3DD3BA9CAD0FBB51.title": "Two skies on one page",
  "quest.3DD3BA9CAD0FBB51.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Craft a horizon chart from two ambrosium shards, two ironwood ingots, survey notes and Travel Rations. Before delivering it, check that your team has arrived in both the Aether and the Twilight Forest.",
    "",
    "On one page, two skies that disagree about the colour of morning. The Observatory kept both."
  ],
  "quest.589D6D9B175C666C.title": "Enter as a guest",
  "quest.589D6D9B175C666C.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Optional: throw an ender pearl at a beehive or bee nest to enter the Bumblezone. Mark where you left and learn the way back first; hitting bees or taking honey carelessly brings Wrath. Confirm when ready.",
    "",
    "Juan's treaty had one clause: take nothing you cannot give back."
  ],
  "quest.72A9A7677DB57D63.title": "Carry a little of the meadow",
  "quest.72A9A7677DB57D63.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Gather two pollen puffs from pollen piles in the Bumblezone, using a tool without Silk Touch.",
    "",
    "Pollen from the treaty meadow. Juan's bees still remember the smell of the greenhouse."
  ],
  "quest.10D4D0C6845BF1A4.title": "Wax from the treaty hives",
  "quest.10D4D0C6845BF1A4.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Prepare two Productive Bees wax: ordinary honeycomb goes through the centrifuge, with no special breeding needed.",
    "",
    "The treaty was sealed in wax: Juan's way of saying it could be melted and made again."
  ],
  "quest.155E722412CD338B.title": "Two living supports",
  "quest.155E722412CD338B.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Prepare two living matrices, each from two magebloom fibers, two source gems and a calibration frame.",
    "",
    "Terra's frame, Juan's fibers, B.'s gems: the three of them still hold together in one object."
  ],
  "quest.780224C0B0190A32.title": "A small agreement",
  "quest.780224C0B0190A32.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Combine two pollen puffs, two Productive Bees wax and two living matrices into one ecosystem capsule.",
    "",
    "A whole meadow's agreement, small enough to carry. Heliodor's Altar of Renewal was built around one of these."
  ],
  "quest.7201D80B58E95944.title": "A dark edge for the vessel",
  "quest.7201D80B58E95944.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Mine EvilCraft dark ore for two dark gems; check the tool tier and the Origins of Darkness guide first.",
    "",
    "The Temple of the Sacred Light is ringed with dark stone. Its builders knew the light needed a boundary."
  ],
  "quest.13E112503294DBB6.title": "Steel with a remembered purpose",
  "quest.13E112503294DBB6.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "At Malum's Spirit Altar, an iron ingot, four refined soulstone, three wicked, one earthen and one arcane spirit make one soul-stained steel ingot. For two, gather eight refined soulstone, six wicked, two earthen and two arcane spirits.",
    "",
    "B. was Bodhi, the temple's priest. He forged the sanctuary's seals from this steel, and he was the one who said no."
  ],
  "quest.26ECD64E96DE924C.title": "A second listening glass",
  "quest.26ECD64E96DE924C.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Craft a second spectral lens for the containment seal, with the same crystal, spirits, mechanism and frame.",
    "",
    "One lens for the archive, one for the seal. Bodhi's note: 'Whatever you listen to, you must also be able to close.'"
  ],
  "quest.7DB1A841D53C017A.title": "Keep the silence legible",
  "quest.7DB1A841D53C017A.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Optional: set the archive's materials apart from the seal's and check which lens each one consumes. Confirm once they are separated.",
    "",
    "In the temple, one line of testimony stays unreadable. Bodhi left it that way on purpose: some gaps should not be filled with a convenient answer."
  ],
  "quest.429BA86EC20C7A84.title": "Close the vessel gently",
  "quest.429BA86EC20C7A84.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "Craft one containment seal from two dark gems, two soul-stained steel ingots and a spectral lens; reactor rods for thorium fission ask for one as well.",
    "",
    "The seal is Bodhi's answer to the temple's machine: not a cage for the light, a boundary around it."
  ],
  "quest.4BC3DA06CD2E169A.title": "Voices in the Glass",
  "quest.4BC3DA06CD2E169A.quest_desc": [
    "Listen to the fragments",
    "",
    "Open the Atlas and deliver one spectral lens to Voices in the Glass; keep the second lens for the seal. Reinforced energisers and motors also take a spectral lens.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's crystal plays back a council session. A woman's voice, calm and certain: 'We will not worship the light. We will &mown&r… hold it.' The others call her Aurelia."
  ],
  "quest.6F61C77D6FFCC3F3.title": "Above and Beyond the Canopy",
  "quest.6F61C77D6FFCC3F3.quest_desc": [
    "Compare distant skies",
    "",
    "Once your team has arrived in the Aether and the Twilight Forest, deliver one horizon chart to Above and Beyond the Canopy in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Repose, a small chest that slowly mends the gear inside.",
    "",
    "The Observatory's last chart marks a point above the Aether's clouds, circled in gold: where the light came from."
  ],
  "quest.3329AFECCED6CAAD.title": "The Pollinators Agreement",
  "quest.3329AFECCED6CAAD.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A living agreement",
    "",
    "Once your team has arrived in the Bumblezone, deliver one ecosystem capsule to The Pollinators Agreement in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Renewal, which rebuilds the land the world first generated around it.",
    "",
    "Juan's treaty still holds: the bees kept working after the witnesses left. Some promises outlive the people who made them."
  ],
  "quest.09ED3CB7AB982A11.title": "A Vessel for Restless Memory",
  "quest.09ED3CB7AB982A11.quest_desc": [
    "The Temple · What was sealed",
    "",
    "After Voices in the Glass, deliver one containment seal to A Vessel for Restless Memory in the Atlas. It gives you an Altar of Time: hostile creatures around it move in slow motion and drop far more.",
    "",
    "In the Temple of the Sacred Light the memory opens. Aurelia's council fused the sacred light with Terra's machines to build a god that would obey. Bodhi warned them; the crater is what his warning looked like."
  ],
  "quest.0E407D24B1E4BA07.title": "The Sun Spirit",
  "quest.0E407D24B1E4BA07.quest_desc": [
    "The Aether · The Sun Spirit",
    "",
    "Defeat a Sun Spirit in one of the Aether's gold dungeons; the compass leads there after the silver dungeon. Only its own ice crystals, struck back at it, can wound it. The first one your team defeats drops the Heart of Heliodor, and the server records it.",
    "",
    "It did not destroy Heliodor: it stopped it, and kept the Heart so no one could try again. Bodhi, through the noise: 'It was never &mtheirs&r… never anyone's to take.'"
  ],
  "quest.2BAA7A0AC06298AA.title": "A Clear Voice",
  "quest.2BAA7A0AC06298AA.quest_desc": [
    "The Aether · The Sun Spirit",
    "",
    "Deliver the Heart of Heliodor to A Clear Voice in the Atlas. Only your team's own Heart counts, the one your Sun Spirit dropped. The Atlas keeps it; you will need it again in Solsticio.",
    "",
    "The crystal settles into the Atlas like a key into a lock, and the noise falls away. Terra, whole for the first time: 'There you are. We have always been able to hear you.'"
  ],
  "quest.360D23E7AD32EF6E.title": "The Atlas keeps their voices",
  "quest.360D23E7AD32EF6E.quest_desc": [
    "The Observatory · The witnesses",
    "",
    "With the five projects recorded, the Heart among them, deliver three paper and one copper ingot to The Voices of the Atlas, then choose Advance.",
    "",
    "The temple's last page, read aloud at last: the fusion did not destroy Heliodor, because the Sun Spirit stopped it first and froze everyone inside the light. Terra: 'Now you know what we did. Help us leave without doing it again.'"
  ],
  "image.5D3B686B381AC801.title": "&#E8DCB5Listen to the\\nfragments",
  "image.5A3B25ECD442E8FD.title": "&#E8DCB5Compare distant\\nskies",
  "image.29EE397B163A9AB6.title": "&#E8DCB5Juan\\nA living agreement",
  "image.4D895E524719B78E.title": "&#E8DCB5The Temple\\nWhat was sealed",
  "image.4B16CD2CA0C39EE9.title": "IV · Voices of the Atlas",
  "chapter.068A1E3F716693DD.title": "V · The Ark",
  "chapter.068A1E3F716693DD.chapter_subtitle": [
    "With the Heart of Heliodor in the Atlas, the voice arrives whole: they are alive, inside the light. Build the Ark that opens the way without repeating the fusion."
  ],
  "quest.6E93F29B79991680.title": "A whole voice",
  "quest.6E93F29B79991680.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's plan",
    "",
    "The three projects below prepare the Ark's plan; its six modules, their batches and the activation follow in V · The Activation. Only deliveries in the Atlas record them. Confirm when ready.",
    "",
    "With the Heart in the Atlas, Terra's voice arrives whole: 'We are alive, inside the light. We call it the Entrelumen. Build the Ark, and this time do not try to own what you open.'"
  ],
  "quest.7B041D8C096D588D.title": "Two alloys for the bypass",
  "quest.7B041D8C096D588D.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Make two Mekanism atomic alloys in the Metallurgic Infuser: infused alloy with 20 diamond infusion gives reinforced alloy, and reinforced alloy with 40 refined-obsidian infusion gives atomic alloy.",
    "",
    "Terra designed the Ark's bus with a second path around every part. The fusion machine had none."
  ],
  "quest.3B42EB9382C43AAF.title": "A second path for the order",
  "quest.3B42EB9382C43AAF.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Prepare two PneumaticCraft printed circuit boards: an Empty PCB from the Pressure Chamber, exposed in a UV Light Box and etched, then assembled with two capacitors and two transistors.",
    "",
    "The boards that ran Juan's routes now carry the Ark's orders. Nothing in it is new, and that is the point."
  ],
  "quest.616121CD1220D7F0.title": "Keep the hands at work",
  "quest.616121CD1220D7F0.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Set aside two handling cores for the bus, each from two blank router modules, a precision mechanism and a power regulator.",
    "",
    "Hands that pass a part on and keep their tools. Terra wants the Ark built by many hands, never by one machine."
  ],
  "quest.6C6D77098E537A3C.title": "Know what the buffer holds",
  "quest.6C6D77098E537A3C.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Add one inventory sensor to the bus recipe: Menril chunks, LaserIO logic chips and a routing matrix, as in act III.",
    "",
    "The fusion drew power until nothing was left. The Ark has to know when it is full, and stop."
  ],
  "quest.765DEE642FC97F72.title": "A bus with a way around",
  "quest.765DEE642FC97F72.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "In a crafting grid combine two atomic alloys, two printed circuit boards, two handling cores and one inventory sensor: seven slots make one Ark Connection Bus. Modern Industrialization's nuclear reactor and Ad Astra's NASA workbench ask for one too.",
    "",
    "The Ark's spine. Terra: 'If one route fails, the others carry it. That is all I wanted from the start.'"
  ],
  "quest.612B6CF528DB5881.title": "Field note: empty, refill, resume",
  "quest.612B6CF528DB5881.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: label one input buffer, note its count, cut its supply and let a small job draw it down; restore it and check that the next batch finishes once. Confirm after observing it.",
    "",
    "A pause that can be resumed is what Heliodor lacked. The fusion had only one speed."
  ],
  "quest.7A6A246A99FABD76.title": "A Network that Recovers",
  "quest.7A6A246A99FABD76.quest_desc": [
    "A network that recovers",
    "",
    "Deliver one Ark Connection Bus to A Network That Recovers in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "The first piece of the Ark is a way around failure. Terra, quietly: 'Aurelia asked me for a god. For you, I am building a door.'"
  ],
  "quest.6A0476FB91872873.title": "Metal from an open sky",
  "quest.6A0476FB91872873.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Make two Nature's Aura sky ingots at a flower-decorated Offering Table, using a Spirit of Calling crafted from Overworld and Nether aura bottles, a diamond, infused iron and tainted gold. Infused iron gives one ingot; tainted gold gives two.",
    "",
    "Juan grew metal under the open sky long before the council wanted the sky itself."
  ],
  "quest.1CCC9F83FE8B9B51.title": "A harvest with a ceiling",
  "quest.1CCC9F83FE8B9B51.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Prepare two imperium essences: four tertium around an infusion crystal make one, and each lower tier also takes four, so two imperium cost eight tertium, or 128 inferium.",
    "",
    "Juan's fear, even now inside the light, is running out. A reserve that grows back is his part of the Ark."
  ],
  "quest.60C09916BD96526A.title": "Carry the habitat forward",
  "quest.60C09916BD96526A.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Set aside two ecosystem capsules, each from two pollen puffs, two Productive Bees wax and two living matrices, as in act IV.",
    "",
    "The treaty meadow, carried into the Ark. Juan wants the bees to come along."
  ],
  "quest.409935D6C0EBDC29.title": "Leave the nursery growing",
  "quest.409935D6C0EBDC29.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Add two propagation cores (prudentium, wax and a living matrix each), budgeted apart from the imperium and capsules.",
    "",
    "The greenhouse recipe again, doubled. Juan's nursery is the one part of Heliodor that never stopped."
  ],
  "quest.6F3334D0429BBA36.title": "The reserve's engine",
  "quest.6F3334D0429BBA36.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Combine two sky ingots, two imperium essences, two ecosystem capsules and two propagation cores in a crafting grid. Eight slots make one renewal engine; Modern Industrialization's quantum circuits need one too.",
    "",
    "Juan's rule, built into a machine: take only what can grow back."
  ],
  "quest.5DE0AEDC6388B1EE.title": "Field note: take one, grow one",
  "quest.5DE0AEDC6388B1EE.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: take one bounded batch from your crops, your hive and your aura route, and let each recover before repeating. Confirm after trying it.",
    "",
    "Juan asks the question he has asked for years inside the light: will there be enough tomorrow?"
  ],
  "quest.0FA172F312611EF8.title": "Renewable Horizons",
  "quest.0FA172F312611EF8.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · A reserve that grows back",
    "",
    "Deliver one renewal engine to Renewable Horizons in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "Juan, from inside the Entrelumen: 'Take only what can grow back before the next person needs it. I have fed a whole city on that rule.'"
  ],
  "quest.2BA2EF5E6E24A403.title": "Two meals before departure",
  "quest.2BA2EF5E6E24A403.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Cook two Farmer's Delight fish stews in a cooking pot, from raw fish with tomato sauce and onion.",
    "",
    "Aurelia's charter for the Ark begins, surprisingly, with food. Whoever comes through must be fed."
  ],
  "quest.3B412771A4C57233.title": "Something fresh on the shelf",
  "quest.3B412771A4C57233.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Make two mixed salads from a leafy green, tomato, beetroot and bowl.",
    "",
    "A fresh plate on the charter's list, in Juan's hand. Aurelia signed underneath without changing a word."
  ],
  "quest.77320E2B7BDC2510.title": "A count the next person can read",
  "quest.77320E2B7BDC2510.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Add one AE2 calculation processor, printed in the Inscriber, to the Habitation Charter.",
    "",
    "Aurelia counts everything; it is how she governs. For once, the count is for the people arriving, not for the council."
  ],
  "quest.7CDE8A7F14D2DA00.title": "Food for the road and the return",
  "quest.7CDE8A7F14D2DA00.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Set aside two packs of Travel Rations (two vegetable soups and two cooked fish fillets each), apart from the stew and salad.",
    "",
    "The same rations Juan packed for the workshop's long shifts. This time they are for a door that opens both ways."
  ],
  "quest.7D7BB71A417C6A1F.title": "A charter for an inhabited place",
  "quest.7D7BB71A417C6A1F.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Combine two fish stews, two mixed salads, one calculation processor and two packs of Travel Rations: seven slots make one Habitation Charter, and the four bowls come back to you.",
    "",
    "Aurelia's seal on a promise: whoever crosses will find a place to live. She has not yet said what she wants in return."
  ],
  "quest.64A39E89998AE121.title": "Field note: a room someone can use",
  "quest.64A39E89998AE121.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: walk from your arrival point to a lit bed, a reachable kitchen and a pantry with readable stock, and ask whether a newcomer could manage alone. Confirm after the walk.",
    "",
    "Soon, people who have not walked in the sun for years will come through. Bodhi asks only that they feel welcome."
  ],
  "quest.41D22D9557C9E920.title": "A Place Worth Returning To",
  "quest.41D22D9557C9E920.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · A place to return to",
    "",
    "Deliver one Habitation Charter to A Place to Return To in the Atlas.",
    "",
    "The first day's sentence, complete at last. Terra: 'Make room for those who have not arrived yet. We are the ones.'"
  ],
  "quest.49D5419C7B57F699.title": "Field note: a visible pause",
  "quest.49D5419C7B57F699.quest_desc": [
    "Optional field notes · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: if you enjoy ComputerCraft, build a small panel that shows a buffer's count and whether it is paused; a sign and a manual stop work just as well. Confirm after comparing it with the real container.",
    "",
    "Terra's workshop had a board like this on every wall. Nobody should have to guess whether a machine is running."
  ],
  "quest.2186E0A1EC9CA518.title": "A door, not a god",
  "quest.2186E0A1EC9CA518.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's plan",
    "",
    "When the three projects are recorded, deliver three paper and one copper ingot to World Network in the Atlas. The six module projects open next, in V · The Activation; there is no Advance here.",
    "",
    "The Ark's plan is complete: six modules around a controller that opens a rift in the light. Once you activate it, the Ark will forge the Light Key. Bodhi's only condition: 'Open it. Never own it.'"
  ],
  "image.282226BC39CBEDE9.title": "&#E8DCB5A network that\\nrecovers",
  "image.190ECD9B1C347E05.title": "&#E8DCB5Juan\\nA reserve that grows\\nback",
  "image.30AFDFA039D87D2A.title": "&#E8DCB5Aurelia\\nA place to return to\\n ",
  "image.6FD005BB32A7B418.title": "V · The Ark",
  "chapter.74FF10FB2B3398AB.title": "V · The Activation",
  "chapter.74FF10FB2B3398AB.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Six modules around a controller, six batches and one deliberate act: the Ark opens a seam in the light and forges the Light Key."
  ],
  "quest.7DC68DC8093ED0F0.title": "The Ark takes shape",
  "quest.7DC68DC8093ED0F0.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's controller",
    "",
    "Build six different Ark modules, place them around the controller and commission them one batch at a time; activating the Ark forges the Light Key and opens act VI. This optional page only introduces the chapter: confirm when ready.",
    "",
    "Terra spreads the plan across the Atlas: six chambers, one for each discipline of Heliodor. 'The fusion wanted one machine to hold everything. This time, six hands hold one door.'"
  ],
  "quest.6ADB6852EF50938D.title": "A controller, not a throne",
  "quest.6ADB6852EF50938D.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The Ark's controller",
    "",
    "Craft the Ark Controller shapelessly from one lodestone, one signal core and one diamond, and keep it: owning it records nothing. Place it where all six module blocks can stay nearby; a normal interaction reports the current batch and any missing block.",
    "",
    "Aurelia wanted a throne at the centre of the fusion machine. Terra built a controller instead: anyone can read it, and it obeys only a team that finished its work."
  ],
  "quest.6E755C961BFC8754.title": "A bus with a second path",
  "quest.6E755C961BFC8754.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "Set aside two Mekanism atomic alloys for the Engineering Module. Its delivery also takes two calibration frames, two energy couplers and one Ark Connection Bus: the same seven parts as its crafting recipe, so a lost module can be made again.",
    "",
    "Terra draws a bypass beside every line of the Ark. The fusion machine had one path for everything, and nowhere to go when it failed."
  ],
  "quest.0AF7E5AD8DAA6FA2.title": "A boundary with a witness",
  "quest.0AF7E5AD8DAA6FA2.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "Reserve two Occultism iesnium ingots. Iesnium hides as Nether netherrack: Otherworld Goggles reveal it and an Infused or Iesnium Pickaxe mines it; smelt the raw ore. Two spectral lenses and two containment seals complete the Arcane Module's delivery and recipe.",
    "",
    "Bodhi asks for a boundary around the strange light, with a window in it. 'Seal what could hurt us. Never seal it from sight.'"
  ],
  "quest.32C7CF38D764EF3C.title": "A reserve that answers",
  "quest.32C7CF38D764EF3C.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "The Nature Module takes one renewal engine, two ecosystem capsules and two living matrices; the same five inputs craft a replacement if the block is lost. Keep your settlement's own reserve where it is.",
    "",
    "Juan's rule, now inside the Ark: if one supply fails, a living system must be able to begin again. He learned it feeding a frozen city."
  ],
  "quest.2C387677AC04141E.title": "Routes with readable stores",
  "quest.2C387677AC04141E.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "Prepare two routing matrices, two handling cores and one Ark Connection Bus for the Logistics Module. The same five inputs craft a replacement without reopening the one-time Atlas project; holding them only completes this lesson.",
    "",
    "Aurelia counts everything, and for once Terra agrees: before a route changes, anyone should be able to check what it carries."
  ],
  "quest.41D8D1F4B9303A79.title": "A room for whoever follows",
  "quest.41D8D1F4B9303A79.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "Set aside one Habitation Charter, two packs of Travel Rations and two living matrices for the Habitation Module; the same five inputs craft a replacement later. Count these two packs apart from the eight the commissioning will ask for.",
    "",
    "Juan packed rations like these for Terra's long shifts. Aurelia signs for every pack: nobody crossing the light should arrive to an empty kitchen."
  ],
  "quest.2A320DF4401C30B7.title": "A chart with a return line",
  "quest.2A320DF4401C30B7.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "The Exploration Module takes one horizon chart, one spectral lens, two Twilight Forest steeleaf ingots, two Aether zanite gemstones and a bottle of the dragon's breath. Search Hollow Hill chests for steeleaf (Labyrinth chests are a chance, not a promise) and mine zanite ore without Silk Touch.",
    "",
    "Terra draws the way home before the way in. The fusion's engineers never marked a return; the Ark's first line is one."
  ],
  "quest.0755047847D475BE.title": "The old doorway",
  "quest.0755047847D475BE.quest_desc": [
    "The End · A witnessed journey",
    "",
    "Craft Eyes of Ender from ender pearls and blaze powder. A thrown eye leads toward a stronghold, and its portal frame needs eyes to open; bring enough for both. Carrying eyes only prepares the trip: your campaign still has to enter the End.",
    "",
    "The Atlas remembers this doorway from Heliodor's oldest charts. They never used it. They were too busy looking up."
  ],
  "quest.29624D0B73CD7B51.title": "Field note: a way home",
  "quest.29624D0B73CD7B51.quest_desc": [
    "The End · A witnessed journey",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: pack food, protection and blocks before the stronghold portal and agree on a return route. In a new End, defeating the dragon opens the exit home; on a shared world it may already be open, and your team needs no second kill. Confirm when you have a plan.",
    "",
    "Bodhi asks one thing of every journey: that it ends where it began, with everyone."
  ],
  "quest.0ED905C35BF0C497.title": "A horizon actually crossed",
  "quest.0ED905C35BF0C497.quest_desc": [
    "The End · A witnessed journey",
    "",
    "Enter the End with your current team. The server witnesses real entry, login or respawn there; an earlier visit counts, even before act V. Joining a team does not bring your personal travels with you, and clicking this task does nothing.",
    "",
    "Terra needs the End's silence measured for the exploration module: the one place the light of the Aether never reached."
  ],
  "quest.50643B60ED2D63DF.title": "Engineering: a path around failure",
  "quest.50643B60ED2D63DF.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver two calibration frames, two energy couplers, one Ark Connection Bus and two Mekanism atomic alloys to Engineering Module in the Atlas. Placed, an empty hand reads the team's diagnosis; a damaged tool with its repair material in the offhand gets a quarter of its durability back, no experience spent.",
    "",
    "Terra: 'Everything breaks. What matters is whether you can fix it.'"
  ],
  "quest.7B4CB4FC66705C6B.title": "Arcane: a boundary that holds",
  "quest.7B4CB4FC66705C6B.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver two spectral lenses, two containment seals, one Occultism iesnium ingot and one nether star from the Wither to Arcane Module in the Atlas. Placed, it opens the team's field journal, takes its stabilization batch when crouch-used empty-handed, and splits a book of several enchantments into single volumes, one ordinary book per extra volume.",
    "",
    "Bodhi keeps the strange light behind glass: sealed, never hidden."
  ],
  "quest.32E5B9B04FF003DE.title": "Nature: growth with reserves",
  "quest.32E5B9B04FF003DE.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver one renewal engine, two ecosystem capsules, one living matrix and one wet sponge from an Elder Guardian to Nature Module in the Atlas. Placed, it opens the restoration journal and takes its batch when crouch-used empty-handed. Mark a site with a bookmarked compass; then bone meal and saplings bring back its biome's cover and trees, leaving built blocks alone.",
    "",
    "Juan: 'Take only what can grow back.'"
  ],
  "quest.5B5E7641B77420D5.title": "Logistics: a count before movement",
  "quest.5B5E7641B77420D5.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver two routing matrices, two handling cores and one Ark Connection Bus to Logistics Module in the Atlas. Placed, an empty hand opens its 27-slot depot, crouching adds to the current Ark batch, and a routing matrix records and refills a personal expedition kit from the depot.",
    "",
    "Aurelia's ledger, turned outward: everyone can see what the Ark holds before they leave."
  ],
  "quest.0984C0DF0C9E836E.title": "Habitation: a place to arrive",
  "quest.0984C0DF0C9E836E.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network, deliver one Habitation Charter, two packs of Travel Rations and two living matrices to Habitation Module in the Atlas. Placed, it opens the supply journal and takes its provisioning batch when crouch-used empty-handed; used with a bed, it reserves a temporary respawn and keeps your old home.",
    "",
    "Aurelia promised a place to live to whoever crosses. Juan makes sure there is dinner."
  ],
  "quest.105A416A3980602B.title": "Exploration: the return marked first",
  "quest.105A416A3980602B.quest_desc": [
    "Six distinct contributions",
    "",
    "After World Network and a witnessed End arrival, deliver one horizon chart, one spectral lens, two Twilight Forest steeleaf ingots, two Aether zanite gemstones and one bottle of the dragon's breath to Exploration Module in the Atlas. Placed, it opens the journey journal and takes the final chart when crouch-used; with a filled map, it fills blank pixels from your other maps of that area.",
    "",
    "Terra's charts all start with the way home."
  ],
  "quest.6FAA2E089CEFD78E.title": "Field note: six blocks in reach",
  "quest.6FAA2E089CEFD78E.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: place the controller and keep all six module blocks within three blocks horizontally, one below or two above it. Inspect the controller to see which ones it finds; the server checks the real blocks at every batch and at activation.",
    "",
    "Six chambers close enough to hear each other. Terra built the fusion machine as one piece; the Ark is six, side by side."
  ],
  "quest.790F7DA7C34DE333.title": "I · Calibrate the bypass",
  "quest.790F7DA7C34DE333.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "With all six module projects credited and their blocks around the controller, bring four additional calibration frames and two additional power regulators. Crouch and use the controller with an empty main hand; it takes what you carry toward the batch, and partial deposits survive a restart. Inspect it for the remainder.",
    "",
    "Terra checks every bypass twice. The fusion was never checked once."
  ],
  "quest.3FDD095D9F8F9109.title": "II · Hold the boundary",
  "quest.3FDD095D9F8F9109.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The second batch takes two additional containment seals at the controller, with the six module blocks still in place and the same crouched, empty-handed use. The first batch is already credited: repeating it takes nothing and skips nothing.",
    "",
    "Bodhi watches the seals settle. 'A boundary you can check again tomorrow is worth more than one you swear by today.'"
  ],
  "quest.0CC3F84AEB9FD36C.title": "III · Keep a living reserve",
  "quest.0CC3F84AEB9FD36C.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The third batch takes two additional ecosystem capsules. Deposit them with the six module blocks present; the server records each accepted amount and credits the step when the batch is complete.",
    "",
    "Juan will not call a reserve renewable because the diagram is green. He waits to see it grow back, the way he has waited inside the light for years."
  ],
  "quest.42B7C481E3710955.title": "IV · Route the first load",
  "quest.42B7C481E3710955.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The fourth batch takes two additional routing matrices, apart from the ones the Logistics Module consumed. A deposit can be partial; inspect the controller for the exact remainder before bringing more.",
    "",
    "Aurelia wants the Ark's routes legible even after someone leaves the team. It is the first rule of hers Terra ever agreed with."
  ],
  "quest.63EF631DCCEDFEC9.title": "V · Provision a welcome",
  "quest.63EF631DCCEDFEC9.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The fifth batch takes eight more packs of Travel Rations, apart from the two the Habitation Module used. Keep every module block in place and deposit them crouching with an empty main hand.",
    "",
    "Juan's arithmetic is blunt: a door that brings people through must also feed them when they arrive, without quietly emptying the kitchen at home."
  ],
  "quest.2924970994B829D6.title": "VI · Chart a return",
  "quest.2924970994B829D6.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "The sixth and last batch takes one additional horizon chart, apart from the one the Exploration Module consumed. After it, inspect the controller: six batches can be complete while the activation still waits for your explicit choice.",
    "",
    "Terra folds the chart so the route home stays on its outer face. 'Whoever crosses should always see the way back.'"
  ],
  "quest.70A235F354AA1ED4.title": "The Ark opens the light",
  "quest.70A235F354AA1ED4.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark · Six recoverable batches",
    "",
    "After six credited batches, with World Network complete, the End journey witnessed and all six modules beside the controller, crouch and interact with it once more with an empty main hand. That act activates the Ark, consumes nothing and forges your team's Light Key. Act VI begins.",
    "",
    "The light parts along a seam. Bodhi, very quietly: 'Open it. Never own it.' Behind it, Solsticio."
  ],
  "quest.58F2D36080402035.title": "Afterward: two routes",
  "quest.58F2D36080402035.quest_desc": [
    "After the activation · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: make two different ways to move one useful supply between your settlements, then pause one and see whether the other is understandable and usable. Note what failed and what was easy to repair.",
    "",
    "Terra's favourite test, older than the fusion: a system is only as good as its second path."
  ],
  "quest.3554A2E575F882C0.title": "Afterward: a shared reserve",
  "quest.3554A2E575F882C0.quest_desc": [
    "After the activation · self-reported",
    "",
    "Optional, self-reported: pick one renewable food or material reserve, let a visitor take a known amount and time how long your usual process takes to replace it. Note what would make the reserve fair to share.",
    "",
    "Juan's question, the one he asks Solsticio every morning: if someone new arrives today, will there be enough tomorrow?"
  ],
  "image.74D63C02CC64588E.title": "&#E8DCB5Terra\\nThe Ark's controller\\n ",
  "image.1A15A4B9687FEFF5.title": "&#E8DCB5Six distinct contributions",
  "image.373F236C52896BC6.title": "&#E8DCB5The End\\nA witnessed journey",
  "image.4D2C12DBA367955C.title": "&#E8DCB5After the activation\\nself-reported\\n ",
  "image.67E978C9D0FD2690.title": "V · The Activation",
  "chapter.74950145DD0B7777.title": "VI · Solsticio",
  "chapter.74950145DD0B7777.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The capital of Heliodor, frozen inside the Entrelumen. Cross with the Light Key: the voices are waiting in person."
  ],
  "quest.0C1B162D867478B1.title": "Inside the light",
  "quest.0C1B162D867478B1.quest_desc": [
    "The Light Key · The crossing",
    "",
    "Hold use with your Light Key until the ring closes. It carries you into Solsticio and breaks as you cross; what is left takes you home and back.",
    "",
    "Noon over copper and glass, and nobody has aged a day. Terra is already waving."
  ],
  "quest.4B9FF6036B58B45C.title": "The City That Never Dawns",
  "quest.4B9FF6036B58B45C.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · The town hall",
    "",
    "Talk to Aurelia in the town hall, beside the portal.",
    "",
    "'Three relics and the key that brought you. Juan, Terra and Bodhi each hold one. The Heart of Heliodor I would keep myself, of course.'"
  ],
  "quest.2B8961936F4D5A47.title": "Seeds of the World",
  "quest.2B8961936F4D5A47.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · The gardens",
    "",
    "Bring Juan seeds of eight different species from outside: wheat, beetroot, melon, carrot, potato, berries, cocoa, Farmer's Delight crops...",
    "",
    "'Same seeds since the light fell. The beds are tired. Variety, not sacks.'"
  ],
  "quest.4B4467623D387F88.title": "A Harvest for Everyone",
  "quest.4B4467623D387F88.quest_desc": [
    "Juan · The gardens",
    "",
    "Bring Juan four different Farmer's Delight meals, sixteen of each; Central Kitchen or Slice and Dice can cook them. He gives you the Luminous Seed.",
    "",
    "'A city eats every day. Feed it, and the seed that carries the light is yours.'"
  ],
  "quest.0FB869472B3FEFE1.title": "Power from Outside",
  "quest.0FB869472B3FEFE1.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The workshop",
    "",
    "Bring Terra four Generator Coils, two Advanced Solar Heating Plates and a charged battery from any energy mod (100,000 FE or more). She gives you the Terraprism diagram.",
    "",
    "'Frozen light runs machines badly. I need power from outside. Charged means full.'"
  ],
  "quest.1F02073F3CFFC2AF.title": "Channelling the Light",
  "quest.1F02073F3CFFC2AF.quest_desc": [
    "Terra · The workshop",
    "",
    "Bring Terra one Luminosity of each discipline, all six; the natives of the trading hall sell them once they have seen their biome. She gives you the Terraprism.",
    "",
    "'It takes the light and gives it back as power people can use. That is all I ever wanted it to do.'"
  ],
  "quest.67AAA396175290D7.title": "Good Works",
  "quest.67AAA396175290D7.quest_desc": [
    "Bodhi · The chapel",
    "",
    "Do the errands of the four innkeepers, two each. Every errand raises your relation with Bodhi; at five, he listens.",
    "",
    "'I do not bless on request. Help the people here; I will hear about it.'"
  ],
  "quest.301807F294656252.title": "The Blessing",
  "quest.301807F294656252.quest_desc": [
    "Bodhi · The chapel",
    "",
    "Talk to Bodhi: your Atlas gives back the Heart of Heliodor. Hand it to him and it becomes the Blessed Heart of Heliodor. If the Sun Spirit still has it, beat it first.",
    "",
    "'It was never a machine's heart. With love, then.'"
  ],
  "quest.3D6E10D1A9FBFA20.title": "The Table of Two Lights",
  "quest.3D6E10D1A9FBFA20.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · The town hall",
    "",
    "With the three relics, talk to Aurelia in the town hall and to Bodhi in the chapel, in either order.",
    "",
    "She wants the crystal to rule the light; he fears a second fusion. The only way out is that nobody keeps it."
  ],
  "quest.59DCA82BB3F25E0A.title": "The Portal",
  "quest.59DCA82BB3F25E0A.quest_desc": [
    "The portal · The Entrelumen",
    "",
    "Right-click the town hall portal with each of your three relics, then with your own Broken Light Key in your pack. The first team to open it frees the Entrelumen for everyone, and every shop gets cheaper.",
    "",
    "Still a shelter. No longer a prison."
  ],
  "quest.2F34597F922F9618.title": "Elections in Solsticio",
  "quest.2F34597F922F9618.quest_desc": [
    "Aurelia · The town hall",
    "",
    "Three days after the portal first opens, the square votes. Then talk to Aurelia.",
    "",
    "'Elected. It sounds different from appointed.' Nobody asks too loudly about the new windows."
  ],
  "image.38A380ECBB629012.title": "VI · Solsticio",
  "chapter.551D4E474ABCF322.title": "An Inventory That Remembers",
  "quest.3D6A85207D225A5A.title": "Self-check: Two columns in the margin",
  "quest.3D6A85207D225A5A.quest_desc": [
    "Mara's margin",
    "",
    "After the first light answered, Mara drew TAKE and LEAVE beside the map. Choose one supply to carry through a hurried return and one material to leave at the workshop. Decide which column each belongs in, then mark this note.",
    "",
    "These notes are optional. A square fills when you carry its item and takes nothing from you; a circle is yours to mark after you try its exercise. Neither holds up the journey."
  ],
  "quest.73A9E5C7AAD95425.title": "A bag for the road",
  "quest.73A9E5C7AAD95425.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "Make a basic Sophisticated Backpack with leather, string and a wooden chest; check the recipe for their placement. Put an ordinary block inside, close the bag, then find and remove it again. Look for the backpack action under Controls if you want quick access. This basic bag is enough for the exercises ahead."
  ],
  "quest.0BD095E6B6E17434.title": "A place that stays",
  "quest.0BD095E6B6E17434.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Combine an ordinary chest and a lever to make a Sophisticated Storage chest. Set it beside the bench you use and give it one job: incoming stone, repair supplies or food for the next journey. Put a matching stack inside and leave room for your return. The bag travels with you; this chest tells anyone coming home where to look."
  ],
  "quest.06DF53C2BFE4AFD2.title": "Self-check: What must stay aboard",
  "quest.06DF53C2BFE4AFD2.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "Pack food for a short trip and a spare tool in places you can remember. Keep the working tool within reach; the spare is for a broken handle. Leave a food reserve at home so an empty return can still lead to another departure.",
    "",
    "Before you leave, open the bag and the home chest and point to each reserve. Mark this note when you can find both without searching every slot."
  ],
  "quest.5D95843A3184F140.title": "Self-check: An empty slot with a name",
  "quest.5D95843A3184F140.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "In the chest's settings, set Memory on one slot holding a common workshop material. Remove its last stack, then try putting the same material and a different one back. Notice where each goes. If the result differs from your plan, revisit the slot and its setting before using scarce stock. The empty space can keep a place for tomorrow's stone."
  ],
  "quest.6C84395CBBF885D1.title": "The bag learns to gather",
  "quest.6C84395CBBF885D1.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "The basic Pickup Upgrade uses an Upgrade Base, a sticky piston, string and redstone; check the recipe viewer for their placement. Put it in the backpack's upgrade slot and open its settings. Start with one plentiful block in the filter. Leave rare tools out of the first ground test; the next note follows two ordinary drops."
  ],
  "quest.7C2785BCD9168E16.title": "A second stack within reach",
  "quest.7C2785BCD9168E16.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "The Refill Upgrade can supply a selected inventory stack from the backpack. Its recipe uses an Upgrade Base, an ender pearl, a chest, iron and redstone; check the recipe viewer before crafting it. Keep spare torches in the bag for the first trial: each torch you use leaves a gap you can see. Keep another reserve at home before relying on the bag in a cave."
  ],
  "quest.075CA7AC583930A5.title": "A rule at the workshop door",
  "quest.075CA7AC583930A5.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Make a Sophisticated Storage Filter Upgrade for the workshop chest. It governs items moved into or out of storage by a hopper or other transport; the backpack's Pickup Upgrade has a different job. Choose one plentiful block to allow and another cheap block to reject, then set the rule in the upgrade's controls. Test both before sending scarce materials through."
  ],
  "quest.4063D2008AF59266.title": "A shared doorstep",
  "quest.4063D2008AF59266.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "A Storage Controller gives connected Sophisticated Storage blocks one place for deposits and external item transfer. Its recipe starts with a wooden storage block and comparators; check the recipe viewer for the arrangement. Place it near two stores you can inspect easily, with a different common material in each. Keep the individual stores useful so you can trace a deposit to its shelf."
  ],
  "quest.77EC138087997CE7.title": "Self-check: Two drops, one decision",
  "quest.77EC138087997CE7.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "Install Pickup and set its filter for one plentiful block. In a safe place, drop that block and a different expendable item, one at a time. Look in the backpack, your inventory and the ground to find both. If the route surprises you, adjust the filter and repeat with cheap materials. Mark this note when you can account for both drops."
  ],
  "quest.2B06BADADE64C6EC.title": "Self-check: The last torch is visible",
  "quest.2B06BADADE64C6EC.quest_desc": [
    "What travels with you",
    "",
    "The basic backpack has one upgrade slot. Remove Pickup or the previous upgrade and install Refill. Put spare torches in the bag and select torches in Refill's settings. Use one from your inventory, then compare the carried stack with the bag's reserve. Remove the spare torches and repeat to see what happens when the reserve runs out. Keep food and the spare tool in their own places, ready for the trip home."
  ],
  "quest.76C13553573D6B65.title": "Self-check: The chest accepts one kind",
  "quest.76C13553573D6B65.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Fit the Filter Upgrade to the workshop chest and feed it through a hopper. Try one permitted block, then one rejected block, separately. Check the hopper and chest after each attempt; a rejected item may wait upstream. Manual insertion and piped insertion can follow different rules. Mark this note once you know where both blocks ended, and clear the hopper before a real batch."
  ],
  "quest.0AA71C8CE15A3C4D.title": "Self-check: One entrance, two shelves",
  "quest.0AA71C8CE15A3C4D.quest_desc": [
    "A bench with a memory",
    "",
    "Place the controller beside two connected Sophisticated Storage blocks. Put a different ordinary material in each store, then make a small deposit through the controller. Find the deposited items in the physical stores and take them back out. If nothing moves, inspect the connections before adding more shelves. Mark this note after you can follow the route in both directions."
  ],
  "quest.2D86B44DFFE54B85.title": "The return has a gesture",
  "quest.2D86B44DFFE54B85.quest_desc": [
    "The return route",
    "",
    "The Backpack Deposit Upgrade moves items from the bag into an inventory you sneak-right-click. Its recipe uses an Upgrade Base, a piston, a wooden chest, iron and redstone; check the recipe viewer for the layout. Put ordinary stone in the workshop chest and in your bag before trying Match Inventory Contents. Keep food and a spare tool in the bag so you can see what stays with you."
  ],
  "quest.6A3E9ACF03298C69.title": "Self-check: The bag comes home lighter",
  "quest.6A3E9ACF03298C69.quest_desc": [
    "The return route",
    "",
    "Swap the previous upgrade for Deposit in the basic backpack's single upgrade slot. Put a small stack of stone in the bag beside the food and spare tool you chose to keep. Stock the workshop chest with stone, set Deposit to Match Inventory Contents, and sneak-right-click that chest with the bag. Count stone in both places, then check the food and tool. If the result surprises you, retrieve the items and repeat with cheap stock. Mark this note after the travel reserve stays aboard."
  ],
  "quest.56BE1D70BFD96C1B.title": "Self-check: A shelf after the network",
  "quest.56BE1D70BFD96C1B.quest_desc": [
    "One shelf stays local",
    "",
    "Sera's later sketches show a digital network; Mara keeps a physical shelf beside the bench. When you have AE2, close its terminal and take one food stack and one repair supply from that local shelf. Decide which reserve should remain within reach if the network is unavailable. Mark this note after you can retrieve both without the terminal, then restock the shelf for the next return."
  ],
  "image.6CFB251A3F6DA4D4.title": "&#E8DCB5What travels with you",
  "image.0A016725085D1DEB.title": "&#E8DCB5A bench with a memory",
  "image.228EA175BAB72CD1.title": "&#E8DCB5The return route",
  "chapter_group.192C7E7D9BC8BCFF.title": "Heliodor's Legacy",
  "chapter_group.7B00A650A207F91E.title": "Quality of Life",
  "chapter_group.56152B099337B914.title": "Technology",
  "chapter_group.4D74159E6A679408.title": "Magic",
  "chapter_group.4D7F6E113F6DB815.title": "Exploration",
  "chapter.0216243AA5083CE1.title": "Waking Among Ruins",
  "chapter.0216243AA5083CE1.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Empty pockets, a ruined sun patio and the light that guards Heliodor's places."
  ],
  "quest.7B2FDFC0D74F1790.title": "You Wake Among Ruins",
  "quest.7B2FDFC0D74F1790.quest_desc": [
    "Every world starts the same: you appear beside a ruined sun patio with empty pockets. The ruin, its compass and the Atlas are your only guides.",
    "",
    "No tutorial, no kit, no welcome committee. Heliodor has been busy being frozen."
  ],
  "quest.51F1081FE91AE567.title": "Empty Pockets, on Purpose",
  "quest.51F1081FE91AE567.quest_desc": [
    "The pack turns off every join gift: Ars Nouveau's notebook, the Integrated Dynamics manual, Silent Gear's blueprints, the Actually Additions booklet and more. Every one of those books is still craftable.",
    "",
    "Nothing is lost, only not gifted. Not even the plush toy."
  ],
  "quest.5DF068ECC8A3C79B.title": "Quirk: the Aether Says Hi",
  "quest.5DF068ECC8A3C79B.quest_desc": [
    "One gift survives: the first time you enter the Aether, it hands you its Book of Lore and golden parachutes. It is not a login gift, it is a safety net.",
    "",
    "Floating islands, long drops. Take the hint."
  ],
  "quest.54D8683481D00162.title": "The Start Ruin",
  "quest.54D8683481D00162.quest_desc": [
    "A new world places it once, on the flattest ground within 64 blocks of spawn: a tuff and calcite patio with an oxidized copper sun, eight quartz columns (four broken) and the &eHeliodor Pedestal&r in the middle.",
    "",
    "World spawn moves beside it, and your first login faces it."
  ],
  "quest.3A3D2F69F7A51597.title": "Take the Compass",
  "quest.3A3D2F69F7A51597.quest_desc": [
    "Use the pedestal: it gives each player one &eHeliodor Compass&r per world, ever. Its first target is the ruin itself, until you wake the Atlas with a book and a copper ingot.",
    "",
    "Everything else about it: The Heliodor Compass chapter."
  ],
  "quest.04910797C8A95EC6.title": "First Steps That Work",
  "quest.04910797C8A95EC6.quest_desc": [
    "Tree, wooden tools, crafting table, stone, coal. Then go after &ecopper&r: the Atlas and its first projects want copper ingots, paper and glass.",
    "",
    "The compass will send you to a village for bread and paper, then to trial chambers, full of copper and tuff like the ruin."
  ],
  "quest.393FB3DA62E83A3D.title": "The Light Keeps These Places",
  "quest.393FB3DA62E83A3D.quest_desc": [
    "Inside a protected ruin nobody can break or place blocks, and neither can explosions, pistons, flowing fluids, spreading fire, griefing mobs or trampling. Frames, paintings and armor stands are safe too.",
    "",
    "The server checks at the moment it happens: creative, spectator and noclip get the same polite no."
  ],
  "quest.73BFA7978DF2985A.title": "Free, Sealed and Locked",
  "quest.73BFA7978DF2985A.quest_desc": [
    "Right-clicks inside a protected place fall in three groups. &eFree&r: doors, buttons, levers, beds, simple workstations, ender chests and the pedestal. &eSealed&r: containers, lecterns and altars, which open when your team reaches that place's act. &eLocked&r: anything else that would change a block, and anvils.",
    "",
    "A frame's item can be taken once your team is unlocked; the frame stays."
  ],
  "quest.76BB64F3BA0C95E3.title": "Why Ruins Are Protected",
  "quest.76BB64F3BA0C95E3.quest_desc": [
    "Ruins are the story's levels: their lore and key pieces open when your team gets there, whatever tricks anyone tries.",
    "",
    "It also stops a friend from blowing up the exact spot the compass is pointing at. Do not ask how we know."
  ],
  "quest.0430D747262F84EB.title": "Quirk: Tools Stop at the Edge",
  "quest.0430D747262F84EB.quest_desc": [
    "Ultimine, gadgets, construction sticks, Carry On and the land-shaping altars all act as a player, so they stop at a ruin's edge; Carry On's break check before lifting is refused too.",
    "",
    "Build around a ruin, not into it."
  ],
  "quest.3C0CF3ADDFD6F214.title": "The Same Light Covers Solsticio",
  "quest.3C0CF3ADDFD6F214.quest_desc": [
    "The city at the end of the story uses the same protection, gated by act VI. The exception is the player plots: 16 by 16, one per team, where only your team builds.",
    "",
    "How to claim one: the Solsticio chapter."
  ],
  "quest.2D3295A6543F9E15.title": "Tip: Your Spawn Is the Ruin",
  "quest.2D3295A6543F9E15.quest_desc": [
    "Until you sleep in a bed, you respawn at the start ruin. Set a bed or a Comforts sleeping spot near your first base early.",
    "",
    "Tombstone keeps your items in a grave where you fall, so the walk back only costs you dignity."
  ],
  "quest.3925C4CC5C5C7AE4.title": "For Operators: Older Worlds",
  "quest.3925C4CC5C5C7AE4.quest_desc": [
    "Only brand-new worlds get the start ruin. In an older one, an operator places it with &e/entrelumen admin ruin&r (running it twice does nothing) and toggles a personal protection bypass for repairs with &e/entrelumen admin protection bypass&r."
  ],
  "quest.5BBA78C05C867FBA.title": "Quirk: Blind Spots",
  "quest.5BBA78C05C867FBA.quest_desc": [
    "A few things slip past: blocks changed by mods that skip the usual game events, projectiles breaking fragile blocks such as pots, and plot machines placing fluids or blocks right against a protected one (placed that way, they cannot spread further).",
    "",
    "Found a hole? Report it. Heliodor has enough holes already."
  ],
  "quest.0616E7C527841913.title": "Ready to Leave the Patio",
  "quest.0616E7C527841913.quest_desc": [
    "Empty pockets, a compass that knows the way and ruins that will not let you dig them up. Craft the Atlas and let it start talking.",
    "",
    "Good luck, traveller. Mind the columns: four are already broken."
  ],
  "chapter.7E9AE182E0AEBD76.title": "The Living Atlas",
  "chapter.7E9AE182E0AEBD76.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Projects, deliveries, act components and the Ark: how the story moves."
  ],
  "quest.23BA57C16A45AEBB.title": "A Book That Answers Back",
  "quest.23BA57C16A45AEBB.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Living Atlas&r moves the story. Each act is a set of projects, each project a delivery; finish them all and the next act opens. Along the way it hands out rewards and tells, in broken fragments, what happened to Heliodor.",
    "",
    "Someone is talking through it. The interference is not your fault."
  ],
  "quest.2B3B9A46DA117973.title": "Get the Atlas",
  "quest.2B3B9A46DA117973.quest_desc": [
    "Craft it from a &ebook&r and a &ecopper ingot&r; its first project, The Atlas Awakens, asks for exactly that. Open it with right-click, with &e/entrelumen&r, or by using a Survey Station with an empty hand.",
    "",
    "Waking it is also the compass's first target."
  ],
  "quest.5F6D93279A928C87.title": "Reading the Atlas",
  "quest.5F6D93279A928C87.quest_desc": [
    "Left page: the act's projects and their state. Right page: the selected project, its materials (carried and missing) and the projects it needs first. &eDeliver&r sends the materials, &eRefresh&r asks the server again and &eAdvance&r appears when the act is done.",
    "",
    "The list opens with the compass entry and its fragments."
  ],
  "quest.21132BDE339A66BD.title": "Delivery Rules",
  "quest.21132BDE339A66BD.quest_desc": [
    "Deliveries take from your &emain inventory and offhand&r only: backpacks, shulker boxes and the ender chest do not count. Only projects of your &ecurrent act&r, after their prerequisites.",
    "",
    "A delivered project cannot be delivered again, so reconnecting never duplicates a reward. Nice try."
  ],
  "quest.622A0BC02FB63453.title": "Tip: the Atlas From Chat",
  "quest.622A0BC02FB63453.quest_desc": [
    "&e/entrelumen status&r lists your act's pending projects, their prerequisites and, for each material, how many you carry and lack. &e/entrelumen deliver <project>&r delivers by name with the button's rules, and the chat suggests names as you type."
  ],
  "quest.1DBCB83716EBFCBF.title": "Act I: A Light Among Ruins",
  "quest.1DBCB83716EBFCBF.quest_desc": [
    "Five projects, ordinary materials:\n- The Atlas Awakens: a book, a copper ingot;\n- A Table for Travellers: 3 bread, 4 bowls;\n- Assemble the Lens: 4 copper ingots, 4 glass (&eRaw Lens&r);\n- Field Survey: 3 paper, a compass (&eSurvey Notes&r);\n- First Signal: lens, notes, 4 copper ingots (&eSignal Core&r).",
    "",
    "Then press Advance."
  ],
  "quest.161CC52C300C99FD.title": "Act Components",
  "quest.161CC52C300C99FD.quest_desc": [
    "From act II, projects ask for &6act components&r: prototypes crafted in an ordinary grid from two or three mods plus an earlier component. The recipes are public and never check your act.",
    "",
    "In EMI, &eR&r on a component shows its recipe and &eU&r everything it unlocks."
  ],
  "quest.097843E8ED7FB61E.title": "Act II: The Lost Crafts",
  "quest.097843E8ED7FB61E.quest_desc": [
    "Four components, then the closing project:\n- &eCalibration Frame&r: Create and Immersive Engineering, plus the raw lens;\n- &eEnergy Coupler&r: Actually Additions and Create;\n- &eLiving Matrix&r: Ars Nouveau, plus a frame;\n- &eTravel Rations&r: see the Kitchen chapter.",
    "",
    "Workshop Archive closes the act and gives &eTerra's Arm&r."
  ],
  "quest.77007F86F56D8B6C.title": "Act III: Routes of Exchange",
  "quest.77007F86F56D8B6C.quest_desc": [
    "Five components; three pay an altar:\n- &eRouting Matrix&r (AE2, PneumaticCraft, Actually Additions): &eAltar of Peace&r;\n- &ePropagation Core&r (Mystical Agriculture, bee wax): &eAltar of Growth&r;\n- &ePower Regulator&r (Mekanism, Immersive Engineering);\n- &eInventory Sensor&r (Integrated Dynamics, LaserIO);\n- &eHandling Core&r (Modular Routers, Create): &eAltar of Levelling&r.",
    "",
    "Exchange Route closes the act."
  ],
  "quest.58244B38F375C1C7.title": "Act IV: Voices of the Atlas",
  "quest.58244B38F375C1C7.quest_desc": [
    "The expedition act: the Atlas records journeys by itself when your team arrives, and asks for four components:\n- &eSpectral Lens&r (Occultism, Malum);\n- &eHorizon Chart&r (Aether, Twilight; its project needs both reached): &eAltar of Repose&r;\n- &eEcosystem Capsule&r (Bumblezone; its project needs it reached): &eAltar of Renewal&r;\n- &eContainment Seal&r (EvilCraft, Malum): &eAltar of Time&r."
  ],
  "quest.37DC25FD6EE9DEA9.title": "The Heart of Heliodor",
  "quest.37DC25FD6EE9DEA9.quest_desc": [
    "Act IV ends at the &6Sun Spirit&r, boss of the Aether's gold dungeon. It drops the &eHeart of Heliodor&r, once per campaign. Deliver it in A Clear Voice; only then can Voices of the Atlas close the act.",
    "",
    "On the ground it cannot burn, despawn or fall into the void. It has been lost once already."
  ],
  "quest.1866D1F9DD733322.title": "Act V: The Ark",
  "quest.1866D1F9DD733322.quest_desc": [
    "Knowing the truth, you build the Ark. First three components: &eArk Connection Bus&r (Mekanism, PneumaticCraft, handling cores, a sensor), &eRenewal Engine&r (Nature's Aura, Mystical Agriculture, capsules, cores) and &eHabitation Charter&r (fish stew, mixed salad, AE2, rations).",
    "",
    "World Network then opens six module projects: Engineering, Arcane, Nature, Exploration (once the End is reached), Logistics and Habitation."
  ],
  "quest.72C3A1232F9FF6FF.title": "Assemble the Ark",
  "quest.72C3A1232F9FF6FF.quest_desc": [
    "Place the &eArk Controller&r with the six module blocks within three blocks sideways, one below and two above. Crouch on it with an empty hand to deposit what the current module still needs; partial deposits stay.",
    "",
    "The bill: Engineering 4 calibration frames and 2 regulators, Arcane 2 seals, Nature 2 capsules, Logistics 2 routing matrices, Habitation 8 rations, Exploration a horizon chart."
  ],
  "quest.3DD568980F26C458.title": "The Activation",
  "quest.3DD568980F26C458.quest_desc": [
    "With all six modules supplied, World Network done and the End reached, crouch on the controller with an empty hand. The Ark forges the &6Light Key&r for whoever activated it, and the campaign enters &eact VI, Solsticio&r.",
    "",
    "The door has been waiting a long time. Knock politely."
  ],
  "quest.62CBF13A5CB4C3E5.title": "What the Built Ark Does",
  "quest.62CBF13A5CB4C3E5.quest_desc": [
    "With all six modules in place, each offers a service: &eEngineering&r repairs a tool with its anvil material, no XP; &eArcane&r clears prior-work penalties for books and levels; &eNature&r restores a site marked with a bookmarked compass; &eExploration&r merges your maps of one area; &eLogistics&r keeps a shared depot and expedition kits; &eHabitation&r is a temporary respawn, with a bed."
  ],
  "quest.306B717DBAA85638.title": "The Survey Station",
  "quest.306B717DBAA85638.quest_desc": [
    "Copper, glass, smooth stone and a signal core make a movable bookmark. With an empty hand it opens the Atlas; with a vanilla compass it points that compass at itself, like a lodestone, and the link survives moving the station.",
    "",
    "The Ark's Nature service uses such a compass to mark its site."
  ],
  "quest.4E722FFB64F4F76D.title": "Components Unlock the World",
  "quest.4E722FFB64F4F76D.quest_desc": [
    "A component closes a few milestones, never a pile of basics: the metallurgic infuser and the mining portal (Calibration Frame), the AE2 and Refined Storage controllers (Routing Matrix), Mekanism's jetpack and Psi's CAD Assembler (Power Regulator), the Digital Miner and the Lumen Shelf (Spectral Lens). The other steps of an act take its material: an alloy of Mekanism, ironwood or zanite.",
    "",
    "&eU&r on a component in EMI shows everything it opens."
  ],
  "quest.21BEA1DA85BCD908.title": "Quirk: Psi Waits for Act III",
  "quest.21BEA1DA85BCD908.quest_desc": [
    "Psi's CAD Assembler carries a Power Regulator; its psigem cores keep their native recipes. No assembler, no CAD, no spells: plan Psi alongside your act III logistics.",
    "",
    "When in doubt, EMI shows your version's recipe."
  ],
  "quest.621B66430D137B31.title": "Tip: Automate the Components",
  "quest.621B66430D137B31.quest_desc": [
    "Components are ordinary shaped recipes, each a small drawing, so any storage network can autocraft them, and later ones eat earlier ones. Set up a pattern for each early in act III.",
    "",
    "In act V the Ark swallows frames, regulators, seals, capsules, matrices and rations by the handful."
  ],
  "quest.4B04E34A144A490D.title": "Rewards Come From the Atlas",
  "quest.4B04E34A144A490D.quest_desc": [
    "Story rewards come from the Atlas when you deliver, never from the quest book: the Atlas, lens, notes, signal core, Terra's Arm and the six altars. Each comes once per campaign to whoever delivered, or drops at their feet if the inventory is full, and a chat line names it.",
    "",
    "The quest book only keeps score."
  ],
  "quest.2C31D583B80F31E8.title": "Why the Atlas Stutters",
  "quest.2C31D583B80F31E8.quest_desc": [
    "Until the Heart of Heliodor reaches it, the Atlas speaks in fragments: crossed-out words, gaps and short glitches, always with readable parts. From act V the text comes through clear.",
    "",
    "Do not skip them. The lore is a puzzle, and you are holding the pieces."
  ],
  "quest.45AF0BF75021DA63.title": "The Story in Your Hands",
  "quest.45AF0BF75021DA63.quest_desc": [
    "Projects, deliveries, components and the Ark: the rest is walking the road.",
    "",
    "Keep the Heliodor Compass close. It already knows where the Atlas wants you next."
  ],
  "chapter.34DC677E5D339B3F.title": "The Heliodor Compass",
  "chapter.34DC677E5D339B3F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Where it points, what its colors mean and why it sometimes rests."
  ],
  "quest.40194B53EA674D94.title": "Never Lost",
  "quest.40194B53EA674D94.quest_desc": [
    "The Heliodor Compass always points to the next place the story needs: a structure, a dungeon, a guardian or another world. Meet the condition and it turns to the next one on its own.",
    "",
    "It never sends you thousands of blocks away and never spins for show."
  ],
  "quest.70E93F659F6828C9.title": "Take It From the Pedestal",
  "quest.70E93F659F6828C9.quest_desc": [
    "Use the &eHeliodor Pedestal&r in the start ruin, with anything in hand, to get your compass: &eone&r per player, per world, ever. A second try only reminds you. No recipe makes another.",
    "",
    "If you die, Tombstone keeps it in your grave. Otherwise, treat it like your house keys."
  ],
  "quest.6F6A288871FD98BD.title": "Carry It to Attune It",
  "quest.6F6A288871FD98BD.quest_desc": [
    "A fresh compass is not attuned yet: carry it a moment. While carried it refreshes about once a second, so it follows you as you walk.",
    "",
    "Hover it for its state; the Atlas's first entry shows the target, why it matters and the fragments you recovered."
  ],
  "quest.5B6FBD4B88937613.title": "Needle Colors",
  "quest.5B6FBD4B88937613.quest_desc": [
    "The needle's color tells you which world the target is in: &3turquoise&r Overworld, &4red&r Nether, &5violet&r End, &6gold&r Aether, &2green&r Twilight Forest, &bsky blue&r another world (Bumblezone, Solsticio) and &7grey&r no trace, locked or nothing pending.",
    "",
    "Grey is not broken. Grey is waiting."
  ],
  "quest.704E2DF71D58FC0A.title": "What the Needle Is Saying",
  "quest.704E2DF71D58FC0A.quest_desc": [
    "The tooltip shows one of five states: &ePointing&r (follow it), &eAnother dimension&r (travel there first), &eSearching&r (a short spin while the server looks), &eNo trace nearby&r (advance the Atlas or try another region) and &eLocked&r (the next act opens it).",
    "",
    "When there is nothing left for now, it says that too."
  ],
  "quest.76B34644E6DE0B02.title": "Never Thousands of Blocks",
  "quest.76B34644E6DE0B02.quest_desc": [
    "It searches at most &e1,500 blocks&r around you. Anything farther reads as no trace nearby instead of dragging you across the map; walk 512 blocks from a failed search and it looks again.",
    "",
    "The story never asks for epic treks, jetpacks or chunk-loading."
  ],
  "quest.22D3EA2BD8DBF425.title": "The Compass Follows the Team",
  "quest.22D3EA2BD8DBF425.quest_desc": [
    "It follows your team's campaign: everyone sees the same target, new destinations are announced to all, and a condition met by any online member counts for everyone. A new party inherits its founder's progress.",
    "",
    "Reached stays reached: losing an item never rewinds it."
  ],
  "quest.44DBD22DB832F5A1.title": "Quirk: Found Places Are Shared",
  "quest.44DBD22DB832F5A1.quest_desc": [
    "Every place a search finds is remembered for the whole world. If another team already found a fortress near you, your compass points there without searching.",
    "",
    "Searches run a little each tick and never wait for chunks, so they never freeze the server."
  ],
  "quest.60F361B6A2A611B1.title": "The Route: Acts I and II",
  "quest.60F361B6A2A611B1.quest_desc": [
    "Early targets, each until its condition:\n- &eThe Ruin Where You Woke&r, until the Atlas awakens;\n- &eThose Who Stayed&r, a village, until Field Survey;\n- &eThe Proving Halls&r, the trial chambers, until First Signal;\n- &eBuried Streets&r, trail ruins, until Workshop Archive closes act II."
  ],
  "quest.265E3B24DA46A5F4.title": "The Route: Acts III and IV",
  "quest.265E3B24DA46A5F4.quest_desc": [
    "Then the other worlds.\n- Act III: a &eNether fortress&r (until someone carries a blaze rod), the &eTwilight Forest&r and the &eNaga's Courtyard&r.\n- Act IV: the &eAether&r, the Slider's &eBronze Dungeon&r, the &eLich's Tower&r, the &eBumblezone&r, the &eSilver Dungeon&r and the &eGolden Dungeon&r, where the Sun Spirit keeps the Heart of Heliodor.",
    "",
    "Guardian targets advance when the boss falls."
  ],
  "quest.2F469EE97767853E.title": "The Route: Acts V and VI",
  "quest.2F469EE97767853E.quest_desc": [
    "The last stretch.\n- Act V: the &eDrowned Monument&r (until someone carries a wet sponge), the &eStronghold&r (until your team reaches the End) and &eThe End&r itself (until the dragon falls).\n- Act VI: &eSolsticio&r, until your team crosses into the city.",
    "",
    "Keep what the Wither, the dragon and the Elder Guardian drop: later recipes want it."
  ],
  "quest.251DFE202BDBF604.title": "Tip: Early Work Counts",
  "quest.251DFE202BDBF604.quest_desc": [
    "If your team already met a later condition, say it reached the Twilight Forest early, the compass skips that target the moment its act opens.",
    "",
    "Nothing done early is wasted. Curiosity is never punished here."
  ],
  "quest.301485EAA30C69E6.title": "Other Compasses",
  "quest.301485EAA30C69E6.quest_desc": [
    "Off the story path, &eNature's Compass&r finds biomes and &eExplorer's Compass&r finds structures; Solsticio's cartographer sells both, plus survey maps.",
    "",
    "The Heliodor Compass only follows the story. Do not ask it for a jungle."
  ],
  "quest.6BBD7EE9A8E018A1.title": "Fragments of Lore",
  "quest.6BBD7EE9A8E018A1.quest_desc": [
    "Many targets add a lore fragment to the Atlas's compass entry, newest first. The early ones keep the mystery; the whole truth arrives with the Heart of Heliodor.",
    "",
    "Read them in order and the static starts to make sense."
  ],
  "quest.7C5FFA4CF9C12078.title": "Follow the Light",
  "quest.7C5FFA4CF9C12078.quest_desc": [
    "When in doubt, hover the compass for its state, or open the Atlas for the target and why it matters.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's light has waited a long time. It can wait for you to read a tooltip."
  ],
  "chapter.073625DCC50D40F5.title": "World Tiers: the Story Decides",
  "chapter.073625DCC50D40F5.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Apotheosis difficulty tiers, raised by the story and never by you."
  ],
  "quest.0F7D705A8BA5E65A.title": "A World That Grows With You",
  "quest.0F7D705A8BA5E65A.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis has five &eWorld Tiers&r: Haven, Frontier, Ascent, Summit and Pinnacle. Each makes monsters tougher and loot better. Here the &estory&r raises them: when your team's campaign reaches a new stage, the world climbs one tier by itself.",
    "",
    "No guessing whether you are ready. The story decides; you survive it."
  ],
  "quest.5BC7B113AE36BF58.title": "The Ladder",
  "quest.5BC7B113AE36BF58.quest_desc": [
    "- &eHaven&r: from the start, through acts I and II;\n- &eFrontier&r: once act II is complete;\n- &eAscent&r: once act III is complete, as the expeditions begin;\n- &eSummit&r: once act IV is complete and the Ark begins;\n- &ePinnacle&r: when your team activates the Ark and opens act VI.",
    "",
    "Chat announces each step: \"The story sets your World Tier to...\"."
  ],
  "quest.729DB33C65E3D107.title": "It Only Goes Up",
  "quest.729DB33C65E3D107.quest_desc": [
    "Your tier is the &ehighest you ever reached&r. Dying, leaving a team or joining one that is behind never lowers it; joining one that is ahead raises you at once.",
    "",
    "It is stored on you, so it follows you across dimensions and restarts. Like prices: it only goes up."
  ],
  "quest.3E2EAA408A21FC08.title": "Pack Change: Hands Off the Dial",
  "quest.3E2EAA408A21FC08.quest_desc": [
    "&eCtrl+T&r still opens Apotheosis's World Tier screen, where you can read every tier's details, but the activate button stays disabled. If anything moves your tier outside the story, the pack puts it back within a second.",
    "",
    "You may look. You may not touch."
  ],
  "quest.2C2A73CEB13367AD.title": "Read the Details",
  "quest.2C2A73CEB13367AD.quest_desc": [
    "On the World Tier screen, the details button lists what each tier changes: buffs and debuffs for players and monsters, and the odds of each loot rarity and gem purity.",
    "",
    "Apotheosis's guidebook, the Chronicle of Shadows, explains rarities, affixes and gems."
  ],
  "quest.3EA0CA6AD9E05199.title": "Invaders From Frontier On",
  "quest.3EA0CA6AD9E05199.quest_desc": [
    "From &eFrontier&r, Apotheosis &einvaders&r can appear: tough mini-bosses in affixed gear. Haven has none, and no epic or mythic loot. The pack spaces them 10 minutes apart instead of three.",
    "",
    "They like the Twilight Forest. Dress for the occasion."
  ],
  "quest.15289447AA613BCF.title": "Loot Rarity by Tier",
  "quest.15289447AA613BCF.quest_desc": [
    "Better rarities only drop at higher tiers: in this pack &euncommon&r materials come from Haven on, &erare&r ones higher up, &eepic&r from Ascent and &emythic&r from Summit.",
    "",
    "Salvage affixed loot at a &eSalvaging Table&r for the rarity materials that reforging and gems use. That sword with the silly name is an ingredient."
  ],
  "quest.69C926655A9EDEF3.title": "Spawner Augments Follow Tiers",
  "quest.69C926655A9EDEF3.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis's spawner runes are replaced by ENTRELUMEN &espawner augments&r: copper medallions that tweak a spawner where it stands. Each takes an act component, from act III to act V, in place of Apotheosis's materials.",
    "",
    "Silk Touch does not pick up spawners in this pack."
  ],
  "quest.057E195FC015C164.title": "The Godforged Pearl",
  "quest.057E195FC015C164.quest_desc": [
    "The &eLuminous Ingot&r needs Apotheosis's &eGodforged Pearl&r, which only comes from salvaging mythic loot. Mythic loot starts at Summit, so the pearl arrives with the Ark act, right before Solsticio.",
    "",
    "Mythic drops go to the Salvaging Table, not to the trophy shelf."
  ],
  "quest.116957591A1DC800.title": "Enchanting Climbs in Steps",
  "quest.116957591A1DC800.quest_desc": [
    "The pack spaces Apothic Enchanting's strongest shelves by act: about 45 Eterna in acts I and II, 60 in act III, 80 to 90 in act IV and 100 in act V. Four ENTRELUMEN shelves join the ladder: Cartographer's, Patina, Lumen and Horizon.",
    "",
    "From act V, the Atlas Library writes any eligible enchantment up to level 40."
  ],
  "quest.1EA195F042214D5C.title": "The Atlas Library",
  "quest.1EA195F042214D5C.quest_desc": [
    "An upgrade on Apothic's Ender Library: deposit enchanted books into a shared pool of &elumen&r, then write any eligible enchantment onto a book, even ones you never deposited. Its level cap follows the Eterna around it; 100 Eterna reaches level 40.",
    "",
    "A deposit is worth less than writing costs, curses are refused and breaking it keeps the pool. No infinite loops, sorry."
  ],
  "quest.18276CF7A859D7F0.title": "Tip: Gear Up Before Advancing",
  "quest.18276CF7A859D7F0.quest_desc": [
    "The world hardens the moment an act closes, so upgrade before pressing Advance on acts II and III: better armor, a few gems, food for the satiety buffs.",
    "",
    "There is no timer. The current tier will wait as long as you like."
  ],
  "quest.1988E6C9176E95D5.title": "Quirk: Items That Need a Tier",
  "quest.1988E6C9176E95D5.quest_desc": [
    "Some Apotheosis items say \"Requires World Tier\" and stay inert until your tier gets there. The story raises it, so just keep advancing the Atlas.",
    "",
    "No button to press. Well, there is one, but it is disabled."
  ],
  "quest.7D0FE71142574884.title": "For Operators",
  "quest.7D0FE71142574884.quest_desc": [
    "&e/entrelumen admin set <act>&r moves the story, and the tier with it. The tier still never drops: lowering it means clearing the player's stored story tier offline, deliberately not a command. Apotheosis's own tier command is undone at the next sync."
  ],
  "quest.373527F04C56E65F.title": "Difficulty With a Reason",
  "quest.373527F04C56E65F.quest_desc": [
    "Five tiers, raised by the story and never lowered, each with tougher monsters and better loot. Play the acts at your own pace.",
    "",
    "The world keeps time with you, not with the clock."
  ],
  "chapter.197D584486CC04B0.title": "Terra's Arm",
  "chapter.197D584486CC04B0.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Heliodor's inventor built herself a longer reach. Three more blocks, and a lot of scaffolding you will not need."
  ],
  "quest.204B7548FB3ED6C6.title": "An Arm Built to Reach",
  "quest.204B7548FB3ED6C6.quest_desc": [
    "Terra, Heliodor's inventor, built herself a cyborg arm to reach where the machine would not let her. It closes act II and does one thing: it lets you reach blocks from farther away.",
    "",
    "Small on paper. Huge the first time you roof a house without scaffolding."
  ],
  "quest.26B8D05294234A42.title": "Earn It in Act II",
  "quest.26B8D05294234A42.quest_desc": [
    "Finish act II's four prototype projects (Calibration Frame, Energy Coupler, Living Matrix and Travel Rations), then deliver &eWorkshop Archive&r: three paper and a copper ingot. The Atlas hands &eTerra's Arm&r to whoever delivers.",
    "",
    "No recipe. The sunken workshop ruin also keeps one in a chest."
  ],
  "quest.75CB722DD2FD6FE4.title": "Wear It on a Hand",
  "quest.75CB722DD2FD6FE4.quest_desc": [
    "It is a curio: press &eG&r (or use the Curios button in your inventory) and put the arm in a &ehands&r slot, which the pack guarantees every player.",
    "",
    "In a pocket it does nothing. Arms work better attached."
  ],
  "quest.2AB0505CB19719FA.title": "Three More Blocks",
  "quest.2AB0505CB19719FA.quest_desc": [
    "Worn, it adds &e+3 block reach&r: break, place and use blocks from 7.5 blocks away instead of 4.5. The tooltip shows the bonus in blue, like vanilla attribute lines.",
    "",
    "It is checked twice a second, so it switches on a moment after you put it on."
  ],
  "quest.0779CD7A84AB475B.title": "Blocks, Not Swords",
  "quest.0779CD7A84AB475B.quest_desc": [
    "Only &eblock&r reach grows. Attacking and interacting with creatures keep the normal range, so it gives no edge in combat.",
    "",
    "Terra built a tool, not a weapon."
  ],
  "quest.5385DF51A7FAC937.title": "Quirk: Two Arms, Same Reach",
  "quest.5385DF51A7FAC937.quest_desc": [
    "Players have two hands slots, but a second arm adds nothing: the bonus is one modifier, on or off, and taking off one of two keeps it. Other sources of block reach do stack with its flat +3."
  ],
  "quest.129FF0157ED39EF3.title": "Tip: Building Tall",
  "quest.129FF0157ED39EF3.quest_desc": [
    "Place the top rows of a wall, a roof ridge or a ceiling light without scaffolding, and reach across gaps. With a Construction Stick, extend faces you could not reach before.",
    "",
    "Scaffolding makers hate this one trick."
  ],
  "quest.51CF708529CE925C.title": "Tip: Machine Rooms",
  "quest.51CF708529CE925C.quest_desc": [
    "Reach the machine behind another, the lever past a pipe run or the chest at the back of a shelf without walking around. Dense rooms of LaserIO nodes and Create contraptions get much friendlier."
  ],
  "quest.25B9C7768CA15451.title": "Tip: Fields and Trees",
  "quest.25B9C7768CA15451.quest_desc": [
    "Harvest a wider strip of field from the path, reach the top logs and fruit of tall trees, and plant without stepping on farmland. With Ultimine, start a vein you would otherwise have to climb to."
  ],
  "quest.23E4CF25D0448A74.title": "Quirk: Carry On Reaches Too",
  "quest.23E4CF25D0448A74.quest_desc": [
    "The pack scales Carry On's pick-up distance with your reach, so the arm also lets you lift chests, furnaces and animals from farther away."
  ],
  "quest.3589E9C66EE3ADC7.title": "Reach Opens No Doors",
  "quest.3589E9C66EE3ADC7.quest_desc": [
    "More reach bypasses nothing: Heliodor's ruins, Solsticio outside your plot and other teams' claims refuse breaking and placing from any distance, and the server checks.",
    "",
    "The long arm of the law is still longer."
  ],
  "quest.79F61128A0C573B6.title": "One Arm per Campaign",
  "quest.79F61128A0C573B6.quest_desc": [
    "Atlas rewards come once per campaign, to whoever delivers, so the Atlas gives a team one arm: hand it to your main builder or pass it around. Replaying or reconnecting never makes a second.",
    "",
    "It survives fire and lava, and Tombstone keeps it in your grave if you die."
  ],
  "quest.2021A7FC13489E8C.title": "Terra's Story",
  "quest.2021A7FC13489E8C.quest_desc": [
    "Terra wanted technology to make life in Heliodor better, and she built the Atlas from inside the light. At the close of act II the Atlas returns her arm to you and, for the first time, half-speaks her name.",
    "",
    "Her later gifts, the Terraprism among them, come in the story's final act."
  ],
  "quest.77D6E1B05A0CB693.title": "Quirk: a Curio by Data",
  "quest.77D6E1B05A0CB693.quest_desc": [
    "Held in your hand, in armor slots or in a backpack, the arm is a trophy with a line of lore. It only works from the Curios hands slot, which the pack adds by data even if other mods stop adding it."
  ],
  "quest.35F251C084EFAC2E.title": "Three Blocks Closer",
  "quest.35F251C084EFAC2E.quest_desc": [
    "Put it on, look up at the unfinished roof, and finish it from the ground.",
    "",
    "Terra would be glad to see it working again."
  ],
  "chapter.19D7B33A90883E23.title": "The Six Altars of Heliodor",
  "chapter.19D7B33A90883E23.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Earned in the Atlas, fed with fuel and left to work. And copied, if you love them."
  ],
  "quest.3CC1A133C8AFFEA6.title": "Machines That Remember the Land",
  "quest.3CC1A133C8AFFEA6.quest_desc": [
    "Six blocks you place, feed and leave working: they restore land, flatten it, keep monsters away, grow crops, slow enemies and mend gear. None is crafted from scratch: the Atlas grants one of each in acts III and IV, and an original can be copied.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's groundskeepers, still clocking in."
  ],
  "quest.4905B81B132E440D.title": "How Every Altar Works",
  "quest.4905B81B132E440D.quest_desc": [
    "&eFuel in your main hand&r feeds it; hoppers and pipes can too, but nothing comes out. An &eempty hand&r shows its status and outlines its area. &eCrouching with an empty hand&r pauses or resumes it (Levelling and Repose use it differently).",
    "",
    "Fuel burns only while it works and its area is loaded. Broken, it drops with its fuel and contents."
  ],
  "quest.1B998C29999C119B.title": "Where Each Altar Comes From",
  "quest.1B998C29999C119B.quest_desc": [
    "One per Atlas project, once per campaign, to whoever delivers:\n- act III: &ePeace&r (Routing Matrix), &eGrowth&r (Propagation Core) and &eLevelling&r (Handling Core);\n- act IV: &eRenewal&r (Ecosystem Capsule), &eRepose&r (Horizon Chart) and &eTime&r (Containment Seal)."
  ],
  "quest.1E38047DAE4742C0.title": "Copies, Like Smithing Templates",
  "quest.1E38047DAE4742C0.quest_desc": [
    "Altar in the center, its act's component in the four side slots, diamonds in the corners: two altars come out. Peace takes a Routing Matrix; Growth and Renewal a Propagation Core; Levelling a Handling Core; Repose a Horizon Chart; Time a Containment Seal.",
    "",
    "Like a smithing template: the original survives, the copy costs the act."
  ],
  "quest.25E87DD1392D07A3.title": "Altar of Peace",
  "quest.25E87DD1392D07A3.quest_desc": [
    "Burns &ecandles&r, 10 minutes each. While lit, no hostile mob spawns naturally in the &e129-block cube&r around it: 64 blocks each way, up and down included, so a deep mine below still bites. It replaces Torchmaster's Mega Torch.",
    "",
    "About six candles an hour keep a base safe; bees make the wax renewable."
  ],
  "quest.3D589D8B4BEB4346.title": "What Peace Does Not Stop",
  "quest.3D589D8B4BEB4346.quest_desc": [
    "Only &enatural&r monster spawns are refused. Spawners, trial spawners, eggs, summons, conversions, raids, patrols, zombie sieges and every boss still happen, and a modded hostile filed outside the monster category may slip through.",
    "",
    "Peace, not a force field."
  ],
  "quest.63161B4946C2017A.title": "Altar of Growth",
  "quest.63161B4946C2017A.quest_desc": [
    "Burns &ebone blocks&r, 3 minutes each. Crops and saplings in the &e33 by 33&r field around it, from four blocks below to four above, grow about &e20 times&r faster, and ripe harvests drop &edouble&r.",
    "",
    "Seeds never double and unripe crops get nothing. Melons, pumpkins, cane, cactus and bamboo only grow faster, and Mystical Agriculture essence is not multiplied."
  ],
  "quest.7B978688277626D4.title": "Altar of Time",
  "quest.7B978688277626D4.quest_desc": [
    "Burns &eamethyst shards&r, 2 minutes each. Hostile mobs in the &e33-block cube&r move and strike at a third of their strength, and their projectiles fly at a third of the speed. Monsters a player kills inside drop &etriple&r loot and experience.",
    "",
    "Bosses are never slowed or multiplied. They have a schedule to keep."
  ],
  "quest.6878AADB79EAAC41.title": "Quirk: Only Real Kills Triple",
  "quest.6878AADB79EAAC41.quest_desc": [
    "Triple loot needs a real player's kill: fake-player grinders, pets and traps get the slow motion, not the bonus. Nether stars, dragon eggs, mob heads and trial keys never multiply, and gear a mob wore drops once.",
    "",
    "Slowed mobs hit a third as hard, not a third as often: their cadence comes from behavior, not stats."
  ],
  "quest.3112575E98734D79.title": "Altar of Repose",
  "quest.3112575E98734D79.quest_desc": [
    "A four-slot coffer that slowly mends what it holds, like Mending without orbs. It burns &eBottles o' Enchanting&r, one a minute, only while something inside is damaged; every 5 seconds each item regains a point, so a bottle is 12 points for one item or 48 for four.",
    "",
    "Pipes insert only damaged items and pull only whole ones, so a pipe through it is a repair line. Crouch with an empty hand to see progress."
  ],
  "quest.2D38C4F6A4B505C4.title": "Quirk: Slow on Purpose",
  "quest.2D38C4F6A4B505C4.quest_desc": [
    "From zero, an iron chestplate takes about 20 minutes, an elytra about 36 and a diamond pickaxe over two hours. Mending with the same bottle is faster but needs you there. Energy or custom-bar durability is not mended, and unbreakable items are refused.",
    "",
    "Cheap, patient and unattended, like a good grandmother."
  ],
  "quest.57AABE5F2FCD4F97.title": "Altar of Renewal",
  "quest.57AABE5F2FCD4F97.quest_desc": [
    "Rebuilds the land the world generator made in the &e49 by 49&r square around it: refills dug pits, gives bare dirt back its cover and regrows the original trees and plants. Near your team's Ark nature site it grows to 65 by 65.",
    "",
    "It eats &ebone meal&r or other fertilizers: each pays 10 seconds of work, about four blocks. The whole square must stay loaded, so stay close."
  ],
  "quest.0F468D5DF1795B72.title": "What Renewal Leaves Alone",
  "quest.0F468D5DF1795B72.quest_desc": [
    "Never builds, containers, crops, paths, placed leaves or block entities, and never blocks placed into entities. No ores, closed caves, flooded or bottomless pits, or holes more than 16 blocks below the original surface: level those first.",
    "",
    "No pumpkins or melons either: it restores land, not lunch. Claims and ruins refuse its work at no cost."
  ],
  "quest.531B7B268260E855.title": "Altar of Levelling",
  "quest.531B7B268260E855.quest_desc": [
    "Flattens a square centered on itself at its own height, with a 4-block slope into the land on every side. Burns &ecoal, charcoal or redstone&r, a minute each.\n- Empty hand: 10-second preview; use again during it to start; while working, pause or resume.\n- Crouch during the preview: next size, 9, 17, 25 or 33 blocks wide.\n- Crouch otherwise: its 27-slot buffer; a block in hand goes in."
  ],
  "quest.5014C34B7A0D89C2.title": "Moves Matter, Never Makes It",
  "quest.5014C34B7A0D89C2.quest_desc": [
    "Every block it cuts goes to its buffer or an adjacent container, as an iron tool would drop it (grass gives dirt, stone gives cobblestone). Holes fill only from the buffer or a container beside it; out of material, it waits.",
    "",
    "It copies the surrounding top, subsurface and deep blocks, so the flat looks natural. Builds, containers and fluids refuse their column."
  ],
  "quest.726D5571973055F5.title": "Quirk: Everything Is Symmetric",
  "quest.726D5571973055F5.quest_desc": [
    "Every area is a square centered on the altar, worked in rings from the center out, and the Levelling slope is the same on every side. Put the altar at the exact center of what you want to affect.",
    "",
    "Heliodor built with symmetry. Its altars never learned any other way."
  ],
  "quest.77C6298820A4A20A.title": "Altars Act as Their Owner",
  "quest.77C6298820A4A20A.quest_desc": [
    "The owner is whoever placed the altar, or the first player who fed it. Altars that change blocks act on the owner's behalf, so claims, protected ruins and Solsticio refuse them exactly as they would refuse the owner.",
    "",
    "In a team, place them where your claims allow the work."
  ],
  "quest.6CE054C946B800A9.title": "Tip: Stack the Effects",
  "quest.6CE054C946B800A9.quest_desc": [
    "Peace over the base, Growth in the middle of the fields, Time in the mob room where you fight, Repose next to the bed where you drop damaged gear.",
    "",
    "If you copy one, copy Growth first."
  ],
  "quest.2DE34E6E418790EF.title": "Six Gifts From the Past",
  "quest.2DE34E6E418790EF.quest_desc": [
    "Peace for the base, Growth for the fields, Levelling and Renewal for the land, Time for the fights and Repose for the gear.",
    "",
    "Heliodor could not save itself, but it left very good tools."
  ],
  "chapter.0882BD4FA4DB1326.title": "Luminosities and Luminous Gear",
  "chapter.0882BD4FA4DB1326.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Six Luminosities, one ingot, the best gear in the pack and creative items made of light."
  ],
  "quest.71E023F277E7AA8B.title": "Light, Held in Your Hand",
  "quest.71E023F277E7AA8B.quest_desc": [
    "Heliodor's light, held in six shapes, is the pack's final material. Only Solsticio's natives trade the six &6Luminosities&r, and from them come the &eLuminous Ingot&r, by far the strongest gear in the pack and the recipes for creative items.",
    "",
    "The top of the ladder, and it glows."
  ],
  "quest.3564F46BB7183E54.title": "The Six Luminosities",
  "quest.3564F46BB7183E54.quest_desc": [
    "One per discipline: &6Engineering&r copper-orange, &5Arcane&r violet, &aNature&r green, &bExploration&r sky blue, &3Logistics&r turquoise and &eHabitation&r warm gold.",
    "",
    "No recipe makes them, and the pack removes any that would. Only Solsticio's awake natives sell them."
  ],
  "quest.457C56A252E9B15D.title": "The Luminous Ingot",
  "quest.457C56A252E9B15D.quest_desc": [
    "Six Luminosities, one of each, fill the outer columns of the grid. The middle column fuses magic, the divine and the machine: a Nature's Aura &esky ingot&r, an Apotheosis &egodforged pearl&r and a Mekanism &eatomic alloy&r. One recipe, one ingot.",
    "",
    "Fireproof, faintly glowing, and it repairs any luminous piece at an anvil."
  ],
  "quest.19A3618A96EB4B87.title": "Gathering the Middle Column",
  "quest.19A3618A96EB4B87.quest_desc": [
    "The &esky ingot&r is Nature's Aura magic, from its altar and aura. The &egodforged pearl&r only comes from salvaging mythic Apotheosis loot, which drops from World Tier Summit on. The &eatomic alloy&r is Mekanism's top alloy.",
    "",
    "All three are Ark materials too, so your act V setup keeps paying off."
  ],
  "quest.7251812C8E588515.title": "Netherite, Then Luminous",
  "quest.7251812C8E588515.quest_desc": [
    "The nine luminous pieces (four armor, five tools and weapons) come from the smithing table, like netherite from diamond: a &enether star&r as the template, the matching &enetherite&r piece and a &eLuminous Ingot&r. Enchantments, affixes, gems, name and wear carry over.",
    "",
    "A full kit: 9 ingots, 9 stars, 9 netherite pieces."
  ],
  "quest.143B871581ED4583.title": "By Far the Strongest",
  "quest.143B871581ED4583.quest_desc": [
    "Armor &e60&r for the set (12, 22, 16, 10), toughness &e15&r and knockback resistance 0.25 per piece (immune with all four), enchantability &e60&r. Tools mine at speed &e60&r, harvest everything and last 32,768 uses; the sword hits for &e30&r at 1.6 per second, the axe &e32&r at 1.0.",
    "",
    "AttributeFix lifts vanilla's armor cap, so none of it is wasted."
  ],
  "quest.225BFC5F2FF7C7F4.title": "It Never Breaks",
  "quest.225BFC5F2FF7C7F4.quest_desc": [
    "At its last durability point a piece goes &edim&r: armor stops protecting, tools mine at hand speed and weapons lose their bonus, like an elytra that stops gliding. Repair it and it lights up again.",
    "",
    "Fireproof, and both Mending and the Luminous Ingot at an anvil work."
  ],
  "quest.1B716F47603A296D.title": "Repaired by Light",
  "quest.1B716F47603A296D.quest_desc": [
    "Once a second, the light at your eyes repairs every luminous piece you carry, wear or hold: brightness minus 11 points each, nothing below light 12, about 4 a second in full sun. The night sky does not count.",
    "",
    "A drained chestplate is whole in under 17 minutes of sun. Solar-powered, like Heliodor."
  ],
  "quest.4B504EF68D518396.title": "The Full Set: Flight",
  "quest.4B504EF68D518396.quest_desc": [
    "All four armor pieces, lit: &ecreative-style flight&r without energy, steady night vision and no fall damage. Take one off and only the set's flight goes; other flight sources keep working. If you were airborne, you get 8 seconds of slow falling.",
    "",
    "Losing the set never kills you. Gravity asks nicely first."
  ],
  "quest.1C42854FA3D4A9F7.title": "The Luminous Sword",
  "quest.1C42854FA3D4A9F7.quest_desc": [
    "Every hit marks the target with Glowing for 5 seconds and deals &e25% more&r damage to undead. Handy in the Twilight Forest and against the Wither's escort.",
    "",
    "The undead never liked the light."
  ],
  "quest.6EEF0D18FEFDC6B1.title": "Gear That Lights the Way",
  "quest.6EEF0D18FEFDC6B1.quest_desc": [
    "With LambDynamicLights, lit luminous armor and tools shine at full brightness around you, and the ingot and Luminosities glow a little in hand. Dim pieces give no light.",
    "",
    "Caves hate you now."
  ],
  "quest.360B04E85E0041D8.title": "Luminous in Silent Gear",
  "quest.360B04E85E0041D8.quest_desc": [
    "The ingot is also a &eSilent Gear&r material, the best of all 138, with its own trait, &eRadiant&r: radiant pieces count toward the luminous set bonus, give dynamic light and are repaired by light. The main part adds Holy V, Lustrous V, Refractive and Kitty Vision, and is fireproof.",
    "",
    "Salvaging it never returns Luminosities."
  ],
  "quest.5961E56C53335CFC.title": "Quirk: Two Rivals Remain",
  "quest.5961E56C53335CFC.quest_desc": [
    "Two powered systems still do something luminous does not: a charged MekaSuit can absorb up to all damage, and Draconic's chaotic shield grows with damage modules.",
    "",
    "They are the ceiling for players who build the infrastructure; luminous is cheaper and needs no power."
  ],
  "quest.6DF9E392A1E87CB0.title": "Creative Items From Light",
  "quest.6DF9E392A1E87CB0.quest_desc": [
    "Twelve creative items get a recipe here, never a sale: among them Mekanism's energy cube (it comes out full), Create's creative motor, Ars Nouveau's source jar and Draconic's capacitor. Each grid is symmetric: Luminosities of two disciplines in the corners, two boss drops on the axis, the mod's expensive material and its best non-creative version in the middle.",
    "",
    "48 Luminosities for all twelve."
  ],
  "quest.750242C1312F40F8.title": "The Boss Drops Matter",
  "quest.750242C1312F40F8.quest_desc": [
    "Creative recipes use a &enether star&r (Wither), a &edragon heart&r (Draconic Evolution's Ender Dragon drop) and a &ewet sponge&r (Elder Guardian), and every luminous piece takes a star as its template.",
    "",
    "Act VI wants more than one of each: farm the Wither and pay the dragon a few more visits."
  ],
  "quest.3FEFFE5C3CDE9AF1.title": "Pack Change: No Duplicators",
  "quest.3FEFFE5C3CDE9AF1.quest_desc": [
    "Creative items that copy items get no recipe: the creative crate, storage cell and bin, Functional Storage's creative vending upgrade, the creative router module and Sophisticated's infinity upgrades. They would clone Luminosities, stars and pearls.",
    "",
    "No recipe turns luminous or creative items back into their inputs either."
  ],
  "quest.592061ECDBD42A57.title": "Tip: Count Your Light",
  "quest.592061ECDBD42A57.quest_desc": [
    "A full luminous set takes 54 Luminosities (nine ingots), and all twelve creative items 48 more. Each awake native sells up to four per restock, once a game day.",
    "",
    "Wake all six early in act VI and visit often; after the liberation, prices drop further."
  ],
  "quest.45F621229EAF6C22.title": "The Brightest Things You Own",
  "quest.45F621229EAF6C22.quest_desc": [
    "Gear that never breaks and flies, and creative items forged from light: the top of ENTRELUMEN's ladder.",
    "",
    "What you do with it is yours. The city and the world stay open, and now you glow in the dark."
  ],
  "chapter.670A7FABD9529818.title": "Solsticio: the City in the Light",
  "chapter.670A7FABD9529818.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The Light Key, your plot, sixteen shops, half-price villagers and the natives who sell Luminosities."
  ],
  "quest.23154202E971D33D.title": "The Capital of Heliodor",
  "quest.23154202E971D33D.quest_desc": [
    "Heliodor's capital, frozen inside the Entrelumen: an island city of gardens, copper and glass under an eternal noon. You reach it in act VI, after activating the Ark.",
    "",
    "Everyone inside has been waiting a very long time. Try not to be late."
  ],
  "quest.5B07250B9653E98A.title": "The Light Key",
  "quest.5B07250B9653E98A.quest_desc": [
    "Activating the Ark forges the &eLight Key&r for whoever activates it; teammates craft their own from an amethyst shard, two gold ingots, a Spectral Lens and a Horizon Chart. A key works only for teams whose Ark is active.",
    "",
    "Hold use for two seconds while a ring of light closes around you. Let go early and nothing is spent."
  ],
  "quest.384435517F0C36BE.title": "Broken, and Better for It",
  "quest.384435517F0C36BE.quest_desc": [
    "The key opens the way once and breaks as you cross. The &eBroken Light Key&r is bound to you: use it the same way to go home and back, as often as you like. Only its owner can use it.",
    "",
    "Home is where you last left the Overworld, or your bed, or world spawn, always checked for a safe spot. Mounts stay behind."
  ],
  "quest.23E16658D1A73696.title": "No Night, No Monsters",
  "quest.23E16658D1A73696.quest_desc": [
    "Eternal noon: no weather, no night, no hostile spawns, and interiors are never pitch black. Fall off the edge or walk past the border and the barrier of light brings you back to the arrival point, so the void never kills you.",
    "",
    "The first visit places the whole city. If the key says try again, give it a moment."
  ],
  "quest.0EEC4C8640CDE7BA.title": "Your Team's Plot",
  "quest.0EEC4C8640CDE7BA.quest_desc": [
    "The first member of a team to stand in the city claims a 16 by 16 plot for the team's campaign: one per team, kept while the campaign exists. Inside it your team builds freely; the rest of the city is protected.",
    "",
    "When every plot is taken, newcomers can still visit, and an operator can free one."
  ],
  "quest.2A148EEE6F6F68CD.title": "The Town Hall Portal",
  "quest.2A148EEE6F6F68CD.quest_desc": [
    "The Ayuntamiento holds a dormant portal with four sockets. Set act VI's &ethree relics&r in it (Juan's Luminous Seed, Terra's Terraprism and Bodhi's Blessed Heart of Heliodor), then show it your broken key: it opens for everyone.",
    "",
    "Walking in sends anyone home. The key is only shown, never kept."
  ],
  "quest.727A4BC4EDD7F47B.title": "A Waystone for Everyone",
  "quest.727A4BC4EDD7F47B.quest_desc": [
    "When the portal opens, a global Solsticio waystone appears in the Town Hall, so every waystone in the world can reach the city. Without Waystones, a twin portal appears near world spawn instead.",
    "",
    "Arriving on the portal never bounces you back: it rests for a few seconds and while you stand in it."
  ],
  "quest.3805C8D7CD312447.title": "How the Market Works",
  "quest.3805C8D7CD312447.quest_desc": [
    "The sixteen shops sell and never buy, so no loop turns items back into emeralds. Prices are in &eemeralds&r up to 64 and &eemerald blocks&r above; some offers want a second item, like a book.",
    "",
    "Shops restock once a game day when someone opens them, popular offers get dearer for a while, and reputation and Hero of the Village still count."
  ],
  "quest.4AC078B71F8995FF.title": "The Sixteen Shops",
  "quest.4AC078B71F8995FF.quest_desc": [
    "The highlights: &eLucerna&r sells enchanted books at vanilla maximum (&eMending&r for 40 emeralds and a book); &eCenit&r, rarities like elytra, totems and shulker shells; &eBrasa&r, circuits, alloys and machine parts from many tech mods; &eFulgor&r, the netherite upgrade and every armor trim.",
    "",
    "Plus twelve more, from seeds to curiosities."
  ],
  "quest.39908CEF070C2E51.title": "Offers That Wait for Your Act",
  "quest.39908CEF070C2E51.quest_desc": [
    "Some offers carry an act: elytra wait for VI, totems and shulker shells for V, heart of the sea, trident and netherite scrap for IV, echo shards for III, plus a few books and parts. Until then they show out of stock, with a hint on the action bar.",
    "",
    "It matters when a team arrives early through another team's portal or waystone."
  ],
  "quest.79D8A04CF5081F62.title": "Pack Change: Never for Sale",
  "quest.79D8A04CF5081F62.quest_desc": [
    "No emeralds, nether stars, dragon eggs, sponges, beacons, wither skulls, spawners, spawn eggs, Luminous Ingots or their rare ingredients, Light Keys or portal relics. Luminosities come only from their own native.",
    "",
    "Some things you still earn in the world. Bosses need a reason to exist."
  ],
  "quest.56F6DFDD05003993.title": "Move Villagers In",
  "quest.56F6DFDD05003993.quest_desc": [
    "Bring any Overworld villager into the &etrading hall&r and it &esettles&r: same profession and trades, but &ehalf price&r forever, wherever it trades later, and it restocks on its own daily.",
    "",
    "Carry them with Easy Villagers (&eAlt+O&r), a minecart or Carry On. A librarian with good books is the classic move."
  ],
  "quest.11E8992E59258C44.title": "The Six Natives",
  "quest.11E8992E59258C44.quest_desc": [
    "Six natives wait around the trading hall, their &eLuminosity&r out of stock until they have stood in their Overworld biome:\n- &eIgnea&r, engineering: Badlands;\n- &eArcadio&r, arcane: Swamp or Mangrove Swamp;\n- &eSilvano&r, nature: Jungle;\n- &eBrisa&r, exploration: Jagged, Frozen or Stony Peaks;\n- &eMarea&r, logistics: Warm, Lukewarm or Deep Lukewarm Ocean;\n- &eSolana&r, habitation: Sunflower Plains.",
    "",
    "Right-click a sleeping native to hear its wish."
  ],
  "quest.1EB57C6214238492.title": "Wake a Native",
  "quest.1EB57C6214238492.quest_desc": [
    "Carry it to its biome (Easy Villagers, a minecart or Carry On) and set it down: it wakes and stays awake for good, even back in Solsticio. Awake, it sells its Luminosity for &e8 emerald blocks&r plus a catalyst from its discipline, up to 4 per restock, and its other offers at half price.",
    "",
    "None of the six biomes is rare, and Nature's Compass finds them."
  ],
  "quest.18DB6AE80E859DE8.title": "Prices After the Liberation",
  "quest.18DB6AE80E859DE8.quest_desc": [
    "When the Entrelumen is freed, every price in the city drops: shopkeepers sell at &e60%&r, stacking with native and settled-villager discounts, so an awake native's Luminosity costs 5 emerald blocks. Prices round, never go below one item and always drop by at least one.",
    "",
    "Freedom has perks. Aurelia would like you to notice."
  ],
  "quest.25906E351DD1BD36.title": "Quirk: Shopkeepers Stay Put",
  "quest.25906E351DD1BD36.quest_desc": [
    "Shopkeepers and innkeepers refuse carrying mods, cannot be hurt and never level up; if one vanishes, a new one takes the post. Natives and ordinary residents can be carried off, and only their death brings a replacement.",
    "",
    "Residents chat, and some of their lines are rumors worth hearing."
  ],
  "quest.63AD5F7059C1A754.title": "Tip: Plan Your Emeralds",
  "quest.63AD5F7059C1A754.quest_desc": [
    "Six Luminosities per ingot, nine ingots per set, eight Luminosities per creative item: it adds up. Start an emerald income before act VI with Easy Villagers traders, farms of what villagers buy or your own trading hall.",
    "",
    "Heliodor runs on light. Its shops run on emeralds."
  ],
  "quest.62F97D06472111F4.title": "Tip: Motes and Frame Rate",
  "quest.62F97D06472111F4.quest_desc": [
    "The drifting motes of light are client-side and follow your particle setting: halved on Decreased, gone on Minimal. For finer control, the ENTRELUMEN client config has &esolsticio.ambientMotes&r (on or off) and &esolsticio.moteDensity&r (0 to 8, default 2).",
    "",
    "The city is big: if frames drop, lower particles or render distance."
  ],
  "quest.3DAE84462B7F4FCF.title": "A Home Inside the Light",
  "quest.3DAE84462B7F4FCF.quest_desc": [
    "Cross and return, build on your plot, trade, move villagers in and wake the six natives. The city stays open for as long as you play.",
    "",
    "Stay for the noon. It never ends."
  ],
  "chapter.08B147AC6886788B.title": "The Pack's Controls",
  "chapter.08B147AC6886788B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Every key the preset moved, grouped by what you are doing."
  ],
  "quest.6D8C6475ADC2E030.title": "A Keyboard for 300 Mods",
  "quest.6D8C6475ADC2E030.quest_desc": [
    "V, B, R, G, H, C, Z and the arrows were each claimed by five or six mods. The pack's key preset moves the clashing ones to free keys or to Alt, Ctrl and Shift combinations, and only fills keys you never set yourself: change one and your choice stays.",
    "",
    "Three hundred mods, one keyboard. Somebody had to negotiate."
  ],
  "quest.587CCA4077F3D371.title": "Find Any Key",
  "quest.587CCA4077F3D371.quest_desc": [
    "&eControlling&r (Options, Controls, Key Binds) adds a search box and a conflict filter; red keys are used twice, which is fine when they act in different places.",
    "",
    "Unbound on purpose: Accessories' own screen (the Aether's stays on &eI&r), Crafting on a Stick's second Curios key, Ars Nouveau's next and previous spell slot (use the F6 radial), Twilight's goggle zoom (Just Zoom covers it) and the Key Bundles radial."
  ],
  "quest.3010187592F12FD0.title": "Everyday Keys",
  "quest.3010187592F12FD0.quest_desc": [
    "- &eF8&r quest book (it used to sit on the grave key).\n- &eG&r Curios: Terra's Arm and the Ultimine curio go there.\n- &eV&r (hold) FTB Ultimine.\n- &eB&r the backpack you wear or carry.\n- &eR&r Tool Belt radial, &eShift+R&r its slot inventory.\n- &eJ&r full map, &eM&r new waypoint, &eK&r claim manager.\n- &eZ&r zoom (Just Zoom)."
  ],
  "quest.1FFF4DEA44FFBB8C.title": "Map and Waypoints",
  "quest.1FFF4DEA44FFBB8C.quest_desc": [
    "&eJourneyMap&r is the pack's map: &eJ&r opens it full-screen, &eM&r makes a waypoint where you stand and, inside the map, &eB&r one at the cursor.",
    "",
    "FTB Chunks' map key is unbound and its minimap off: it only handles teams and claims, with its claim manager on &eK&r."
  ],
  "quest.2B804294ADD68A3D.title": "R and Shift+R: the Tool Belt",
  "quest.2B804294ADD68A3D.quest_desc": [
    "With a Tool Belt in its slot, hold &eR&r for a radial menu that swaps your held item with one on the belt; &eShift+R&r opens the belt's slots.",
    "",
    "R is also the recipe key inside screens, but the belt only opens with no screen open, so they never clash. Aircraft dismount moved to &eF12&r for the same reason."
  ],
  "quest.5560B3BDAFB2503C.title": "V: Ultimine",
  "quest.5560B3BDAFB2503C.quest_desc": [
    "Hold &eV&r while breaking a block to break the whole connected vein, up to the reach of the vein resonator worn in a Curios charm slot (8, 16, 32 or 64 blocks by tier; without one there is no Ultimine), at extra hunger per block. With V held, Shift and the mouse wheel (or up and down arrows) switch shape: shapeless, tunnels or 3x3.",
    "",
    "Modern Industrialization's 3x3 tool toggle moved to &eAlt+V&r."
  ],
  "quest.6EFB8442677ABC33.title": "Mekanism Armor: Alt + Arrows",
  "quest.6EFB8442677ABC33.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism's armor mode keys left V, G, J and B for the arrows with &eAlt&r: &eAlt+Up&r helmet, &eAlt+Left&r chestplate, &eAlt+Down&r leggings, &eAlt+Right&r boots.",
    "",
    "The MekaSuit HUD toggles with Ctrl and the module tweaker with Alt, each plus the key where US keyboards have the backslash."
  ],
  "quest.606412CA5CDED070.title": "Flight and Travel Keys",
  "quest.606412CA5CDED070.quest_desc": [
    "- &eF4&r Iron Jetpacks engine, &eAlt+H&r its hover.\n- &eShift+F4&r Modern Industrialization flight.\n- &eCtrl+F4&r Ad Astra suit flight, &eAlt+R&r Ad Astra radio.\n- &eAlt+E&r Ender IO Staff of Travelling.\n- &eF12&r get off an Immersive Aircraft plane, &eCtrl+F12&r its boost.",
    "",
    "Every way of flying got its own key. Crashing is still shared."
  ],
  "quest.48B114C209222330.title": "Magic Keys",
  "quest.48B114C209222330.quest_desc": [
    "- &eF6&r Ars Nouveau spell radial, &e0&r its crown potion radial.\n- Iron's Spells wheel on the key left of 1 (grave accent on US keyboards), &eAlt+Q&r cast from the spellbook.\n- &eAlt+F&r Psi's main key (C stays for the vanilla hotbar save and the Ars book).\n- Mahou Tsukai: &eAlt+M&r magic circle, &eShift+Y&r mystic code, &eCtrl+H&r selective displacement, &eAlt+.&r settings, &ePage Up/Down&r its guns."
  ],
  "quest.16A91FEE3BA9C17E.title": "Exploration and Armor Abilities",
  "quest.16A91FEE3BA9C17E.quest_desc": [
    "- Aether: &eHome&r invisibility cloak; Deep Aether &eShift+Home&r skyjade transparency, &eAlt+G&r stratus dash, &eShift+H&r slider eye.\n- Twilight: the US semicolon key swaps the hotbar, and Shift plus it handles item display maps.\n- Eternal Starlight: &eH&r switches crest.\n- Deeper and Darker: &eAlt+B&r boost, &eAlt+N&r transmit.\n- Cataclysm armor: &eAlt+J&r, &eAlt+K&r helmet, &eAlt+L&r chestplate, &eAlt+I&r boots."
  ],
  "quest.181BA0D5FFEF2462.title": "Utility Keys",
  "quest.181BA0D5FFEF2462.quest_desc": [
    "- &eAlt+O&r pick up a villager (Easy Villagers).\n- &eShift+M&r Simple Magnets, &eCtrl+M&r Ender IO magnet.\n- US apostrophe key: Supplementaries quiver.\n- &eO&r Occultism ender satchel, &eShift+O&r its storage remote, &eInsert&r its satchel.\n- &eF10&r clear notifications.\n- &eEnd&r Building Gadgets range, &eShift+End&r settings, &eCtrl+End&r anchor.\n- &eAlt+T&r, &eShift+T&r Just Dire Things.\n- &eAlt+P&r, &eAlt+Y&r Draconic; &eAlt+U&r Hostile Neural Networks; &eAlt+Z&r Oritech implants (hold)."
  ],
  "quest.5085B25979D0B540.title": "Ctrl+T, Ctrl+O and Shift+T",
  "quest.5085B25979D0B540.quest_desc": [
    "Three Apotheosis keys keep their native combinations: &eCtrl+T&r opens the World Tier screen (readable, but the story sets the tier), &eCtrl+O&r toggles radial mining on gear that has it, and &eShift+T&r in an inventory links the hovered item in chat for your team to admire."
  ],
  "quest.2AD44E12B13F4108.title": "LittleTiles Keys",
  "quest.2AD44E12B13F4108.quest_desc": [
    "LittleTiles, the small-block builder, has its own set: &eN&r mirror, &eU&r mark, &eCtrl+I&r configure the held tool (&eShift+I&r secondary settings), &eCtrl+Home&r building mode, &eCtrl+Z&r undo, &eCtrl+Y&r redo.",
    "",
    "How to use them: the Building Tools chapter."
  ],
  "quest.7120653E6832BDAE.title": "Tip: Keys Named by Position",
  "quest.7120653E6832BDAE.quest_desc": [
    "A few preset keys are named after US symbols, the semicolon and the apostrophe, and on a Spanish or Latin American keyboard those physical keys print something else.",
    "",
    "Do not hunt for the symbol: read the label in Controls, which shows what your layout prints, or rebind it."
  ],
  "quest.4625B97E61B1C74D.title": "Tip: Key Bundles",
  "quest.4625B97E61B1C74D.quest_desc": [
    "&eKeyBind Bundles&r gathers rarely used actions into a radial menu behind one key. It ships unbound: bind &eOpen Bundle radial menu&r in Controls and build bundles from its screen.",
    "",
    "Good candidates: armor abilities, magic toggles, every Mahou Tsukai key."
  ],
  "quest.0C7671DD3A4A0940.title": "Quirk: Alt, Ctrl and Shift Win",
  "quest.0C7671DD3A4A0940.quest_desc": [
    "When a modified combination and a plain key share a letter, the combination whose modifier you hold wins: &eAlt+Q&r casts a spell without dropping your item, and &eCtrl+O&r toggles radial mining instead of opening the ender satchel.",
    "",
    "If a combination ever fires both actions, report it."
  ],
  "quest.38BCA7D778496F93.title": "Pack Change: Client Defaults",
  "quest.38BCA7D778496F93.quest_desc": [
    "A new profile also gets the pack's performance settings (see Performance, Sound and Screen), auto-jump off and the pack's resource pack enabled.",
    "",
    "They are only defaults: if your launcher already made an options file, existing values stay and only missing ones are added."
  ],
  "quest.487DF43C29D28D87.title": "Your Keyboard, Your Rules",
  "quest.487DF43C29D28D87.quest_desc": [
    "Everything here is a suggestion: keep what feels natural, rebind the rest with Controlling and put rare actions in a bundle.",
    "",
    "When a new tool shows up, check back here: its key is probably already waiting."
  ],
  "chapter.64B80719A7DF9516.title": "Recipes and Information",
  "chapter.64B80719A7DF9516.chapter_subtitle": [
    "EMI, Jade and the tooltips: how to find out what anything does without leaving the game."
  ],
  "quest.3CF1DB3935AAE039.title": "Where Answers Live",
  "quest.3CF1DB3935AAE039.quest_desc": [
    "Three hundred mods, and nobody remembers every recipe. You do not need a wiki: the game tells you how to make an item, what it is for, what a block holds and what an enchantment or effect does.",
    "",
    "R, U and a little curiosity replace most forum threads."
  ],
  "quest.55262A03C2144680.title": "EMI: the Item List",
  "quest.55262A03C2144680.quest_desc": [
    "The item column on the right of your inventory is &eEMI&r, the recipe viewer; its search bar sits at the bottom. Names follow your game language, and untranslated mods show English. &eCtrl+F&r jumps to the search, &eCtrl+O&r hides the whole overlay, and the mouse wheel turns pages."
  ],
  "quest.61CA4F1B5C30E59D.title": "R: How Do I Make This?",
  "quest.61CA4F1B5C30E59D.quest_desc": [
    "Hover any item, in EMI or any inventory, and press &eR&r (or left-click it in the list): every recipe that makes it appears, one tab per machine or crafting type. Hover a tab's icon to see which blocks run it, and &eBackspace&r goes back.",
    "",
    "The most-pressed key in the pack, by a mile."
  ],
  "quest.31B358B0E659662B.title": "U: What Is This For?",
  "quest.31B358B0E659662B.quest_desc": [
    "&eU&r over an item (or right-click in the list) shows every recipe that uses it: the fastest way to decide whether that strange drop is worth keeping.",
    "",
    "Try U on a machine to see everything it can process."
  ],
  "quest.0E7FE69D2A058E7E.title": "Search Like a Pro",
  "quest.0E7FE69D2A058E7E.quest_desc": [
    "EMI search understands prefixes: &e@create&r filters by mod, &e#c:ingots&r by tag, &e$fortune&r searches tooltips, a leading &e-&r excludes (&edirt -@minecraft&r), &e|&r means or (&etin|lead&r), slashes make a regular expression and quotes keep spaces together.",
    "",
    "Try one and you will never scroll again."
  ],
  "quest.566F682243FD07BC.title": "A: Favorites",
  "quest.566F682243FD07BC.quest_desc": [
    "&eA&r over an item pins it to the favorites bar on the left; A on a recipe pins that exact recipe, and A again removes it. Favorites survive between sessions.",
    "",
    "Keep there what you craft often: rations, torches, the next act component."
  ],
  "quest.53291CF6E456E08B.title": "The + Button Fills the Grid",
  "quest.53291CF6E456E08B.quest_desc": [
    "The small &e+&r beside a recipe moves its ingredients from your inventory into the open grid or machine, and &eShift+click&r fills as many batches as you can afford.",
    "",
    "Open the crafting table first, then look up the recipe. The other way round, nothing happens."
  ],
  "quest.3EC6B1E3A960D9DD.title": "The Recipe Tree",
  "quest.3EC6B1E3A960D9DD.quest_desc": [
    "On a recipe, &eView Recipe Tree&r draws the whole chain down to raw materials with the total cost. Click a node to pick its recipe (Shift lets EMI choose from your inventory), right-click to fold a branch, and crafting mode adds &bsynthetic favorites&r: the steps you still have to make.",
    "",
    "Made for act components."
  ],
  "quest.406D38FB9E0D4DF3.title": "Default Recipes",
  "quest.406D38FB9E0D4DF3.quest_desc": [
    "When an item has several recipes, &eCtrl+click&r the output of the one you prefer to make it the default for the tree and synthetic favorites.",
    "",
    "Handy when the same plate comes from Create, Immersive Engineering and Mekanism and you only built one of them."
  ],
  "quest.6CE1567F3B363FF1.title": "Why JEI Is Installed Too",
  "quest.6CE1567F3B363FF1.quest_desc": [
    "EMI is the viewer you see, but JEI stays so that add-ons written for it still reach you: EMI reads JEI plugins and shows their pages inside its own interface, from Mekanism multiblocks to villager professions.",
    "",
    "A page that looks slightly different probably comes from a JEI plugin."
  ],
  "quest.4B4E944BB1EAB381.title": "Pages You Did Not Know About",
  "quest.4B4E944BB1EAB381.quest_desc": [
    "&eJust Enough Professions&r (which workstation gives which job), &eJust Enough Breeding&r (what each animal eats), &eJust Enough Archaeology&r (what each suspicious block drops), &eJust Enough Mekanism Multiblocks&r (sizes and parts) and &eSmithing Template Viewer&r (what each template makes).",
    "",
    "U over a lectern, a cow or a brush finds them fast."
  ],
  "quest.66D47A11A965B2B7.title": "Jade: What Am I Looking At?",
  "quest.66D47A11A965B2B7.quest_desc": [
    "The small panel at the top of the screen is &eJade&r: the name of the block or creature you look at, its mod and useful state such as a machine's energy, a crop's growth or a furnace's progress; Jade Addons covers more mods.",
    "",
    "The mod name alone solves half the questions in a big pack."
  ],
  "quest.674B69F2C86D4CA3.title": "Jade's Keypad Keys",
  "quest.674B69F2C86D4CA3.quest_desc": [
    "&eNumpad 0&r opens Jade's settings (hide lines you do not care about), &eNumpad 1&r hides the panel, &eNumpad 2&r toggles fluids, and &eNumpad 3&r and &eNumpad 4&r show recipes and uses of what you are looking at.",
    "",
    "No keypad? Rebind them in Controls. Laptops, we see you."
  ],
  "quest.0F7DBD2F6C93F685.title": "Tooltips That Explain",
  "quest.0F7DBD2F6C93F685.quest_desc": [
    "&eEnchantment Descriptions&r explains every enchantment; &eAppleSkin&r shows a food's hunger and saturation and previews them on the bar; &eEquipment Compare&r sets armor or weapons beside yours while you hold &eLeft Shift&r; and &eF3+H&r, extended by Better Advanced Tooltips, adds IDs, durability and technical data."
  ],
  "quest.712D684D42FF0AF7.title": "Peek Inside Containers",
  "quest.712D684D42FF0AF7.quest_desc": [
    "&eShulker Box Tooltip&r shows a shulker box's contents without placing it: &eLeft Shift&r for a compact view, &eAlt+Shift&r for the full grid, &eLeft Ctrl&r to lock the preview.",
    "",
    "Sophisticated Backpacks list their contents when you hold Shift over them."
  ],
  "quest.64CCA8C454B93ADC.title": "What Does This Effect Do?",
  "quest.64CCA8C454B93ADC.quest_desc": [
    "Search an effect's name in EMI: &eJust Enough Effect Descriptions&r adds a page per effect with an explanation and the items that cause it.",
    "",
    "Handy for the satiety system's random buffs and the potions from Solsticio's apothecary."
  ],
  "quest.2136A30BA938D958.title": "Two Recipes, One Grid",
  "quest.2136A30BA938D958.quest_desc": [
    "When two recipes share a pattern, &ePolymorph&r adds a small button beside the output slot so you can pick the result.",
    "",
    "If the table hands you the \"wrong\" item, look for that button before blaming the recipe."
  ],
  "quest.3DE198C3AFAF7F1C.title": "Guide Books Are Crafted",
  "quest.3DE198C3AFAF7F1C.quest_desc": [
    "Nobody hands you a book on login, but every manual is still craftable: Ars Nouveau's Worn Notebook, the Integrated Dynamics manual, the Actually Additions booklet, Modern Industrialization's guidebook, Silent Gear's material book, the PneumaticCraft and Psi manuals and more.",
    "",
    "EMI has each recipe, and the Akashic Tome keeps them all in one."
  ],
  "quest.4178311F064476BB.title": "Tip: Which Mod Is This?",
  "quest.4178311F064476BB.quest_desc": [
    "Item tooltips in EMI end with the mod's name in blue italics, and Jade shows it for blocks in the world.",
    "",
    "When a wiki and the game disagree, trust the game: the pack changes some recipes, and EMI always shows the version you really have."
  ],
  "quest.7C55DEA7E7A3F179.title": "Pack Change: One Slot for the Act",
  "quest.7C55DEA7E7A3F179.quest_desc": [
    "Milestones swap one slot on their drawing's axis for an &6act component&r (Calibration Frame, Routing Matrix, Spectral Lens...): the AE2 and Refined Storage controllers, the Digital Miner or the Botany Pots upgrades. Other steps take an act material: a Mekanism alloy, ironwood or zanite.",
    "",
    "Unfamiliar ENTRELUMEN item in a grid? Press &eR&r on it; the Atlas chapter has the rest."
  ],
  "quest.73F28D876C6411ED.title": "Pack Change: One Route per Recipe",
  "quest.73F28D876C6411ED.quest_desc": [
    "Where mods copy each other's recipes, the pack switches off the copies so each recipe shows once in EMI; the kitchen machines are the classic case (see The Kitchen).",
    "",
    "Apotheosis's own item comparison is off too: Equipment Compare already does it on Shift."
  ],
  "quest.43CB273891F7D134.title": "Pack Change: No Recipe on Purpose",
  "quest.43CB273891F7D134.quest_desc": [
    "The six &6Luminosities&r (only Solsticio's natives trade them), item duplicators such as the creative crate, storage cell, bin and infinity upgrades, and Torchmaster's Mega Torch (the Altar of Peace replaces it) have no recipe at all.",
    "",
    "When U shows uses but R shows nothing, read the tooltip: it usually says where the item comes from."
  ],
  "quest.180B2B2465B8EE5E.title": "F7 and F9: Light and Chunk Lines",
  "quest.180B2B2465B8EE5E.quest_desc": [
    "&eMore Overlays&r adds two world toggles: &eF7&r marks blocks where hostile mobs can spawn because the light is too low, and &eF9&r draws chunk borders, handy before claiming land or building a chunk-sized farm.",
    "",
    "Light a cave with F7 on until no marks remain."
  ],
  "quest.4221014B1F59149C.title": "You Can Look Anything Up",
  "quest.4221014B1F59149C.quest_desc": [
    "R for recipes, U for uses, A for favorites, the tree for long chains, Jade for the world and tooltips for everything else.",
    "",
    "The wiki can rest now."
  ],
  "chapter.31A61F4C1354DBD2.title": "Inventory Without Pain",
  "chapter.31A61F4C1354DBD2.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Mouse gestures, sorting, trash, portable stations, magnets and the Tool Belt."
  ],
  "quest.40752BE0BC2CF1E7.title": "Less Clicking, More Playing",
  "quest.40752BE0BC2CF1E7.quest_desc": [
    "Big pack, big inventory. A handful of small mods remove clicks: drag gestures, one-key sorting, a trash slot, crafting tables on a stick, magnets and a tool belt. None of them touches progression.",
    "",
    "Moving items should never feel like a second job."
  ],
  "quest.43411C7BA4F791B5.title": "Mouse Tweaks",
  "quest.43411C7BA4F791B5.quest_desc": [
    "In any inventory: hold &eright click&r and drag over empty slots to drop one item in each; hold &eleft click&r with a stack and drag to gather the same kind; &eShift&r plus left-drag with an empty hand sends every slot you touch across; the &emouse wheel&r over an item moves it one at a time."
  ],
  "quest.2ED5039CAADCDB2D.title": "Sorting With Inventory Tweaks",
  "quest.2ED5039CAADCDB2D.quest_desc": [
    "&eInventory Tweaks Refoxed&r is the pack's only sorter: the &ebackslash&r key sorts your inventory and the &egrave-accent&r key the open chest (check Controls for your layout's labels).",
    "",
    "It also refills a hotbar slot from your inventory when a tool breaks or a stack runs out."
  ],
  "quest.728C08F385A0AAAB.title": "Vanilla Tricks Worth Knowing",
  "quest.728C08F385A0AAAB.quest_desc": [
    "&eDouble-click&r gathers every item of a kind onto the cursor; &eShift+double-click&r moves all those stacks across. &e1-9&r swap the hovered slot with the hotbar, &eF&r with the offhand. &eQ&r over a slot drops one, &eCtrl+Q&r the whole stack.",
    "",
    "Minecraft had these all along. Nobody told you."
  ],
  "quest.29FA4CC3289502F3.title": "Crafting Tweaks",
  "quest.29FA4CC3289502F3.quest_desc": [
    "Small buttons beside the crafting grid &erotate&r it, &ebalance&r and &espread&r ingredients, and &eclear&r it back to your inventory (force clear drops items if you are full). They show up on many modded stations too.",
    "",
    "With EMI's + button, shaped recipes become painless."
  ],
  "quest.099E800BF0796631.title": "Fuel Goes Where It Should",
  "quest.099E800BF0796631.quest_desc": [
    "&eFuel Goes Here&r sends Shift-clicked coal, charcoal or any fuel to a furnace's fuel slot first, not the input.",
    "",
    "Fast Workbench and Fast Furnace cache recipe lookups, so crafting and smelting stay quick with this many recipes."
  ],
  "quest.768C2BFC98D0D302.title": "Getting Rid of Things",
  "quest.768C2BFC98D0D302.quest_desc": [
    "&eTrashSlot&r adds a trash slot to your inventory; it keeps the last item until you trash another, so a misclick can be undone. &eTrash Cans&r are blocks that void whatever pipes send them (items, fluids, energy or everything), with a 9-entry filter on the item and fluid ones.",
    "",
    "Farm overflow goes to a can, not to the floor."
  ],
  "quest.12F24BEA959401E4.title": "Quirk: TrashSlot on Servers",
  "quest.12F24BEA959401E4.quest_desc": [
    "TrashSlot works in single player, but on a dedicated server only if the server has it too; otherwise it says so in chat and turns itself off.",
    "",
    "A Trash Can block does the same job for everyone."
  ],
  "quest.5117E4B67334A4B3.title": "Stations on a Stick",
  "quest.5117E4B67334A4B3.quest_desc": [
    "&eCrafting On A Stick&r turns the crafting table, stonecutter, loom, cartography table, smithing table, grindstone and anvil into hotbar items you right-click to open anywhere.",
    "",
    "Perfect for early expeditions, when every slot counts."
  ],
  "quest.3B11AF8418138B60.title": "The Tool Belt",
  "quest.3B11AF8418138B60.quest_desc": [
    "A &eTool Belt&r (leather, string and an iron ingot) goes in its own slot, and its tools leave your hotbar free: hold &eR&r for the radial menu, &eShift+R&r for the belt's slots.",
    "",
    "It starts small; combine it with a &eBelt Pouch&r in an anvil for more room."
  ],
  "quest.5131D32867AE6A92.title": "One Book for All Books",
  "quest.5131D32867AE6A92.quest_desc": [
    "The &eAkashic Tome&r (a book and a bookshelf) stores every guide book in one item: craft it with a book to add it, then &eShift+right-click&r to pick which one it becomes.",
    "",
    "Ars Nouveau, Integrated Dynamics, PneumaticCraft, Psi and friends, all in one pocket."
  ],
  "quest.580411F1188ABEEA.title": "Magnets",
  "quest.580411F1188ABEEA.quest_desc": [
    "&eSimple Magnets&r pull items and experience to you while switched on (&eShift+M&r). The basic one has a fixed range; the advanced one adjusts range and filters, so it can ignore cobblestone.",
    "",
    "Near farms your magnet must not loot, place a &eDemagnetization Coil&r."
  ],
  "quest.7A572E4824CB3002.title": "Item Collectors",
  "quest.7A572E4824CB3002.quest_desc": [
    "An &eItem Collector&r (an ender pearl on obsidian) picks up dropped items around it and holds them for a hopper or pipe; the advanced one has a configurable range and a filter.",
    "",
    "Put one under a tree farm or in a mob room. Fewer loose items, less lag."
  ],
  "quest.0295F66723444CF2.title": "Tip: Experience in Clumps",
  "quest.0295F66723444CF2.quest_desc": [
    "&eClumps&r merges nearby experience orbs into one, so a mob farm or a big smelting session no longer carpets the floor with orbs, and picking them up is instant.",
    "",
    "Less disco, more XP."
  ],
  "quest.4E08471DA70A04CF.title": "A Real Backpack",
  "quest.4E08471DA70A04CF.quest_desc": [
    "Sophisticated Backpacks carry dozens of slots, open with &eB&r and take upgrades that pick up, sort, restock and feed you. Start with a basic one.",
    "",
    "Tiers and upgrades: the Storage chapter."
  ],
  "quest.1398AE437E30A689.title": "Pack Change: Nothing to Start",
  "quest.1398AE437E30A689.quest_desc": [
    "No mod puts items in your inventory when you join: books, kits and plushies are all switched off, and everything here is crafted from ordinary materials.",
    "",
    "Why: the start chapter, Waking Among Ruins."
  ],
  "chapter.4208B1046BA4147D.title": "Building Tools",
  "chapter.4208B1046BA4147D.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Framed blocks, tiny tiles, construction sticks, gadgets and measuring tape: detail and scale."
  ],
  "quest.552EB40238B52126.title": "Tools for Builders",
  "quest.552EB40238B52126.quest_desc": [
    "Two kinds of tools: some for &edetail&r (shapes smaller than a block, blocks that wear any texture) and some for &escale&r (placing, swapping and copying hundreds of blocks at once). Only the heavy machines at the end wait for the story.",
    "",
    "Scaffolding optional. Taste not included."
  ],
  "quest.39516BD2BFA84B5C.title": "Construction Sticks",
  "quest.39516BD2BFA84B5C.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a face with a &eConstruction Stick&r and it lays a whole new layer of that block from your inventory. Wooden, copper, iron, diamond and netherite tiers place more at once, and there is an undo.",
    "",
    "Templates add upgrades such as placing in mid-air, replacing, destroying or running on energy; EMI shows how."
  ],
  "quest.7486910B168693D2.title": "Measure Before You Build",
  "quest.7486910B168693D2.quest_desc": [
    "The &eTape Measure&r (gray wool, yellow wool and an iron ingot) shows the size between two positions you mark. Measure the plot, the farm or the machine room before placing a block.",
    "",
    "LittleTiles has its own Little Measure Tape for tiny work. Measure twice, place once."
  ],
  "quest.3289836EB14EC8B3.title": "FramedBlocks: Any Texture",
  "quest.3289836EB14EC8B3.quest_desc": [
    "&eFramedBlocks&r makes shapes (slabs, stairs, panels, slopes, corners, doors, fences and many more) from an empty frame; right-click a placed one with any block to wear its texture: a copper sloped roof, a stone door.",
    "",
    "Craft each shape normally or pick it at the &eFraming Saw&r, which lists them all."
  ],
  "quest.66D34FD3FF9FAF0A.title": "Framed Tools and Tricks",
  "quest.66D34FD3FF9FAF0A.quest_desc": [
    "The &eFramed Wrench&r rotates and configures framed blocks and the &eFramed Hammer&r toggles styles and recovers the camo; &eglowstone dust&r makes one glow and a &eFramed Reinforcement&r makes it blast-proof.",
    "",
    "The &eFramed Blueprint&r copies a framed block with its camo and places copies from your materials."
  ],
  "quest.2ABFC8B03407EFD0.title": "LittleTiles: Inside a Block",
  "quest.2ABFC8B03407EFD0.quest_desc": [
    "Build with pieces much smaller than a block: the &eLittle Chisel&r places shapes of a block, the &eHammer&r carves them out, the &eGlove&r selects and moves pieces, the &ePaint Brush&r colors them, the &eBag&r holds materials and colors, and the &eBlueprint&r copies small builds.",
    "",
    "&eCtrl+I&r sets grid size and shape; the full key list is in the Controls chapter."
  ],
  "quest.76FD0835952BE5CB.title": "Quirk: Tiny Tiles Cost Frames",
  "quest.76FD0835952BE5CB.quest_desc": [
    "Each LittleTiles block can hold a lot of geometry, paid by your graphics card rather than the server. A few detailed rooms are fine; a whole city of micro-detail will drop your frame rate.",
    "",
    "LittleTiles for statues, furniture and signs; FramedBlocks or Copycats for big surfaces."
  ],
  "quest.4C2F9A63176C8DFE.title": "LittleTiles Doors",
  "quest.4C2F9A63176C8DFE.quest_desc": [
    "The Little Blueprint saves a selection as a structure, and some structures move: doors slide or rotate by the distance and angle you choose, and can open with a right-click.",
    "",
    "A secret bookshelf door made of tiny pieces is a rite of passage."
  ],
  "quest.27D44B4CD8346A17.title": "Building Gadgets 2",
  "quest.27D44B4CD8346A17.quest_desc": [
    "Five powered gadgets: &eBuilding&r places shapes (walls, floors, surfaces), &eExchanging&r swaps an area's blocks, &eCopy-Paste&r and &eCut-Paste&r copy or move whole structures, and &eDestruction&r clears a box. Each has undo in its radial menu.",
    "",
    "Charge them in any FE charger, like a Mekanism energy cube's charge slot."
  ],
  "quest.1815847FD7276ACD.title": "Gadget Keys and Templates",
  "quest.1815847FD7276ACD.quest_desc": [
    "With a gadget in hand, &eShift+End&r opens its settings, &eEnd&r changes the range and &eCtrl+End&r (Anchor) locks the preview so you can walk around it.",
    "",
    "The &eTemplate Manager&r stores Copy-Paste templates for reuse."
  ],
  "quest.5E8ECEB07E12638F.title": "Quirk: Protected Areas",
  "quest.5E8ECEB07E12638F.quest_desc": [
    "Other teams' claims, Heliodor ruins and Solsticio outside your plot refuse breaking and placing, so do not plan big gadget jobs there. On your own land, gadgets, sticks and altars act as you and follow your team's claim settings."
  ],
  "quest.48FE30F982594D40.title": "Flatten Land the Pack's Way",
  "quest.48FE30F982594D40.quest_desc": [
    "For big flat areas, the &eAltar of Levelling&r (act III) levels a square with a smooth symmetric slope and moves soil without creating any.",
    "",
    "Sizes, fuel and gestures: The Six Altars of Heliodor."
  ],
  "quest.50C34B4F07576EBA.title": "Pack Change: Heavy Builders",
  "quest.50C34B4F07576EBA.quest_desc": [
    "The &eRFTools Builder&r needs a Handling Core and the &eMining Gadgets&r a reinforced alloy, both act III, because they move or mine huge volumes.",
    "",
    "Everything else here is free from day one."
  ],
  "quest.6480EAD988459A99.title": "Tip: a Builder's Workflow",
  "quest.6480EAD988459A99.quest_desc": [
    "Measure with the tape, flatten with the Altar of Levelling or a Destruction Gadget, raise walls with a Construction Stick, swap materials with the Exchanging Gadget, then add detail with FramedBlocks, Macaw's and LittleTiles.",
    "",
    "Then Copy-Paste your best house and call it a street."
  ],
  "quest.3E2BA0EA29D6168D.title": "Detail and Scale",
  "quest.3E2BA0EA29D6168D.quest_desc": [
    "Pieces smaller than a block, any texture on any shape, thousands of blocks placed without breaking a sweat.",
    "",
    "Every good house needs a garden. The farming chapters are next door."
  ],
  "chapter.4259956EC2B18EFD.title": "Building: Blocks and Variants",
  "chapter.4259956EC2B18EFD.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Chipped, Rechiseled, Macaw's, Create Deco and functional glass: where every variant comes from and how to find it."
  ],
  "quest.3FD036B18FD541E2.title": "Thousands of Blocks, One Idea",
  "quest.3FD036B18FD541E2.quest_desc": [
    "Thousands of decorative blocks, but only a few sources: a workbench, a chisel, the stonecutter or the crafting table. Learn the sources, not the blocks.",
    "",
    "The story never asks for any of them. Build however you like; the cube house is also valid. Technically."
  ],
  "quest.4499259E5C4284D8.title": "Find Every Variant",
  "quest.4499259E5C4284D8.quest_desc": [
    "Hover a block and press &eU&r in EMI: every recipe that uses it appears, including each Chipped, chisel and stonecutter variant. Search &e@chipped&r, &e@mcw&r or &e@createdeco&r to browse a whole mod.",
    "",
    "This one trick replaces most building wikis."
  ],
  "quest.3FD169F826E0CEC2.title": "Chipped Workbenches",
  "quest.3FD169F826E0CEC2.quest_desc": [
    "Hundreds of vanilla variants, one to one, in seven benches: &eMason Table&r (stone, bricks, concrete, terracotta), &eCarpenters Table&r (wood), &eGlassblower&r (glass), &eLoom Table&r (wool, carpets), &eBotanist Workbench&r (dirt, sand, leaves, ice, pumpkins), &eAlchemy Bench&r (mineral blocks, amethyst, waxed copper) and &eTinkering Table&r (lamps, bars, redstone).",
    "",
    "Nothing is lost."
  ],
  "quest.16FFDBCA7DA034F1.title": "The Rechiseled Chisel",
  "quest.16FFDBCA7DA034F1.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click with the &eChisel&r, put blocks in, pick a variant (many with connected textures) and take them out; previews show 1x1, 3x1 or 3x3.",
    "",
    "Here it also reaches Chipped's variants through Rechiseled: Chipped, so one tool covers both families."
  ],
  "quest.2E768D0705A83924.title": "Chiseling by the Stack",
  "quest.2E768D0705A83924.quest_desc": [
    "Once you have a Create workshop, the &eMechanical Chisel&r (Rechiseled: Create) converts blocks by itself: give it rotation, set the output filter and feed it by belt or funnel.",
    "",
    "For when a build needs a few thousand of the same chiseled brick. It happens."
  ],
  "quest.2E270670E1203AAD.title": "Macaw's: Nine Families",
  "quest.2E270670E1203AAD.quest_desc": [
    "Roofs, Windows, Doors, Trapdoors, Fences and Walls, Bridges, Stairs and Balconies, Paths and Pavings, and Lights and Lamps. Wooden pieces are crafted; most stone roofs, stairs, fences and bridges and nearly all paths come from the &estonecutter&r.",
    "",
    "Drop stone in a stonecutter and scroll: dozens of Macaw's options appear."
  ],
  "quest.1901870848FC4CA2.title": "Macaw's Moving Parts",
  "quest.1901870848FC4CA2.quest_desc": [
    "Windows open and some resize to fill bigger openings, shutters and blinds open with a click, gates stack two high, trapdoors and barn doors open like vanilla ones, and many lights switch on and off.",
    "",
    "Right-click things before deciding they are only decoration."
  ],
  "quest.5612D039A8FE9624.title": "Create Deco: Industrial Style",
  "quest.5612D039A8FE9624.quest_desc": [
    "Colored bricks, sheet metal, catwalks with railings and stairs, bars, mesh fences, supports, industrial doors and windows, hull blocks, placards, shipping containers and lamps in several metals.",
    "",
    "Almost all of it comes from the stonecutter, from bricks, andesite alloy, iron, copper, brass or zinc."
  ],
  "quest.29A2A50413524CD2.title": "Glass That Does Things",
  "quest.29A2A50413524CD2.quest_desc": [
    "&eGlassential&r glass: redstone (full signal), light (full glow), ghostly (anything walks through), ethereal (players pass, mobs do not; reverse does the opposite; dark versions block light), one-way (a secret window), smart (frosts with redstone) and protected (blast-proof), plus glass doors and trapdoors.",
    "",
    "Secret doors and mob-proof windows, sorted."
  ],
  "quest.0D2382C1E7856E7F.title": "Light as a Material",
  "quest.0D2382C1E7856E7F.quest_desc": [
    "Macaw's Lights and Lamps (garden, wall and ceiling lights, chandeliers, fans), &eSimply Light&r edge strips and flush blocks that switch with redstone, Supplementaries sconces and candle holders, Create Deco lamps and Glassential light glass.",
    "",
    "Hide light in floors and ceilings instead of dotting torches everywhere."
  ],
  "quest.75651965718D0718.title": "Copycat Blocks",
  "quest.75651965718D0718.quest_desc": [
    "&eCopycats+&r adds Create copycat shapes (slabs, stairs, beams, panels and more) that take the look of any block you right-click them with. With FramedBlocks, curves and thin details in any material become easy.",
    "",
    "FramedBlocks and LittleTiles: the Building Tools chapter."
  ],
  "quest.2B856A81E120ECF9.title": "Hard-Light Bridges",
  "quest.2B856A81E120ECF9.quest_desc": [
    "&eLaser Bridges and Doors&r source blocks project a solid bridge or fence of light while powered by redstone; cut the signal and it vanishes.",
    "",
    "Drawbridges, hangar doors and lever-operated gates, with a sci-fi hum included."
  ],
  "quest.2DD56B446E130054.title": "Tip: Three Materials and Depth",
  "quest.2DD56B446E130054.quest_desc": [
    "Pick two or three main materials plus one accent and repeat them; Heliodor's own palette is tuff, calcite, quartz and waxed oxidized copper. Then add depth: windows one block back, walls framed with logs or pillars, trims, roof overhangs.",
    "",
    "A row of stairs or slabs at the base of a flat wall changes everything."
  ],
  "quest.1BD763C4EC00F8A4.title": "Tip: Roofs and Paths",
  "quest.1BD763C4EC00F8A4.quest_desc": [
    "Roofs make the silhouette: Macaw's Roofs has steep, low, attic and rounded roofs in wood, stone and terracotta, so mix two slopes on one house. Paths make the village: patterned Macaw's pavings sit well beside shovel paths.",
    "",
    "For slopes that meet the terrain smoothly, the Altar of Levelling."
  ],
  "quest.195C0B8F12D7F1C5.title": "Look at Solsticio",
  "quest.195C0B8F12D7F1C5.quest_desc": [
    "Solsticio, the city at the end of the story, is built from the same kinds of blocks you have, around a copper, glass and calcite palette. When you get there, look closely and steal ideas.",
    "",
    "Your plot there is 16 by 16, and it is yours to fill."
  ],
  "quest.3F67FB5103402B8C.title": "Pack Change: Building Is Free",
  "quest.3F67FB5103402B8C.quest_desc": [
    "No decorative block, workbench or chisel carries an act component, and no quest or Atlas project asks for a specific decorative block. Everything here is available from day one with ordinary materials.",
    "",
    "Build the house you want before the story asks anything of you."
  ],
  "quest.4A560963002F55E4.title": "A Palette in Your Hands",
  "quest.4A560963002F55E4.quest_desc": [
    "U in EMI for variants, seven Chipped benches, one chisel, the stonecutter for Macaw's and Create Deco, glass that does things and light as a material.",
    "",
    "Heliodor was all copper, glass and gardens. No pressure."
  ],
  "chapter.640F39A02855835E.title": "Furniture and Functional Decor",
  "chapter.640F39A02855835E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Handcrafted, Another Furniture, Refurbished Furniture, kitchens, Supplementaries and Amendments: rooms that work."
  ],
  "quest.62707CA5C04CB701.title": "A House, Not a Box",
  "quest.62707CA5C04CB701.quest_desc": [
    "Three furniture sets with different jobs, two kitchen systems, and Supplementaries and Amendments, with hundreds of small blocks that actually do something.",
    "",
    "Walls make a shelter; furniture makes a home."
  ],
  "quest.01D40C5A681156DE.title": "Handcrafted: the Living Room",
  "quest.01D40C5A681156DE.quest_desc": [
    "The classic set: chairs, benches, couches, tables, desks, nightstands, cupboards, shelves, counters and fancy beds in every wood, and you can sit on the seats.",
    "",
    "Dress them with &ecushions&r and &esheets&r in sixteen colors, then finish with trims, crockery, jars and mounted trophies."
  ],
  "quest.41732879A0DB8E73.title": "Another Furniture: Cozy Details",
  "quest.41732879A0DB8E73.quest_desc": [
    "It fills the gaps: seats and tables, &eshelves&r that display, &edrawers&r that store, &ecurtains&r and &eshutters&r that open, flower boxes, lattices, awnings, lamps joined by a &elamp connector&r and a &eservice bell&r for the counter.",
    "",
    "Its &eHammer&r restyles some placed pieces."
  ],
  "quest.39FE892EFCB015B7.title": "Refurbished Furniture: Appliances",
  "quest.39FE892EFCB015B7.quest_desc": [
    "Furniture that works: fridges and freezers that store and freeze, stoves and ovens that cook, microwaves, toasters, grills, sinks, cutting boards and frying pans. Most pieces come from its own &eWorkbench&r, which needs electricity.",
    "",
    "Its kitchen recipes get their own EMI tabs."
  ],
  "quest.17776D09FC64AB58.title": "Electricity for Your Home",
  "quest.17776D09FC64AB58.quest_desc": [
    "Refurbished Furniture runs its own small grid: fuel an &eElectricity Generator&r and link it with the &eWrench&r (one node, then the other) to the workbench, lights, TV or computer.",
    "",
    "A screen that says it lacks power needs a link to a running generator. Check the cable before the fuse."
  ],
  "quest.5EA0DD3021C6C45E.title": "Mail Between Players",
  "quest.5EA0DD3021C6C45E.quest_desc": [
    "The &ePost Box&r sends packages to any &eMailbox&r: pick one from the list (search players with @), load the package slots, add a message and send.",
    "",
    "The friendliest way to share items without meeting up. The computer has a paddle-ball game, for the slow days."
  ],
  "quest.05F5E01F06961171.title": "A Kitchen That Cooks for You",
  "quest.05F5E01F06961171.quest_desc": [
    "&eCooking for Blockheads&r turns connected kitchen blocks into one kitchen, and its &eCooking Table&r lists and crafts every food the kitchen can make. The fridge, counters, spice rack and fruit basket store ingredients; the sink gives water, the oven bakes, the tool rack lends tools; milk jars and the ice unit supply milk, snow and ice."
  ],
  "quest.4602CFEDAF691E57.title": "Pantry Storage",
  "quest.4602CFEDAF691E57.quest_desc": [
    "&eStorage Delight&r adds kitchen furniture that stores: cabinets with stone countertops or glass doors, drawers and bookshelves with doors, in every wood.",
    "",
    "With a Cooking for Blockheads kitchen, you get a pantry that looks the part."
  ],
  "quest.7A6CE5FCA1EB96A0.title": "Supplementaries: Keep and Show",
  "quest.7A6CE5FCA1EB96A0.quest_desc": [
    "The &eJar&r holds and shows bowls, bottles, buckets, cookies and small mobs; the &eSack&r is a portable, heavy bag; the &eSafe&r locks to its owner or a key; the &eItem Shelf&r, &ePedestal&r and &eHat Stand&r show off items and armor; the &eNotice Board&r pins a book or map for everyone."
  ],
  "quest.2A79E25091CC60D7.title": "Supplementaries: Decoration",
  "quest.2A79E25091CC60D7.quest_desc": [
    "Flags with banner patterns, awnings and buntings on ropes, &etimber frames&r that take any full block for half-timbered walls, flower boxes, planters and doormats, sconces and stackable candle holders, &eblackboards&r you can draw on, globes and &eway signs&r that point to places.",
    "",
    "Character, one block at a time."
  ],
  "quest.460D72D9BCBC9693.title": "Supplementaries: Gadgets",
  "quest.460D72D9BCBC9693.quest_desc": [
    "The &eHourglass&r is a redstone timer filled with any sand or powder, the &eWind Vane&r reacts to weather, the &eTurn Table&r spins the block on top, the &eFaucet&r pours from jars, cauldrons and tanks, &eRope&r and &ePulley&r climb and haul, a &eLock Block&r opens only for its &eKey&r, and the Clock, Crank and Bellows feed your machinery."
  ],
  "quest.2C5C641F7EA38538.title": "Supplementaries: Carry Tools",
  "quest.2C5C641F7EA38538.quest_desc": [
    "The &eQuiver&r holds arrows and picks which to shoot (open it with the US apostrophe key), the &eSlingshot&r throws blocks and items, the &eCannon&r shoots almost anything, the &eCage&r catches small or tamed animals, &ePresents&r wrap items for a player, and the &eLunch Basket&r carries food.",
    "",
    "Yes, the cannon. Almost anything."
  ],
  "quest.3D63FBB8415A0FF7.title": "Amendments: Vanilla, Improved",
  "quest.3D63FBB8415A0FF7.quest_desc": [
    "Lanterns hang on walls and flower pots from ceilings; banners hang from ceilings and carpets lie on stairs and slabs; tools hang on tripwire hooks; skulls stack and take candles; cauldrons hold potions and mix dyes; cakes can be eaten from any side, and two stack into a double cake.",
    "",
    "Vanilla, minus the old annoyances."
  ],
  "quest.132C807FE691F1ED.title": "Quirk: Cake Bites Count",
  "quest.132C807FE691F1ED.quest_desc": [
    "A bite of an Amendments directional cake still counts for ENTRELUMEN's satiety overflow: food eaten from a block, like cake or a Farmer's Delight pie, is measured like food from your hand.",
    "",
    "How surplus food turns into buffs: the Satiety chapter."
  ],
  "quest.32DC6502B2C871AA.title": "Tip: Where You Can Sit",
  "quest.32DC6502B2C871AA.quest_desc": [
    "Handcrafted and Another Furniture chairs, benches, stools and couches seat you with an empty-hand right-click; sneak to stand up.",
    "",
    "Purely cosmetic, and exactly what co-op evenings and screenshots needed."
  ],
  "quest.655997FD290E2F74.title": "Quirk: Heavy Furniture Stays",
  "quest.655997FD290E2F74.quest_desc": [
    "Carry On refuses Cooking for Blockheads kitchen blocks, Farmer's Delight blocks and Sophisticated and Functional storage on purpose. Break and replace them, or use Packing Tape on Sophisticated chests.",
    "",
    "Plain chests, barrels and furnaces still travel."
  ],
  "quest.2BE277607ACAB07B.title": "Pack Change: One Role per Set",
  "quest.2BE277607ACAB07B.quest_desc": [
    "Each furniture set has a job: Handcrafted for classics, Refurbished Furniture for working appliances, Another Furniture for cozy details and Storage Delight for kitchen storage. Macaw's Furniture stayed out as a third palette with nothing new to do.",
    "",
    "Macaw's windows, doors, roofs and lights are in: the Blocks and Variants chapter."
  ],
  "quest.1F47E9121F669203.title": "Home, Furnished",
  "quest.1F47E9121F669203.quest_desc": [
    "A living room to sit in, a kitchen that cooks, appliances with power, jars and shelves full of things, and vanilla blocks that finally hang where you want.",
    "",
    "Now invite someone over. The Post Box is right there."
  ],
  "chapter.07F1D898223AE695.title": "Helpers in the World",
  "chapter.07F1D898223AE695.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Ultimine, Carry On, pocket villagers, elevators, lights, beds for the road and small fixes."
  ],
  "quest.325DD88D37F6C953.title": "Work Smarter Outside",
  "quest.325DD88D37F6C953.quest_desc": [
    "Inventory helpers save clicks; these save hours. Mining veins, moving chests, pocketing villagers, climbing, lighting and sleeping far from home, each with a limit the pack sets.",
    "",
    "Know the limit and nothing surprises you. Mostly."
  ],
  "quest.6F7BA1BEB737FF7F.title": "Ultimine: One Swing, One Vein",
  "quest.6F7BA1BEB737FF7F.quest_desc": [
    "Hold &eV&r and break a block: every connected block of the same kind goes with it, up to the reach of your vein resonator (&e8&r, &e16&r, &e32&r or &e64&r blocks by tier); it goes in a Curios charm slot, and without one Ultimine is off. Each extra block costs hunger and tool durability, so eat and bring a good pick; the HUD warns when you are too hungry.",
    "",
    "It respects claims and ruins."
  ],
  "quest.34D3B9788044C1CF.title": "Ultimine Shapes",
  "quest.34D3B9788044C1CF.quest_desc": [
    "With V held, &eShift&r and the wheel (or up and down) cycle shapes: &eShapeless&r follows the vein (ores, trees), &eSmall&r and &eLarge tunnel (3x3)&r dig corridors, &eSmall square (3x3)&r clears flat ground, and &eMining&r and &eEscape tunnel&r do branch mining and a staircase up.",
    "",
    "The outline shows what breaks before you swing."
  ],
  "quest.4721D87B06E32449.title": "Ultimine With Right Click",
  "quest.4721D87B06E32449.quest_desc": [
    "With V held, right-click actions multiply too: an &eaxe&r strips logs or scrapes and unwaxes copper, a &eshovel&r makes paths, a &ehoe&r tills a whole field, and on crops it harvests every ripe one in reach.",
    "",
    "Even without V, right-clicking a ripe crop harvests it."
  ],
  "quest.07E6520EC32BD592.title": "Carry On: Pick Up a Chest",
  "quest.07E6520EC32BD592.quest_desc": [
    "With an &eempty hand&r, &esneak and right-click&r a chest, furnace or barrel to lift it with everything inside, and right-click again to set it down; passive animals and villagers ride along too.",
    "",
    "You move slower, heavier blocks slow you more, and you cannot attack. Only blocks with an inventory lift."
  ],
  "quest.4A3DBA14B5939CD9.title": "What Carry On Refuses",
  "quest.4A3DBA14B5939CD9.quest_desc": [
    "A long blacklist keeps things from breaking: every ENTRELUMEN block, spawners, vaults and Lootr chests; whole mods with multiblocks or networks (Create, AE2, Refined Storage, MI, Oritech, IE, Industrial Foregoing, Powah, Functional and Sophisticated Storage, Ender Storage, Farmer's Delight, FramedBlocks, LittleTiles, Waystones); Mekanism casings and ports; Ender IO conduits; hostiles, bosses, frames and armor stands."
  ],
  "quest.706F751CEDE5DD09.title": "Quirk: Stacks, Players, Reach",
  "quest.706F751CEDE5DD09.quest_desc": [
    "Carried animals stack on top of each other, up to 10. Players can be picked up too, so behave in co-op. Pick-up distance follows your reach, so Terra's Arm stretches it as well.",
    "",
    "A tower of ten sheep is technically allowed."
  ],
  "quest.090C768610DD6B3B.title": "Villagers in Your Pocket",
  "quest.090C768610DD6B3B.quest_desc": [
    "&eEasy Villagers&r turns villagers into items: look at one and press &eAlt+O&r, then place it anywhere or inside one of its blocks: &eTrader&r (compact trading), &eFarmer&r (it grows crops), &eBreeder&r, &eIncubator&r and &eConverter&r (more villagers, grown babies, cured zombies).",
    "",
    "In a trading screen, &eC&r cycles its trades."
  ],
  "quest.5D3FA46224B03D71.title": "Pack Change: Two Blocks Wait",
  "quest.5D3FA46224B03D71.quest_desc": [
    "The &eIron Farm&r needs a Living Matrix (act II) and the &eAuto Trader&r a Handling Core (act III), each on the top of its drawing; the other Easy Villagers blocks keep their native recipes.",
    "",
    "Worth knowing later: villagers settled in Solsticio's trading hall trade cheaper forever."
  ],
  "quest.400261324AFA96E7.title": "Elevators",
  "quest.400261324AFA96E7.quest_desc": [
    "Two &eElevator&r blocks in the same column, with room to stand on each: &ejump&r to go up, &esneak&r to go down, instantly. They come in all sixteen dye colors.",
    "",
    "If one refuses to teleport, try two of the same color: the server may require it."
  ],
  "quest.078A1C5D7D7FE457.title": "Light Without Torch Spam",
  "quest.078A1C5D7D7FE457.quest_desc": [
    "The &eFeral Flare Lantern&r places invisible lights in dark areas around it, great for caves; the &eFrozen Pearl&r clears them; the &eDread Lamp&r stops bats, squid and other passive spawns nearby.",
    "",
    "The Mega Torch is gone here: the Altar of Peace does its job."
  ],
  "quest.3AE12491BA59667D.title": "Beds for the Road",
  "quest.3AE12491BA59667D.quest_desc": [
    "&eComforts&r adds the &eSleeping Bag&r, for nights far from home (it can wear out), and the &eHammock&r, hung between two &eRope and Nail&r blocks, for sleeping through the day.",
    "",
    "The server decides how many players must sleep to skip time. Somebody will always be mining."
  ],
  "quest.7FF3C0D9AEEBFA79.title": "Small Fixes You Will Notice",
  "quest.7FF3C0D9AEEBFA79.quest_desc": [
    "&eClean Swing&r hits mobs through tall grass, &eHey Berry Shut Up&r lets leggings and boots shrug off berry bushes and cactus, &eAccelerated Decay&r drops leaves fast after you fell a tree, boats hop ashore or survive lava (Jump Boat, Fireproof Boats), and &eJust Zoom&r zooms on &eZ&r."
  ],
  "quest.0BFCB9842C3F988B.title": "Tip: Test Your Damage",
  "quest.0BFCB9842C3F988B.quest_desc": [
    "A &eTarget Dummy&r shows the damage of every hit and your damage per second. Compare weapons, enchantments and Apotheosis gems before a boss, not during."
  ],
  "quest.6D0284FD17470EC0.title": "Tip: Safe Zones Come Later",
  "quest.6D0284FD17470EC0.quest_desc": [
    "A whole base free of natural hostile spawns is the &eAltar of Peace&r, an act III reward (see The Six Altars of Heliodor).",
    "",
    "Until then, light is your friend: &eF7&r shows where mobs can spawn."
  ],
  "quest.147332C8C4BF6261.title": "A Lighter World",
  "quest.147332C8C4BF6261.quest_desc": [
    "Veins in one swing, chests on your back, villagers in your pocket, elevators, lit caves and a bed anywhere.",
    "",
    "The world is just as big. It just weighs less now."
  ],
  "chapter.0F589FD1738516F7.title": "Moving Items, Fluids and Energy",
  "chapter.0F589FD1738516F7.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Pipes, filters, laser nodes, routers and cables: which one to use and how energy crosses between mods."
  ],
  "quest.6611059F058DEAC6.title": "Stop Carrying, Start Piping",
  "quest.6611059F058DEAC6.quest_desc": [
    "Sooner or later everything should flow on its own: ore to the crusher, ingots to chests, fuel to generators, power to machines. The pack's transport systems overlap on purpose, from the simplest to the most flexible.",
    "",
    "Pick the one whose style you like. Nobody is grading the spaghetti."
  ],
  "quest.4D925148310D452A.title": "Early: Hoppers and Create",
  "quest.4D925148310D452A.quest_desc": [
    "Before pipes, you already have vanilla hoppers and droppers, and Create's belts, chutes, funnels and mechanical arm, which move items with rotation and look great doing it.",
    "",
    "Create's logistics has its own chapter."
  ],
  "quest.05CCF43C232C2870.title": "Pipez: the Everyday Pipe",
  "quest.05CCF43C232C2870.quest_desc": [
    "Item, fluid, energy and gas pipes, plus a &eUniversal Pipe&r for all four, that connect on their own to whatever they touch. They do not pull by themselves: right-click the end at the source with the &ePipe Wrench&r to make it extract.",
    "",
    "Sneak-right-click with the wrench to cut a connection you do not want."
  ],
  "quest.4D5DE8F1242EB133.title": "The Extraction Menu",
  "quest.4D5DE8F1242EB133.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click an extracting end to set &edistribution&r (nearest, furthest, round robin, random), &eredstone mode&r, and &efilters&r by item ID or #tag, with data matching, inversion and a destination picked with the &eFilter Destination Tool&r.",
    "",
    "The menu also shows how much the pipe moves per tick."
  ],
  "quest.2B72673A26EA44B0.title": "Faster Pipes",
  "quest.2B72673A26EA44B0.quest_desc": [
    "A &epipe upgrade&r in the extraction menu raises speed (Basic, Improved, Advanced, Ultimate) and unlocks more options.",
    "",
    "One upgrade per extracting side, not per pipe: upgrade only where items enter the line."
  ],
  "quest.5B9D62223F724826.title": "Fluids",
  "quest.5B9D62223F724826.quest_desc": [
    "Fluid pipes work like item pipes: Pipez fluid pipes, Mekanism mechanical pipes, Create fluid pipes driven by a mechanical pump, and Ender Storage tanks for long distances.",
    "",
    "A Fluid Trash Can at the end of a line voids the overflow."
  ],
  "quest.014A8F84EBC9F691.title": "Energy Between Mods",
  "quest.014A8F84EBC9F691.quest_desc": [
    "Most tech mods here speak &eFE&r, so one cable feeds machines from any of them: Pipez energy pipes, Mekanism universal cables or Immersive Engineering wires. An &eEnergy Meter&r in a line shows the flow.",
    "",
    "The exception is &eCreate&r, which runs on rotation."
  ],
  "quest.449E5E1DB3B1C498.title": "Rotation and Electricity",
  "quest.449E5E1DB3B1C498.quest_desc": [
    "&eCreate: Crafts and Additions&r has the &eAlternator&r (rotation to FE) and &eElectric Motor&r (FE to rotation), with wires. &eCreate: New Age&r, Heliodor's own technology, spins a &eGenerator Coil&r between magnets, collects it with carbon brushes and turns it back into rotation with motors.",
    "",
    "Its carbon brushes take an Energy Coupler (act II), and its better motors act materials."
  ],
  "quest.5F37A164B3A0D59F.title": "Wireless Energy (Act III)",
  "quest.5F37A164B3A0D59F.quest_desc": [
    "&eFlux Networks&r moves energy without cables: &eFlux Plugs&r feed a network and &eFlux Points&r deliver wherever the same network reaches.",
    "",
    "Plugs take a reinforced alloy (act III); points and the controller keep their native recipes."
  ],
  "quest.739B53602D9058E2.title": "Mekanism Transmitters",
  "quest.739B53602D9058E2.quest_desc": [
    "&eLogistical transporters&r for items, &emechanical pipes&r for fluids, &epressurized tubes&r for chemicals and &euniversal cables&r for energy, four tiers each; transporters can be color-coded and sorted with a &eLogistical Sorter&r.",
    "",
    "Machines pick what each face does in their &eside configuration&r tab, and &eMekanism Covers&r hide transmitters behind any block's look."
  ],
  "quest.193756AA70D33B62.title": "LaserIO: Beams, Not Pipes",
  "quest.193756AA70D33B62.quest_desc": [
    "&eLaser Nodes&r sit beside machines, linked by beams with the &eLaser Wrench&r, and each side takes &ecards&r for items, fluids, energy, chemicals or redstone. Each card runs in &eExtract&r, &eInsert&r, &eStock&r or &eSensor&r mode on a channel color, with optional filters (basic, tag, mod, count, data).",
    "",
    "Overclockers speed it up. Made for compact machine rooms."
  ],
  "quest.1FB4FD3C079FE46A.title": "XNet: One Controller (Act III)",
  "quest.1FB4FD3C079FE46A.quest_desc": [
    "Connectors touch the machines, thin cables join them to a &eController&r, and its menu defines up to eight channels (item, fluid, energy or logic) with rules per connector: a whole logistics network, hidden.",
    "",
    "The controller takes a reinforced alloy, so it arrives in act III; routers need a controller anyway. Its manual is craftable."
  ],
  "quest.0736402840CEA2F5.title": "Modular Routers",
  "quest.0736402840CEA2F5.quest_desc": [
    "A &eModular Router&r does whatever its modules say: &eSender&r pushes items to other inventories, &ePuller&r pulls, &eDropper&r and &eFlinger&r throw, &ePlacer&r and &eBreaker&r handle blocks, &eVacuum&r collects drops, &eExtruder&r builds lines of blocks. Upgrades add speed and range.",
    "",
    "Every module starts from a Blank Module; Mekanistic Routers adds chemicals."
  ],
  "quest.1CED0A985AB18B7C.title": "Integrated Tunnels",
  "quest.1CED0A985AB18B7C.quest_desc": [
    "For programmers: items, fluids and energy through Integrated Dynamics networks, with importers and exporters driven by variable cards and logic. The most flexible system here, and the slowest to learn.",
    "",
    "Its guide is the Integrated Dynamics manual, craftable from day one."
  ],
  "quest.1E0C97FDD675306D.title": "Which One Should I Use?",
  "quest.1E0C97FDD675306D.quest_desc": [
    "A few machines: &ePipez&r, extracting only where needed. A dense room: &eLaserIO&r. A big, tidy base: &eXNet&r from act III, or a storage network. Placing, breaking and odd jobs: &eModular Routers&r. A factory worth watching: &eCreate&r.",
    "",
    "Mixing is fine: most bases end up with three of them."
  ],
  "quest.2E5A18FC60DED15A.title": "Tip: Filter With Tags",
  "quest.2E5A18FC60DED15A.quest_desc": [
    "&e#c:ores&r catches every ore from every mod and &e#c:ingots&r every ingot: Pipez filters take a #tag, and LaserIO has a Tag Filter.",
    "",
    "F3+H shows an item's tags in its tooltip, and EMI searches them with #."
  ],
  "quest.2FA69EC10654DE68.title": "Quirk: a Full Chest Stops All",
  "quest.2FA69EC10654DE68.quest_desc": [
    "When the destination fills, the line backs up and the machine upstream stops. Plan for overflow: a Void upgrade in a drawer, a Trash Can at the end of the line, or a second destination further down.",
    "",
    "Every factory learns this once."
  ],
  "quest.6E189022971819C4.title": "Things Flow on Their Own",
  "quest.6E189022971819C4.quest_desc": [
    "Items, fluids and energy now move without you. The last step is a storage network that knows where everything is and crafts on request.",
    "",
    "The spaghetti is optional. The satisfaction is not."
  ],
  "chapter.3BF93B1AC8D3E2BD.title": "Performance, Sound and Screen",
  "chapter.3BF93B1AC8D3E2BD.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Settings that keep a 300-mod pack smooth, quiet when you want it and readable."
  ],
  "quest.31CFA01185FA98C4.title": "A Heavy Pack on a Normal PC",
  "quest.31CFA01185FA98C4.quest_desc": [
    "ENTRELUMEN is meant to run on ordinary PCs: it ships with rendering and memory optimizations and a cautious first profile, and leaves you room to tune.",
    "",
    "Three hundred mods, one potato-friendly start."
  ],
  "quest.572656FC02703CC9.title": "What Is Already Optimized",
  "quest.572656FC02703CC9.quest_desc": [
    "Already in: &eSodium&r (a faster renderer with its own video pages), &eImmediatelyFast&r (text, items and HUD), &eModernFix&r and &eFerriteCore&r (loading and memory), &eAllTheLeaks&r (leak fixes for long sessions) and &eAI Improvements&r (lighter mob thinking on the server).",
    "",
    "Another optimizer on top usually brings conflicts, not frames."
  ],
  "quest.375C479FC614F2AE.title": "The First Profile",
  "quest.375C479FC614F2AE.quest_desc": [
    "A new profile starts at render distance &e10&r, simulation &e6&r, a &e120 FPS&r cap without VSync, fast graphics, no clouds, fewer particles, no entity shadows, entity distance 75%, darkness and screen effects at half, GUI scale 3.",
    "",
    "A safe start, not a rule: raise render distance first, since simulation distance costs the server far more."
  ],
  "quest.5D3F2F532595406E.title": "Sodium's Video Settings",
  "quest.5D3F2F532595406E.quest_desc": [
    "Options, Video Settings opens Sodium's pages (General, Quality, Performance, Advanced) plus pages other mods add. Hover any option to read what it does and what it costs.",
    "",
    "On a weak PC: lower render distance, keep particles decreased and leave the performance options alone."
  ],
  "quest.5F9D459224CCEDBF.title": "Dynamic Lights",
  "quest.5F9D459224CCEDBF.quest_desc": [
    "&eLambDynamicLights&r makes held torches, lanterns and glowing items light your surroundings, and lights up burning or glowing entities. Its page sits in Sodium's video settings, where you can lower it or turn it off.",
    "",
    "Solsticio's luminous gear shines with it too. Obviously."
  ],
  "quest.39B57F7649021B1E.title": "Silence the Factory",
  "quest.39B57F7649021B1E.quest_desc": [
    "&eExtreme Sound Muffler&r adds a &eMuffler&r button to your inventory that lists nearby sounds: lower or mute any, for the whole world or only inside an &eanchor&r area around your machines. Right-drag the button if it covers something.",
    "",
    "Leave combat sounds on. They are the ones that keep you alive."
  ],
  "quest.689260C1B854A07B.title": "Fewer Pop-ups",
  "quest.689260C1B854A07B.quest_desc": [
    "&eToast Control&r handles the top-right notifications: recipe unlocks, advancements and tutorial hints. &eF10&r clears the ones on screen, and its settings block whole kinds.",
    "",
    "You miss nothing important: quests and the Atlas speak in their own screens and in chat."
  ],
  "quest.3E474B9B801F50F6.title": "A HUD That Scales",
  "quest.3E474B9B801F50F6.quest_desc": [
    "Health and armor grow far past vanilla here: Spice of Life adds hearts for food variety and late armor passes 20. &eColorful Hearts&r stacks extra hearts in colored rows and &eOverloaded Armor Bar&r does the same for armor, so the HUD never swallows the screen.",
    "",
    "&eNot Enough Animations&r adds eating and map animations; purely cosmetic."
  ],
  "quest.187F30877B47077A.title": "Protect Your Save",
  "quest.187F30877B47077A.quest_desc": [
    "&eCherished Worlds&r lets you mark a world as a favorite: it stays at the top of the list and resists accidental deletion. &eSimple Backups&r makes automatic ZIP copies and announces them in chat.",
    "",
    "Restore a backup only with the game or server closed. Future you will thank you."
  ],
  "quest.29E494460AEDC6F2.title": "Solsticio's Motes of Light",
  "quest.29E494460AEDC6F2.quest_desc": [
    "The drifting motes in Solsticio are client-side and follow your particle setting: halved on Decreased, gone on Minimal.",
    "",
    "Finer controls live in the ENTRELUMEN client config; the Solsticio chapter has them."
  ],
  "quest.00C6A92105A1B302.title": "Tip: Find the Lag",
  "quest.00C6A92105A1B302.quest_desc": [
    "When the game or server stutters, &espark&r says why: an operator runs &e/spark profiler&r, reproduces the lag and stops it to see which mod or machine eats the time; &e/spark tps&r shows server ticks per second.",
    "",
    "Check the obvious first: item piles, giant farms in loaded chunks, too many force-loaded chunks."
  ],
  "quest.53171C9A7C748B49.title": "Tip: The Floor Is Not Storage",
  "quest.53171C9A7C748B49.quest_desc": [
    "Every dropped item is an entity the server must tick, and farms that spill their output are the classic cause of lag. Collect with hoppers, Item Collectors or machine outputs, void overflow with a Trash Can, and let Clumps merge experience orbs."
  ],
  "quest.44DC2092AA284411.title": "Pack Menus and Loading Screen",
  "quest.44DC2092AA284411.quest_desc": [
    "FancyMenu and Drippy Loading Screen dress up the title and loading screens without touching your settings.",
    "",
    "At a very high GUI scale a button may fall off screen: drop the scale to 3 or 2."
  ],
  "quest.4CEFDFA59AAE55AB.title": "Quirk: GUI Scale and Big Screens",
  "quest.4CEFDFA59AAE55AB.quest_desc": [
    "Many modded screens are wider than vanilla ones (the Atlas is 300 by 210 GUI units), so at a high GUI scale in a small window they may not fit.",
    "",
    "If a screen looks cut off, lower the GUI scale in Options, Video Settings."
  ],
  "quest.02071930B3199174.title": "Smooth and Quiet",
  "quest.02071930B3199174.quest_desc": [
    "Play the way your PC likes: the story never needs a jetpack, a huge render distance or chunk-loading.",
    "",
    "A quiet factory is a happy factory. Or at least a muffled one."
  ],
  "chapter.4BDF7403C3C5E93F.title": "Satiety: When Food Overflows",
  "chapter.4BDF7403C3C5E93F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "An ENTRELUMEN system: variety gives hearts, and food past a full bar becomes short random buffs."
  ],
  "quest.25C480F01ADDB1DD.title": "Nothing Eaten Is Wasted",
  "quest.25C480F01ADDB1DD.quest_desc": [
    "In vanilla, hunger stops at 20 and saturation cannot exceed hunger, so whatever a meal adds beyond that is lost. Here that surplus becomes random buffs: the bigger it is, the more and longer they last. Variety is rewarded separately, with hearts.",
    "",
    "Second helpings finally have a purpose."
  ],
  "quest.5F3E54942A4BE8EF.title": "Hearts for Variety",
  "quest.5F3E54942A4BE8EF.quest_desc": [
    "&eSpice of Life: Carrot Edition&r counts the different foods you eat and grants a heart at &e10, 25, 45, 70 and 100&r, five on top of the base ten, kept through death.",
    "",
    "The food book tracks your list, and a message above the hotbar shows progress when you eat something new."
  ],
  "quest.795AA46FEC18B774.title": "What Counts as Surplus",
  "quest.795AA46FEC18B774.quest_desc": [
    "A meal's surplus is the hunger that did not fit under 20 plus the saturation that did not fit under your new hunger level, in vanilla food points (one point is half a drumstick), never more than the food gives.",
    "",
    "Since you can only eat below 20 hunger, most surplus is &esaturation&r: a rich meal when you are not very hungry."
  ],
  "quest.20A33F8FE7351249.title": "How Many Buffs, How Long",
  "quest.20A33F8FE7351249.quest_desc": [
    "The surplus becomes a &eworth&r: below 2 points, nothing; from 2, one buff, plus one every 10 points, up to three. Durations grow with worth and max out at 20 points, and at 16 or more buffs that allow it come at level II.",
    "",
    "The action bar lists what you got, with a few sparkles."
  ],
  "quest.632BB29C19DACBBF.title": "The Buff Pool",
  "quest.632BB29C19DACBBF.quest_desc": [
    "Drawn at random, weighted, without repeats: &eHaste&r and &eSpeed&r (most common, up to II, 30 to 180 s), &eAbsorption&r (up to II, 30 to 120 s), &eRegeneration&r (5 to 20 s), &eStrength&r (20 to 90 s), &eResistance&r (20 to 60 s), &eWater Breathing&r and &eNight Vision&r (60 to 300 s) and &eLuck&r (up to II, 60 to 300 s).",
    "",
    "A buff only adds or extends; it never replaces a stronger one."
  ],
  "quest.1D8BC6BE01CD5AD2.title": "Worked Examples",
  "quest.1D8BC6BE01CD5AD2.quest_desc": [
    "With no recent overeating: bread at 19 hunger and 15 saturation is 5 points, one level I buff; Farmer's Delight roast chicken at 14 and 8 is 17 points, two buffs at level II where allowed; a golden carrot at 16 and 10 is about 6 points, one buff; a cookie at 19 and 19 is 1 point, nothing.",
    "",
    "Big meals when you are nearly full pay best."
  ],
  "quest.1220B712D2C97C4B.title": "Glut and Cooldown",
  "quest.1220B712D2C97C4B.quest_desc": [
    "After a buff, nothing more is granted for 10 seconds. Every surplus also feeds a hidden &eglut&r that halves every 5 minutes, and the more glut you carry, the less new surplus is worth (it still builds during the cooldown). Death clears it.",
    "",
    "One good meal every few minutes keeps its value; five honey bottles in a row buy one buff and a stomachache."
  ],
  "quest.32CAE9BA1FB1D9A1.title": "Try It Yourself",
  "quest.32CAE9BA1FB1D9A1.quest_desc": [
    "Eat until the hunger bar is almost full, then have a big Farmer's Delight meal like a stew or a roast. The action bar names the buffs you got, and their icons join your other effects.",
    "",
    "Dessert, but it counts as strategy."
  ],
  "quest.1B78187A9833F748.title": "Cakes and Pies Count",
  "quest.1B78187A9833F748.quest_desc": [
    "Food eaten straight from a block counts too: cakes and candle cakes, Farmer's Delight pies and cheesecakes, and any modded block that feeds you. The bite itself is measured, so Amendments' directional cakes work as well.",
    "",
    "A Farmer's Delight pie slice at 19 hunger and 19 saturation is worth 2.8 points: one buff."
  ],
  "quest.4663BF9002371246.title": "What Does Not Count",
  "quest.4663BF9002371246.quest_desc": [
    "No buffs in creative or spectator, and none for fake players such as Create deployers. A plain cake bite at 19 hunger is only 1 point: glut, no buff.",
    "",
    "The system looks at how much overflowed, never at which food, so it never interferes with Spice of Life's list."
  ],
  "quest.4054F7EA70F42E88.title": "Tip: Always-Edible Foods",
  "quest.4054F7EA70F42E88.quest_desc": [
    "Golden apples, chorus fruit, suspicious stew, honey bottles and some drinks can be eaten at full hunger, so they are the only way to overflow hunger itself, not just saturation.",
    "",
    "Space them out: the glut rule remembers."
  ],
  "quest.43703C2F4A489567.title": "Tip: Solsticio's Bakery",
  "quest.43703C2F4A489567.quest_desc": [
    "In Solsticio, Miga the baker sells bread, cake, pies, cookies, golden carrots and Farmer's Delight sweets: variety for Spice of Life and rich food to overflow.",
    "",
    "A whole shop built around dessert."
  ],
  "quest.2C9CC72809167189.title": "For Server Owners",
  "quest.2C9CC72809167189.quest_desc": [
    "Every number here lives in &edata/entrelumen/satiety/overflow.json&r: floor, buff count, level II threshold, glut softness and half-life, cooldown, announcement and pool. A datapack can replace it and &e/reload&r applies it.",
    "",
    "Hard caps the file cannot exceed: level II, 600 seconds per buff, five buffs per meal. Harmful or instant effects are skipped."
  ],
  "quest.61DA3B7739F1D466.title": "Quirk: Two Messages at Once",
  "quest.61DA3B7739F1D466.quest_desc": [
    "When a new food both advances Spice of Life and overflows, both want the line above the hotbar; the overflow runs first, so Spice of Life's message is the one you read, while the buff icons and sparkles still show what you got.",
    "",
    "AppleSkin previews a food's hunger and saturation: use it to aim for surplus."
  ],
  "quest.1D5E71D9D5595C84.title": "A Full Belly Pays",
  "quest.1D5E71D9D5595C84.quest_desc": [
    "Many different foods for hearts, rich meals when nearly full for buffs, spaced out so glut stays low. Cakes and pies from the table count too.",
    "",
    "Heliodor ran on sunlight. You run on stew."
  ],
  "chapter.2ACE544778954FE1.title": "Storage: Backpacks, Chests and Drawers",
  "chapter.2ACE544778954FE1.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From the first backpack to a wall of drawers, and when a storage network starts to make sense."
  ],
  "quest.2E471AA517FF0451.title": "Where Does It All Go?",
  "quest.2E471AA517FF0451.quest_desc": [
    "Three storage families, each good at something: &eSophisticated Backpacks&r you carry, with upgrades that work for you; &eSophisticated Storage&r chests and barrels that grow in tiers; and &eFunctional Storage&r drawers for huge amounts of few items. Later, AE2 or Refined Storage tie it all together.",
    "",
    "Modded Minecraft makes piles. This is where the piles go."
  ],
  "quest.5B974C49A559E883.title": "Your First Backpack",
  "quest.5B974C49A559E883.quest_desc": [
    "Carry a &eBackpack&r in your inventory or wear it on your back, and press &eB&r to open it anywhere. Sneak-right-click a block to set it down; pick it up with an empty hand.",
    "",
    "Hold Shift over a backpack in any inventory to peek inside."
  ],
  "quest.393CF1C2E82B4CEB.title": "Bigger Backpacks, Same Contents",
  "quest.393CF1C2E82B4CEB.quest_desc": [
    "Surround a backpack with eight ingots or gems to raise its tier: basic to copper or iron, iron to gold, gold to diamond, and diamond to netherite at a smithing table. Contents and upgrades stay inside, and each tier adds rows and upgrade slots.",
    "",
    "EMI has each step's exact recipe."
  ],
  "quest.73BA0DCCF7B349DD.title": "Upgrades That Work for You",
  "quest.73BA0DCCF7B349DD.quest_desc": [
    "From an &eUpgrade Base&r: &ePickup&r and &eMagnet&r send items straight in (with filters), &eFeeding&r eats for you, &eCompacting&r turns nuggets into ingots and ingots into blocks, &eVoid&r deletes filtered junk, &eRefill&r tops up a hotbar stack, &eTool Swapper&r picks the right tool, and &eCrafting&r, &eStonecutter&r and &eSmelting&r live in tabs."
  ],
  "quest.2C9867271C931906.title": "Restock and Deposit",
  "quest.2C9867271C931906.quest_desc": [
    "With &eDeposit&r, sneak-right-click a chest with the backpack to unload into it; with &eRestock&r, the same click refills the backpack from the chest. Both use filters.",
    "",
    "Deposit for ores and drops, Restock for torches and food: the trip home becomes one click."
  ],
  "quest.2165179220C8395C.title": "Special Upgrades",
  "quest.2165179220C8395C.quest_desc": [
    "&eStack&r upgrades (Starter, tiers 1 to 4, Omega) multiply what each slot holds; &eTank&r and &eBattery&r store fluid or energy, and the &ePump&r and &eExperience Pump&r move fluid and XP; &eInception&r lets backpacks nest; &eEverlasting&r makes it immune to fire, despawn and the void; the &eMob Catcher&r stores passive mobs."
  ],
  "quest.5044BB1E74772210.title": "Chests and Barrels That Grow",
  "quest.5044BB1E74772210.quest_desc": [
    "&eSophisticated Storage&r chests, barrels and shulker boxes come in six tiers, wood to netherite: right-click a placed one with a &etier upgrade&r to upgrade it in place. The &eBasic Tier Upgrade&r even converts a vanilla chest or barrel, contents included.",
    "",
    "They take backpack-style upgrades: pickup, void, compacting, smelting and more."
  ],
  "quest.0CCBDEAD564B0BAC.title": "Moving House With Tape",
  "quest.0CCBDEAD564B0BAC.quest_desc": [
    "Carry On cannot lift Sophisticated Storage, so use &ePacking Tape&r: tape a chest or barrel, break it, and it drops as one item with everything inside. Tape has limited uses; Super Packing Tape lasts longer.",
    "",
    "Shulker boxes do not need it: they always keep their contents."
  ],
  "quest.644FA66A32840A03.title": "Limited Barrels",
  "quest.644FA66A32840A03.quest_desc": [
    "A &eLimited Barrel&r has one to four slots, each holding far more than a stack, with the item and count shown on its face. They behave like Sophisticated drawers and take tier upgrades.",
    "",
    "One per material at the end of a mining line, and the chaos sorts itself."
  ],
  "quest.4C743BC0B3EFF3A8.title": "One Face for Many Chests",
  "quest.4C743BC0B3EFF3A8.quest_desc": [
    "A &eStorage Controller&r joins every Sophisticated chest and barrel touching it, or each other, into one inventory that pipes can use; a &eStorage Link&r, bound with the &eStorage Tool&r, adds a separate group.",
    "",
    "&eStorage Input&r, &eOutput&r and &eI/O&r blocks give automation one access point."
  ],
  "quest.54278DB8E45363FF.title": "Storage on Wheels",
  "quest.54278DB8E45363FF.quest_desc": [
    "&eSophisticated Storage in Motion&r puts a Sophisticated chest, barrel or shulker box on minecarts, boats and rafts.",
    "",
    "A mining cart, a trading boat, a raft full of loot: all very sensible."
  ],
  "quest.00E5D95C0155A1B1.title": "Drawers: Lots of Few Things",
  "quest.00E5D95C0155A1B1.quest_desc": [
    "&eFunctional Storage&r drawers come with 1, 2 or 4 compartments in every wood, each holding huge amounts of one item shown on the front. Right-click with the item to insert, double right-click to insert all you carry, left-click to take out.",
    "",
    "Cobblestone, ores, crops and mob drops, finally tidy."
  ],
  "quest.32B8755F62256BB1.title": "Compacting Drawers",
  "quest.32B8755F62256BB1.quest_desc": [
    "A &eCompacting Drawer&r holds one material in up to three forms and converts automatically: insert iron ingots and it also offers nuggets and blocks. The Simple version handles two forms.",
    "",
    "One at the end of an ore line, and you never craft blocks by hand again."
  ],
  "quest.0B98E9CC224A0976.title": "Drawer Upgrades",
  "quest.0B98E9CC224A0976.quest_desc": [
    "&eStorage&r upgrades (copper, gold, diamond, netherite, max) multiply capacity and the &eIron Downgrade&r shrinks it; &eVoid&r deletes overflow so a full drawer never stalls a farm; &ePusher&r, &ePuller&r and &eCollector&r move items without pipes; &eRedstone&r signals fill level; Water and Obsidian generators produce those resources."
  ],
  "quest.33DD3545E3DC75C6.title": "The Drawer Wall",
  "quest.33DD3545E3DC75C6.quest_desc": [
    "A &eStorage Controller&r turns the drawers around it into one access point that finds the right drawer for anything. Link distant drawers with the &eLinking Tool&r and extend reach with a &eController Access Point&r.",
    "",
    "The &eConfiguration Tool&r locks a drawer to its item, so it keeps its place even empty."
  ],
  "quest.11771CC46C1158B2.title": "More Drawer Tricks",
  "quest.11771CC46C1158B2.quest_desc": [
    "&eFluid drawers&r store fluids the same way; the &eEnder Drawer&r shares contents with every Ender Drawer on its frequency (set with the Linking Tool); the &eArmory Cabinet&r holds many unstackables like tools and armor; &eFramed&r drawers wear any block's look.",
    "",
    "Storage that hides in plain sight."
  ],
  "quest.7C70F44455221695.title": "Ender Storage for the Team",
  "quest.7C70F44455221695.quest_desc": [
    "&eEnder Storage&r chests, tanks and pouches share contents with every other set to the same three colors, in any dimension; dye the stripes to pick a frequency, and a diamond makes it private.",
    "",
    "They take a reinforced alloy (act III), in place of the ender pearl on chests and tanks. Until then, the vanilla ender chest is your personal cross-dimension storage."
  ],
  "quest.784E50C18918D17E.title": "When a Network Pays Off",
  "quest.784E50C18918D17E.quest_desc": [
    "Drawers and chests stop scaling when you spend more time looking for items than using them. That is the moment for a storage network: one terminal that searches everything, crafts on request and feeds machines.",
    "",
    "AE2 or Refined Storage, and when each opens: the Storage Networks chapter."
  ],
  "quest.799B566A885ECFC8.title": "Tip: Sort Once, Then Automate",
  "quest.799B566A885ECFC8.quest_desc": [
    "Drawers for the ten items you have thousands of, Sophisticated chests for everything else, a backpack with Deposit for the trip home, and a Void upgrade on cobblestone drawers so farms and quarries never stall.",
    "",
    "Future you finds everything on the first try."
  ],
  "quest.0C9552E3AC39EE25.title": "Pack Change: No Infinity",
  "quest.0C9552E3AC39EE25.quest_desc": [
    "The Sophisticated infinity upgrades and Functional Storage's Creative Vending Upgrade have no recipe here: they copy any item, which would break Solsticio's economy and the Luminosities. Everything else keeps its native recipe.",
    "",
    "Infinite is a big word. The pack prefers \"a lot\"."
  ],
  "chapter.2AEF3B16A131D400.title": "Teams and Claims",
  "chapter.2AEF3B16A131D400.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Play together with FTB Teams, protect your land with FTB Chunks, and know what the team shares."
  ],
  "quest.3C597B86B27930E7.title": "Solo First, Better Together",
  "quest.3C597B86B27930E7.quest_desc": [
    "Everything can be done alone. With friends, the campaign, the compass and the World Tier become shared, so you can split branches: one cooks, one builds machines, one explores.",
    "",
    "Someone always ends up doing the paperwork. Usually the one with the Atlas."
  ],
  "quest.58EAC9E8C5071663.title": "Create a Party",
  "quest.58EAC9E8C5071663.quest_desc": [
    "The &eMy Team&r button on the side of your inventory creates and names a party and invites online players, who accept from their own My Team screen or the chat message.",
    "",
    "Without a party you are still a team: a team of one."
  ],
  "quest.27E62163ED06BC7B.title": "What the Team Shares",
  "quest.27E62163ED06BC7B.quest_desc": [
    "Atlas projects, acts and milestones are shared and any member can deliver; the compass points everyone to the same objective; the World Tier follows the team's progress; and in Solsticio the team claims one plot.",
    "",
    "Items are not shared: each keeps their own inventory, and a reward goes to whoever delivered."
  ],
  "quest.68A95699EF8E40F9.title": "Joining and Leaving",
  "quest.68A95699EF8E40F9.quest_desc": [
    "Creating a party copies the founder's campaign once. Joining someone else's does not merge histories: you play theirs while your personal campaign waits, and leaving brings you back to it. When the last owner leaves, the party's campaign is archived; an operator can restore it with &e/entrelumen admin recover&r.",
    "",
    "Your World Tier never drops on the way out."
  ],
  "quest.28A8E9C9DECB15C7.title": "Allies",
  "quest.28A8E9C9DECB15C7.quest_desc": [
    "My Team can mark other teams as &eallies&r, who may interact with your claimed land as your settings allow, without joining your campaign.",
    "",
    "Alliances for the neighbors, parties for the people playing your story."
  ],
  "quest.7455FFA73D0FEC2E.title": "Claim Your Land",
  "quest.7455FFA73D0FEC2E.quest_desc": [
    "&eK&r opens the claim manager: &eleft-drag&r claims, &eright-drag&r unclaims, &eTab&r hides the grid and &eAlt&r shows when each claim was made. Claimed chunks keep other teams from breaking, placing or opening containers unless you allow it.",
    "",
    "Up to 500 chunks per player by default. Nobody needs 500. Somebody will try."
  ],
  "quest.0B2F97229BEF1DE1.title": "Keep Machines Running",
  "quest.0B2F97229BEF1DE1.quest_desc": [
    "In the claim manager, &eShift+left-drag&r force-loads claimed chunks so machines keep working while you are away, and &eShift+right-drag&r stops it; the mouse wheel sets when it expires. Default limit: 25 per player.",
    "",
    "Whether they stay loaded with nobody online is a server setting. Force-load only what needs it: every chunk costs server time."
  ],
  "quest.038A595B1B7200A4.title": "Team Protection Settings",
  "quest.038A595B1B7200A4.quest_desc": [
    "My Team also sets whether explosions and mobs can damage your land, who sees your claims on the map, and which fake players (machines that act as players, like Create deployers or block breakers) count as friends.",
    "",
    "If a machine suddenly refuses to work, check the fake player setting first."
  ],
  "quest.21F833844C0F26B6.title": "Quirk: Two Maps, One Visible",
  "quest.21F833844C0F26B6.quest_desc": [
    "FTB Chunks' minimap is off and its map key unbound, so JourneyMap is the map you see; FTB Chunks only handles teams and claims (&eK&r or the inventory side button).",
    "",
    "Prefer the FTB minimap? Your personal config file can turn it back on."
  ],
  "quest.79A1D0DB3C8F0B51.title": "Claims Stop Altars Too",
  "quest.79A1D0DB3C8F0B51.quest_desc": [
    "Land-shaping altars act as their owner, so another team's Altar of Renewal or Levelling skips your claimed chunks and charges nothing for them. The same goes for Ultimine and other tools wielded by outsiders.",
    "",
    "Good fences make good neighbors, even magical ones."
  ],
  "quest.27B135D314100B6A.title": "Tip: Split the Branches",
  "quest.27B135D314100B6A.quest_desc": [
    "Each act asks for several Atlas projects at once, each from a different discipline, so a team of three can take one each: engineering, nature and logistics in act III, for example.",
    "",
    "A delivery counts for the whole team the moment anyone makes it, so no need to pass items around first."
  ],
  "quest.47FFD44331256607.title": "Co-op Comforts",
  "quest.47FFD44331256607.quest_desc": [
    "&eChat Heads&r puts each player's face beside their messages, &eBetter Ping Display&r turns the Tab list bars into milliseconds, and &eNo Chat Reports&r strips signed-report data from server chat.",
    "",
    "None changes the game; they just make a shared server easier to read."
  ],
  "quest.20AD0D6306A80B83.title": "Quirk: Loot Is Per Player",
  "quest.20AD0D6306A80B83.quest_desc": [
    "&eLootr&r gives every player their own loot from dungeon and structure chests, so opening first steals nothing and exploring a ruin together is fine.",
    "",
    "A Lootr chest you already opened looks different from a fresh one."
  ],
  "quest.469B35F5128965CF.title": "Gifts Help, Progress Stays",
  "quest.469B35F5128965CF.quest_desc": [
    "Hand another team anything, even a finished prototype, and they can deliver it to their own Atlas. Progress cannot be gifted: arrivals, boss milestones and completed projects stay with the campaign that earned them.",
    "",
    "The Heart of Heliodor only counts for the team whose member took it from the Sun Spirit."
  ],
  "quest.1923090E6BED7E18.title": "Tip: a Team Frequency",
  "quest.1923090E6BED7E18.quest_desc": [
    "From act III, &eEnder Storage&r shares contents between every chest, tank and pouch with the same three colors, across dimensions. Pick a team code, keep a supply chest at home and give each explorer a pouch.",
    "",
    "How it works: the Storage chapter."
  ],
  "quest.17B1C1BCA708F7EB.title": "A Team With a Home",
  "quest.17B1C1BCA708F7EB.quest_desc": [
    "Party created, land claimed, machines loaded, allies set. From here, the story moves at the speed of the whole team.",
    "",
    "Which means at the speed of whoever is still sorting their inventory."
  ],
  "chapter.276D8209EDDD92FA.title": "Farming: Fields, Orchards and Pots",
  "chapter.276D8209EDDD92FA.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Farmer's Delight, Croptopia, Pam's, Herbs and Harvest, the Market, Botany Pots and the Altar of Growth."
  ],
  "quest.1462635FF1CBC36F.title": "A Garden Before a Factory",
  "quest.1462635FF1CBC36F.quest_desc": [
    "The pack rewards eating many different foods and wants you fed before the story sends you far away: first fields and orchards, then where the hundreds of crops come from, then pots and altars that farm for you.",
    "",
    "Juan, Heliodor's gardener, would approve."
  ],
  "quest.45F807AF9E04E1B8.title": "Farmer's Delight: the Knife",
  "quest.45F807AF9E04E1B8.quest_desc": [
    "Everything starts with a &eKnife&r: on grass, wheat or rice it collects &eStraw&r, on pigs or hoglins it takes ham, and with a &eCutting Board&r it breaks food down (knife in hand, use the board with the item on it).",
    "",
    "Wild cabbages, onions, tomatoes and rice grow in many climates; break them for seeds."
  ],
  "quest.725A3EF33D10C15D.title": "Tomatoes, Rice and Rope",
  "quest.725A3EF33D10C15D.quest_desc": [
    "&eRice&r goes in a shallow water puddle, and &etomatoes&r climb rope hung above them for more fruit per plant; cabbages and onions grow like any crop.",
    "",
    "Tomatoes on a rope: gardening's cheapest skyscraper."
  ],
  "quest.5A06C33CE079E461.title": "Compost and Rich Soil",
  "quest.5A06C33CE079E461.quest_desc": [
    "&eOrganic Compost&r slowly turns into &eRich Soil&r, faster with sunlight, water and mushrooms nearby. Crops grow better on it, and mushrooms planted there become &emushroom colonies&r you can shear again and again.",
    "",
    "Till rich soil for Rich Soil Farmland."
  ],
  "quest.49C3B2317618601A.title": "Hundreds of Crops",
  "quest.49C3B2317618601A.quest_desc": [
    "&eCroptopia&r, &ePam's HarvestCraft 2&r (crops, fruit trees and its food core) and &eMama's Herbs and Harvest&r (herbs, vegetables, dairy and fruit trees) fill the fields. Seeds come from grass and wild gardens, chests and the Market.",
    "",
    "Every new crop is another heart from Spice of Life, eventually."
  ],
  "quest.7804B242B4084A02.title": "Pack Change: One Tomato, Not Four",
  "quest.7804B242B4084A02.quest_desc": [
    "Almost Unified merges 69 crops that several mods add: a tomato, cabbage or lemon drops the same item whatever plant it came from, EMI hides the duplicates, and recipes asking by tag accept it. Priority: Farmer's Delight, then Croptopia, Pam's, and Herbs and Harvest with the Delights.",
    "",
    "One tomato. Finally."
  ],
  "quest.693F292BBFAA480B.title": "Orchards",
  "quest.693F292BBFAA480B.quest_desc": [
    "Pam's Trees and Herbs and Harvest grow wild fruit trees: apples, oranges, cherries, nuts, spices and more. Pick fruit from the leaves and plant saplings at home.",
    "",
    "Pam's crafts a new sapling from eight matching fruits and a sapling, so one tree is enough to start an orchard."
  ],
  "quest.50A6912B6169501B.title": "The Market",
  "quest.50A6912B6169501B.quest_desc": [
    "Place Farming for Blockheads' &eMarket&r and a Merchant comes to run it: emeralds for seeds, saplings and fertilizers, including the Pam's fruit saplings removed from world generation, one emerald each.",
    "",
    "Red &efertilizer&r speeds growth, green raises yield, yellow stops trampling; the &eChicken Nest&r collects eggs and the &eFeeding Trough&r feeds animals ready to breed."
  ],
  "quest.451F078A12EB81B7.title": "Quirk: Nine Trees at the Market",
  "quest.451F078A12EB81B7.quest_desc": [
    "Nine Pam's trees duplicated identical Herbs and Harvest ones (avocado, cherry, cinnamon, lemon, lime, orange, peach, pear and plum), so their Pam's versions no longer generate; buy those saplings at the Market if a recipe insists.",
    "",
    "Thanks to unification, the fruit is the same item either way."
  ],
  "quest.6C13A603F08403DE.title": "Tip: A Whole Field at Once",
  "quest.6C13A603F08403DE.quest_desc": [
    "Hold &eV&r with a hoe to till many blocks, and right-click ripe crops with V held to harvest many at once; even without V, right-clicking a ripe crop harvests it.",
    "",
    "Slice and Dice's &esprinklers&r water or fertilize an area when fed with fluid."
  ],
  "quest.5EDB0491D1D23CD9.title": "Botany Pots",
  "quest.5EDB0491D1D23CD9.quest_desc": [
    "A &eBotany Pot&r grows a crop or sapling without a field: add a soil and a seed and it grows by itself, and its tooltip shows the time and yield from pot, soil and tool. A &eHopper Botany Pot&r harvests into the container below.",
    "",
    "Not every seed fits: press U on it in EMI and look for a Botany Pots page. Botany Trees adds saplings for logs and fruit."
  ],
  "quest.74566BCAF79C084B.title": "Pack Change: Pot Tiers by Act",
  "quest.74566BCAF79C084B.quest_desc": [
    "Better pots cost the act's component, once per tier: the &eElite&r upgrade takes a Propagation Core (III), &eUltra&r an Ecosystem Capsule (IV), &eMega&r a Renewal Engine (V), and every pot of that tier asks for its upgrade. &eHopper&r pots are native. Upgrade items apply to a placed pot of the previous tier and keep its contents.",
    "",
    "Hold Shift over a tiered pot to see its speed and multiplier."
  ],
  "quest.39C08998A87DDC99.title": "The Altar of Growth",
  "quest.39C08998A87DDC99.quest_desc": [
    "Juan's own design and an act III reward: burning bone blocks, it makes crops in a 33 by 33 field grow about 20 times faster and ripe harvests drop double.",
    "",
    "The fine print lives in The Six Altars of Heliodor."
  ],
  "quest.3B1C954C178CDA25.title": "Tip: Animals and Breeding",
  "quest.3B1C954C178CDA25.quest_desc": [
    "Press U over a spawn egg or search the animal in EMI: Just Enough Breeding lists what each one eats to breed, Naturalist and Friends and Foes included.",
    "",
    "A Feeding Trough keeps a pen breeding while you are away."
  ],
  "quest.6B2BADEC75CCEE97.title": "Fields That Feed a Team",
  "quest.6B2BADEC75CCEE97.quest_desc": [
    "Crops from four mods under one name, orchards, a Market, pots that farm alone and, from act III, an altar that runs the field twenty times faster.",
    "",
    "Next stop for all those crops: the kitchen."
  ],
  "chapter.287BB28FDF815488.title": "The Kitchen",
  "chapter.287BB28FDF815488.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Pots, skillets and feasts, the Delights of other worlds, automated cooking with Create, and the pack's rations."
  ],
  "quest.471558A100D47290.title": "Cook Well, Travel Far",
  "quest.471558A100D47290.quest_desc": [
    "Good meals restore more, last longer and give effects, and here they count twice: variety grows your hearts, and food that overflows a full bar becomes short buffs.",
    "",
    "From the first pot to a kitchen that cooks itself, ending with the rations the story asks for."
  ],
  "quest.1B01756BFFD75E45.title": "The Cooking Pot",
  "quest.1B01756BFFD75E45.quest_desc": [
    "Set a &eCooking Pot&r over heat (a Stove, campfire, fire, magma, lava or a lava cauldron), add up to six ingredients and, for bowl meals, a bowl in the container slot. It cooks several servings at once and keeps them; the tooltip says how many.",
    "",
    "Its soups and stews are the backbone of the pack's rations."
  ],
  "quest.36BC5D4950D2E5E3.title": "First Pot: Vegetable Soup",
  "quest.36BC5D4950D2E5E3.quest_desc": [
    "A carrot, a potato, a beetroot and a leafy green like cabbage, served in a bowl. A solid meal and half of the pack's first Travel Rations.",
    "",
    "Press R on it in EMI to check the exact ingredients. Grandma's recipe, now with tags."
  ],
  "quest.0A07CF5E464A415B.title": "Skillet and Stove",
  "quest.0A07CF5E464A415B.quest_desc": [
    "The &eStove&r is a heat source that also cooks food placed on top, like a campfire. The &eSkillet&r cooks on the go: stand near heat with food in your other hand, or sneak to place it as a block.",
    "",
    "Both beat the vanilla furnace for food early on."
  ],
  "quest.2ACD7F355EDDAEF7.title": "Feasts",
  "quest.2ACD7F355EDDAEF7.quest_desc": [
    "Roast chicken, stuffed pumpkin, honey glazed ham and other big meals are placed down and shared: use the feast with a bowl to take a serving.",
    "",
    "Look for &eNourishment&r, which stops the hunger bar from dropping (except when healing with saturation), and &eComfort&r, natural regeneration however hungry you are."
  ],
  "quest.0819A2C4F788D8CE.title": "Pam's Tools and More Cuisines",
  "quest.0819A2C4F788D8CE.quest_desc": [
    "&ePam's HarvestCraft Food Core&r cooks about 180 foods with reusable tools crafted once: juicer, mixing bowl, pot, skillet, saucepan, bakeware, cutting board and grinder. &eHerbs and Harvest&r adds cheese, herbs and sandwiches, and &eSushi Go Crafting&r a sushi station with combined effects.",
    "",
    "Every new dish counts for Spice of Life."
  ],
  "quest.5D3BFA5AA36CAED1.title": "Delights of Other Worlds",
  "quest.5D3BFA5AA36CAED1.quest_desc": [
    "&eMy Nether's Delight&r, &eTwilight's Flavor and Delight&r, &eAether's Delight&r and &eEnd's Delight&r turn each world's creatures and plants into meals made with the same pot and knife.",
    "",
    "Pack a knife on every expedition: each dimension has new ingredients waiting."
  ],
  "quest.418EF78F1339E392.title": "Kitchen Furniture That Cooks",
  "quest.418EF78F1339E392.quest_desc": [
    "The &eCooking for Blockheads&r kitchen crafts any food from what its fridges and counters hold, and &eRefurbished Furniture&r brings stoves, ovens, freezers, grills and frying pans with their own recipes.",
    "",
    "Both are in the Furniture chapter."
  ],
  "quest.2F3A5C5C962B5820.title": "Create: Central Kitchen",
  "quest.2F3A5C5C962B5820.quest_desc": [
    "Once your Create workshop runs, mechanical arms and packagers can feed the real cooking pot, skillet, stove, cutting boards and feasts, and a &eblaze burner&r heats the pot.",
    "",
    "It works backwards too: Farmer's Delight heat sources warm Create's boilers."
  ],
  "quest.210B3C5DF997642D.title": "Slice and Dice",
  "quest.210B3C5DF997642D.quest_desc": [
    "The &eSlicer&r is a kinetic machine that runs cutting-board recipes with whatever tool you give it. The mod also adds &esprinklers&r that spread water, liquid fertilizer, potions or experience over an area, and the &eliquid fertilizer&r itself.",
    "",
    "Slicer plus belt: the onions chop themselves."
  ],
  "quest.494730E1B5502978.title": "Pack Change: Each Recipe Once",
  "quest.494730E1B5502978.quest_desc": [
    "Central Kitchen and Slice and Dice overlapped, so each job has one route: Central Kitchen automates pot recipes (Slice and Dice's basin cooking is off) and the Slicer does cutting boards (Central Kitchen's saw and deployer versions are off).",
    "",
    "Each recipe shows once in EMI; if one seems missing, it lives on the other machine."
  ],
  "quest.2FEA6E9F24C83087.title": "Rations for the Road",
  "quest.2FEA6E9F24C83087.quest_desc": [
    "&eTravel Rations&r are the pack's travel food and an act II delivery, from three recipes with the same drawing (bowls on the axis, dishes at the sides): two Vegetable Soups plus two cooked Aquaculture fish fillets, or plus two Pam's chicken dinners, or two Fish Stews plus two Herbs and Harvest beef cheddar sandwiches. The bowls come back.",
    "",
    "Later the Horizon Chart and the Ark's habitation want them too."
  ],
  "quest.408556EEDFCE671E.title": "The Habitation Charter",
  "quest.408556EEDFCE671E.quest_desc": [
    "In act V the Ark needs a place worth coming back to: the &eHabitation Charter&r takes two Fish Stews, two Mixed Salads, an AE2 Calculation Processor and two Travel Rations.",
    "",
    "A kitchen that cooks itself, fed by an AE2 network, makes it painless."
  ],
  "quest.39FBF2A2093CE2B9.title": "Tip: Variety Is Health",
  "quest.39FBF2A2093CE2B9.quest_desc": [
    "Spice of Life: Carrot Edition grants a heart at &e10, 25, 45, 70 and 100&r different foods, five in all, and death never takes them back.",
    "",
    "Try one new dish a day. How overflow becomes buffs: the Satiety chapter."
  ],
  "quest.5A58BB651213E0B6.title": "A Kitchen With a Plan",
  "quest.5A58BB651213E0B6.quest_desc": [
    "Pot, skillet, feasts, four worlds of Delights, an automated Create kitchen and the rations the story needs.",
    "",
    "Now eat more than you need, on purpose. The Satiety chapter explains why."
  ],
  "chapter.212218BAD3D67D30.title": "Resource Farming: Seeds, Bees and Fish",
  "chapter.212218BAD3D67D30.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Mystical Agriculture, Productive and Modular Bees, and Aquaculture: growing iron, catching treasure."
  ],
  "quest.0B5BD3D3F3ED95E0.title": "When Crops Become Ore",
  "quest.0B5BD3D3F3ED95E0.quest_desc": [
    "Mystical Agriculture grows seeds that yield metals, gems and mob drops, Productive Bees bring back resource combs, and Aquaculture fishes up metal, treasure and fillets. Slow to start, endless once running, and several act components come from them.",
    "",
    "Plant iron today, harvest ingots forever."
  ],
  "quest.252518C96A668BF4.title": "Inferium and Prosperity",
  "quest.252518C96A668BF4.quest_desc": [
    "&eInferium Essence&r drops from mobs, is mined from Inferium Ore (usually Y -32 to 64) and grows from Inferium Seeds; &eProsperity Shards&r come from Prosperity Ore (usually Y -60 to 24).",
    "",
    "The mod's craftable &eguide book&r explains every block."
  ],
  "quest.5805DD7AA45FBD28.title": "Essence Tiers",
  "quest.5805DD7AA45FBD28.quest_desc": [
    "&eInferium, prudentium, tertium, imperium, supremium&r: each step combines the lower essence with an &eInfusion Crystal&r, reused many times, and the Master Infusion Crystal never breaks.",
    "",
    "The story wants prudentium for the Propagation Core (act III) and imperium for the Renewal Engine (act V)."
  ],
  "quest.39DA614DB7567591.title": "The Infusion Altar",
  "quest.39DA614DB7567591.quest_desc": [
    "Resource seeds are made on an &eInfusion Altar&r ringed by eight &eInfusion Pedestals&r (placing the altar shows where): seed base on the altar, ingredients on the pedestals, then a redstone signal or a wand.",
    "",
    "EMI lists every seed's ingredients."
  ],
  "quest.726AFCFBD33EAACA.title": "Resource Crops",
  "quest.726AFCFBD33EAACA.quest_desc": [
    "Plant a resource seed, harvest its essence and craft that into the resource. Bone meal does nothing, but their occasional &eFertilized Essence&r works; a second seed only drops on &eEssence Farmland&r (right-click farmland with an essence), and farmland of the crop's own tier adds another chance.",
    "",
    "Inferium seeds yield more on higher tiers."
  ],
  "quest.375DF0A306B9F117.title": "Speeding Up Mystical Crops",
  "quest.375DF0A306B9F117.quest_desc": [
    "&eGrowth Accelerators&r under the farmland give random growth ticks and stack, &eWatering Cans&r speed crops by hand, and &eMystical Fertilizer&r grows them instantly.",
    "",
    "The Altar of Growth speeds them up too, but never multiplies essence."
  ],
  "quest.6C7A05FE816F93CF.title": "Pack Change: No Essence Shortcuts",
  "quest.6C7A05FE816F93CF.quest_desc": [
    "The Altar of Growth speeds Mystical crops without touching their drops, and Mekanism More Machine's planting recipes for Mystical seeds are removed.",
    "",
    "Essence stays a real farm, which keeps the act components that use it meaningful."
  ],
  "quest.02AF0E7EC2CF26A4.title": "Productive Bees: First Hive",
  "quest.02AF0E7EC2CF26A4.quest_desc": [
    "Find a bee nest, carry bees home in &eBee Cages&r (made with honey bottles) and build an &eAdvanced Beehive&r: you can look inside, take out what they make and move it with the bees still in. New species hide in nests across biomes and dimensions, or come from breeding.",
    "",
    "The mod's guide book is craftable."
  ],
  "quest.6350E535E200243F.title": "Combs Into Resources",
  "quest.6350E535E200243F.quest_desc": [
    "Resource bees bring &ecombs&r; a &eCentrifuge&r splits them into resources, wax and honey (pushed into a tank beside it), and the &ePowered Centrifuge&r uses FE to go faster. An &eExpansion Box&r raises a hive from 3 to 5 bees and allows upgrades.",
    "",
    "The wax goes into the Propagation Core (act III) and the Ecosystem Capsule (act IV)."
  ],
  "quest.3152454A3DAF1728.title": "Breeding and Genes",
  "quest.3152454A3DAF1728.quest_desc": [
    "New species come from breeding two bees with their favorite items, by hand or in a powered &eBreeding Chamber&r, and a &eCatcher&r with cages collects bees flying over it.",
    "",
    "Traits cover productivity, weather tolerance and day or night activity; genes can be extracted and given to another bee with a honey treat."
  ],
  "quest.0EC40D1C07824671.title": "Tip: Hurry a Bee",
  "quest.0EC40D1C07824671.quest_desc": [
    "Whack a hive or nest with a stick to force the bees out, losing their current progress; it only works when it is safe for them to leave.",
    "",
    "Bees hide from rain. Leash them outside in bad weather and some become weather tolerant, at a risk."
  ],
  "quest.1DE5554E846A0B84.title": "Modular Bees: Big Apiaries",
  "quest.1DE5554E846A0B84.quest_desc": [
    "Multiblock hives and centrifuges built from parts (core, casing, feeders, stackers, overclockers, heaters), with ME blocks for AE2. Here the modular hive core takes two ironwood ingots (act IV); parts, ME blocks, overclockers, the stacker and the dragon hive keep their native recipes, since none works without a core.",
    "",
    "Beekeeping, late-game edition."
  ],
  "quest.25D22601D4E688AC.title": "Aquaculture: Better Fishing",
  "quest.25D22601D4E688AC.quest_desc": [
    "Dozens of biome fish, better rods (iron, gold, diamond, neptunium), hooks, bait like worms, lines and bobbers, a &eTackle Box&r for gear and a &eFillet Knife&r for fillets.",
    "",
    "It also fishes up treasure: &eNeptune's Bounty&r chests hold neptunium, a metal for underwater gear."
  ],
  "quest.3D392448BE3407E3.title": "Neptunium Gear",
  "quest.3D392448BE3407E3.quest_desc": [
    "Built for underwater: the rod gets faster bites, the helmet clearer vision, the chestplate breath, the leggings weightlessness and the boots speed; the pickaxe and shovel lose no speed underwater, and the hoe keeps farmland moist.",
    "",
    "Ocean monuments will not know what hit them."
  ],
  "quest.3DFCD4210E1E9F9A.title": "Fillets for the Story",
  "quest.3DFCD4210E1E9F9A.quest_desc": [
    "Two vegetable soups and two cooked Aquaculture fillets make the first &eTravel Rations&r, the travel food the Atlas asks for in act II.",
    "",
    "A &eWorm Farm&r keeps the bait coming."
  ],
  "quest.3D28CDAE58037BFE.title": "Endless Supplies",
  "quest.3D28CDAE58037BFE.quest_desc": [
    "Essence climbing from inferium to supremium, bees bringing resources home and a fishing line that pays in treasure, all producing while you explore.",
    "",
    "Somewhere, a bee is making you iron right now."
  ],
  "chapter.5F5C5CDA9C2B7B1E.title": "Storage Networks: AE2 or Refined Storage",
  "chapter.5F5C5CDA9C2B7B1E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "One terminal for everything you own: how the two networks differ, where the pack gates them, and how to start."
  ],
  "quest.20934DE77061EA1E.title": "A Terminal That Knows Everything",
  "quest.20934DE77061EA1E.quest_desc": [
    "A storage network turns items into data: insert once, then search, count, pull and autocraft from one terminal. The pack offers &eApplied Energistics 2&r and &eRefined Storage&r side by side, both complete; pick one per base.",
    "",
    "The tech guides go deeper into autocrafting."
  ],
  "quest.40255AEA7E3FBC84.title": "AE2 or RS?",
  "quest.40255AEA7E3FBC84.quest_desc": [
    "&eAE2&r is deeper and more rewarding: cables carry limited &echannels&r (8 per normal cable, 32 per dense), so layout matters, and the pack has lots of add-ons for it. &eRefined Storage&r is simpler: no channels, just connect and power, faster to set up.",
    "",
    "Both store items, fluids and, with Mekanism add-ons, chemicals, and both craft on request."
  ],
  "quest.4D7E5DE146382857.title": "Pack Change: When Each Opens",
  "quest.4D7E5DE146382857.quest_desc": [
    "Both networks enter in act III: the Refined Storage &eController&r takes a &eRouting Matrix&r and its &eAutocrafter&r a &eHandling Core&r, while AE2 needs its inscriber's &eLogic Processors&r, the same ones the Routing Matrix is made from.",
    "",
    "The AE2 controller carries a Routing Matrix too, but a small AE2 network without a controller can start a little earlier."
  ],
  "quest.0D69E2FB61D264F7.title": "AE2 Step 1: a Meteorite",
  "quest.0D69E2FB61D264F7.quest_desc": [
    "AE2 starts in a crater: meteorites hold a &eMysterious Cube&r with the four &einscriber presses&r (calculation, engineering, logic, silicon) and sky stone. Presses plus an &eInscriber&r print processors.",
    "",
    "Certus quartz grows from budding certus; charge it in a &eCharger&r and drop it with redstone and nether quartz in water for fluix."
  ],
  "quest.793454F581FA5AB2.title": "AE2 Step 2: a First Network",
  "quest.793454F581FA5AB2.quest_desc": [
    "An &eME Drive&r with a &e1k storage cell&r, a &eterminal&r and power from an energy acceptor or a controller. Without a controller the network handles up to 8 channel devices; with a &eController&r and cables it grows far beyond.",
    "",
    "Your first terminal is the moment the chests start feeling old."
  ],
  "quest.26E80B5A5FA63E3D.title": "Tip: AE2 Has Its Own Guide",
  "quest.26E80B5A5FA63E3D.quest_desc": [
    "AE2 ships an in-game guide with pictures and 3D scenes of every block: craft the &eGuide&r, or bind &eOpen Guide for Items&r in Controls to jump from any AE2 item to its page.",
    "",
    "Read it once; it saves ten forum threads."
  ],
  "quest.5BE6F260A3E327EA.title": "AE2 Add-ons in the Pack",
  "quest.5BE6F260A3E327EA.quest_desc": [
    "&eMEGA Cells&r (much bigger cells), &eExtendedAE&r and &eAdvancedAE&r (better providers, interfaces and crafting), &eApplied Mekanistics&r (chemicals), &eAE2WTLib&r (a wireless universal terminal), &eME Requester&r (keeps chosen items in stock), &eAE2 Network Analyzer&r (see channels and cables) and &eArsEng&r (Ars Nouveau source on the network)."
  ],
  "quest.48E6E7A9BC97530B.title": "RS: a First Network",
  "quest.48E6E7A9BC97530B.quest_desc": [
    "A powered &eController&r, a &eDisk Drive&r with a storage disk and a &eGrid&r or &eCrafting Grid&r, joined by cables or touching. No channels: add as many devices as you like.",
    "",
    "The controller takes a Routing Matrix here, so RS starts in act III."
  ],
  "quest.7F33B19BDC69D950.title": "RS: Growing the Network",
  "quest.7F33B19BDC69D950.quest_desc": [
    "&eImporter&r and &eExporter&r move items in and out of machines, &eConstructor&r and &eDestructor&r place and break blocks, the &eDetector&r emits redstone by amount, a &eWireless Transmitter&r serves a wireless grid, &eNetwork Transmitter&r and &eReceiver&r link distant parts, and the &eAutocrafter&r runs &ePattern Grid&r patterns.",
    "",
    "RS Mekanism Integration adds chemicals."
  ],
  "quest.7E760A5EA79B9C7C.title": "Keep Your Drawers",
  "quest.7E760A5EA79B9C7C.quest_desc": [
    "No need to empty your chests: AE2's &eStorage Bus&r and RS's &eExternal Storage&r read any inventory they face, drawers and storage controllers included, and the terminal shows those items too.",
    "",
    "The drawer wall joins the network without moving a single cobblestone."
  ],
  "quest.3C697DA1AB61BAA2.title": "Autocrafting in One Paragraph",
  "quest.3C697DA1AB61BAA2.quest_desc": [
    "Encode a recipe into a &epattern&r, give the network somewhere to run it (an AE2 pattern provider with a molecular assembler or a machine, or an RS autocrafter) plus a crafting CPU in AE2, then ask the terminal for 64 of anything: it crafts the intermediate steps too.",
    "",
    "Act components are ordinary shaped recipes, so they autocraft like anything else."
  ],
  "quest.2A2C0CF0B5664397.title": "Quirk: Both Can Coexist",
  "quest.2A2C0CF0B5664397.quest_desc": [
    "AE2 in one base and Refined Storage in another is fine, but they do not share storage directly: bridge them through an inventory both can read, like a drawer or chest.",
    "",
    "For one team, one network is almost always easier."
  ],
  "quest.574E671F47BF610A.title": "Tip: Channels Without Tears",
  "quest.574E671F47BF610A.quest_desc": [
    "Each AE2 device uses one channel; normal cables carry 8, dense ones 32, and each controller face feeds 32. Run dense cable as the backbone and branch with normal cable.",
    "",
    "A powered device that stops working probably ran out of channels. The Network Analyzer shows where."
  ],
  "quest.1AE56B10894D452F.title": "The Network Feeds the Story",
  "quest.1AE56B10894D452F.quest_desc": [
    "Several act components are made from network parts: the Routing Matrix from logic processors and a circuit board, the Habitation Charter from a calculation processor, the Inventory Sensor from LaserIO logic chips.",
    "",
    "A network that autocrafts processors makes acts III and V much lighter."
  ],
  "quest.1EE0CB511BEDE3D0.title": "Everything in One Place",
  "quest.1EE0CB511BEDE3D0.quest_desc": [
    "With a network, the whole base is one searchable inventory, and logistics becomes feeding machines instead of finding items.",
    "",
    "You will never again lose a stack of iron in chest number forty."
  ],
  "chapter.04F18C84B664FCFB.title": "Energy in ENTRELUMEN",
  "chapter.04F18C84B664FCFB.chapter_subtitle": [
    "One currency, many names: first generators, units, bridges to rotation and pressure, storage, cables and act gates."
  ],
  "quest.65BC69F4A047247E.title": "FE: one currency",
  "quest.65BC69F4A047247E.quest_desc": [
    "Almost every tech mod runs on Forge Energy (FE), sometimes under another name: RF in Oritech and Industrial Foregoing, OP in Draconic, µI in Ender IO. Any of them powers the others with a plain cable.",
    "",
    "The odd ones out: Mekanism (Joules inside), AE2 (AE), Modern Industrialization (EU), Create (rotation) and PneumaticCraft (pressure)."
  ],
  "quest.06BFA19A5271724A.title": "Free first power",
  "quest.06BFA19A5271724A.quest_desc": [
    "Early generators need no campaign component, on purpose: the Actually Additions and RFTools Coal Generators, the Powah Furnator, the Just Dire Things coal generator, and an Immersive Engineering water wheel or windmill on a Kinetic Dynamo. Throw coal in and your first machines hum."
  ],
  "quest.3ECC537E1727CCDF.title": "Units that convert",
  "quest.3ECC537E1727CCDF.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism counts Joules inside (1 FE = 2.5 J) but shows FE by default. AE2 turns FE into AE one way: 2 FE per AE, via an Energy Acceptor or the controller. MI's EU is worth 10 FE here and converts one way only, so keep MI power inside MI."
  ],
  "quest.01B1492E9A898747.title": "Rotation to FE and back",
  "quest.01B1492E9A898747.quest_desc": [
    "The Crafts and Additions Alternator makes FE from 32 RPM or more; its Electric Motor spins at the speed you set, paid in FE. Create: New Age makes power with Generator Coils ringed by magnets. Pack note: New Age's carbon brushes take an Energy Coupler (Act II)."
  ],
  "quest.521A75B666C9FA3D.title": "Pressure and FE",
  "quest.521A75B666C9FA3D.quest_desc": [
    "PneumaticCraft's Flux Compressor turns FE into air pressure; the Pneumatic Dynamo turns pressure back into FE. Both run hot: give them cooling or they slow down."
  ],
  "quest.36FC798DD6C0C68E.title": "Mid-game generators",
  "quest.36FC798DD6C0C68E.quest_desc": [
    "Pick one that eats something you already farm: Mekanism's Heat, Solar, Wind, Bio or Gas-Burning generators, Powah's Magmator, IF's Biofuel Generator (160 RF/t), Oritech's basic generator (32 RF/t), Ender IO's Stirling, IE's diesel generator."
  ],
  "quest.1D7A85CD9B7D2262.title": "Big power",
  "quest.1D7A85CD9B7D2262.quest_desc": [
    "Late-game plants, each with its own chapter: Oritech's Steam Engine (up to 50,000 RF/t), Mekanism fission with a turbine and later fusion, the Powah Reactor, MI's large boilers and turbines, and the Draconic Reactor for the brave."
  ],
  "quest.572C910CE861DAF6.title": "Storing energy",
  "quest.572C910CE861DAF6.quest_desc": [
    "A buffer between generators and machines smooths every spike: Mekanism Energy Cubes and the Induction Matrix, Powah Energy Cells, RFTools Powercells, Flux Storage, and Draconic's Energy Core at the top. AE2 keeps its own Energy Cells."
  ],
  "quest.12AE0449F841ECD7.title": "Moving energy",
  "quest.12AE0449F841ECD7.quest_desc": [
    "Cables: Mekanism Universal Cables, Pipez Energy Pipes, Powah cables, Ender IO conduits, IE wires. No cables: Flux Networks (even across dimensions), LaserIO energy cards (up to 1,000,000 FE/t), XNet channels, the JDT Energy Transmitter."
  ],
  "quest.4C9F577BAA9D57ED.title": "Energy Meter",
  "quest.4C9F577BAA9D57ED.quest_desc": [
    "Drop it into a cable line to read the flow, instant or smoothed. It can also cap the flow, and computers can read it. The fastest bottleneck hunter in the pack."
  ],
  "quest.2C79BDE68081E6D8.title": "Charging your gear",
  "quest.2C79BDE68081E6D8.quest_desc": [
    "Stand on a Mekanism Chargepad to charge any mod's FE items. The Powah Player Transmitter charges your whole inventory wirelessly through a Binding Card (the dimensional card works anywhere), and a Flux Controller charges its network members."
  ],
  "quest.65B736FBC35BD88E.title": "Energy and the acts",
  "quest.65B736FBC35BD88E.quest_desc": [
    "The Power Regulator (Act III: two Mekanism basic circuits, two steel plates and an Energy Coupler) gates Mekanism's jetpack, Psi's CAD Assembler and the aircraft engine; Flux plugs, dimensional cells, jetpack straps and mining gadgets take a reinforced alloy instead. Generators are never gated."
  ],
  "quest.1D421CED31F05B4F.title": "Quirks worth knowing",
  "quest.1D421CED31F05B4F.quest_desc": [
    "An AE2 network only spends what it has stored per tick: add an Energy Cell before big imports. Oritech power is push-only, so generators must push into pipes. IE wires carry one voltage each; put transformers between LV, MV and HV."
  ],
  "quest.2FB875EDE69CD455.title": "Creative power",
  "quest.2FB875EDE69CD455.quest_desc": [
    "Infinite energy waits at the very end: Mekanism's Creative Energy Cube, Powah's Creative Cell, Create's Creative Motor, AE2's Creative Energy Cell and Draconic's Creative Capacitor each cost two Luminosities (Act VI)."
  ],
  "quest.0E7550D2B4347BBB.title": "Mastery: a power plant",
  "quest.0E7550D2B4347BBB.quest_desc": [
    "One big plant, one big buffer, one wireless link to every corner of the base and to outposts in other dimensions. An Energy Meter on the main line, always in the green."
  ],
  "chapter.7E2F499D96852FED.title": "Ore processing",
  "chapter.7E2F499D96852FED.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Fortune or Silk Touch, and which machine turns one ore into the most ingots, with real numbers for iron."
  ],
  "quest.14B80E1A7F7061F7.title": "Ore, raw or block?",
  "quest.14B80E1A7F7061F7.quest_desc": [
    "Fortune gives raw ore (Fortune III: 2.2 raw iron or gold per ore on average). Silk Touch gives the ore block. Every machine pays differently for each, so pick your pickaxe by the machine you will feed. All numbers here are for iron."
  ],
  "quest.7AD07B9921AA3CD8.title": "Create: crush and wash",
  "quest.7AD07B9921AA3CD8.quest_desc": [
    "Crushing Wheels turn raw iron into 1 Crushed Raw Iron (plus a 75% chance of an XP nugget). Smelt it for 1 ingot, or wash it with a fan for 9 nuggets and a 75% chance of redstone. Silk-touched blocks crush a bit better: 1.75 per stone ore, 2.25 per deepslate ore."
  ],
  "quest.23019D0A97A8F00C.title": "Immersive Engineering",
  "quest.23019D0A97A8F00C.quest_desc": [
    "The Crusher makes 2 dusts per ore block but only 1.33 per raw ore. The Arc Furnace smelts an ore block into 2 ingots plus slag, and a raw ore into 1.5 ingots on average: with Fortune that is 3.3 ingots per ore, no dust step."
  ],
  "quest.2A4733EA6E7036DA.title": "Modern Industrialization: Silk Touch wins",
  "quest.2A4733EA6E7036DA.quest_desc": [
    "The Macerator turns an ore block into 3 raw ores, and each raw into 1.5 dust on average. Silk Touch: 4.5 dust per ore. Fortune: 3.3. The steam Forge Hammer gives 2 raw per ore, 3 with a Hammer tool in its slot."
  ],
  "quest.0BDE2EBD8D54FEFD.title": "Ender IO SAG Mill",
  "quest.0BDE2EBD8D54FEFD.quest_desc": [
    "A raw ore gives 1.8 powder on average (Fortune: about 4 per ore), while an ore block only gives 1.33 raw. Grinding Balls in the mill add bonus output and speed. Keep Fortune for this one."
  ],
  "quest.2B97086271E1EA71.title": "Actually Additions Crusher",
  "quest.2B97086271E1EA71.quest_desc": [
    "An early electric option: an iron ore block becomes 2 raw iron with a 20% chance of raw gold. Fine before Fortune III, then outgrown."
  ],
  "quest.2FC8BA3D26A234E5.title": "Mekanism: 2 to 5 per ore",
  "quest.2FC8BA3D26A234E5.quest_desc": [
    "Per ore block Mekanism gives 2, 3, 4 or 5 ingots by tier; per raw ore about 1.33, 2, 2.67 or 3.33. With Fortune III that is roughly 2.9, 4.4, 5.9 or 7.3 per ore: raw wins at every tier. The details live in the Mekanism ore chapter."
  ],
  "quest.61418A5DA4757B2D.title": "Oritech: the gem route",
  "quest.61418A5DA4757B2D.quest_desc": [
    "The Fragment Forge turns a raw ore into 1.33 clumps. The Centrifuge makes 1 gem per clump dry, 2 with water, 3 with sulfuric acid, and the Foundry turns 2 gems into 3 ingots. Top of the line: about 6 ingots per raw iron, the richest route in the pack."
  ],
  "quest.3BE1CBEF0802DB1C.title": "Cheat sheet",
  "quest.3BE1CBEF0802DB1C.quest_desc": [
    "Ingots per iron ore, Fortune III raw vs Silk Touch block: furnace 2.2 vs 1; Create 2.2 vs 1.75-2.25; IE Arc Furnace 3.3 vs 2; MI Macerator 3.3 vs 4.5; Ender IO about 4 vs 2.4; Mekanism x5 7.3 vs 5; Oritech with acid about 13 vs 12."
  ],
  "quest.714000127752F16B.title": "Byproducts",
  "quest.714000127752F16B.quest_desc": [
    "Processing pays extras: Create washing gives redstone from iron, quartz from gold, clay from copper; the IE Crusher sometimes drops nickel dust from iron; Oritech iron yields nickel, and nickel fragmenting is an early platinum source; the AA Crusher gives raw gold from iron."
  ],
  "quest.23F039D6DBAAD79F.title": "One ingot per metal",
  "quest.23F039D6DBAAD79F.quest_desc": [
    "Almost Unified makes every machine output the same ingot, dust or plate for each metal, preferring vanilla, then Create, IE, Mekanism, Oritech, Ender IO, Ad Astra and MI. JEI hides the duplicates. Loot is not unified, but all copies share tags, so they still work in recipes."
  ],
  "quest.4E3B021E19511C86.title": "Uraninite: energize the ore",
  "quest.4E3B021E19511C86.quest_desc": [
    "Powah’s Energizing Orb turns a silk-touched uraninite ore into 5 uraninite (dense 10, poor 3). Mined normally, the ore drops 2 raw, about 4.4 with Fortune III, one uraninite each. Energizing wins, by a nose."
  ],
  "quest.3B78D5C6732777EF.title": "Mining dimensions",
  "quest.3B78D5C6732777EF.quest_desc": [
    "JAMD portals open throwaway mining worlds so your home stays intact. Pack gates: the Overworld mine needs a Calibration Frame (Act II), the Nether mine a Containment Seal (Act IV), the End mine a Horizon Chart (Act IV)."
  ],
  "quest.41E9F3FDC372449C.title": "Quarries and their gates",
  "quest.41E9F3FDC372449C.quest_desc": [
    "Automated mining comes later: Mekanism's Digital Miner needs a Spectral Lens (Act IV); MI's Electric Quarry, IF's Ore Laser Drill, Oritech's Bedrock Extractor, the RFTools quarry card and Occultism's mineshaft need ironwood (Act IV); the Mining Gadgets a reinforced alloy (Act III)."
  ],
  "quest.1756B7A4FD944A67.title": "Mastery: never smelt raw ore again",
  "quest.1756B7A4FD944A67.quest_desc": [
    "Pick your top route, automate it end to end and feed it with Fortune-mined raw ore (or silk-touched blocks for MI). A chest of raw iron should come out as a small mountain of ingots."
  ],
  "chapter.1EC8C85A19A48FCD.title": "Automation basics",
  "chapter.1EC8C85A19A48FCD.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Hoppers, pipes, machine sides, filters, redstone, buffers and crafting: the habits every factory needs."
  ],
  "quest.19AA52C75FC8F28F.title": "The automation loop",
  "quest.19AA52C75FC8F28F.quest_desc": [
    "Every factory is the same loop: input, machine, output, storage. Build one line, watch it run for a minute, then copy it. If something stops, follow the items: they always pile up right before the problem."
  ],
  "quest.7DABF9C654292148.title": "Hoppers",
  "quest.7DABF9C654292148.quest_desc": [
    "A hopper moves one item every 8 ticks (2.5 per second) into whatever it points at. Chest, hopper, furnace, hopper, chest: your first automatic smelter. A comparator next to a container reads how full it is."
  ],
  "quest.23768FBE28F5B3EA.title": "Pipes that pull",
  "quest.23768FBE28F5B3EA.quest_desc": [
    "Pipez pipes connect to anything, but only pull where you say: click the end touching the source with the Pipe Wrench to make it extract; sneak-click cuts a connection. The extract menu sets distribution, redstone mode and filters."
  ],
  "quest.7B4B6BFE3D5FA17A.title": "Fluids",
  "quest.7B4B6BFE3D5FA17A.quest_desc": [
    "Pipez Fluid Pipes and Mekanism Mechanical Pipes move fluids like items, wrench and all. Create pipes need a Mechanical Pump; its arrow shows the flow. The Ranged Pumps Pump drains a whole lake with FE, scanning outwards block by block."
  ],
  "quest.05B443D66D43BA72.title": "Machine sides",
  "quest.05B443D66D43BA72.quest_desc": [
    "Most tech machines choose what goes in and out by side. In Mekanism, open the side tab or right-click with the Configurator, and turn on auto-eject so output pushes itself into the next pipe. Other mods have the same idea in their I/O tabs."
  ],
  "quest.718B726433BB5A90.title": "Belts, funnels and arms",
  "quest.718B726433BB5A90.quest_desc": [
    "In Create, belts carry items, funnels put them on and take them off, and depots hold one stack for a machine to work on. The brass Mechanical Arm picks from and drops into many targets around it, no belts needed."
  ],
  "quest.20067837AD551995.title": "Filters everywhere",
  "quest.20067837AD551995.quest_desc": [
    "Almost every mover takes a filter: Create funnels and arms, Pipez extract menus (item IDs or #tags), LaserIO filter cards, Modular Routers module slots, the Mekanism Logistical Sorter. Filter at the source and the rest of the line stays clean."
  ],
  "quest.53E12EA132885122.title": "Redstone control",
  "quest.53E12EA132885122.quest_desc": [
    "Run machines only when needed: most have a redstone mode (ignored, on or off when powered). A comparator on a chest turns fill level into a signal, Functional Storage drawers do the same with a Redstone Upgrade, and Utilitarian's Redstone Clock pulses at a rate you set by right-clicking it."
  ],
  "quest.7F0C46AC3082F194.title": "Buffers and overflow",
  "quest.7F0C46AC3082F194.quest_desc": [
    "Put a chest or drawer between machines so a slow step never stalls the fast one. Then decide what happens when storage fills: a Void Upgrade on a drawer or a Trash Can at the end of the line deletes the excess instead of jamming everything."
  ],
  "quest.5268F4017AEE3BBA.title": "Automatic crafting",
  "quest.5268F4017AEE3BBA.quest_desc": [
    "Pick by what you already run: Create Mechanical Crafters for big shaped recipes, the RFTools Crafter (up to 8 recipes in one block), MI's Assembler, or AE2 and Refined Storage patterns once you have a network."
  ],
  "quest.63F545CBDE937710.title": "Farms that feed the line",
  "quest.63F545CBDE937710.quest_desc": [
    "A farm is automation with a field attached: Industrial Foregoing's Plant Sower and Plant Gatherer, Create harvesters on a moving contraption, Mekanism or Powah generators fed by what grows. Always collect the drops: items on the ground are lag."
  ],
  "quest.3944A93667D89759.title": "When lines become a network",
  "quest.3944A93667D89759.quest_desc": [
    "With many lines, a storage network pays off: AE2 or Refined Storage import and export buses feed machines straight from storage, and autocrafting orders the rest. LaserIO and XNet do the same between machines without a central storage."
  ],
  "quest.1E354FE92CDDB0C1.title": "Keep the server happy",
  "quest.1E354FE92CDDB0C1.quest_desc": [
    "Fewer entities, fewer ticks: collect drops, prefer bigger stacks per operation over faster ticking (Modular Routers says it outright), and let idle machines sleep on redstone. Utilitarian's TPS Meter outputs redstone by the dimension's TPS, so a line can pause itself when the server struggles."
  ],
  "quest.65263D529EBC60BC.title": "Machines sleep when nobody is near",
  "quest.65263D529EBC60BC.quest_desc": [
    "Blocks only work in loaded chunks. Claim your base and force-load the machine chunks with FTB Chunks (see the teams chapter), and keep the count small: every loaded chunk costs the server."
  ],
  "quest.4B1C0C1C336CA7BB.title": "Mastery: a line that runs while you sleep",
  "quest.4B1C0C1C336CA7BB.quest_desc": [
    "Raw materials in, finished goods out, overflow handled, no hands. Leave it for a night in-game and come back to full chests and an empty trash log."
  ],
  "chapter.469268F72FFDBD79.title": "Create: rotation and processing",
  "chapter.469268F72FFDBD79.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Shafts, cogs, water wheels and your first machines. In Create, everything runs on rotation."
  ],
  "quest.45837D50D13D7307.title": "Rotation does the work",
  "quest.45837D50D13D7307.quest_desc": [
    "A source makes rotation, shafts and cogs carry it, machines spend it to press, mix, grind and move. No electricity needed.",
    "",
    "Several act components are built from Create sheets, alloy and precision mechanisms, so this workshop pays off early."
  ],
  "quest.2BAB95C4EE0C4C28.title": "Ponder: the built-in manual",
  "quest.2BAB95C4EE0C4C28.quest_desc": [
    "Hover any Create block and hold W (Ponder): an animated scene shows exactly how it works. New Age, Crafts and Additions, Connected and Enchantment Industry have scenes too. When in doubt, Ponder it."
  ],
  "quest.36D2DD9AC13B9B6B.title": "Andesite Alloy",
  "quest.36D2DD9AC13B9B6B.quest_desc": [
    "Andesite and iron (or zinc) nuggets in a 2x2 checkerboard: two of each give one alloy. Later a Mixer makes it from one of each. Shafts, casings, belts and half the early machines start here, so keep a stack handy."
  ],
  "quest.0DFA49B47F44AFC1.title": "Shafts and Cogwheels",
  "quest.0DFA49B47F44AFC1.quest_desc": [
    "Two alloys give 8 Shafts; a shaft and a plank give a Cogwheel. Shafts carry rotation straight; cogwheels pass it to touching cogs, each spinning the opposite way. Machine running backwards? Add or remove one cog."
  ],
  "quest.292FAA46D06198DB.title": "Changing speed",
  "quest.292FAA46D06198DB.quest_desc": [
    "A Large Cogwheel meshes diagonally with a small one: large to small doubles the speed, small to large halves it. Two large ones at a right angle change the axis. Faster machines also eat more stress, so speed up only what needs it."
  ],
  "quest.192801180FAC4131.title": "Gearbox",
  "quest.192801180FAC4131.quest_desc": [
    "Four cogwheels around an Andesite Casing: one block that turns rotation around corners. Side outputs are mirrored; the straight-through side is reversed. Cleaner than a cog spaghetti."
  ],
  "quest.7B2185253A34244F.title": "Water Wheel",
  "quest.7B2185253A34244F.quest_desc": [
    "Eight planks around a shaft. It spins from water flowing past it; more water on more sides adds nothing. A river, a waterfall or a short stream does it. Free, steady early power, and any plank re-skins it."
  ],
  "quest.2EAA71F49CB4FDAC.title": "Large Water Wheel",
  "quest.2EAA71F49CB4FDAC.quest_desc": [
    "Planks around a Water Wheel make the large one: half the speed, much more stress capacity. A large-to-small cog step gets the speed back."
  ],
  "quest.3FBE996BD4292871.title": "Windmill",
  "quest.3FBE996BD4292871.quest_desc": [
    "A Windmill Bearing spins a glued structure with at least 8 sail blocks (Sails and Sail Frames stick without glue). Right-click to start or stop; more sails, more speed. The answer where there is no water."
  ],
  "quest.774F011ABDD83F74.title": "Stress: the real limit",
  "quest.774F011ABDD83F74.quest_desc": [
    "Sources add stress capacity (su); machines spend it, more the faster they spin. Ask for more than you have and the whole network stops. Fix: more sources or slower machines, and split big factories into separate networks."
  ],
  "quest.197D3E006CBF3A20.title": "Goggles and Wrench",
  "quest.197D3E006CBF3A20.quest_desc": [
    "With the Engineer's Goggles on, machines show their stress use and a Stressometer shows the whole network. The Wrench rotates parts; sneak-use it to pick them up intact. Put the Goggles on and forget them there."
  ],
  "quest.32437B2EDDAA6C80.title": "Andesite Casing",
  "quest.32437B2EDDAA6C80.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click stripped logs or wood with Andesite Alloy (a Deployer can do it later). Press, mixer, fan, millstone, drill, saw, bearing and gearbox all wear this casing."
  ],
  "quest.52292575E3352219.title": "Mechanical Press",
  "quest.52292575E3352219.quest_desc": [
    "It presses whatever sits below: items on the ground, a Depot or a moving belt. Ingots become sheets. Over a Basin it compacts 2x2 and 3x3 recipes instead. Sheets are everywhere, including the Act II Calibration Frame."
  ],
  "quest.4332260A46E3D7D2.title": "Create in the act components",
  "quest.4332260A46E3D7D2.quest_desc": [
    "Calibration Frame (Act II): infused from a Raw Lens, whose copper you can press here. Energy Coupler (II): 2 andesite alloys. Handling Core (III) and Spectral Lens (IV): a precision mechanism each. No Create part is gated, so you can never get locked out."
  ],
  "quest.14D03D7EA54ADFD0.title": "Basin and Mixer",
  "quest.14D03D7EA54ADFD0.quest_desc": [
    "A Mechanical Mixer over a Basin automates shapeless recipes and Create mixing (alloys, dough, liquids); some need a Blaze Burner below. The filter picks one recipe when two match. Results leave through a faucet into an inventory below or beside."
  ],
  "quest.175083F5E8E666B3.title": "Blaze Burner",
  "quest.175083F5E8E666B3.quest_desc": [
    "Iron sheets and netherrack make an empty burner; right-click a Blaze (or its spawner) to fill it. Feed it fuel to heat the Basin above, or a Blaze Cake for super-heat. An arm or deployer keeps it fed later."
  ],
  "quest.26297EDEF72560DF.title": "Brass",
  "quest.26297EDEF72560DF.quest_desc": [
    "One copper and one zinc ingot in a heated Basin give 2 Brass Ingots. Zinc ore spawns in the Overworld. Brass opens the second age: brass casing, precision mechanisms, mechanical arms and trains."
  ],
  "quest.1DC4E2140C4FC88C.title": "Encased Fan",
  "quest.1DC4E2140C4FC88C.quest_desc": [
    "Pushes or pulls air depending on its spin, carrying items and mobs with it. At the top or bottom of a Chute it lifts items upward. Put a catalyst block in its stream and it processes items too."
  ],
  "quest.77B5FE48A4FA129E.title": "Bulk processing with fans",
  "quest.77B5FE48A4FA129E.quest_desc": [
    "A block in the air stream processes items flying through: lava or a Blaze Burner smelts, fire smokes, water washes, soul fire haunts. Food in a lava stream burns: smoke it instead. Fan speed only changes range, not processing time."
  ],
  "quest.49913C7985EE46B8.title": "Millstone",
  "quest.49913C7985EE46B8.quest_desc": [
    "Drop items in the top, power it from the side: gravel to flint, wheat to flour, ores and flowers to dust and dye. Slow but cheap; Crushing Wheels do it better in the brass age."
  ],
  "quest.2324180555060EA4.title": "Mechanical Belt",
  "quest.2324180555060EA4.quest_desc": [
    "Six dried kelp make a belt; right-click two shafts to link them, straight, diagonal or vertical, 2 to 20 blocks. Belts carry items and mobs, and the Press, Saw and Spout work on items as they ride past."
  ],
  "quest.3D9C0C0B645B0ABC.title": "Funnels and Depots",
  "quest.3D9C0C0B645B0ABC.quest_desc": [
    "A funnel placed normally pulls from an inventory; placed while sneaking it pushes into it (a wrench flips it). Redstone stops it. A Depot is a one-slot belt for machines and arms. Funnels cannot link two closed containers directly: put a chute or belt between."
  ],
  "quest.7FEAA44F45D5393B.title": "Chutes",
  "quest.7FEAA44F45D5393B.quest_desc": [
    "Chutes drop items straight down between inventories, or diagonally aimed at a side. An Encased Fan at one end pushes items upward. The Goggles show the flow direction."
  ],
  "quest.576CE9D64BAE34C7.title": "Moving structures",
  "quest.576CE9D64BAE34C7.quest_desc": [
    "A Mechanical Bearing rotates the blocks in front of it, a Mechanical Piston slides them, and Super Glue groups them into one contraption. On the move, Drills mine, Saws fell trees and Harvesters reap. Bearing plus saws is the classic first farm."
  ],
  "quest.76212786ECF9AAA2.title": "Drill and Saw",
  "quest.76212786ECF9AAA2.quest_desc": [
    "Standing still, a Drill breaks the block in front and a Saw fells a tree by its bottom log; speed follows rotation. A Saw facing up processes items passing over it: one alloy into 6 shafts (crafting gives 4)."
  ],
  "quest.28659381D2A10DC1.title": "Copper Casing and pipes",
  "quest.28659381D2A10DC1.quest_desc": [
    "Copper on stripped wood gives Copper Casing, body of the fluid machines. A cogwheel on a Fluid Pipe makes a Mechanical Pump. Pipes hold nothing: the pump moves fluid up to 16 blocks, and its arrow, not the rotation, sets the direction."
  ],
  "quest.3DBB3FB6F656AA03.title": "Fluid Tanks",
  "quest.3DBB3FB6F656AA03.quest_desc": [
    "Tanks merge up to 3x3 wide and over 30 tall; pipes use any side and a comparator reads the level. You cannot pour by hand in survival: use a Basin, Item Drain or Spout. A Hose Pulley in a big enough lake pumps forever."
  ],
  "quest.76BB178286CE5FED.title": "Steam Engine",
  "quest.76BB178286CE5FED.quest_desc": [
    "Steam Engines on a Fluid Tank, a shaft clicked into each, heat below and water piped in: a boiler. Each boiler level runs one more engine at full power; the Goggles say what is missing (heat, water or size). Fed Blaze Burners are the real heat."
  ],
  "quest.58F59827A9B35689.title": "Item Vault",
  "quest.58F59827A9B35689.quest_desc": [
    "Vaults merge like tanks (up to 3 wide, three times as long) and hold a lot, but cannot be opened by hand: funnels, chutes and arms move items. A great buffer between machines."
  ],
  "quest.5D15941A9CF83546.title": "Redstone Link",
  "quest.5D15941A9CF83546.quest_desc": [
    "Sends redstone wirelessly up to 256 blocks. Two items in its slots set the frequency; sneak-click switches sender and receiver. A link driving a clutch is the cleanest remote off switch."
  ],
  "quest.2BCA4E743126A82D.title": "Creative Create parts",
  "quest.2BCA4E743126A82D.quest_desc": [
    "The Creative Motor, Fluid Tank and Blaze Cake cost two Luminosities each (Act VI); the Creative Crate cannot be crafted. Plan real power: water, wind and steam take you to the end."
  ],
  "chapter.7D58BA957E127EAE.title": "Silent Gear",
  "chapter.7D58BA957E127EAE.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Tools, weapons and armour built from parts: blueprints, materials and traits, repair kits, alloys and the luminous material."
  ],
  "quest.3E8C6596D76CCEA3.title": "Gear built from parts",
  "quest.3E8C6596D76CCEA3.quest_desc": [
    "A head or blade from main materials, a rod and optional extras: every material adds its own stats and traits, and mixing changes the result. Broken gear does not vanish, it waits for repair. Nobody spawns with blueprints or the material book here; both are cheap to craft."
  ],
  "quest.7436213DB8D718D5.title": "Stone Anvil and crude knife",
  "quest.7436213DB8D718D5.quest_desc": [
    "Start in the Stone Age: cobblestone and dirt make the Stone Anvil and the Crude Tool Parts, which become a Crude Knife. Put a log on the anvil and use the knife on it to get six Template Boards.",
    "",
    "Any knife or dagger works on the anvil, including the Silent Gear ones later."
  ],
  "quest.3574048549EEC217.title": "Templates",
  "quest.3574048549EEC217.quest_desc": [
    "Template Boards around a stick shape a Template for each gear type (pickaxe, sword, helmet...). A template is used up in one craft. Its tooltip tells how many main materials the part needs."
  ],
  "quest.5B513654FB93EAAA.title": "Your first Silent Gear tool",
  "quest.5B513654FB93EAAA.quest_desc": [
    "Craft a template with the main materials to get a head, then the head with a rod to get the tool. A quick recipe does both in one step: template, materials and rod together.",
    "",
    "Stone, flint, iron, copper, gems, bone and many modded metals are valid materials: check a material tooltip for its stats."
  ],
  "quest.6964FE44D886F549.title": "Blueprints",
  "quest.6964FE44D886F549.quest_desc": [
    "Four paper and a blue dye make Blueprint Paper; shape it like a template to get a Blueprint, which is never used up. A Blueprint Book holds many blueprints and works as the selected one; cycle it with the keys its tooltip shows.",
    "",
    "Move from templates to blueprints once you craft the same part often."
  ],
  "quest.7BF828D333F31D0E.title": "Parts beyond the head",
  "quest.7BF828D333F31D0E.quest_desc": [
    "Rods, Bindings, Grips, Tips and Coatings add stats or traits. Netherite only works as a coating: on diamond it behaves almost like vanilla netherite. The Gear Mod Kit removes or repaints parts. Hold Ctrl over a part to see its numbers."
  ],
  "quest.2A6685D98DA1FA5D.title": "The gear roster",
  "quest.2A6685D98DA1FA5D.quest_desc": [
    "Hammer (3x3 stone, ores only when aimed at one), Excavator (3x3 soil), Saw (whole trees), Sickle (clears plants, replants crops), Mattock (tills, digs, chops), Paxel (three in one); katana, machete, dagger, knife, spear, mace, bows, crossbows, slingshot. The Prospector Hammer scans ahead for ores."
  ],
  "quest.67B078299DE88913.title": "Armour",
  "quest.67B078299DE88913.quest_desc": [
    "Helmet, chestplate, leggings and boots come from their own blueprints or templates, built from plates of any armour-capable material. Linings made of fabrics add traits. Armour follows the same rules: it breaks into a repairable state and mixes materials."
  ],
  "quest.767797906C0DD96F.title": "Broken gear and repair kits",
  "quest.767797906C0DD96F.quest_desc": [
    "When durability runs out the item becomes broken, not destroyed. Fill a repair kit by crafting it with materials, then craft the kit with the gear to repair it; a stick empties the kit. Better kits (very crude, crude, sturdy, crimson, azure) hold more and waste less.",
    "",
    "A Red Card upgrade makes an item break for good, like vanilla, if you prefer that."
  ],
  "quest.6BDC2490EB1BE98C.title": "Upgrades",
  "quest.6BDC2490EB1BE98C.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrade Base (paper, planks and stone) and its advanced version start the upgrades: Spoon lets a pickaxe dig like a shovel, Wide Plate adds 1 to the radius of hammers and excavators, Road Maker makes paths with an excavator, and Red Card allows permanent breaking. Craft the upgrade together with the gear."
  ],
  "quest.3DD29656FE7C8536.title": "Fibres and drops",
  "quest.3DD29656FE7C8536.quest_desc": [
    "Wild flax and fluffy plants grow in the world; their fibres make strings and fabrics for bowstrings, cords and linings. Animals sometimes drop sinew and spiders rarely drop fine silk, both better cord materials. Leather scraps drop too."
  ],
  "quest.30DF358C5B7F5045.title": "Silent Gear ores",
  "quest.30DF358C5B7F5045.quest_desc": [
    "Three ores of its own: Bort, a hard gem deep in the Overworld (Y -60 to 10); Crimson Iron all through the Nether; and Azure Silver in the End (Y 16 to 92). They feed the alloys that come next."
  ],
  "quest.43D69EA32C741FCF.title": "Alloys",
  "quest.43D69EA32C741FCF.quest_desc": [
    "Blaze Gold (gold and blaze powder), Crimson Steel (crimson iron, blaze rods and magma cream) and Azure Electrum (azure silver, gold and an ender pearl) can be crafted at a crafting table. Crimson steel is strong all around and fire-resistant; azure electrum is fast but fragile."
  ],
  "quest.6C794340168FB182.title": "Alloy Forge and Tyrian Steel",
  "quest.6C794340168FB182.quest_desc": [
    "The Alloy Forge (blackstone, crimson steel and an iron block) makes the same alloys more efficiently than the crafting table, and it is the only way to make Tyrian Steel: crimson steel, azure electrum, crushed shulker shell and netherite scrap. Tyrian steel is the strongest basic material in Silent Gear."
  ],
  "quest.37B2F02FEFEAD4DB.title": "Compound materials",
  "quest.37B2F02FEFEAD4DB.quest_desc": [
    "Machines that fuse materials into new ones: the Crude Mixer takes anything but marks the result Crude (weaker); the Recrystallizer makes hybrid gems; the Refabricator blends fabrics; the Super Mixer takes any material with no penalty. The result keeps a mix of its inputs' properties."
  ],
  "quest.556CC166B490647F.title": "Material Grader",
  "quest.556CC166B490647F.quest_desc": [
    "Grades a material with a catalyst, raising its stats: grades go from E up to SSS and MAX. Catalyst tiers are Glowing Dust (tier 1), Blazing Dust (tier 2) and Glittery Dust (tier 3); higher tiers reach higher grades. Grade the stack before you use it as a main material."
  ],
  "quest.5A3D56A181853420.title": "Starlight Charger",
  "quest.5A3D56A181853420.quest_desc": [
    "Builds charge under the night sky and applies Starcharged to materials, which raises their stats a lot. It takes a catalyst (blaze gold dust first, then azure silver dust) and its surrounding structure level can take up to 30 seconds to update."
  ],
  "quest.054210025010EBCC.title": "Salvager",
  "quest.054210025010EBCC.quest_desc": [
    "Breaks gear you no longer need back into parts and some of its materials. The luminous material has salvage disabled on purpose, so it never returns Luminosities."
  ],
  "quest.0E364ED62BB2A9DA.title": "Jewellery",
  "quest.0E364ED62BB2A9DA.quest_desc": [
    "Jeweler Tools make rings, bracelets and necklaces, optionally with a gem setting. They sit in accessory slots and carry the traits of their materials, so a ring can add a trait your armour lacks."
  ],
  "quest.3946F41738A526C5.title": "Mastery: the luminous material",
  "quest.3946F41738A526C5.quest_desc": [
    "The Luminous Ingot (Act VI) is a main material with absurd stats: Radiant, Holy V, Lustrous V, Refractive, Kitty Vision, fireproof. Light repairs radiant pieces, they glow, and four worn (luminous armour counts) give flight, night vision and no fall damage. Luminous tips and coatings exist too."
  ],
  "chapter.50DBA07B8CBB4386.title": "Actually Additions",
  "chapter.50DBA07B8CBB4386.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Black quartz, the Atomic Reconstructor and its crystals, generators, laser relays, phantomfaces and handy gadgets."
  ],
  "quest.54BCE8D235829045.title": "A laser that makes crystals",
  "quest.54BCE8D235829045.quest_desc": [
    "A grab bag of automation around the Atomic Reconstructor, whose laser turns materials into crystals. Its Crystal Flux (CF) is plain FE. The Manual (paper and a canola seed) covers everything; craftable, not free. AA crystals go into two act components."
  ],
  "quest.0329621E779C4D03.title": "Black Quartz and the Iron Casing",
  "quest.0329621E779C4D03.quest_desc": [
    "Black Quartz ore spawns underground; smelt or crush it. Four iron, four sticks and a black quartz make the Iron Casing, frame of AA machines. Keep a few: the Energy Coupler (II) takes one."
  ],
  "quest.0A875C7364794AE3.title": "Coal Generator",
  "quest.0A875C7364794AE3.quest_desc": [
    "Iron casing, coal and cobble. Burns anything a furnace burns, only starting new fuel when not full; redstone stops it, a comparator reads it. One runs a reconstructor. The Leaf Generator eats nearby leaves for CF."
  ],
  "quest.1B0EC5EE12C42EFA.title": "Atomic Reconstructor",
  "quest.1B0EC5EE12C42EFA.quest_desc": [
    "Each laser shot (1000 CF) converts what it hits: redstone to Restonia, lapis to Palis, diamond to Diamatine, emerald to Emeradic, iron to Enori, coal to Void. A redstone torch click toggles redstone-off and pulse modes."
  ],
  "quest.356CFF06141D0852.title": "Crystals in the act components",
  "quest.356CFF06141D0852.quest_desc": [
    "Energy Coupler (II): 2 Restonia, an Iron Casing and 2 Create andesite alloys. Routing Matrix (III): 2 Palis. AA itself is native and one of the pack's free early power sources; a coal generator and a reconstructor cover both."
  ],
  "quest.271551CB4A93BB2E.title": "Reconstructor lenses",
  "quest.271551CB4A93BB2E.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click it with a lens: Color recolours, the Miner turns stone into ores (netherrack into nether ores), Disenchanting moves one enchantment to a book, Detonation explodes, Certain Death kills, players included: fence it off. Without a lens it splits multi-enchantment books (155,000 CF each)."
  ],
  "quest.1E645F439719399C.title": "Empowerer",
  "quest.1E645F439719399C.quest_desc": [
    "Crystal on the Empowerer, the four listed modifiers on Display Stands around it, power: Empowered crystal. Empowered Restonia wants red dye, a nether brick, redstone and a brick. Item laser relays can deliver the modifiers automatically."
  ],
  "quest.69AA923D35150556.title": "Canola power",
  "quest.69AA923D35150556.quest_desc": [
    "Wild canola, a Canola Press for oil, a Fermenting Barrel to refine it, an Oil Generator to burn either; crystallized oil burns better. A renewable early power plant."
  ],
  "quest.52F988DC169DB793.title": "Laser relays",
  "quest.52F988DC169DB793.quest_desc": [
    "Link relays with the Laser Wrench (click one, then the other; again to unlink). Energy relays move CF wirelessly in three tiers; Fluid relays move liquids; Item relays plus an Item Interface turn every linked container into one inventory, Advanced ones filtering."
  ],
  "quest.59C0B0D723A37D0A.title": "Phantomfaces",
  "quest.59C0B0D723A37D0A.quest_desc": [
    "A Phantomface acts as a linked block's inventory from a distance: pipe into a machine with no free faces. Liquiface and Energyface do fluids and CF; Phantom Boosters extend the range. Phantom Breakers and Placers work at a distance; the Player Interface reaches a player's inventory."
  ],
  "quest.1A238FF74011D248.title": "Block machines",
  "quest.1A238FF74011D248.quest_desc": [
    "Breakers, Placers, Fluid Placers and Collectors act on the block ahead; the Long-Range Breaker reaches farther; the Vertical Digger mines down, ores only or everything. The Energizer charges CF items, the Enervator drains them, the Experience Solidifier bottles your levels as items."
  ],
  "quest.63A3335C52F9C291.title": "Drill and rings",
  "quest.63A3335C52F9C291.quest_desc": [
    "A CF pickaxe-shovel; sneak-right-click adds upgrades (speed, area, fortune, silk touch, block placing), each tier needing the one below. Rings: Magnetism pulls items, Growth speeds plants, Liquid Banning clears water and lava. The Teleport Staff jumps where you look."
  ],
  "quest.43689517C893C3AD.title": "Automating crystals",
  "quest.43689517C893C3AD.quest_desc": [
    "Face the reconstructor into an Automatic Precision Dropper and put a Ranged Collector nearby with the crystals allow-listed. Drop raw materials in the dropper; the collector gathers the results. Works for any conversion."
  ],
  "quest.2F0A53A8F1D988B3.title": "Farmer and Feeder",
  "quest.2F0A53A8F1D988B3.quest_desc": [
    "The Farmer tills, plants and harvests a 9x9 in front: crops, cactus and cane on sand, wart on soul sand, melons and pumpkins in a checkerboard. The Feeder breeds animals with the right food and stops when the pen is full."
  ],
  "quest.51416817D54FBE2D.title": "Mastery: every crystal, empowered",
  "quest.51416817D54FBE2D.quest_desc": [
    "An automated reconstructor line making every crystal, an Empowerer fed by item relays, and energy relays carrying CF across the base with no cables."
  ],
  "chapter.2F42E1CA910F510D.title": "Applied Energistics 2: first network",
  "chapter.2F42E1CA910F510D.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Meteorites, certus, processors and a first ME network: storage cells, channels, the controller and buses."
  ],
  "quest.1A1CF038370B8C82.title": "Items become data",
  "quest.1A1CF038370B8C82.quest_desc": [
    "Cables link drives full of storage cells, terminals search everything at once, buses import and export, and autocrafting comes later. It all starts at a meteorite; after that it is processors in bulk. Refined Storage is the alternative."
  ],
  "quest.4B78FA1CA4E7379E.title": "Press G",
  "quest.4B78FA1CA4E7379E.quest_desc": [
    "Hover any AE2 item and hold G for its guide page, with 3D scenes you can rotate. Extended AE, Advanced AE, MEGA Cells and AE2WTLib add their own pages. Every number lives there."
  ],
  "quest.1E4E23988E9781B3.title": "Find a meteorite",
  "quest.1E4E23988E9781B3.quest_desc": [
    "Meteorites are common and leave big craters. A Meteorite Compass points to the nearest Mysterious Cube at their centre. Dig in: the good stuff is in the middle."
  ],
  "quest.25592EB7781F3A38.title": "The four presses",
  "quest.25592EB7781F3A38.quest_desc": [
    "The Mysterious Cube drops all four presses (Silicon, Logic, Calculation, Engineering), reusable forever. Around it: certus clusters and budding certus. Take the clusters."
  ],
  "quest.2BF325869777C6A1.title": "Budding certus: careful",
  "quest.2BF325869777C6A1.quest_desc": [
    "Four tiers: Flawless, Flawed, Chipped, Damaged. Growth can degrade any but Flawless. Mining without Silk Touch drops a tier; a Flawless one drops a tier even with Silk Touch and never recovers, so build your farm around it. Degraded blocks recharge in water with charged certus."
  ],
  "quest.750B81F61BFEFF77.title": "Growth Accelerator",
  "quest.750B81F61BFEFF77.quest_desc": [
    "Certus grows painfully slow alone; an accelerator next to the budding block speeds it up enormously. Power it with AE2 energy, or a Crank at first. The guide shows farms that harvest with Annihilation Planes."
  ],
  "quest.553205EE6C9D1141.title": "Charger and Fluix",
  "quest.553205EE6C9D1141.quest_desc": [
    "A Charger makes Charged Certus. Charged certus, redstone and nether quartz thrown into water together become Fluix Crystals. Create's Mixer makes fluix too, easy to automate."
  ],
  "quest.678B55C9B3908621.title": "Inscriber",
  "quest.678B55C9B3908621.quest_desc": [
    "Presses items with the presses. Sided: top input goes to the top slot, bottom to the bottom, side or back to the middle, and results leave by the side or back. A wrench rotates it. One inscriber per step is the classic processor line."
  ],
  "quest.4F1E7EE66CB33834.title": "Processors",
  "quest.4F1E7EE66CB33834.quest_desc": [
    "Logic (gold), Calculation (certus) and Engineering (diamond): press the material into a circuit, silicon into printed silicon, then both plus redstone in a last inscriber. You will need hundreds: automate them first."
  ],
  "quest.2325AF6584F70E3F.title": "AE2 in the act components",
  "quest.2325AF6584F70E3F.quest_desc": [
    "Two Logic Processors go into the Routing Matrix (Act III) with a PneumaticCraft circuit board, two palis crystals and a Calibration Frame; a Calculation Processor goes into the Habitation Charter (Act V). AE2 itself stays native, controller included."
  ],
  "quest.41D20416314D72EE.title": "Your first ME system",
  "quest.41D20416314D72EE.quest_desc": [
    "A Drive, an Energy Acceptor fed any FE, a Terminal on a cable and a few Storage Cells: searchable storage for the whole base. Make the terminal a Crafting Terminal and craft straight from the network."
  ],
  "quest.5A24342389F499DB.title": "Storage cells",
  "quest.5A24342389F499DB.quest_desc": [
    "1k to 256k, up to 63 types each. Each type costs space up front, so one type fits far more than 63 (a 1k cell holds 8,128 of one). Upgrade by crafting with a bigger component, partition in a Cell Workbench. Keep enchanted mob loot out: every variation is a new type."
  ],
  "quest.6A516FC607869EC3.title": "Energy: add a cell",
  "quest.6A516FC607869EC3.quest_desc": [
    "FE turns into AE one way, 2 FE per AE. A network can only spend per tick what it has stored, so a big import into a tiny network can drain and reboot it. One Energy Cell (200k AE) fixes it for most bases."
  ],
  "quest.30F0572B87CBE80E.title": "Channels",
  "quest.30F0572B87CBE80E.quest_desc": [
    "Most devices need a channel: normal cable carries 8, dense 32. Without a controller you get 8 in total. Cable colour only stops colours from connecting. Build like a tree: dense trunk from the controller, normal branches, devices in groups of 8."
  ],
  "quest.00CC66AACA668D42.title": "ME Controller",
  "quest.00CC66AACA668D42.quest_desc": [
    "Each face gives 32 channels. It can be a multiblock up to 7x7x7, all touching, no block with neighbours on more than one axis, one per network. Right-click it for network statistics."
  ],
  "quest.2B3B676137DDEE49.title": "Import, export and storage buses",
  "quest.2B3B676137DDEE49.quest_desc": [
    "Import Buses pull into the network, Export Buses push filtered items out, Storage Buses make any chest or drawer part of the network. Import on a furnace output plus export on its input: automated smelting. Buses take speed, capacity, fuzzy, inverter, redstone and crafting cards."
  ],
  "quest.68FFB486CB3B69CD.title": "ME Interface",
  "quest.68FFB486CB3B69CD.quest_desc": [
    "An inventory wired to the network: machines and pipes insert into it, and it can keep chosen items stocked for whatever pulls from it. It is also the heart of subnetworks and pattern setups."
  ],
  "quest.192520C87BEEA2AC.title": "Wireless access",
  "quest.192520C87BEEA2AC.quest_desc": [
    "A Wireless Access Point (one channel) lets a Wireless Terminal reach the network; Boosters inside raise range and power cost. Link the terminal by placing it in the access point. AE2WTLib adds crafting, pattern and universal wireless terminals."
  ],
  "quest.561A39CD67283B8C.title": "P2P tunnels and the Quantum Bridge",
  "quest.561A39CD67283B8C.quest_desc": [
    "P2P tunnels push one thing through a single cable: ME tunnels carry up to 32 channels, others items, fluids, energy or redstone; tune pairs with a Memory Card. The Quantum Network Bridge links networks across any distance or dimension if both ends are loaded."
  ],
  "quest.59CE9179920C376A.title": "Creative AE2",
  "quest.59CE9179920C376A.quest_desc": [
    "The Creative Energy Cell costs two Luminosities (logistics and engineering, Act VI); the Creative Storage Cell cannot be crafted. The rest is native."
  ],
  "quest.42DAD943EBAF99A3.title": "Mastery: a real network",
  "quest.42DAD943EBAF99A3.quest_desc": [
    "Controller, dense backbone, drives of 64k cells, an energy cell, a wireless access point and an automated processor line: one searchable inventory for the whole base. Next stop, patterns."
  ],
  "chapter.2BF66993F908A056.title": "Create: addons",
  "chapter.2BF66993F908A056.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Enchantment Industry, Connected, Dragons Plus, Copycats+, Deco, Bells and Whistles and Hypertube: what each adds and when to use it."
  ],
  "quest.2ECC24395D9E99C0.title": "The Create family",
  "quest.2ECC24395D9E99C0.quest_desc": [
    "Enchantment Industry automates experience and enchanting; Connected adds smarter kinetics and logistics; Dragons Plus brings fan processing types and fluid tools; Copycats+, Deco and Bells and Whistles are for building; Hypertube shoots players through glass tubes. All have Ponder scenes."
  ],
  "quest.50EABAD3AA74115B.title": "Liquid experience",
  "quest.50EABAD3AA74115B.quest_desc": [
    "Enchantment Industry runs on Liquid Experience. An Experience Hatch stores your levels (click to deposit, sneak-click to withdraw). Item Drains empty experience items, Spouts refill them, and experience leaking from a pipe turns back into orbs. An Experience Lantern soaks up nearby orbs."
  ],
  "quest.638D14DBD895685C.title": "Mechanical Grindstone",
  "quest.638D14DBD895685C.quest_desc": [
    "Eight andesite alloys around a shaft. Click an Item Drain with it for a Grindstone Drain, add another grindstone on top: dropped items get ground and XP nuggets become liquid experience. Crushing Wheels and Deployers that kill mobs now drop XP nuggets, so mob farms feed it directly."
  ],
  "quest.7B70C2EA603E91CF.title": "Blaze Enchanter",
  "quest.7B70C2EA603E91CF.quest_desc": [
    "Smith an Enchanting Table onto a Blaze Burner with the Blaze Upgrade template. Feed it liquid experience, set the level on its panel (vanilla caps at 30) and it enchants what arms or belts bring. A filter item switches to Template mode, writing only enchantments that item can take onto a blank template."
  ],
  "quest.1B6F6F3AE0F6A3A6.title": "Blaze Forger",
  "quest.1B6F6F3AE0F6A3A6.quest_desc": [
    "An anvil run by a blaze on liquid experience: merges enchantments with no repair cost, merges templates, applies a template to an item, or extracts an enchantment onto a blank template. Move a great enchantment from an old tool to a new one."
  ],
  "quest.0FDBAEE270D46484.title": "Super Enchanting",
  "quest.0FDBAEE270D46484.quest_desc": [
    "Feed an Enchanter or Forger a Cake o' Enchanting and it starts seething: the level cap goes far higher, treasure enchantments can roll and the Forger merges conflicting ones. It only takes Super Enchanting Templates. It calls lightning: keep a Lightning Rod nearby."
  ],
  "quest.0CB361E7D10525AD.title": "Printer",
  "quest.0CB361E7D10525AD.quest_desc": [
    "Brass sheet, iron block and a spout. Filter the item to copy and feed the matching fluid: written books, enchanted books, names, train schedules, clipboards, package addresses. Left native on purpose, since every copy costs liquid experience."
  ],
  "quest.11F14228ED3BBB5E.title": "Enchantment Industry and Apotheosis",
  "quest.11F14228ED3BBB5E.quest_desc": [
    "With Apotheosis around: the Brass Bookshelf gives adjustable enchanting stats (needs rotation), the Affix Augmentor upgrades affixes with Apotheotic Essence, the Blaze Composer moves affixes through templates, and a fan through Infused Dragon Breath salvages gear in bulk. Including what you wear: stay out of the stream."
  ],
  "quest.0E1E17A383C2E5C1.title": "Pack changes: XP fluids and the creative shelf",
  "quest.0E1E17A383C2E5C1.quest_desc": [
    "The pack fixes Enchantment Industry's list of other mods' experience fluids (Ender IO, Industrial Foregoing, Just Dire Things, PneumaticCraft, Reliquary, Sophisticated), so they all count. The Creative Bookshelf costs two Luminosities (Act VI)."
  ],
  "quest.75546C046FB78F53.title": "Mastery: beyond vanilla enchanting",
  "quest.75546C046FB78F53.quest_desc": [
    "Strike Blocks of Experience with lightning into Super Experience, craft a Super Enchanting Template and run a seething Enchanter by a lightning rod. With a Forger, gear goes past vanilla limits, all fed by a mob farm and a grindstone drain."
  ],
  "quest.3A4EFB035F8DC1B8.title": "Create: Connected kinetics",
  "quest.3A4EFB035F8DC1B8.quest_desc": [
    "The parts Create lacks: a Brass Gearbox with wrench-set sides, Six-way and Parallel Gearboxes, Centrifugal, Freewheel and Overstress Clutches, a Shear Pin, a Brake, a Crank Wheel and a Cross Connector. The Overstress Clutch and Shear Pin cut a runaway branch before it freezes everything."
  ],
  "quest.5596725A549B09EA.title": "Kinetic Battery",
  "quest.5596725A549B09EA.quest_desc": [
    "Stores stress. Unpowered it charges from rotation at its front; with redstone it discharges at a fixed capacity and speed, spending only what is used, and never while other sources cover the load. Charge it with a windmill by day, spend it at night."
  ],
  "quest.0DEFF29404B28832.title": "Connected logistics",
  "quest.0DEFF29404B28832.quest_desc": [
    "The Brass Chute moves up to 64 items at once. The Inventory Bridge lets one funnel reach two inventories. The Item Silo is a vertical vault, the Fluid Vessel a horizontal tank (weaker as a boiler). Fan Catalysts hold lava, water or fire inside a block: fan processing with no spills."
  ],
  "quest.39CEA4922F07C72B.title": "One copycat family",
  "quest.39CEA4922F07C72B.quest_desc": [
    "Connected's own copycat blocks are off in its config, because Copycats+ covers those shapes. If EMI shows two versions of one shape, use the Copycats+ one."
  ],
  "quest.77BCFA0009CEC5FD.title": "Create: Dragons Plus",
  "quest.77BCFA0009CEC5FD.quest_desc": [
    "The base Enchantment Industry and Central Kitchen build on. The Fluid Hatch fills or drains a tank with buckets and bottles. Dye plus water gives Liquid Dye, which colours items and mobs and makes concrete against lava; liquid Dragon's Breath makes end stone. Its Blaze Upgrade template makes the CEI machines."
  ],
  "quest.238A1E08F4CC4D13.title": "New fan processing types",
  "quest.238A1E08F4CC4D13.quest_desc": [
    "Liquid Dye colours items, mobs and worn armour; Powder Snow freezes; Quicksand does sand paper recipes; a Dragon Head or Dragon's Breath does Ending; a Golden Aercloud from the Aether runs Aether altar recipes in bulk. EMI lists each type with the catalyst it needs."
  ],
  "quest.16D128C530556B90.title": "Copycats+",
  "quest.16D128C530556B90.quest_desc": [
    "Copycat blocks take the look of any full block: click with a material to apply, a wrench removes it, sneak-click with an empty hand toggles connected textures. Dozens of shapes, doors, trapdoors, buttons, ladders and a no-collision Ghost Block, many cut from zinc in a stonecutter."
  ],
  "quest.1089FF521C5397C8.title": "Create Deco and Rechiseled Create",
  "quest.1089FF521C5397C8.quest_desc": [
    "Deco adds sheet metal, coloured bricks, lamps, decals, bars, placards, doors, windows and supports in Create's style; Rechiseled Create adds chisel variants of Create blocks. One placard-dyeing recipe fails to load in 1.21.1 and is disabled; the rest is native."
  ],
  "quest.660ACF6373137B51.title": "Bells and Whistles",
  "quest.660ACF6373137B51.quest_desc": [
    "Train and station dressing: headlights, cowcatchers in many stones, platforms, metro casing, panels, windows, grab bars and steps. Purely decorative; glue it to a train like any block."
  ],
  "quest.387AED26C270661F.title": "Create Hypertube",
  "quest.387AED26C270661F.quest_desc": [
    "Glass tubes that carry players and mobs. Click a placed tube holding another, then place the second to link them. An Entrance needs 16 RPM or more and spins you faster the faster it turns; Accelerators speed up or brake; Splitters branch and you steer with movement keys."
  ],
  "chapter.1015125C7533B2A8.title": "Create: brass and automation",
  "chapter.1015125C7533B2A8.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Filters, deployers, mechanical arms, crafters and sequenced assembly: the second Create age."
  ],
  "quest.6B420EFE153F8BFD.title": "The brass age",
  "quest.6B420EFE153F8BFD.quest_desc": [
    "Brass is where you stop moving items by hand: filtered logistics, the Deployer (a robot copy of you), the Mechanical Arm, Mechanical Crafters, Crushing Wheels and sequenced assembly, which chains machines to build one complex part."
  ],
  "quest.411293F478ED352C.title": "Brass Casing",
  "quest.411293F478ED352C.quest_desc": [
    "A Brass Ingot on stripped wood: the body of the smart machines (crafters, arms, the speed controller, logistics blocks). A Deployer can apply it for you."
  ],
  "quest.40B30AC5E7D15961.title": "Polished Rose Quartz",
  "quest.40B30AC5E7D15961.quest_desc": [
    "One quartz and eight redstone make Rose Quartz. Polish it with Sand Paper in hand (quartz in the off-hand or on the floor), or let a Deployer do it. Mekanism shortcut: the Enrichment Chamber polishes it and the Metallurgic Infuser makes it."
  ],
  "quest.3469F859B3B7AB74.title": "Electron Tube",
  "quest.3469F859B3B7AB74.quest_desc": [
    "Polished Rose Quartz on an Iron Sheet. The brain of every smart block: brass funnels and tunnels, deployers, crafters, smart chutes and observers. Make a handful; they go fast."
  ],
  "quest.21FEAE578271FEFD.title": "Brass Funnel and Tunnel",
  "quest.21FEAE578271FEFD.quest_desc": [
    "A Brass Funnel moves up to a full stack, with an exact amount on its panel and a filter. A Brass Tunnel on a belt has a filter per side: inbound blocks, outbound sorts. Tunnels on side-by-side belts group up and spread items over every exit."
  ],
  "quest.2D7CF472187B0DCC.title": "Tunnel modes",
  "quest.2D7CF472187B0DCC.quest_desc": [
    "Split spreads a stack evenly and skips full exits; Forced Split waits instead. Round Robin keeps stacks whole and cycles; Prefer Nearest favours the closest exit; Randomize picks at random; Synchronize Inputs waits for every belt. Prefer Nearest plus a Weighted Ejector splits exact amounts off a line."
  ],
  "quest.25D97F2683BD89CD.title": "Filters",
  "quest.25D97F2683BD89CD.quest_desc": [
    "A List Filter (iron nuggets and wool) matches a set of items; an Attribute Filter (brass nuggets and wool) matches by attribute, like «can be smelted» or a tag. Either one fits any Create filter slot and replaces a dozen single-item slots."
  ],
  "quest.3D18D702CE0F07CE.title": "Smart Chute, Smart Observer, Threshold Switch",
  "quest.3D18D702CE0F07CE.quest_desc": [
    "The Smart Chute adds a filter and stack size to a chute. The Smart Observer fires redstone when a container, belt, chute or pipe holds its filter item. The Threshold Switch turns on above an upper fill level and off below a lower one: wire it to a clutch for «stop when the chest is full»."
  ],
  "quest.66A1273DEB5E3931.title": "Deployer",
  "quest.66A1273DEB5E3931.quest_desc": [
    "A mechanical player: it places, uses, activates, harvests and attacks at the spot two blocks ahead. Right-click by default; a wrench switches to left-click. With an item in hand it processes whatever sits below on a Depot or belt: sanding, casings, sequenced assembly steps."
  ],
  "quest.3BA376D13AB65787.title": "Deployer tricks",
  "quest.3BA376D13AB65787.quest_desc": [
    "With a filter, a Deployer only acts while holding the matching item and only accepts that item. Redstone stops it after the current swing, so a short pulse off gives exactly one use. On a moving contraption it acts at every spot it passes. Two facing deployers fist-bump."
  ],
  "quest.10FBE1404F8230D8.title": "Mechanical Arm",
  "quest.10FBE1404F8230D8.quest_desc": [
    "Before placing it, right-click its targets with the arm in hand: blue is input, click again for yellow output. It then shuttles items between any number of them. Depots and funnels bridge blocks it cannot reach, and a Brass Funnel target lends the arm its filter."
  ],
  "quest.55DA919A83044D72.title": "Arm modes",
  "quest.55DA919A83044D72.quest_desc": [
    "With several outputs: Round Robin cycles and skips full targets, Forced Round Robin waits, Prefer First fills the first target first. Redstone pauses it. Great first jobs: feeding Blaze Burners and serving Farmer's Delight pots and cutting boards."
  ],
  "quest.45749A42F9EAE9F2.title": "Sequenced assembly",
  "quest.45749A42F9EAE9F2.quest_desc": [
    "Some parts are built in steps: the base becomes an unfinished item that passes a list of machines (deployers, press, spout, saw) a set number of times. EMI shows the steps and loops. A belt looping back to its start runs it hands-free; failed runs drop scrap."
  ],
  "quest.2EC497FEE0F48D91.title": "Precision Mechanism",
  "quest.2EC497FEE0F48D91.quest_desc": [
    "Golden Sheet, then 5 loops of: deploy a Cogwheel, a Large Cogwheel and an Iron Nugget. About 80% become Precision Mechanisms, the rest scrap. It unlocks the Mechanical Arm, speed controller, train controls and Factory Gauge, and feeds two act components."
  ],
  "quest.2F08CF2E4CA2DB25.title": "Precision in the act components",
  "quest.2F08CF2E4CA2DB25.quest_desc": [
    "Handling Core (Act III): 2 Modular Routers blank modules, a Precision Mechanism and a Power Regulator. The Spectral Lens (IV) takes one too. The Handling Core gates the RFTools Builder, the Refined Storage Autocrafter and the Easy Villagers Auto Trader. Automate mechanisms early."
  ],
  "quest.1900C15D452488A4.title": "Rotation Speed Controller",
  "quest.1900C15D452488A4.quest_desc": [
    "Brass casing and a precision mechanism: it drives a Large Cogwheel on top at the speed set on its panel. The Sequenced Gearshift instead runs a timed list of turns on each redstone pulse. Use the controller to run a line at exactly the speed a recipe or stress budget needs."
  ],
  "quest.5E11DCB2FA716F05.title": "Mechanical Crafters",
  "quest.5E11DCB2FA716F05.quest_desc": [
    "A grid of crafters automates any recipe, plus big ones like the 5x5 Crushing Wheels. Wrench their arrows so every path ends at one exit. Crafting starts when every slot is filled, or on a redstone pulse for smaller recipes. Slot Covers mark empty slots; linked backs share one input."
  ],
  "quest.64B6B5D47D1EB737.title": "Crushing Wheels",
  "quest.64B6B5D47D1EB737.quest_desc": [
    "A pair from a 5x5 mechanical recipe (alloy, planks, stone). Place them side by side spinning into each other and drop items on top. Raw ore becomes Crushed Ore with a chance of XP nuggets; netherrack becomes Cinder Flour for Blaze Cakes. Speed is throughput."
  ],
  "quest.41BF50CEC2C30E7E.title": "Create ore math",
  "quest.41BF50CEC2C30E7E.quest_desc": [
    "Raw iron gives 1 crushed (plus 75% of an XP nugget): smelt it for 1 ingot or wash it for 9 nuggets and 75% redstone. Gold washes into quartz, copper clay, zinc gunpowder. Silk-touched ores give 1.75 (stone) or 2.25 (deepslate). Other mods multiply more: see Ore processing."
  ],
  "quest.7E52D88B6EC82066.title": "Spout and Item Drain",
  "quest.7E52D88B6EC82066.quest_desc": [
    "A pipe-fed Spout fills whatever sits below: buckets, bottles, potions, honey, the lava in a Blaze Cake. An Item Drain does the reverse, pouring items' fluid into its buffer. Both are pipe-only machines."
  ],
  "quest.44862012259D890D.title": "Blaze Cake",
  "quest.44862012259D890D.quest_desc": [
    "Compact egg, sugar and Cinder Flour into a Blaze Cake Base, then fill it with lava from a Spout. A Blaze Burner that eats it goes super-heated, which some recipes need. Arms or deployers keep cakes coming."
  ],
  "quest.7DA2CEAEEF72E8D0.title": "Weighted Ejector",
  "quest.7DA2CEAEEF72E8D0.quest_desc": [
    "Sneak-click to aim it, then place it: anything set on it (items, mobs, you) gets launched to the target, straight ahead at any height. Aimed at an inventory it waits for space, and it can hold items until a stack size is reached."
  ],
  "quest.6DCD494665B52E7A.title": "Display Links and Boards",
  "quest.6DCD494665B52E7A.quest_desc": [
    "A Display Link reads a source (stock, boiler status, train arrivals, stress) and writes it on a Display Board, Nixie Tubes or a sign. Click the display first, then place the link on the source. Boards need rotation and grow as big as you build them."
  ],
  "quest.109581D1AA0DA93E.title": "Automated kitchen",
  "quest.109581D1AA0DA93E.quest_desc": [
    "Central Kitchen automates Farmer's Delight pots, skillets, stoves and feasts; Slice and Dice's Slicer does the cutting board and its sprinklers water and fertilize. Pack config turns off the overlaps: no Slice and Dice basin cooking, no cutting-board recipes copied onto saws or deployers."
  ],
  "quest.6B61C2C2A53BC093.title": "Mastery: a self-running line",
  "quest.6B61C2C2A53BC093.quest_desc": [
    "Precision Mechanisms with no hands: golden sheets in, one deployer per part, a belt that loops back, a funnel catching mechanisms and scrap. The same belt-machines-loop pattern builds every sequenced part in Create and its addons."
  ],
  "chapter.5D5EB6605945AC19.title": "Create: electricity",
  "chapter.5D5EB6605945AC19.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Crafts and Additions bridges rotation and FE; New Age is the solar and magnetic technology of Heliodor."
  ],
  "quest.404CF660853785A7.title": "Rotation meets electricity",
  "quest.404CF660853785A7.quest_desc": [
    "Crafts and Additions turns rotation into FE (the power most tech mods use) and back, with wires, a rolling mill and a tesla coil. Create: New Age is Heliodor's tech: sun-heated plates, magnets and coils, energizers and a thorium reactor. Both start from Create parts you know."
  ],
  "quest.1BFAB003A278D495.title": "Rolling Mill",
  "quest.1BFAB003A278D495.quest_desc": [
    "A rotation-powered press for long parts: an ingot gives 2 rods, a plate 2 wires, bamboo or paper becomes straw. Drop items on top; a belt and two funnels automate it."
  ],
  "quest.160207A457B0B0F2.title": "Connectors and spools",
  "quest.160207A457B0B0F2.quest_desc": [
    "Small Connectors link FE blocks with Copper Spool wire (4 links each); Large Connectors take gold or electrum spools and 6 links. Click two connectors with a spool to wire them. A wrench cycles Push, Pull and None: generator side pushes, machine side pulls."
  ],
  "quest.40D2195EF4AA050D.title": "Alternator",
  "quest.40D2195EF4AA050D.quest_desc": [
    "Rotation in, FE out, but only from 32 RPM up, and more the faster it spins. The bridge that lets a water wheel or steam engine run Mekanism, Powah or IE machines. A fast alternator is a hungry one: watch the stress."
  ],
  "quest.2942848DCFF562A8.title": "Electric Motor",
  "quest.2942848DCFF562A8.quest_desc": [
    "FE in, rotation out. Scroll its back panel to set the RPM; higher RPM costs more energy. Computers can drive it as a peripheral. A motor on a battery bank is silent, compact rotation anywhere."
  ],
  "quest.007932E8F2D12779.title": "Modular Accumulator",
  "quest.007932E8F2D12779.quest_desc": [
    "A stackable multiblock battery. Set one connector as input and one as output; it also pushes into blocks above and below. A Portable Energy Interface pair charges one riding a train as it passes."
  ],
  "quest.5572EB452CE49149.title": "Tesla Coil",
  "quest.5572EB452CE49149.quest_desc": [
    "Charges FE items below it and runs charging recipes (gold ingots, sheets and wires into electrum). Powered by redstone it also shocks nearby mobs and players. Over a depot, it is a charging station for tools and jetpacks."
  ],
  "quest.6AAB9425E04AADB7.title": "Liquid Blaze Burner",
  "quest.6AAB9425E04AADB7.quest_desc": [
    "Use Straw on a Blaze Burner and it drinks liquid fuel by bucket or pipe. Lava keeps it lit 20000 ticks a bucket; Bioethanol, and the biofuel of Industrial Foregoing and Oritech, super-heat it. Goodbye, coal by hand."
  ],
  "quest.70608772E702AD35.title": "Farming fuel",
  "quest.70608772E702AD35.quest_desc": [
    "Seeds compacted give Seed Oil; crops, leaves or flowers mixed hot with plant oil give Biomass; sugar, cinder flour and two biomass make Bioethanol. Biomass also presses into pellets. A wheat farm plus a mixer is renewable fuel."
  ],
  "quest.2D13EC7992A1F5E6.title": "New Age: sunlight as heat",
  "quest.2D13EC7992A1F5E6.quest_desc": [
    "New Age has no photovoltaic panels: solar plates make heat, heat pipes carry it to a boiler or a Stirling engine, and electricity comes from Generator Coils spinning among magnets. Light, heat, rotation, electricity, and light again in its street lights: Heliodor's loop."
  ],
  "quest.55D2351D5C48CA80.title": "Magnetite and thorium",
  "quest.55D2351D5C48CA80.quest_desc": [
    "Magnetite blocks and Thorium ore spawn in the Overworld. Magnetite makes motors and magnets; crushed thorium has a 10% chance of Radioactive Thorium for reactor fuel. Thorium has no common ore tag here on purpose, so dimensional miners skip it: dig for it."
  ],
  "quest.41BC5584D4C11B0F.title": "Generator Coil and brushes",
  "quest.41BC5584D4C11B0F.quest_desc": [
    "A spinning Generator Coil ringed by magnets makes electricity, collected by Carbon Brushes. Stronger magnets turn more stress into power, and the coil draws more stress too. Pack change: the brushes, one set per generator, take an Energy Coupler (Act II) in place of an andesite alloy; coils keep their recipe."
  ],
  "quest.0CC87E8CE3690B51.title": "Magnet tiers",
  "quest.0CC87E8CE3690B51.quest_desc": [
    "Weakest to strongest: Redstone Magnets, Layered Magnets (overcharged iron and gold), Netherite Magnets (overcharged diamonds and netherite scrap) and Fluxuated Magnetite. The Goggles show a coil's force and efficiency. Better magnets first: efficiency is free power."
  ],
  "quest.1AF466ECB9C6F7F2.title": "Wires and connectors",
  "quest.1AF466ECB9C6F7F2.quest_desc": [
    "A Saw cuts a copper sheet into 4 Copper Wires, which link Electrical Connectors. New Age blocks push power to their neighbours; a connector in Pull mode (wrench) takes power from other mods' blocks, but never drains energizers or motors."
  ],
  "quest.25041E85AE09DAA7.title": "Energizer",
  "quest.25041E85AE09DAA7.quest_desc": [
    "With electricity and rotation it energizes items below on a depot or belt: iron to Overcharged Iron (1000 energy), gold (2000), diamond (10000). Pack change: the Advanced Energizer needs a reinforced alloy (Act III), the Reinforced one two ironwood ingots (Act IV)."
  ],
  "quest.30DCDED6F3E8103A.title": "New Age motors",
  "quest.30DCDED6F3E8103A.quest_desc": [
    "Electricity back into rotation. A wrench sets speed, stress capacity stays fixed; Motor Extensions behind it raise the capacity multiplier, and energy use with it. Redstone turns it off. Pack change: Advanced Motor needs a reinforced alloy (III), Reinforced an ironwood ingot (IV)."
  ],
  "quest.4FD6592D778686FD.title": "Solar heating plate",
  "quest.4FD6592D778686FD.quest_desc": [
    "In daylight it makes heat; Heat Pipes spread it and a Heat Pump pushes it on. Too much heat in one block melts it into lava, so always give heat somewhere to go. Pack change: the Basic plate takes an infused alloy (II); plates go by the dozen, so no component."
  ],
  "quest.4C05F500C1209A2A.title": "Boiler Heater",
  "quest.4C05F500C1209A2A.quest_desc": [
    "Like a Blaze Burner under a Create boiler, but it burns heat instead of fuel: more heat in, more out. Solar plates, pipes and a heater make a sun-powered steam engine. The Stirling Engine is the small version."
  ],
  "quest.022A04310ADE0F93.title": "Thorium reactor",
  "quest.022A04310ADE0F93.quest_desc": [
    "Reactor Rods, a Fuel Acceptor for Nuclear Fuel and Heat Vents to pipes. Radiation kills: wear leather armour or seal it in Reactor Casing or Glass. If nothing takes its heat, it melts down. Pack change: Reactor Rods need an ironwood ingot (Act IV)."
  ],
  "quest.37752415929A2864.title": "Street lights",
  "quest.37752415929A2864.quest_desc": [
    "Street Lights run on electricity; Lamp Posts are their poles. A lit road, a small nod to Solsticio, the city that keeps light."
  ],
  "quest.3B52B315368D80BC.title": "Two pricey recipes",
  "quest.3B52B315368D80BC.quest_desc": [
    "New Age can make an Enchanted Golden Apple by sequenced assembly (4 loops, 2,000,000 energy per energizing step) and Bottles o' Enchanting at 50000 energy each. Renewable, but costly."
  ],
  "quest.00B8D71B50937179.title": "Mastery: the Reinforced Motor",
  "quest.00B8D71B50937179.quest_desc": [
    "Close Heliodor's loop: sun heats a boiler, the boiler spins coils, coils feed energizers, and energized parts build the Reinforced Motor (Spectral Lens, Act IV). Crafts and Additions then shares the power with every FE mod."
  ],
  "chapter.0A79A5AC2E05D0F7.title": "Create: trains and packages",
  "chapter.0A79A5AC2E05D0F7.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Scheduled trains on your own rail network, and the Create 6 package network: packagers, frogports, stock tickers and factory gauges."
  ],
  "quest.77BE54FD7A175F6D.title": "Moving things far",
  "quest.77BE54FD7A175F6D.quest_desc": [
    "Belts are for one room. For distance, Create has trains (you and cargo on tracks) and packages (boxed items with an address, shipped by chain, train or hand). Trains and train postboxes keep working in unloaded chunks."
  ],
  "quest.696B32ED0CC51858.title": "No Steam 'n' Rails",
  "quest.696B32ED0CC51858.quest_desc": [
    "Steam 'n' Rails is not in the pack: its official releases stop at 1.20.1. You get Create's standard tracks, stations, signals and bogeys. To move yourself between buildings, Create Hypertube is the other option."
  ],
  "quest.1054891D3522FCFA.title": "Sturdy Sheet",
  "quest.1054891D3522FCFA.quest_desc": [
    "Crush obsidian into powder, then a short sequenced assembly: a Spout adds 500 mB of lava and a Press stamps it twice. One spout and one press over a looping belt keep sheets coming for casings and schedules."
  ],
  "quest.3EDBCACC92228200.title": "Train Casing",
  "quest.3EDBCACC92228200.quest_desc": [
    "A Sturdy Sheet on Brass Casing. Base of every railway block (stations, controls, signals, observers, doors), and used on a track it places a bogey while assembling a train."
  ],
  "quest.42C367280974A1FA.title": "Train Tracks",
  "quest.42C367280974A1FA.quest_desc": [
    "Sequenced assembly: a stone, smooth stone or andesite slab gets two iron or zinc nuggets, then a press. To lay track, click an existing piece, then a second spot: it fills straights, turns and slopes for you."
  ],
  "quest.497E4DA8ED2F1F47.title": "Laying track well",
  "quest.497E4DA8ED2F1F47.quest_desc": [
    "Hold sprint for the longest possible bend. Blocks in your off-hand pave under new track. Track laid into a Nether portal builds its twin on the other side, so trains cross dimensions."
  ],
  "quest.212CC36CDB8FECE1.title": "Train Station",
  "quest.212CC36CDB8FECE1.quest_desc": [
    "Train Casing and a compass. Select a track, place the station beside it. Stations are waypoints and assembly yards: switch to assembly mode and scheduled trains stay away while you build. A map clicked on it adds a marker."
  ],
  "quest.0CEABA006D2B2118.title": "Your first train",
  "quest.0CEABA006D2B2118.quest_desc": [
    "In assembly mode, use Train Casing on the track for bogeys, glue your blocks, put Train Controls on board and confirm at the station. A second set of controls lets it leave both ways. Drive with movement keys; the wheel sets top speed."
  ],
  "quest.2E7F74B4329FF2BD.title": "Train quirks",
  "quest.2E7F74B4329FF2BD.quest_desc": [
    "Trains only turn back into blocks at a station. Fuel in chests or barrels on board speeds them up, fuel in vaults is never burned. Sprint blows the whistle. In unloaded chunks trains still obey signals, but drills and other on-board machines stop."
  ],
  "quest.071C64C7436E52EA.title": "Train Schedule",
  "quest.071C64C7436E52EA.quest_desc": [
    "A program of stops, waits and conditions. Give it to a conductor seated at the controls: any mob or a Blaze Burner. Placed on a station, it copies itself to every train that stops there."
  ],
  "quest.78BDDCA133A5B020.title": "Train Signals",
  "quest.78BDDCA133A5B020.quest_desc": [
    "Signals split track into segments, one train each: no collisions. Scheduled trains never pass a signal from behind unless another faces the other way. Brass mode (wrench) also holds a train that could not clear the next segment: use it at busy junctions."
  ],
  "quest.4BD65852229A6C01.title": "Train Observer",
  "quest.4BD65852229A6C01.quest_desc": [
    "Select a track, place it nearby: it emits redstone when a train passes, optionally filtered by cargo. Doors, counters, loading triggers."
  ],
  "quest.2F45D98085540ED4.title": "Loading moving contraptions",
  "quest.2F45D98085540ED4.quest_desc": [
    "A Portable Storage Interface on the train and one on the ground, 1 or 2 blocks apart, connect as it passes; the train leaves once items stop moving. The fluid version does the same with tanks. Pair them with a station stop for automatic cargo runs."
  ],
  "quest.517A7FAE8B813A33.title": "Cardboard",
  "quest.517A7FAE8B813A33.quest_desc": [
    "Four pulpable items (bamboo, sugar cane, saplings) and 250 mB of water mix into Pulp; a press makes Cardboard. Packagers need it, and so does the whole package network."
  ],
  "quest.1E0F58C5183DBF70.title": "Packager",
  "quest.1E0F58C5183DBF70.quest_desc": [
    "Attached to an inventory, a redstone pulse boxes its items into a package you can carry. A package fed into a packager unwraps back into the inventory, only if everything fits. Contents stay together on belts, chains and trains."
  ],
  "quest.478FB83FAE0F57D1.title": "Addresses",
  "quest.478FB83FAE0F57D1.quest_desc": [
    "A sign on a packager stamps its text as the address. A Package Filter (zinc nuggets and wool) routes by address through funnels, tunnels and chutes. A clipboard clicked on frogports learns their addresses and auto-completes them later."
  ],
  "quest.49BFAD9BA3EA1AC8.title": "Chain Conveyor",
  "quest.49BFAD9BA3EA1AC8.quest_desc": [
    "A large cogwheel ringed by andesite casings; link two with chains. They carry rotation and packages, and you can ride them with a wrench (look at the branch you want at junctions). The roads of the package network."
  ],
  "quest.3C2865BB6A36E878.title": "Package Frogport",
  "quest.3C2865BB6A36E878.quest_desc": [
    "Click a chain conveyor with it, place it nearby and give it an address. Packages for other addresses ride the chain to the matching frogport; ones with no valid destination loop in place. It also feeds the inventory below it."
  ],
  "quest.1A3D29FDC0AED65F.title": "Postboxes and trains",
  "quest.1A3D29FDC0AED65F.quest_desc": [
    "A Postbox near a station with an address: trains stopping there pick up packages for elsewhere and drop off packages for here. Works in unloaded chunks, so a far outpost ships ore home without you."
  ],
  "quest.49C070B70EA98451.title": "Stock Link",
  "quest.49C070B70EA98451.quest_desc": [
    "Starts a stock network; click an existing link before placing a new one to join. Linked packagers expose their inventory to the network. Unlimited range, but packages still need a physical route. Full redstone stops a link; weaker redstone lowers its priority."
  ],
  "quest.41C4000F78AD0C5B.title": "Stock Ticker",
  "quest.41C4000F78AD0C5B.quest_desc": [
    "Bind it to a link and seat a mob or a Blaze Burner in front: your stock keeper. Right-click the keeper to browse the network and order items to any address. Hand it a Schematicannon clipboard and it orders a whole build."
  ],
  "quest.42885664A4CDB7C2.title": "Redstone Requester",
  "quest.42885664A4CDB7C2.quest_desc": [
    "Linked like the ticker, it orders a fixed list on every redstone pulse. One button, one delivery: the perfect «refill my building materials» switch."
  ],
  "quest.2D4095C7B60D3B42.title": "Table Cloth shops",
  "quest.2D4095C7B60D3B42.quest_desc": [
    "Packager, link and ticker make a shop: interact with the keeper holding a Table Cloth to create a trade, place it and price it. Buyers pay at the cashier, goods come out packaged, payment stays in the ticker. Trading without opening your chests."
  ],
  "quest.481386E35D624FCF.title": "Factory Gauge",
  "quest.481386E35D624FCF.quest_desc": [
    "A Stock Link plus a precision mechanism. On a packager it keeps one item stocked there by ordering from the network. Off a packager it sends ingredients to an address for processing; chained gauges form a board. On wrench-linked 3x3 crafters it arranges recipes itself."
  ],
  "quest.377C162FFC963F8A.title": "Re-Packager",
  "quest.377C162FFC963F8A.quest_desc": [
    "Big orders arrive split and can get mixed with other packages. A powered Re-Packager waits for every fragment and ships them as one package, in order. Factory gauges feeding crafters work much better with one."
  ],
  "quest.524CEFA7BBD1F988.title": "Mastery: the outpost line",
  "quest.524CEFA7BBD1F988.quest_desc": [
    "A train on a schedule with a postbox at each end, and a factory board at home keeping key items stocked by itself. AE2 or Refined Storage can take over storage later; packages stay the best way to move goods far without chunk loading."
  ],
  "chapter.57FF44A1C27D93F3.title": "Ender IO",
  "chapter.57FF44A1C27D93F3.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Grains of Infinity, alloys, capacitors, the SAG Mill, compact conduits, soul binding and travel anchors."
  ],
  "quest.18CC95E2E7626D94.title": "Compact tech",
  "quest.18CC95E2E7626D94.quest_desc": [
    "Capacitor-driven machines, special alloys, conduits that carry items, fluids, energy and redstone in one block, and soul devices. Its Micro Infinity (µI) is plain FE. The pack runs 8.2.11-beta, whose manual is a placeholder: EMI and tooltips are your guide."
  ],
  "quest.7DA214A4F9BC59FA.title": "Grains of Infinity",
  "quest.7DA214A4F9BC59FA.quest_desc": [
    "Light a fire on bedrock or deepslate in the Overworld: bedrock gives 1 to 3 grains 80% of the time, deepslate one grain 40% of the time and turns to cobble. Flint and steel at the world floor is the classic farm."
  ],
  "quest.7E0D175CBBC7CDD3.title": "Void Chassis and capacitors",
  "quest.7E0D175CBBC7CDD3.quest_desc": [
    "Iron and grains make the Void Chassis. Every machine needs a capacitor inside or it will not run: Basic, then Double-Layer and Octadic for speed and efficiency. Loot capacitors from dungeons carry random bonuses."
  ],
  "quest.6676A6EF8CFE49DE.title": "Stirling Generator and solar",
  "quest.6676A6EF8CFE49DE.quest_desc": [
    "The Stirling Generator burns furnace fuel, more efficiently with better capacitors. Photovoltaic Modules make power under open daylight. Capacitor Banks store it and grow when placed together."
  ],
  "quest.64098CFB83DA95CD.title": "Alloy Smelter",
  "quest.64098CFB83DA95CD.quest_desc": [
    "Makes Ender IO's alloys: Conductive, Energetic, Vibrant, Pulsating, Redstone, Dark Steel, Soularium and more (Dark Steel is iron, coal and obsidian). Everything later needs them: automate it early."
  ],
  "quest.175EF0469BEB8905.title": "SAG Mill and grinding balls",
  "quest.175EF0469BEB8905.quest_desc": [
    "Grinds ores with chance-based bonuses: a raw ore gives 1.8 dust on average. Grinding balls (Dark Steel, Energetic, Vibrant) raise output or cut power until they wear out. EMI shows the chances."
  ],
  "quest.467FB019AFE5FA43.title": "Conduits",
  "quest.467FB019AFE5FA43.quest_desc": [
    "Item, fluid, energy and redstone conduits share one block. Eight at a time from Conduit Binder and alloys, upgradable with more alloy. Each connection has its own screen: insert, extract, channel colour, priority, round robin, filters. Facades hide them behind any block."
  ],
  "quest.5DD4477B3B2385DE.title": "Conduit Probe and Yeta Wrench",
  "quest.5DD4477B3B2385DE.quest_desc": [
    "The Probe copies one connection's settings onto another; the Yeta Wrench rotates and configures. Crafting a configured machine alone in the grid wipes its settings: the fastest reset."
  ],
  "quest.1A93F83E09C77EC2.title": "More machines",
  "quest.1A93F83E09C77EC2.quest_desc": [
    "Slice'N'Splice makes parts like the Zombie Electrode from heads and alloys, the VAT ferments fluids, the Painting Machine re-skins blocks, the Enchanter makes chosen enchanted books, the Farming Station tends crops, chargers top up gear, and the Crafter automates recipes."
  ],
  "quest.576BD65CB87BF19A.title": "Soul Vials and the Soul Binder",
  "quest.576BD65CB87BF19A.quest_desc": [
    "A Soul Vial captures a mob's soul (the tooltip says which mobs work). The Soul Binder joins souls with items into mob-specific parts. Soularium, made with soul sand or soil, frames these machines."
  ],
  "quest.1D4A911B1A08FD3B.title": "Travel Anchors and the Staff",
  "quest.1D4A911B1A08FD3B.quest_desc": [
    "Anchors let you teleport between anchors you look at; the Staff of Travelling blinks you forward or to anchors (Alt+E in this pack). Pack change: both need a reinforced alloy (Act III), like the other teleporters."
  ],
  "quest.135564FDD80E7A6E.title": "Pack changes to Ender IO",
  "quest.135564FDD80E7A6E.quest_desc": [
    "Travel Anchor and Staff (III), Powered Spawner (IV), Octadic Capacitor (V). A data fix makes Enchantment Industry accept Ender IO's XP Juice. Unique alloys are untouched by Almost Unified."
  ],
  "quest.0BCADE43AF94113C.title": "Powered Spawner",
  "quest.0BCADE43AF94113C.quest_desc": [
    "A Broken Spawner, an ensouled chassis, soularium, vibrant crystals and a Z-Logic Controller: it spawns or clones its bound mob with energy. Pack change: an Ecosystem Capsule (IV) takes the Z-Logic Controller's place."
  ],
  "quest.72370EF5D8B4B9E2.title": "Handy blocks",
  "quest.72370EF5D8B4B9E2.quest_desc": [
    "Fused Quartz and Clear Glass (some glow, some block light), Dark Steel doors, bars and a fast ladder, timed Resetting Levers, silent pressure plates, obelisks (attractor, aversion, inhibitor, relocator, weather, XP) and the Vacuum Chest that sucks up items."
  ],
  "quest.76EAC1BDC93AA5BB.title": "Mastery: a base on conduits",
  "quest.76EAC1BDC93AA5BB.quest_desc": [
    "Octadic-capacitor machines, automatic alloys, Soul Binder parts and travel anchors in every room. Octadics need an atomic alloy (V): a good long-term goal."
  ],
  "chapter.43600649F9C8F913.title": "Immersive Engineering",
  "chapter.43600649F9C8F913.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Hammers and multiblocks, wires on poles, coke, steel, the metal press and crusher, oil, diesel and the excavator."
  ],
  "quest.56C0E235A8D6BCD8.title": "Industry by hand",
  "quest.56C0E235A8D6BCD8.quest_desc": [
    "Multiblocks built from blocks and formed with a hammer, power over visible wires on poles, and a chain from coke to steel to oil, all on FE. Its manual (a book and a lever) is complete. IE supplies the Calibration Frame's copper wire (II) and the Power Regulator's steel plates (III)."
  ],
  "quest.2B1BA98A994FB367.title": "Engineer's Hammer and tools",
  "quest.2B1BA98A994FB367.quest_desc": [
    "The Hammer forms multiblocks, configures blocks and turns an ingot into a plate. Wire Cutters remove wires and turn a plate into wire. The Screwdriver fine-tunes machines, the Voltmeter reads energy and redstone. Build a shape, then hammer the right block."
  ],
  "quest.16C6724941C8D5A0.title": "Copper wire for the Calibration Frame",
  "quest.16C6724941C8D5A0.quest_desc": [
    "IE wire cutters and a Create Saw turn copper plates into wire for your networks. The Power Regulator (III) takes 2 IE Steel Plates, hammered from steel ingots."
  ],
  "quest.6342BA3BE73211E7.title": "Coke Oven",
  "quest.6342BA3BE73211E7.quest_desc": [
    "27 Coke Bricks in a 3x3x3 cube, hammered on a side centre. Coal becomes Coal Coke, logs become charcoal, and Creosote Oil builds up: pull it with a bucket or pipe, the oven will not push it. Creosote makes Treated Wood."
  ],
  "quest.06A796A61550B901.title": "Blast Furnace and steel",
  "quest.06A796A61550B901.quest_desc": [
    "The Crude Blast Furnace (27 blast bricks) turns iron and coke into steel and slag, which must be emptied, and it cannot be automated. The Improved one (reinforced bricks) takes a hopper on top, outputs by itself and speeds up with two powered preheaters."
  ],
  "quest.0168B4C9C96BFEAC.title": "Alloy Kiln",
  "quest.0168B4C9C96BFEAC.quest_desc": [
    "Eight kiln bricks in a 2x2x2 cube: melts metals into Electrum and Constantan without dust, and makes insulating glass. Normal fuel, no power."
  ],
  "quest.47A1ECFDC78DB908.title": "IE ores",
  "quest.47A1ECFDC78DB908.quest_desc": [
    "Bauxite, lead, silver, nickel and uranium, at the heights in the manual's Ores page. Almost Unified ranks IE right after Create, so shared metals often come out as IE's. Industrial Hemp seeds drop from tall grass; hemp makes Tough Fabric."
  ],
  "quest.793BFE553E1E2058.title": "Kinetic Dynamo and first power",
  "quest.793BFE553E1E2058.quest_desc": [
    "The Kinetic Dynamo turns IE windmills and waterwheels into power (other mods' rotation does not count). Windmills like open space and storms, and cloth sails; up to three waterwheels share a shaft. The Thermoelectric Generator runs on a hot and a cold block."
  ],
  "quest.05A81D1DB02F0938.title": "Wires, connectors and relays",
  "quest.05A81D1DB02F0938.quest_desc": [
    "Click a coil on one connector, then another; blocks in the way break it. Connectors feed in or out, relays only join, transformers change voltage. The weakest wire sets the limit, and too many connectors on one wire burn it. Insulate LV and MV near paths."
  ],
  "quest.7FB271D328A5C07B.title": "Engineer's Workbench and blueprints",
  "quest.7FB271D328A5C07B.quest_desc": [
    "Crafts from Blueprints (molds, components, ammo) and upgrades the drill and revolver. Some blueprints are only found or bought from villagers. Metal Press molds come from here."
  ],
  "quest.562BC248458CD11F.title": "Metal Press and Crusher",
  "quest.562BC248458CD11F.quest_desc": [
    "The Press shapes plates, rods and wire with molds and packs 4 or 9 items into blocks. The Crusher turns ores to dust (2 per ore block) and crushes anything alive that falls in. Both take power on top; a screwdriver inverts their redstone."
  ],
  "quest.3D738FF3AE2B8D0E.title": "Arc Furnace",
  "quest.3D738FF3AE2B8D0E.quest_desc": [
    "A huge multiblock for big smelting and alloy batches, fast but power-hungry: an ore block gives 2 ingots plus slag. Its graphite electrodes wear out after about four days of nonstop use."
  ],
  "quest.2ADA08C03E175F63.title": "Mineral veins and the Excavator",
  "quest.2ADA08C03E175F63.quest_desc": [
    "Survey Tools on natural rock point to hidden veins; a Core Sample Drill tells contents and yield. The Excavator, a giant bucket wheel, digs the vein out slowly. A steady mixed-ore source near home."
  ],
  "quest.485936812C7CF65C.title": "Plant oil, ethanol and diesel",
  "quest.485936812C7CF65C.quest_desc": [
    "The Squeezer presses plant oil, the Fermenter makes ethanol, the Refinery mixes them into biodiesel. The Diesel Generator, IE's main high-voltage source, burns it fast. IE plant oil also fuels Create's liquid burner."
  ],
  "quest.29ABDA7768135140.title": "Conveyors and cloches",
  "quest.29ABDA7768135140.quest_desc": [
    "IE conveyors move items and mobs with no power; the hammer turns or tilts them. The Garden Cloche grows crops with power and water, faster with fertilizer, and outputs the harvest."
  ],
  "quest.2A77986568EE89F3.title": "Drill, revolver and toolbox",
  "quest.2A77986568EE89F3.quest_desc": [
    "The fuel-powered Mining Drill takes Workbench upgrades; the Revolver fires crafted cartridges; the Toolbox carries tools as a placeable box. The skyhook zips you along your power lines."
  ],
  "quest.2725113511A576AF.title": "Mastery: high voltage",
  "quest.2725113511A576AF.quest_desc": [
    "HV lines across the base, a diesel plant fed by squeezer and fermenter, an excavator on a rich vein and a press making plates on demand. Steel plates, wire and treated wood are worth mass-producing."
  ],
  "chapter.3C61790E81E68D20.title": "Industrial Foregoing",
  "chapter.3C61790E81E68D20.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Latex and plastic, machine frames, farms and mob machines, biofuel, laser drills and the Infinity tools."
  ],
  "quest.741230D6934E57D0.title": "Automate the chores",
  "quest.741230D6934E57D0.quest_desc": [
    "Powered machines on frames handle the boring parts: tree tapping, farms, animals and mobs, enchanting helpers, fluid generators and a laser drill pulling ores from the void. Machines take range, speed and efficiency addons; EMI shows every rate."
  ],
  "quest.39204F03E7858E49.title": "Latex",
  "quest.39204F03E7858E49.quest_desc": [
    "A Tree Fluid Extractor facing a log drains Latex, slowly eating (stripping first) the log. Several extractors share a log, and power speeds them up. A row of trees plus a row of extractors: the base of plastic."
  ],
  "quest.727410A74B375E43.title": "Dry rubber and plastic",
  "quest.727410A74B375E43.quest_desc": [
    "The Latex Processing Unit turns 750 mB latex and 500 mB water into Dry Rubber; smelt it into Plastic, which most IF machines want. IF plastic counts for other mods asking for the common tag."
  ],
  "quest.5D0DB71E2671162C.title": "Machine frames",
  "quest.5D0DB71E2671162C.quest_desc": [
    "Every machine sits on a frame: Pity, Simple, Advanced, Supreme. The frame tier decides what you can build. The Pitiful Generator burns fuel even when full: a starter only."
  ],
  "quest.7B14B966A928BC45.title": "Addons",
  "quest.7B14B966A928BC45.quest_desc": [
    "Range addons grow the work area (1 per tier), Speed addons run the bar faster, Efficiency addons cut ticks per operation (10%, 20%). Range first on farms, speed and efficiency on processors."
  ],
  "quest.4D1BE172ABD25E27.title": "Dissolution Chamber",
  "quest.4D1BE172ABD25E27.quest_desc": [
    "A shapeless crafter with up to 8 items and one fluid in, items or fluid out, slots locked to the current recipe. Advanced IF parts and the Infinity tools come from here. Feed it by pipe."
  ],
  "quest.0C88FF716F10EB13.title": "Plant farms",
  "quest.0C88FF716F10EB13.quest_desc": [
    "Sower plants, Fertilizer boosts, Gatherer chops whole trees and harvests crops (making a little Sludge; with Ether Gas it replants). The Hydroponic Bed speeds crops with power and water, lava for Nether crops."
  ],
  "quest.29AFDBA1ED9999CA.title": "Animal machines",
  "quest.29AFDBA1ED9999CA.quest_desc": [
    "Feeder breeds, Rancher shears and milks, Baby Separator moves babies behind it, Sewer collects Sewage and turns experience into Essence. A pen with all four needs nobody."
  ],
  "quest.72C5245C8ADF8D10.title": "Mob machines",
  "quest.72C5245C8ADF8D10.quest_desc": [
    "The Mob Crusher kills like a player (loot plus Essence, or loot with random Fortune); the Slaughter Factory grinds mobs into Liquid Meat and pink slime. The Mob Imprisonment Tool carries a mob. Pack change: an Ecosystem Capsule (IV) takes the Mob Duplicator's nether wart."
  ],
  "quest.4478747B4E03DE0C.title": "Bioreactor and biofuel",
  "quest.4478747B4E03DE0C.quest_desc": [
    "The Bioreactor turns organics plus water into Biofuel, more per item the more variety inside. The Biofuel Generator burns it at 160 RF/t and stops when full. It also super-heats a Create liquid burner."
  ],
  "quest.02B9CCE34B2AF277.title": "Mycelial generators",
  "quest.02B9CCE34B2AF277.quest_desc": [
    "Small generators, each burning something different. The Mycelial Reactor (Dissolution Chamber) pays big only while one of every kind runs at once. A collector's power plant."
  ],
  "quest.5C7DAD790FAABD23.title": "Laser drills",
  "quest.5C7DAD790FAABD23.quest_desc": [
    "An Ore Laser Base, powered by Laser Drills one block away, pulls ores from nothing; coloured lenses bias the odds (EMI lists them). The Fluid Laser Base does fluids, and Ether Gas over a Wither. Pack change: Ore base needs an ironwood ingot (IV), Fluid base a reinforced alloy (III)."
  ],
  "quest.54F34F4D22EB3F58.title": "Enchanting machines",
  "quest.54F34F4D22EB3F58.quest_desc": [
    "The Extractor pulls enchantments into books or Essence, the Applicator is an anvil paid in Essence, the Factory enchants at level 30, the Sorter splits enchanted from plain. Fed by a mob crusher, enchanting becomes a pipeline."
  ],
  "quest.7BCF4869E3A03331.title": "Conveyors and transporters",
  "quest.7BCF4869E3A03331.quest_desc": [
    "IF Conveyors move items, mobs and (flat) fluids; glowstone speeds them. Transporters move items, fluids or world actions between inventories one block apart, several in one block. Black Hole Units hold 2,147,483,647 of one item; Black Hole Tanks the same in mB."
  ],
  "quest.3476A97FD3FC45EC.title": "Infinity tools",
  "quest.3476A97FD3FC45EC.quest_desc": [
    "Drill, Saw, Hammer, Trident, Launcher, Backpack and Nuke from the Dissolution Chamber, stronger with more stored power (Poor to Artifact); biofuel inside replaces power and drops teleport to you. Sneak-right-click opens them. Pack change: Drill needs a reinforced alloy (III), Nuke an ironwood ingot (IV)."
  ],
  "quest.71A29C6CA68EFB8B.title": "Pack changes to IF",
  "quest.71A29C6CA68EFB8B.quest_desc": [
    "Gated: Fluid Laser Base and Infinity Drill (III), Ore Laser Base, Mob Duplicator and Infinity Nuke (IV). Fixed: IF's Curios slot list (two invalid names removed), and Enchantment Industry now accepts IF Essence. Plastic, frames and farms stay native."
  ],
  "quest.611CC8944281877D.title": "Mastery: chores solved",
  "quest.611CC8944281877D.quest_desc": [
    "An ore laser with drills and lenses, a mob tower feeding an enchanting line and an Infinity tool levelled high. IF does the chores; you keep the exploring."
  ],
  "chapter.0523A72316E8384F.title": "Just Dire Things",
  "chapter.0523A72316E8384F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Goo that transforms blocks, four material tiers with upgradable tools and armour, simple and advanced machines, portals and time."
  ],
  "quest.2E126AE3714D3399.title": "Goo-driven progression",
  "quest.2E126AE3714D3399.quest_desc": [
    "Goo blocks transform the blocks beside them. Each of four goo tiers unlocks a material (Ferricore, Blazegold, Celestigem, Eclipse Alloy) with upgradable tools and armour, plus simple (no power) and advanced (FE) machines. The guide book is craftable; JEI has a Goo Spreading tab."
  ],
  "quest.33971CF3851DF109.title": "Primogel Goo",
  "quest.33971CF3851DF109.quest_desc": [
    "Clay, dirt, rotten flesh and sugar make Primogel Goo. Place it and right-click it with its food to activate it (the block tells you which). Then put an iron block next to it: the goo turns it into a Raw Ferricore Block. Goo that runs out goes Exhausted and needs feeding again."
  ],
  "quest.029C6C63C1D5064D.title": "Ferricore",
  "quest.029C6C63C1D5064D.quest_desc": [
    "Mine the Raw Ferricore Block for Raw Ferricore and smelt it into Ferricore Ingots, a sturdier iron. They make the first tools and armour, the Ferricore Wrench (rotates blocks, links swappers) and Blank Upgrades."
  ],
  "quest.6DA306F2EF01A023.title": "Better coal",
  "quest.6DA306F2EF01A023.quest_desc": [
    "A coal block next to Primogel Goo becomes Primal Coal, which lasts longer and gives more FE in generators. Each higher goo upgrades the previous coal: Blaze Ember, Voidflame Coal and Eclipse Ember, the densest fuel of all."
  ],
  "quest.5AC1205779494828.title": "Tools and their keys",
  "quest.5AC1205779494828.quest_desc": [
    "Each material has pickaxe, axe, shovel, hoe, sword, bow (and paxel at the top tiers). Hold Shift over a tool to see which upgrades it takes. In this pack, Alt+T switches all of a tool's abilities on or off and Shift+T opens its settings, where you toggle each upgrade and bind hotkeys; you can also Shift-click the tool in hand."
  ],
  "quest.70326800B28E4D69.title": "Upgrades",
  "quest.70326800B28E4D69.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrades are crafted from a Blank Upgrade and installed with the tool in a Smithing Table. Some are passive (Ore Miner mines connected ores, Tree Feller fells whole trees), some are used on demand (Ore Scanner shows ores through walls), and some cost durability or FE (Smelter smelts drops). The Hammer upgrade mines 3x3 on blazegold, 5x5 on celestigem and 7x7 on eclipse alloy."
  ],
  "quest.3C94D3074187F71D.title": "Armour and its upgrades",
  "quest.3C94D3074187F71D.quest_desc": [
    "Every tier has armour with its own upgrades, installed the same way: night vision, step height, negate fall damage, run and swim speed, lava immunity, elytra wings and more. Open the tool settings with a tool in hand and click a worn piece to toggle its abilities."
  ],
  "quest.1153F5D0877F380F.title": "Blazebloom Goo and Blazegold",
  "quest.1153F5D0877F380F.quest_desc": [
    "Primogel Goo with blaze powder, redstone and nether wart makes Blazebloom Goo. It turns a gold block into Raw Blazegold, smelted into Blazegold Ingots for the second tier."
  ],
  "quest.456AD35C5C20C680.title": "Tier templates",
  "quest.456AD35C5C20C680.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrade Templates move a tool or armour piece to the next tier in a Smithing Table without losing its installed upgrades. A template can be copied with two ingots of its material."
  ],
  "quest.6A34D999CCB88294.title": "Simple machines",
  "quest.6A34D999CCB88294.quest_desc": [
    "Simple machines need no power and act on the block or entity in front: Block Breaker (uses a tool you give it), Block Placer, Clicker (right, left or held clicks with an item, even on mobs), Dropper, Sensor, Swapper and fluid machines. Set their speed in ticks and their redstone mode, including one action per pulse."
  ],
  "quest.2491EF53E6ED64AE.title": "Advanced machines and power",
  "quest.2491EF53E6ED64AE.quest_desc": [
    "Advanced machines run on FE, cover a set area, filter, and charge FE items inside them. Power them with the coal generator (special coals give more) or the Fuel Generator. The Energy Transmitter beams FE to machines in its area, with a small intended loss."
  ],
  "quest.58C445EC82D97FF7.title": "Pocket Generator and canisters",
  "quest.58C445EC82D97FF7.quest_desc": [
    "The Pocket Generator burns coal (better with the special coals) to keep your FE tools and armour charged on the go. The Fluid Canister holds 8 buckets and can auto-fill other containers; the Fuel Canister feeds the pocket generator."
  ],
  "quest.5CA0446ED94B38A0.title": "Polymorphic fluid and refined fuels",
  "quest.5CA0446ED94B38A0.quest_desc": [
    "Drop a Polymorphic Catalyst (blazegold and nether wart) into water to get Polymorphic Fluid, the base of JDT fluids. Drop Blaze Ember into it and let Blazebloom Goo refine it into a fuel; higher coals and goos make better refined fuels for the Fuel Generator."
  ],
  "quest.3C3DDECD763F0D21.title": "VoidShimmer Goo and Celestigem",
  "quest.3C3DDECD763F0D21.quest_desc": [
    "Blazebloom Goo with ender pearls, end stone and dragon's breath makes VoidShimmer Goo, so you need the End first. It turns a diamond block into Raw Celestigem, used for energy storage and teleportation."
  ],
  "quest.7C8D885F7153DA80.title": "Portal Guns",
  "quest.7C8D885F7153DA80.quest_desc": [
    "Left-click fires a blue portal and right-click an orange one; players and items pass between them. The Advanced Portal Gun adds a favourites menu to open a portal to a saved spot from anywhere, and runs on Portal Fluid, which must be stabilised with VoidShimmer Goo to exist outside the End.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: both guns need a reinforced alloy (Act III)."
  ],
  "quest.3C0722B85E6E4444.title": "Shadowpulse Goo and Eclipse Alloy",
  "quest.3C0722B85E6E4444.quest_desc": [
    "VoidShimmer Goo with sculk, a sculk shrieker and echo shards makes Shadowpulse Goo: a trip to the Deep Dark. It turns a netherite block into Raw Eclipse Alloy, the strongest material of the mod."
  ],
  "quest.08FFBA668B6B01AB.title": "Flight upgrade",
  "quest.08FFBA668B6B01AB.quest_desc": [
    "The Flight upgrade gives creative-style flight in survival for your armour, draining FE to keep you up: carry a Pocket Generator.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: it needs a Horizon Chart (Act IV)."
  ],
  "quest.730A505CE9A6F44A.title": "Time Crystals and the Time Wand",
  "quest.730A505CE9A6F44A.quest_desc": [
    "Shadowpulse Goo turns budding amethyst into a Budding Time Crystal that must soak time energy in the Overworld, Nether and End, in that order; it shatters if mined, so move it some other way. The Time Wand speeds any ticking block for 30 seconds. Pack change: the wand needs an atomic alloy (V)."
  ],
  "quest.7A52BC6A10427B4A.title": "Paradox Machine",
  "quest.7A52BC6A10427B4A.quest_desc": [
    "Takes a snapshot of an area (raw ore blocks and entities) and can later rewind it to that moment. Overusing it creates a Paradox that grows and devours blocks, items and entities for good: read the book before experimenting.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: it needs an atomic alloy (Act V)."
  ],
  "quest.182D2ECF5D2DE057.title": "Mastery: Eclipse Alloy gear",
  "quest.182D2ECF5D2DE057.quest_desc": [
    "Carry your favourite pickaxe through all four tiers with templates, keeping every upgrade, and finish it in Eclipse Alloy: 7x7 hammer, ore miner, smelter, and drops sent straight to a bound chest if your tool takes Drop Teleport."
  ],
  "chapter.0775FB2AC54A1E8D.title": "Mekanism: machines and infusion",
  "chapter.0775FB2AC54A1E8D.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Osmium, steel, the Metallurgic Infuser, circuits and alloys, upgrades, factories and the addons that extend Mekanism."
  ],
  "quest.1AB796481B24C657.title": "Heavy industry",
  "quest.1AB796481B24C657.quest_desc": [
    "Electric machines, chemicals piped like fluids, ore processing up to five ingots per ore, its own logistics, reactors and the MekaSuit. Mekanism machines take FE from any mod. Ores, energy and logistics each have their own chapter."
  ],
  "quest.453870346F22C04D.title": "Osmium and friends",
  "quest.453870346F22C04D.quest_desc": [
    "Osmium ore shows up at almost any height; Mekanism also adds tin, lead, uranium and fluorite. Mine plenty of osmium: nearly every machine, starting with the Infuser, eats it."
  ],
  "quest.19CB5696848FEBD9.title": "Metallurgic Infuser",
  "quest.19CB5696848FEBD9.quest_desc": [
    "Furnace, iron, osmium and redstone. It combines an item with a stored infuse type (carbon, redstone, diamond, refined obsidian): material on the left, item in the middle. Steel, circuits and every alloy come from here. Left ungated so Mekanism can start in Act II."
  ],
  "quest.3C5B69282B68529E.title": "Enrich first",
  "quest.3C5B69282B68529E.quest_desc": [
    "One coal gives 10 carbon in the Infuser; enriched in an Enrichment Chamber it gives 80. Same for redstone, diamond and obsidian. Once you have the chamber, feed the Infuser enriched materials: eight times less mining."
  ],
  "quest.091376A558055EC0.title": "Steel",
  "quest.091376A558055EC0.quest_desc": [
    "Iron plus carbon makes Enriched Iron; that plus carbon makes Steel Dust; smelt it. Any steel ingot works where a recipe asks for steel (Almost Unified shows IE's)."
  ],
  "quest.49BE73F80D49E351.title": "Steel Casing",
  "quest.49BE73F80D49E351.quest_desc": [
    "Steel, glass and an osmium ingot: the frame of almost every Mekanism machine. Make a few at once."
  ],
  "quest.632A4DCDEDCA47B9.title": "Control circuits",
  "quest.632A4DCDEDCA47B9.quest_desc": [
    "Osmium infused with redstone is a Basic Control Circuit. Each tier up: the previous circuit plus two alloys, or infused (Advanced redstone, Elite diamond, Ultimate refined obsidian). Pack change: two basic circuits go into the Power Regulator (Act III)."
  ],
  "quest.4B74368CFAAEB506.title": "The alloy chain",
  "quest.4B74368CFAAEB506.quest_desc": [
    "Infused Alloy is copper plus redstone; Reinforced is that plus diamond; Atomic is that plus refined obsidian. Each tier of circuits, installers and cables wants its alloy. Pack change: the alloys mark the acts. Infused is Act II material, Reinforced Act III (jetpack straps, Flux plugs, mining gadgets) and Atomic Act V (the Ark Bus, rockets, Draconic cores); only the infuser makes them."
  ],
  "quest.4F591F844FDAF9EA.title": "Enrichment Chamber",
  "quest.4F591F844FDAF9EA.quest_desc": [
    "Your first ore doubler: one ore block, two dusts. It also enriches infuse materials and turns gravel into flint. Pair it with an Energized Smelter."
  ],
  "quest.54780C8D09E34E22.title": "The basic set",
  "quest.54780C8D09E34E22.quest_desc": [
    "Energized Smelter (electric furnace), Crusher (ingots to dust), Precision Sawmill (more planks plus sawdust), Combiner (raw ore and cobble back into ore blocks), Osmium Compressor (dusts into special ingots like refined obsidian). Same GUI everywhere: energy, sides, upgrades."
  ],
  "quest.6F5634156B7CBD6D.title": "Side configuration",
  "quest.6F5634156B7CBD6D.quest_desc": [
    "Each face gets a colour (input, output, energy or nothing), and auto-eject pushes results out by itself. The Configurator does it in the world and rotates blocks; a Configuration Card copies settings between machines. Most «my machine does nothing» is a side set wrong."
  ],
  "quest.661FA7821F2D1A57.title": "Upgrades",
  "quest.661FA7821F2D1A57.quest_desc": [
    "Speed (faster), Energy (efficiency and capacity), Chemical, Muffling, Filter (heavy water pumping), Stone Generator and Anchor (keeps the chunk loaded), each with a maximum. Speed without Energy drinks power: add both."
  ],
  "quest.44FCC2FE085BE2FB.title": "Factories and tier installers",
  "quest.44FCC2FE085BE2FB.quest_desc": [
    "Factories run several jobs at once: Basic 3, Advanced 5, Elite 7, Ultimate 9. Craft one from a machine, or click a placed machine with a Tier Installer to upgrade it in place, contents kept. Most processing machines have one. One upgraded factory replaces a row of machines."
  ],
  "quest.0D7CDFC225E69930.title": "Bins and personal storage",
  "quest.0D7CDFC225E69930.quest_desc": [
    "A Bin holds a big stack of one item, in tiers. Personal Chests and Barrels hold 54 slots, open from your inventory and can be locked to you. The Cardboard Box picks up a whole block with its contents."
  ],
  "quest.66246893B6524D29.title": "Formulaic Assemblicator",
  "quest.66246893B6524D29.quest_desc": [
    "An electric crafting table: write a recipe onto a Crafting Formula and it crafts from what you feed it. Great for small automated recipes before AE2 or Refined Storage."
  ],
  "quest.22BECC4BB3890D57.title": "Mekanism Tools",
  "quest.22BECC4BB3890D57.quest_desc": [
    "Tools and armour in osmium, bronze, steel, lapis, refined glowstone and refined obsidian, plus a Paxel (pickaxe, axe and shovel) for every material, vanilla included. The Atomic Disassembler is a powered all-in-one with several mining modes."
  ],
  "quest.5806AB6DDADBB8C8.title": "Jetpack and gear",
  "quest.5806AB6DDADBB8C8.quest_desc": [
    "The Jetpack burns hydrogen from an Electrolytic Separator and switches between Regular, Hover and off; in this pack it burns 2.5 mB per tick instead of 1, like every jetpack. Scuba gear and Free Runners cover water and falls. In this pack, Mekanism mode keys are Alt plus the arrow keys."
  ],
  "quest.2AA764325E9BCC16.title": "MekaSuit and Meka-Tool",
  "quest.2AA764325E9BCC16.quest_desc": [
    "Powered armour and tool that take modules (jetpack, gravitational modulation, vision, fortune, silk touch, vein mining and more) at a Modification Station; many stack. Expensive: plan it after fission and atomic alloy."
  ],
  "quest.2E9CD35014A85B5B.title": "Mekanism Extras",
  "quest.2E9CD35014A85B5B.quest_desc": [
    "Goes past Ultimate with Absolute, Supreme, Cosmic and Infinite factories, cubes, cables, tanks, bins and induction parts. Adds Naquadah ore (rare near bedrock, commoner in the End near the void), a Naquadah Reactor and a Stack Upgrade. Its Creative Upgrade has no recipe here."
  ],
  "quest.2116AE17C6925F49.title": "Mekanism: More Machine",
  "quest.2116AE17C6925F49.quest_desc": [
    "Planting Station, CNC Stamper, Lathe, Rolling Mill, Presser, Recycler, Ambient Gas Collector, wireless charging and transmission, large machines and more factories. Pack change: replicators removed and their data emptied, planting compat off, so nothing copies items or seeds from thin air."
  ],
  "quest.49145D699B5F7037.title": "Dictionary and tags",
  "quest.49145D699B5F7037.quest_desc": [
    "Point it at any item, block or fluid to see its tags. With Almost Unified and several mods making the same metal, tags are what recipes really ask for. A machine refuses an ingot? Check its tags."
  ],
  "quest.68A3BD4A0922BE6C.title": "Creative Mekanism",
  "quest.68A3BD4A0922BE6C.quest_desc": [
    "Creative Energy Cube, Fluid Tank and Chemical Tank cost two Luminosities each (Act VI); the Creative Bin cannot be crafted. The rest of Mekanism stays native, apart from the components noted here."
  ],
  "quest.0D42E7962747E44D.title": "Mastery: Ultimate tier",
  "quest.0D42E7962747E44D.quest_desc": [
    "Ultimate Tier Installers need Atomic Alloy and Ultimate circuits. Push your main factories to Ultimate and they run 9 at a time. Extras goes further, and the reactors pay for it all."
  ],
  "chapter.4724990E0FB0E0AA.title": "Mekanism: ore processing",
  "chapter.4724990E0FB0E0AA.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From two to five ingots per ore: enrichment, purification, injection and dissolution, and when raw ore beats Silk Touch."
  ],
  "quest.0B942D4A129D62CE.title": "Four stacked tiers",
  "quest.0B942D4A129D62CE.quest_desc": [
    "Each tier puts one machine in front of the last chain: Enrichment (2 per ore), Purification (3), Chemical Injection (4), Dissolution with washing and crystallizing (5). Build in order; nothing from an earlier tier is wasted."
  ],
  "quest.23DDAEDB68C22955.title": "Tier 1: Enrichment (x2)",
  "quest.23DDAEDB68C22955.quest_desc": [
    "One ore block gives 2 dusts; 3 raw ores give 4, a raw block 12. Smelt the dust anywhere. Auto-eject the chamber into an Energized Smelter and every ore doubles."
  ],
  "quest.1C262970740A5BD8.title": "Raw ore or Silk Touch?",
  "quest.1C262970740A5BD8.quest_desc": [
    "Per ore block: 2, 3, 4 or 5 ingots. Per raw ore: about 1.33, 2, 2.67 or 3.33. Fortune III averages 2.2 raw per iron or gold ore, so roughly 2.9, 4.4, 5.9 or 7.3: raw wins at every tier. Never Combine raw back into ore blocks (8 raw per block)."
  ],
  "quest.665DAC3A063D6BCE.title": "Oxygen",
  "quest.665DAC3A063D6BCE.quest_desc": [
    "An Electrolytic Separator splits water into hydrogen and oxygen; send the oxygen by Pressurized Tube. Hydrogen fuels jetpacks and gas generators, or gets dumped. Shortcut: flint in a machine's chemical slot becomes oxygen."
  ],
  "quest.03EDC15E24003218.title": "Tier 2: Purification (x3)",
  "quest.03EDC15E24003218.quest_desc": [
    "Oxygen turns one ore block into 3 Clumps (a raw ore into 2). A Crusher makes Dirty Dust, the Enrichment Chamber cleans it. Chain: ore, purification, crusher, enrichment, smelter."
  ],
  "quest.22349F7776839BAD.title": "Hydrogen chloride",
  "quest.22349F7776839BAD.quest_desc": [
    "Brine (from a Thermal Evaporation Plant) splits into sodium and chlorine in a separator; a Chemical Infuser joins chlorine and hydrogen. Easier start: salt dust in the machine's chemical slot turns straight into hydrogen chloride."
  ],
  "quest.69531B1053799E84.title": "Tier 3: Chemical Injection (x4)",
  "quest.69531B1053799E84.quest_desc": [
    "Hydrogen chloride turns one ore block into 4 Shards (3 raw ores into 8). Shards go into purification as clumps and down the chain. It is an elite machine: better circuits and alloys."
  ],
  "quest.79384642C4B83DC2.title": "Sulfuric acid",
  "quest.79384642C4B83DC2.quest_desc": [
    "Oxidize sulfur dust, infuse with oxygen, then with water vapour. Or shortcut: sulfur dust in the Dissolution Chamber's chemical slot becomes acid. Sulfur comes from gunpowder injected with HCl, or coal gasified in a Pressurized Reaction Chamber."
  ],
  "quest.4BF21CA6DB94B673.title": "Tier 4: Dissolution (x5)",
  "quest.4BF21CA6DB94B673.quest_desc": [
    "Sulfuric acid dissolves an ore block into 1000 mB of dirty slurry (3 raw give 2000). A Chemical Washer cleans it, a Crystallizer makes one crystal per 200 mB: 5 per ore. Crystals enter injection and continue down. Three ultimate machines: plan the space."
  ],
  "quest.1542F3F004374F41.title": "Laying out the chain",
  "quest.1542F3F004374F41.quest_desc": [
    "Build backwards from the smelter, auto-ejecting each machine into the next. Items by Logistical Transporter, chemicals by Pressurized Tube, water by Mechanical Pipe. When one stage bottlenecks, upgrade it to a factory in place."
  ],
  "quest.7AAD6A41961878DE.title": "Thermal Evaporation Plant",
  "quest.7AAD6A41961878DE.quest_desc": [
    "A tower of Thermal Evaporation Blocks with one Controller and Valves: water in, brine out; brine in, lithium out. It runs faster when hotter. Brine feeds HCl and salt; lithium feeds tritium for fusion."
  ],
  "quest.0DEC133F39D372BF.title": "Every ore in the pack counts",
  "quest.0DEC133F39D372BF.quest_desc": [
    "Recipes use common tags (c:ores/iron, c:raw_materials/iron), so other mods' ores run the same chain and Almost Unified hands you the pack's ingot at the end. New Age thorium has no common ore tag on purpose."
  ],
  "quest.6EFE26582A231FEF.title": "Processing factories",
  "quest.6EFE26582A231FEF.quest_desc": [
    "Enriching, purifying and injecting have factories: an Ultimate Purifying Factory handles 9 ores on one oxygen supply. One Speed and one Energy upgrade per stage; raise the tier where the queue grows."
  ],
  "quest.6F0050EE9FA20B34.title": "Naquadah and silver",
  "quest.6F0050EE9FA20B34.quest_desc": [
    "Extras adds Naquadah ore (rare near bedrock, commoner in the End near the void) with its own dust, clump, shard and crystal steps; More Machine adds silver. Same chain. Naquadah fuels the Extras reactor."
  ],
  "quest.097681B4961E86A7.title": "Mastery: five per ore",
  "quest.097681B4961E86A7.quest_desc": [
    "Automate the whole x5 line, dissolution to smelter. It is the richest per ore block among the classic chains; Oritech's acid gem route goes further per raw ore (see Ore processing)."
  ],
  "chapter.02DDF32800651F47.title": "Modern Industrialization",
  "chapter.02DDF32800651F47.chapter_subtitle": [
    "From the Forge Hammer and steam to electricity, oil, nuclear power and the quantum tier: a factory that never stops."
  ],
  "quest.3DA37A4FD2C99709.title": "A factory in ages",
  "quest.3DA37A4FD2C99709.quest_desc": [
    "Steam Age with bronze and steel, Electric Age with cables, voltage tiers, oil and multiblocks, then nuclear, fusion and quantum. MI's guidebook (a book and copper nuggets) explains every step; it is not given on join, but it is craftable. MI thinks in continuous lines, not one-off crafts."
  ],
  "quest.6A9E672D5673C8DD.title": "Run machines nonstop",
  "quest.6A9E672D5673C8DD.quest_desc": [
    "Electric MI machines overclock the longer they run and lose it when idle, so MI's own guide warns against driving them on demand from AE2 or RS. Run lines constantly into buffers and let storage pull from the buffers."
  ],
  "quest.0DA5E26857F9CA09.title": "Forge Hammer",
  "quest.0DA5E26857F9CA09.quest_desc": [
    "Your first MI machine, by hand: an ore block gives 2 raw (3 with a Hammer tool in its slot), double ingots become plates, rods, rings and bolts. The Steam Mining Drill mines 3x3 with Silk Touch, the perfect partner."
  ],
  "quest.469475EF9C03C3A6.title": "Bronze",
  "quest.469475EF9C03C3A6.quest_desc": [
    "Hammer copper and tin into dusts, combine into bronze dust, smelt. A Mixer gives a better ratio later; nine tiny dusts make one. Build a Bronze Compressor before the boiler: plates get much cheaper."
  ],
  "quest.47D69210583ECE20.title": "Bronze Boiler and steam machines",
  "quest.47D69210583ECE20.quest_desc": [
    "The boiler heats up and feeds steam to adjacent machines. Bronze machines run up to 2 EU/t and 1 mB of steam is 1 EU, so a hot boiler feeds four. Compressor, Macerator, Mixer, Cutting Machine, and a steam Furnace that uses ten times less fuel than vanilla. A Water Pump keeps it full."
  ],
  "quest.6161797455ACD079.title": "Machine handling",
  "quest.6161797455ACD079.quest_desc": [
    "Steam machines take inputs from any side. Lock a slot to one item, scroll to cap it, turn on auto-eject. A wrench rotates, and sneaking sets the output side; break machines with a pickaxe, not the wrench. Hold a wrench near a multiblock controller to see what is missing."
  ],
  "quest.295CC424254D2956.title": "MI pipes",
  "quest.295CC424254D2956.quest_desc": [
    "Three pipes fit in one block; colours do not mix. Fluid pipes carry one fluid and connect to blocks only when wrenched. Item pipes start as whitelists, so nothing moves until you set the filter or switch to blacklist. Motors speed item pipes up."
  ],
  "quest.057F22F8C91B1B17.title": "Coke Oven",
  "quest.057F22F8C91B1B17.quest_desc": [
    "Controller, 21 bricks and three hatches (items in, items out, steam in) turn coal into coke; a fluid output hatch catches creosote. Hatches replace bricks anywhere. Coke burns four times longer than coal and leads to steel."
  ],
  "quest.045F585D14FC7B1D.title": "Steel and the Steam Blast Furnace",
  "quest.045F585D14FC7B1D.quest_desc": [
    "Coke dust plus iron gives Uncooked Steel Dust, cooked in a Steam Blast Furnace (coke oven shape in fire clay bricks, one extra hollow layer). Steel machines are twice as fast with new recipes; sneak-click a bronze machine with a Steel Upgrade to convert it."
  ],
  "quest.65B2AF2AA4A5C977.title": "Steam Quarry",
  "quest.65B2AF2AA4A5C977.quest_desc": [
    "A steam multiblock that eats bronze drills to dig below bedrock and returns ores (EMI lists them). Steel-hungry: build it after a few blast furnaces. Pack change: the Electric Quarry needs two ironwood ingots (Act IV)."
  ],
  "quest.06A9F570B460CEDF.title": "Electric Age",
  "quest.06A9F570B460CEDF.quest_desc": [
    "The Steam Turbine turns 1 mB of steam into 1 EU (up to 32 mB/t) and outputs only to cables on its output side. Cables have tiers (copper, silver, tin LV; cupronickel, electrum MV); single-block machines take LV only; transformers step between. Here 1 EU = 10 FE."
  ],
  "quest.347E05CC70B27244.title": "Rubber and cables",
  "quest.347E05CC70B27244.quest_desc": [
    "Coke dust and water mix into Raw Synthetic Oil, the blast furnace cooks it, and with paper it becomes Rubber Sheets. A Wiremill makes wires; wire plus rubber is cable. Automate rubber early: every machine needs cables."
  ],
  "quest.48D47667F4C39134.title": "Assembler and electric machines",
  "quest.48D47667F4C39134.quest_desc": [
    "Electric machines overclock up to 32 EU/t. The Assembler automates almost any crafting recipe, 3 per machine with slot locks: hulls, circuits, motors, pistons, robot arms and conveyors first. Lubricant (creosote and redstone) poured on a machine overclocks it by hand."
  ],
  "quest.3250F4E861F3B865.title": "MI ore numbers",
  "quest.3250F4E861F3B865.quest_desc": [
    "Forge Hammer: an ore block gives 2 raw, 3 with the tool. Macerator: an ore block gives 3 raw, each raw 1.5 dust on average, so silk-touched ore pays best here (4.5 per ore). Hammering 3 raw with the tool gives 4 dusts."
  ],
  "quest.70048ADDD1887B1D.title": "Tanks, barrels, trash",
  "quest.70048ADDD1887B1D.quest_desc": [
    "Bronze tanks hold 4 buckets, bronze barrels 32 stacks of one item; both keep contents when broken and stack when equal. Steel tanks hold 16 buckets. The Automatic Trash Can deletes whatever you pipe in."
  ],
  "quest.3E3A5EE58B8536B4.title": "Electric Blast Furnace and aluminium",
  "quest.3E3A5EE58B8536B4.quest_desc": [
    "Heatproof casings, two hollow layers of cupronickel coils, heatproof again; controller at the bottom and at least one energy hatch. It unlocks aluminium from electrolyzed bauxite. Multiblocks overclock to 128 EU/t, more with overclock upgrades."
  ],
  "quest.1E682E77776C3BD2.title": "Oil and diesel",
  "quest.1E682E77776C3BD2.quest_desc": [
    "The Oil Drilling Rig pumps crude from below bedrock; a Distillery or Distillation Tower splits it into fuels. Diesel Generators burn only when needed; a hot Large Steam Boiler gets about twice the energy from the same fuel. Pack change: the Diesel Jetpack needs a reinforced alloy (III) and burns 2.5 times its native diesel per tick."
  ],
  "quest.5AB3105DF0C1755B.title": "Large boilers and turbines",
  "quest.5AB3105DF0C1755B.quest_desc": [
    "The Large Steam Boiler makes 256 mB/t fully heated but wastes unused heat: run it at full output. Then Advanced and High Pressure boilers (1 mB of HP steam = 8 EU) and the Large Steam Turbine, up to 16384 EU/t, with a Heat Exchanger to recover water."
  ],
  "quest.3D484AC9377B043F.title": "Nuclear Reactor",
  "quest.3D484AC9377B043F.quest_desc": [
    "Nuclear casings with hatches on top forming the grid; fuel releases fast and thermal neutrons and water hatches make steam. It breeds plutonium, deuterium and tritium, and cannot explode or irradiate the map: overheating only damages what is inside. Pack change: the controller needs an Ark Bus (V)."
  ],
  "quest.151D921ED00F5879.title": "Machine upgrades",
  "quest.151D921ED00F5879.quest_desc": [
    "An Advanced Machine Hull moves a machine to MV (MV cables only then). Overdrive Modules keep efficiency through pauses at an energy cost; Redstone Control Modules let redstone drive machines. Configurable Chests and Tanks auto-eject into lines."
  ],
  "quest.65D901EA3E3872A0.title": "Fusion and the quantum tier",
  "quest.65D901EA3E3872A0.quest_desc": [
    "The Fusion Reactor turns deuterium, tritium and helium-3 into helium plasma for the Plasma Turbine (about 1 MEU/t). The Singularity opens quantum gear: upgrade, sword, armour, barrel and tank. The Gravichestplate flies and cancels fall damage."
  ],
  "quest.0BE0CA8DF9D8CF09.title": "Pack changes to MI",
  "quest.0BE0CA8DF9D8CF09.quest_desc": [
    "Replicator removed, Nether Star from the Implosion Compressor removed (the Wither stays the only source). Gated: Diesel Jetpack (III), Gravichestplate (IV), Electric Quarry (IV), Nuclear Reactor (V), Quantum Circuits (V), with their assembler twins removed. MI has the lowest metal priority in Almost Unified."
  ],
  "quest.43475F84B3C8A758.title": "Mastery: day and night",
  "quest.43475F84B3C8A758.quest_desc": [
    "A working fusion setup or the quantum tier: by then the factory runs on its own, as MI intends. The pack's best armour is still the Luminous set, not the Quantum one."
  ],
  "chapter.38F7F6E21E23959C.title": "Powah!",
  "chapter.38F7F6E21E23959C.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Energizing, tiered generators from Starter to Nitro, energy cells, the Ender network and wireless charging."
  ],
  "quest.2DCEE31825883254.title": "Seven tiers of FE",
  "quest.2DCEE31825883254.quest_desc": [
    "Compact FE generation. Every machine comes in seven tiers (Starter, Basic, Hardened, Blazing, Niotic, Spirited, Nitro), each making, storing and moving more. The signature trick is energizing: charging items into new materials. The in-game book lists stats per tier."
  ],
  "quest.1F371F6CAEB5D31A.title": "Dielectric paste",
  "quest.1F371F6CAEB5D31A.quest_desc": [
    "Shapeless: three coal or charcoal, two clay and a lava bucket (or two coal, a clay and blaze powder). It makes the dielectric casings and rods behind every Powah block. Starter machines only need basics."
  ],
  "quest.04AF1F9556CFEA5B.title": "Generators",
  "quest.04AF1F9556CFEA5B.quest_desc": [
    "Furnator burns solid fuel, Magmator hot fluids like lava, the Thermo Generator sits on a hot block with a coolant, the Solar Panel wants sun (a Lens of Ender lets it see through blocks). Higher tiers produce more. A Starter Furnator plus a Magmator on a lava pump: solid Act II power."
  ],
  "quest.13F36FB6A1E76C79.title": "Energizing Orb and rods",
  "quest.13F36FB6A1E76C79.quest_desc": [
    "The Orb needs no power: Energizing Rods within 9x9, sitting on cables or FE blocks, feed it. More and better rods, faster. Link rods with the Powah Wrench in Link mode (its other modes: Config and Rotate)."
  ],
  "quest.0B8FAFE3ED58698A.title": "Energized Steel and crystals",
  "quest.0B8FAFE3ED58698A.quest_desc": [
    "Iron and gold become Energized Steel, blaze into Blazing Crystals, diamonds into Niotic (300,000 FE), emeralds into Spirited (1,000,000 FE). Each tier is built from its material. Nitro: a Nether Star, two redstone blocks and a blazing block, 20,000,000 FE for 16 crystals."
  ],
  "quest.0CF0FB72E18ED249.title": "Pack change: tier capacitors",
  "quest.0CF0FB72E18ED249.quest_desc": [
    "Every machine needs its tier's capacitor, and each takes an act material instead of one paste: Niotic an Ironwood Ingot (IV), Spirited a Sky Ingot (V), Nitro Atomic Alloy (V). A 36-block Niotic reactor costs 36 ironwood. Starter to Blazing stay native."
  ],
  "quest.16ACDFEC566167E4.title": "Cables and Energy Cells",
  "quest.16ACDFEC566167E4.quest_desc": [
    "Energy Cables move power; the wrench in Config mode sets each side. Energy Cells store FE in tiers. Batteries charge the items in your inventory."
  ],
  "quest.202763CA4CCA4E60.title": "Energy Hopper and Discharger",
  "quest.202763CA4CCA4E60.quest_desc": [
    "The Hopper charges chargeable items inside the inventory next to it, like a chest of tools. The Discharger drains charged items back into cables. Chest plus Energy Hopper: a team charging station."
  ],
  "quest.5BE24994F4FBEE4D.title": "Ender network",
  "quest.5BE24994F4FBEE4D.quest_desc": [
    "Ender Cells store energy in a channel of your personal network, reachable anywhere; Ender Gates connect blocks to it. Shift-click cells or batteries into an Ender Cell to add their capacity. A wireless battery between bases."
  ],
  "quest.4E6361BFFEB4C669.title": "Player Transmitter",
  "quest.4E6361BFFEB4C669.quest_desc": [
    "Charges your inventory, armour and off-hand wirelessly: same dimension with a Binding Card, any dimension with a Dimensional one (right-click to bind it to yourself). Needs a Player Aerial Pearl, an Aerial Pearl used on a zombie or husk. Forget chargers forever."
  ],
  "quest.6F04A087B6A5D44E.title": "Uraninite",
  "quest.6F04A087B6A5D44E.quest_desc": [
    "Poor, normal and dense ore below Y 64, 20 and 0. Energizing silk-touched ore gives 3, 5 or 10, a little more than Fortune raw; uranium ingots from other mods energize into uraninite too. Dry Ice, the reactor coolant, is found underground or energized from two blue ice."
  ],
  "quest.5A9CC0F268D579EC.title": "Powah Reactor",
  "quest.5A9CC0F268D579EC.quest_desc": [
    "Hold 36 reactor blocks and place them on a free 3x4 area: it builds itself. It burns uraninite, takes carbon and redstone boosts and a solid coolant like dry ice, and in Auto mode stops when full and restarts below 70%. A Niotic or better one pays the act material 36 times."
  ],
  "quest.37CFA4BF8EA40332.title": "Charged Snowball",
  "quest.37CFA4BF8EA40332.quest_desc": [
    "Energize a snowball (500,000 FE) and throw it: lightning where it lands. Charged creepers on demand, or lightning for recipes that want it."
  ],
  "quest.453C8E2B6048152C.title": "Creative Energy Cell",
  "quest.453C8E2B6048152C.quest_desc": [
    "Two Luminosities (engineering and habitation, Act VI). Until then, Nitro is the ceiling."
  ],
  "quest.19C1BD8B46C7ED1D.title": "Mastery: Nitro",
  "quest.19C1BD8B46C7ED1D.quest_desc": [
    "Nitro crystals, a Nitro capacitor with its atomic alloy, and a Nitro reactor or generators. Add a Player Transmitter and an Ender network: power anywhere."
  ],
  "chapter.7F41FAB4B3A9AD70.title": "AE2: autocrafting and addons",
  "chapter.7F41FAB4B3A9AD70.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Patterns, pattern providers, crafting CPUs and the pack's AE2 addons: Extended AE, Advanced AE, MEGA Cells, AE2WTLib, Applied Mekanistics and more."
  ],
  "quest.44AB1B644596CE70.title": "Let the network craft",
  "quest.44AB1B644596CE70.quest_desc": [
    "Three pieces: patterns (recipes on items), pattern providers that push ingredients to machines, and crafting CPUs that plan the job. Ask the terminal for 64 of something and the network crafts every step. The addons then remove the limits."
  ],
  "quest.1B1E6D801ECE853D.title": "Patterns",
  "quest.1B1E6D801ECE853D.quest_desc": [
    "Encode Blank Patterns in a Pattern Encoding Terminal: crafting patterns for the crafting table, processing patterns for anything else (furnace, Mekanism, a Create line), plus smithing and stonecutting ones. Stick to one wood type in every pattern: fewer headaches."
  ],
  "quest.00455A2B03F16107.title": "Pattern Provider",
  "quest.00455A2B03F16107.quest_desc": [
    "Pushes a complete batch of ingredients to adjacent machines, round-robin across faces; results can come back into the provider. It never holds ingredients, so you cannot pipe out of it. Results must enter the system (provider, interface, import bus), not a chest behind a storage bus."
  ],
  "quest.07B9805451689768.title": "Molecular Assembler",
  "quest.07B9805451689768.quest_desc": [
    "Against a provider, it receives the crafting pattern and ingredients and ejects the result back. Surround a provider with assemblers to craft in parallel."
  ],
  "quest.138B171B22C0BA4F.title": "Crafting CPU",
  "quest.138B171B22C0BA4F.quest_desc": [
    "A solid box with at least one Crafting Storage (1k to 256k); Co-Processing Units add parallel steps. One job per CPU, so build two to ask for two things at once. Middle-click in the terminal requests crafts of items you already hold."
  ],
  "quest.763DE2302EE8A82C.title": "What it cannot do",
  "quest.763DE2302EE8A82C.quest_desc": [
    "No recursive recipes (an item that makes more of itself); the guide has a workaround. Providers push to one side per batch: for machines that want inputs on different faces, use an interface subnetwork or Advanced AE's provider. Keep an Energy Cell: big jobs spike power."
  ],
  "quest.1EE79393C2041D02.title": "Keeping things in stock",
  "quest.1EE79393C2041D02.quest_desc": [
    "An export bus or interface with a Crafting Card orders crafts of what it should export or stock. A Level Emitter with one signals while an item crafts or runs low. ME Requester does it for you: set an amount per item and it keeps that much."
  ],
  "quest.1D9A38C2746E325D.title": "Extended AE",
  "quest.1D9A38C2746E325D.quest_desc": [
    "Bigger devices: Extended Pattern Provider, Drives, Interfaces and IO buses, an Extended Pattern Access Terminal, plus the Circuit Cutter and Crystal Assembler for bulk processors and crystals. Its Entro crystal is a second crystal line with budding blocks."
  ],
  "quest.2532A52AED357D7E.title": "Assembler Matrix",
  "quest.2532A52AED357D7E.quest_desc": [
    "An Extended AE multiblock of assemblers and providers: a solid box 3 to 7 per side with at least one Pattern Core and one Craft Core. Many jobs at once, few channels. It replaces walls of providers and assemblers."
  ],
  "quest.0E1BDAE616808553.title": "Advanced AE",
  "quest.0E1BDAE616808553.quest_desc": [
    "The Advanced Pattern Provider picks the face each ingredient goes to, so one block feeds sided machines (hello, Mekanism) with no pipes. Also: a Quantum Crafter that crafts straight from the network, a Reaction Chamber, advanced IO buses and Quantum Armor. Upgrade providers in place."
  ],
  "quest.401FD97051B632E6.title": "Quantum Computer",
  "quest.401FD97051B632E6.quest_desc": [
    "Runs unlimited jobs at once while it has crafting storage. The Quantum Core alone is 256M of storage and 8 threads; as a multiblock with more blocks it goes further. One computer replaces a room of CPUs."
  ],
  "quest.1662C1571EF019DD.title": "MEGA Cells",
  "quest.1662C1571EF019DD.quest_desc": [
    "Cells from 1M to 256M for items, fluids and chemicals, plus matching crafting storage and co-processors (four threads each). Starts with Sky Steel (sky stone, iron, charged certus in an Extended or Advanced AE machine). The Bulk Cell stores one item with no type limit: perfect for cobble."
  ],
  "quest.03168997211BBE88.title": "Applied Mekanistics",
  "quest.03168997211BBE88.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism chemicals in AE2: chemical cells 1k to 256k, portable cells and a chemical P2P tunnel. Buses, interfaces and providers handle chemicals, so AE2 autocrafts through Mekanism. Normal chemical cells refuse radioactive chemicals; MEGA has a cell for those."
  ],
  "quest.286E35060397F0CB.title": "AE2WTLib wireless terminals",
  "quest.286E35060397F0CB.quest_desc": [
    "Wireless crafting, pattern and other terminals, combinable into one Universal Terminal. Upgrades: Restock tops up the stack in your hand, Magnet Card pulls items into the network, Quantum Bridge Card reaches home from any dimension if loaded. The best quality-of-life item in AE2."
  ],
  "quest.7170B24DC402C8AD.title": "Small helpers",
  "quest.7170B24DC402C8AD.quest_desc": [
    "Import and Export Cards move items between chosen inventory slots and the network. The ME Network Analyser lists every device and its status: the fastest way to find a missing channel. Ars Energistique stores Ars Nouveau source in AE2."
  ],
  "quest.79AE6322C80A6B72.title": "AE2 in this pack",
  "quest.79AE6322C80A6B72.quest_desc": [
    "AE2 and its addons are native. Refined Storage, the alternative, has its controller and autocrafter gated in Act III; AE2 feeds the story instead through its processors. Quantum Armor is late gear, but the Luminous set stays the best."
  ],
  "quest.36A1DD7F3539AEA8.title": "Mastery: the base builds itself",
  "quest.36A1DD7F3539AEA8.quest_desc": [
    "Ask for a stack of Ultimate Control Circuits and watch: processing patterns through Mekanism, crafting in assemblers, planned by a Quantum Computer, stored in MEGA cells. Your job now is adding patterns."
  ],
  "chapter.774FEAB2CEAA7221.title": "CC: Tweaked",
  "chapter.774FEAB2CEAA7221.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Computers, turtles and monitors programmed in Lua: optional, but they can read and drive half of the pack."
  ],
  "quest.53ADB2066E8E7D23.title": "Computers, optional and powerful",
  "quest.53ADB2066E8E7D23.quest_desc": [
    "Lua computers, robotic turtles, monitors, modems and printers. Fully optional: no quest needs code, and the Act V network milestone accepts a computer panel as one route among others. Never programmed? The built-in programs (help, edit, go, excavate) already do a lot."
  ],
  "quest.37FECE288D04614F.title": "Your first Computer",
  "quest.37FECE288D04614F.quest_desc": [
    "Stone, redstone and a glass pane. Right-click to open the terminal: \"help\" lists topics, \"programs\" lists commands, \"edit name\" opens the editor and \"lua\" gives you a live prompt to try code.",
    "",
    "Hold Ctrl+T for a second to stop a stuck program, Ctrl+R to reboot and Ctrl+S to shut down. A file called startup runs by itself when the computer boots."
  ],
  "quest.799E84461222BBB3.title": "IDs and labels",
  "quest.799E84461222BBB3.quest_desc": [
    "Every computer has a numeric ID (\"id\") and keeps it when broken, so its files travel with it. \"label set Name\" names it; a Name Tag or an anvil also works. Labelled turtles keep their fuel when picked up.",
    "",
    "Crafting a computer into a turtle or an advanced model keeps its ID and data."
  ],
  "quest.6D824B2F8096F006.title": "Advanced Computer",
  "quest.6D824B2F8096F006.quest_desc": [
    "Gold instead of stone. The advanced models show colour and accept mouse clicks, which makes menus and buttons possible. You can upgrade a normal computer in place by surrounding it with gold: it keeps its ID and files.",
    "",
    "The same gold upgrade exists for pocket computers."
  ],
  "quest.5935F07739DC4924.title": "Disk Drive and floppies",
  "quest.5935F07739DC4924.quest_desc": [
    "A Disk Drive beside a computer mounts a floppy as the folder \"disk\". Floppies carry programs between computers, and a startup file on a disk runs at boot. Craft floppies from paper, redstone and a dye.",
    "",
    "Space: 1 MB per computer or turtle and 125 KB per floppy by default. Music discs in a drive can be played too."
  ],
  "quest.750F233DF2536F5C.title": "Redstone from a computer",
  "quest.750F233DF2536F5C.quest_desc": [
    "Computers read and emit redstone on all six sides with no extra block: \"redstone probe\" lists inputs, \"redstone set left true\" turns a side on and \"redstone pulse\" sends pulses. In Lua, the rs API does the same with analog levels.",
    "",
    "The Redstone Relay is a separate block with six sides of its own that a computer controls through a wired modem, for when you need many signals far away."
  ],
  "quest.72792D7D894661AF.title": "Monitors",
  "quest.72792D7D894661AF.quest_desc": [
    "Monitors placed together join into one big screen, up to 8 wide and 6 tall by default. \"monitor right edit notes\" runs any program on the monitor at that side; in Lua, wrap the monitor and use term.redirect or write to it directly.",
    "",
    "Monitors can also be reached through a wired modem, so the screen does not have to touch the computer."
  ],
  "quest.0EDD0B86A59684EF.title": "Advanced Monitors",
  "quest.0EDD0B86A59684EF.quest_desc": [
    "Gold monitors, four per craft. They show colour and fire a monitor_touch event with the X and Y of every right-click, so a wall of them becomes a touch panel with buttons.",
    "",
    "Keep text short: the bigger the screen, the more data the server sends when it changes."
  ],
  "quest.542F669BB6979A73.title": "Wired Modems and cables",
  "quest.542F669BB6979A73.quest_desc": [
    "Networking Cable (six per craft) links Wired Modems. Put a modem on a machine or chest and right-click it: the chat confirms the peripheral name, and every computer on the cable can wrap it by that name.",
    "",
    "Any inventory becomes a peripheral: list its items and push or pull stacks between chests. On NeoForge, tanks and energy storage are readable too."
  ],
  "quest.227AE57B09C73B93.title": "Wireless Modems and rednet",
  "quest.227AE57B09C73B93.quest_desc": [
    "Stone around an ender pearl. A Wireless Modem reaches 64 blocks near the ground, growing above Y 96 up to 384 at the build limit. The rednet API sends to an ID or broadcasts, and \"rednet.host\" plus \"rednet.lookup\" let programs find each other by name.",
    "",
    "Open the modem first: rednet.open with its side."
  ],
  "quest.646AABCD481A864F.title": "Ender Modem",
  "quest.646AABCD481A864F.quest_desc": [
    "Gold around an eye of ender. It works like a wireless modem with no distance limit, and messages cross dimensions, so a base in the Overworld can talk to a mine elsewhere.",
    "",
    "It also fits turtles and pocket computers as an upgrade."
  ],
  "quest.68AA1FD1CEA5B6F0.title": "GPS cluster",
  "quest.68AA1FD1CEA5B6F0.quest_desc": [
    "Four computers with ender modems at the corners of a small cube, three on one level and one above, each running «gps host x y z» with its exact coordinates in startup. Anything in range then finds itself with «gps locate». One wrong coordinate breaks everyone's answer."
  ],
  "quest.73AB617F80FCFB33.title": "Turtles",
  "quest.73AB617F80FCFB33.quest_desc": [
    "A computer, iron and a chest make a Turtle: a computer that moves, digs and places blocks. Turtles need fuel: put coal or a lava bucket in its inventory and run \"refuel\". The tank holds 20,000 fuel on a normal turtle and 100,000 on an advanced one, and each move spends some.",
    "",
    "\"go forward 3 up\" and \"turn left\" drive it without code."
  ],
  "quest.610BEE60A4D95BA8.title": "Mining Turtle",
  "quest.610BEE60A4D95BA8.quest_desc": [
    "Craft a turtle beside a diamond pickaxe (or use \"equip\" from its inventory) to get a Mining Turtle. \"tunnel 20\" digs a 3x2 tunnel, and \"excavate 5\" mines a 5x5 shaft down to bedrock and brings the loot back up.",
    "",
    "Other diamond tools give other turtles: axe (Felling), shovel (Digging), hoe (Farming) and sword (Melee). Only diamond tools work by default."
  ],
  "quest.38ADE6A69AF1BC9D.title": "Crafty Turtle",
  "quest.38ADE6A69AF1BC9D.quest_desc": [
    "A crafting table as upgrade makes a Crafty Turtle. Lay out a recipe in its inventory and run \"craft all\" or call turtle.craft in Lua. A turtle has two upgrade sides, so a mining and crafty turtle is possible."
  ],
  "quest.0C1C4EA1AE54B0F0.title": "Pocket Computer",
  "quest.0C1C4EA1AE54B0F0.quest_desc": [
    "A computer you carry: stone, a golden apple and a glass pane. Use it to talk to your base over rednet or to run \"gps locate\" on the move. It takes one upgrade: wireless or ender modem, or a speaker; \"equip\" puts on the first valid item from your inventory."
  ],
  "quest.5535489EE629D423.title": "Printer",
  "quest.5535489EE629D423.quest_desc": [
    "The Printer takes paper and dye as ink and prints pages from code. Join two or more printed pages with string into Printed Pages, or add leather for a Printed Book. Handy for logbooks and base maps."
  ],
  "quest.0587FAAACBDF8D55.title": "Speaker",
  "quest.0587FAAACBDF8D55.quest_desc": [
    "Stone, a note block and redstone. A speaker plays note block instruments, any game sound by name, or audio: \"speaker play file.dfpwm\" handles DFPWM and mono 8-bit WAV at 48 kHz. Up to 8 notes per tick by default.",
    "",
    "Turtles and pocket computers accept it as an upgrade."
  ],
  "quest.160BD6F65223664A.title": "Internet programs",
  "quest.160BD6F65223664A.quest_desc": [
    "The HTTP API is on: \"wget\" and \"pastebin get\" download programs and \"pastebin run\" runs one directly. Requests to private and local network addresses are blocked by default.",
    "",
    "Read any downloaded code before running it: a program has full control of the computer and whatever it is wired to."
  ],
  "quest.77AB5A14AB23ED5D.title": "Create and computers",
  "quest.77AB5A14AB23ED5D.quest_desc": [
    "Speedometer, Stressometer, Sequenced Gearshift, speed controller, train Station, Signal and Track Observer, Stock Ticker and Packager are peripherals; a Display Link can print «From Computer» on boards. Crafts and Additions' Digital Adapter reaches pulleys, pistons and bearings."
  ],
  "quest.4D9218F6064FD671.title": "Other mods on the wire",
  "quest.4D9218F6064FD671.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism machines and multiblock ports, Immersive Engineering, PneumaticCraft, the Energy Meter, New Age and Crafts and Additions parts, and Draconic Evolution all answer computers; Ender IO redstone conduits show up as bundled redstone. «peripheral.getMethods» lists what each offers."
  ],
  "quest.7CC68FC53723A2DB.title": "Tips and limits",
  "quest.7CC68FC53723A2DB.quest_desc": [
    "Command Computers are creative-only: they need an operator in creative, and survival players cannot break them. By default all computers share a single server thread, so an endless loop without a sleep or os.pullEvent slows everyone; use events and timers instead of busy loops.",
    "",
    "The in-game \"help\" is short but accurate for this version."
  ],
  "quest.06E2AB6EF48F3F74.title": "Mastery: the base panel",
  "quest.06E2AB6EF48F3F74.quest_desc": [
    "Tie it together: an advanced computer on a wired network reads your energy storage and main chests, shows the numbers on an advanced monitor wall with touch buttons, and hears remote turtles or outposts over an ender modem.",
    "",
    "The same panel is a valid, optional way to watch the Act V network, never a requirement."
  ],
  "chapter.259F401BEDE48434.title": "Draconic Evolution",
  "chapter.259F401BEDE48434.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Draconium, fusion crafting, dislocators and energy crystals; then wyvern, draconic and chaotic tools, the energy core and the reactor."
  ],
  "quest.368A87DE8F18AFCB.title": "Endgame power fantasy",
  "quest.368A87DE8F18AFCB.quest_desc": [
    "Four tiers: Draconium, Wyvern, Draconic (awakened) and Chaotic, all on OP, which is plain FE. Pack pacing: draconium, fusion crafting and the Dislocator open in Act III; the Wyvern Core and the Draconic Core need an atomic alloy (Act V); chaotic still means the Chaos Guardian."
  ],
  "quest.25EAC6BC8B22C4D5.title": "Tips and keys",
  "quest.25EAC6BC8B22C4D5.quest_desc": [
    "Keys in this pack: Place Item is Alt+P (sets a held item down as a display block) and Tool Config is Alt+Y and Tool Modules Shift+U; Toggle Flight and Toggle Item Dislocator are listed under Controls. Draconic and chaotic tools mine any block.",
    "",
    "Modular tools have an AOE Safe Mode that cancels area mining when a block entity is in range: keep it on near your base."
  ],
  "quest.4EB8C042E050A063.title": "Draconium",
  "quest.4EB8C042E050A063.quest_desc": [
    "Draconium Ore drops 2 to 4 Draconium Dust, plus more with Fortune; smelt the dust into ingots. In the Overworld it hides between Y -64 and -48 in about one chunk of ten; in the Nether, larger veins between Y 4 and 16 in about one chunk of thirty; in the End, three small veins per chunk in end stone.",
    "",
    "The Ender Dragon also drops around 64 dust when killed."
  ],
  "quest.6FAF1D5F3B08ABED.title": "Draconium Core",
  "quest.6FAF1D5F3B08ABED.quest_desc": [
    "Draconium ingots, gold and a diamond make the Draconium Core, the part inside almost every Draconic block. Make a few: the Fusion Crafting Core, injectors, Generator and crystals all start here."
  ],
  "quest.3BB338A92B22481C.title": "Generator",
  "quest.3BB338A92B22481C.quest_desc": [
    "A furnace-style generator that burns solid fuel for OP. Its modes trade output for efficiency: Eco and Eco Plus stretch fuel, Normal matches other basic generators, Performance and Overdrive burn faster for more power. Enough to charge your first fusion crafts."
  ],
  "quest.41FBB0214C9BD641.title": "Fusion Crafting Core",
  "quest.41FBB0214C9BD641.quest_desc": [
    "The catalyst goes in the Core, every other ingredient in its own injector facing it, 2 to 16 blocks away, each fed OP by pipe. When it reads Ready to craft, press Craft: it charges, then fuses. «Too close» or «tier too low»: check spacing and injector tiers."
  ],
  "quest.6278042A667B5A83.title": "Fusion injectors",
  "quest.6278042A667B5A83.quest_desc": [
    "You need one injector per ingredient, so build a few. Every recipe has a tier, and each injector must reach it: Draconium injectors do draconium recipes, Wyvern injectors unlock wyvern ones, and so on. Better injectors also speed things up: charging and crafting take 300, 220, 140 or 60 ticks by the lowest tier used.",
    "",
    "Injectors have a single item or stack mode for feeding by automation."
  ],
  "quest.38319050D58B029A.title": "Draconium Chest",
  "quest.38319050D58B029A.quest_desc": [
    "Your first fusion craft: a huge chest with a crafting grid and a built-in furnace section that runs on OP and can auto-smelt everything, only filtered items, or keep a sticky filter. Shulker boxes, bags and pouches are refused, so nobody nests storage inside it."
  ],
  "quest.624AC266DD69B3EF.title": "Dislocator",
  "quest.624AC266DD69B3EF.quest_desc": [
    "Sneak and right-click to save your position, facing and dimension; right-click later to teleport back, with a limited number of uses. Bound variants exist: a pair that sends you to its twin, and one bound to a player, who must agree by sneaking.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: the Dislocator needs a reinforced alloy (Act III), which also gates everything crafted from it."
  ],
  "quest.60A22B2D626E2F40.title": "Item Dislocator",
  "quest.60A22B2D626E2F40.quest_desc": [
    "A magnet built around a Dislocator that pulls nearby drops to you. Toggle it with its key (Toggle Item Dislocator). Near farms, a Dislocation Normalization Field Projector stops magnets from grabbing items dropped within 5 blocks."
  ],
  "quest.2B0EBB5CB8D7C41A.title": "Dislocator portals",
  "quest.2B0EBB5CB8D7C41A.quest_desc": [
    "A Dislocator Receptacle holding a bound Dislocator opens a portal inside a frame of Draconium Infused Obsidian, leading to the Dislocator's saved spot. Frames can be large, up to 256 by 256.",
    "",
    "A Dislocator Pedestal holds a Dislocator for anyone who walks up to use it."
  ],
  "quest.44330FBEB7C072BC.title": "Energy crystals",
  "quest.44330FBEB7C072BC.quest_desc": [
    "Crystals move OP without cables. Relay crystals pass energy along, I/O crystals take it from or give it to the block they sit on, and wireless crystals feed several receivers. Link them with the Crystal Binder: sneak and right-click the first device, then right-click the second.",
    "",
    "Links cannot cross dimensions, and each crystal has a range and link limit."
  ],
  "quest.410E749CBE021D8F.title": "Mob Grinder",
  "quest.410E749CBE021D8F.quest_desc": [
    "Kills mobs in an adjustable area with OP (80 per point of health) and can collect their drops into a neighbouring inventory and store their XP for you to claim. An optional weapon slot makes it attack with that weapon.",
    "",
    "It uses a Wyvern Energy Core, not a Wyvern Core, so it is available before Act V."
  ],
  "quest.52FF4E101C5D8D6A.title": "Disenchanter and gadgets",
  "quest.52FF4E101C5D8D6A.quest_desc": [
    "The Disenchanter pulls one enchantment off an item onto a book, paying the XP level cost shown on its screen. Other gadgets: Entity Detectors that emit redstone by mob count, Flux and Fluid Gates that throttle flow by redstone, a Potentiometer, a Rain Sensor and the decorative Particle Generator."
  ],
  "quest.7C622A55EE0714E6.title": "Wyvern Core",
  "quest.7C622A55EE0714E6.quest_desc": [
    "The Wyvern Core opens the second tier: Wyvern injectors, capacitors, modular tools and armour, the Energy Core and the Celestial Manipulator.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: its recipe takes an atomic alloy (Act V) in place of one draconium core. It also needs a nether star."
  ],
  "quest.6FC734E34DCB6224.title": "Modular tools and armour",
  "quest.6FC734E34DCB6224.quest_desc": [
    "Wyvern tools, bow, chestpiece and capacitor fuse from a diamond item or Wyvern Core, a Wyvern Energy Core and wyvern injectors, and need energy modules to run. Each has a module grid (Shift+U) and a config screen (Alt+Y). Upgrades fuse the previous tier as catalyst: nothing wasted."
  ],
  "quest.0583F603465CFA25.title": "Modules",
  "quest.0583F603465CFA25.quest_desc": [
    "Modules start from a Module Core and fill the grid: energy, speed, damage, area, jump, auto-feed, night vision, junk filter and ender collection, plus shields, undying and flight for the chestpiece. Flight offers creative-style and elytra flight, each with its own toggle.",
    "",
    "Higher-tier modules fit only in items of their tier or above."
  ],
  "quest.5D1F8676AE15787F.title": "Energy Core",
  "quest.5D1F8676AE15787F.quest_desc": [
    "A multiblock battery with eight tiers, from about 45 million OP at tier 1 to a practically bottomless tier 8. Its screen has a build guide and an Assemble Core button that places the structure from your inventory; stabilizers go around it, and the higher tiers need advanced stabilizers. Energy Pylons connect it to your network.",
    "",
    "Needs a Wyvern Core, so it is an Act V project."
  ],
  "quest.6ECBE13B33353C78.title": "Advanced Dislocator",
  "quest.6ECBE13B33353C78.quest_desc": [
    "A fusion upgrade that stores a named list of places. Ender pearls are its fuel: one pearl is one teleport or four blinks (short hops up to 32 blocks where you look), and it holds up to 1,024. Keys for teleport, blink and scrolling the list are under Controls."
  ],
  "quest.3A406FA50C7C7ADF.title": "Celestial Manipulator",
  "quest.3A406FA50C7C7ADF.quest_desc": [
    "Skips to sunrise, noon, sunset or midnight, and starts or clears rain and storms, for OP. It needs a Wyvern Core and a dragon egg; in this pack the egg returns every time the dragon dies, so more than one player can build it."
  ],
  "quest.1530700DF8E3E846.title": "Dragon Heart and awakened draconium",
  "quest.1530700DF8E3E846.quest_desc": [
    "Killing the Ender Dragon drops a Dragon Heart. Fuse it with four draconium blocks as catalyst and six Draconium Cores on wyvern injectors (50 million OP) to get four Awakened Draconium Blocks. Respawn the dragon for more hearts."
  ],
  "quest.73AFDC7DD2D99015.title": "Draconic Core and the draconic tier",
  "quest.73AFDC7DD2D99015.quest_desc": [
    "The Draconic Core (Awakened Core) is fused from four Wyvern Cores, awakened ingots and a nether star. Draconic tools and armour then fuse the wyvern item with netherite ingots, awakened ingots, a Wyvern Core and a Draconic Energy Core, on draconic injectors.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: an atomic alloy (Act V) replaces one of the awakened ingots in the Draconic Core."
  ],
  "quest.5791246A44136D6D.title": "Chaos Islands and the Chaos Guardian",
  "quest.5791246A44136D6D.quest_desc": [
    "Chaos Islands sit on a grid about 10,000 blocks apart in the outer End. Guardian Crystals shield the Chaos Guardian, a boss far above the dragon; breaking the Chaos Crystal afterwards gives 5 Chaos Shards. Chaotic weapons crack crystal shields later. Bring full wyvern or draconic gear and a way home."
  ],
  "quest.38D5FD5FBCE2625C.title": "Draconic Reactor",
  "quest.38D5FD5FBCE2625C.quest_desc": [
    "The Reactor burns awakened draconium into chaos for enormous OP. Its core sits between Reactor Stabilizers, which draw power out, and an Energy Injector that feeds the containment field. Watch temperature, field strength and saturation; SAS shuts it down safely, and each part can drive a comparator.",
    "",
    "Warning: the large explosion is enabled in this pack. Build it far from anything you love."
  ],
  "quest.3D5FC627AD89EF21.title": "Mastery: Chaotic Core",
  "quest.3D5FC627AD89EF21.quest_desc": [
    "The Chaotic Core fuses chaos fragments, awakened ingots and four Draconic Cores for 100 million OP. It unlocks chaotic injectors, tools, armour and capacitor, the strongest energy-powered gear in the pack.",
    "",
    "Beyond it, the Creative Capacitor is crafted only with Luminosities in Act VI."
  ],
  "chapter.6A7DBBFF70117355.title": "Gadgets: lasers, jetpacks, rooms, simulations",
  "chapter.6A7DBBFF70117355.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Mining Gadgets, Iron Jetpacks, Compact Machines and Hostile Neural Networks: four powerful tools and the pack rules around them."
  ],
  "quest.3B5FFFE461585A6E.title": "Four big gadgets",
  "quest.3B5FFFE461585A6E.quest_desc": [
    "A mining laser, FE jetpacks, pocket rooms inside a single block and simulated mob farms. All four open around Act III, each behind one campaign component, and their top tiers ask for later acts."
  ],
  "quest.6E90715BDE070851.title": "Mining Gadget",
  "quest.6E90715BDE070851.quest_desc": [
    "A mining laser that runs on FE: hold use to carve blocks away, many at once with size upgrades. Three models exist, MK1 to MK3. Sneak and use it to open its settings (range, filters, which blocks to void).",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: all three models need a reinforced alloy (Act III)."
  ],
  "quest.41F61EBCEC886584.title": "Modification Table and upgrades",
  "quest.41F61EBCEC886584.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrades start from a Blank Upgrade Module and go in through the Modification Table: size up to 7x7, range (+5 per tier), efficiency, fortune, silk touch, magnet, void junk, freezing for lava and water, a light placer, batteries. Each one raises the FE cost per block."
  ],
  "quest.144026C64EC13947.title": "Iron Jetpacks",
  "quest.144026C64EC13947.quest_desc": [
    "FE jetpacks in a ladder of materials, wood up to emerald. Each tier is built from that material's cell, thrusters and capacitor on top of the previous chain, flying faster with a bigger battery. Pack change: the Leather Strap needs a reinforced alloy (III), so every chain starts there. And every jetpack burns 2.5 times its native energy per tick."
  ],
  "quest.656441966D4972F1.title": "Flying a jetpack",
  "quest.656441966D4972F1.quest_desc": [
    "Wear it on your chest or in the back accessory slot and charge it like any FE item. In this pack F4 toggles the engine and Alt+H toggles hover, which holds your height and lets you drift down slowly. Ascend, descend, throttle and HUD have their own keys under Controls; sprinting goes faster but burns more."
  ],
  "quest.1D92B4FDC73E4492.title": "Coils and top tiers",
  "quest.1D92B4FDC73E4492.quest_desc": [
    "Coils go into the thrusters: basic (iron), advanced (gold), elite (diamond) and ultimate (emerald).",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: the Elite Coil needs a zanite gemstone from the Aether (Act IV) and the Ultimate Coil atomic alloy from Mekanism (Act V), which gates the diamond, platinum and emerald jetpacks."
  ],
  "quest.5BA77EC956046C58.title": "Compact Machine parts",
  "quest.5BA77EC956046C58.quest_desc": [
    "A Compact Machine is a block with a whole room inside. Its parts: Compact Machine Walls (eight from polished deepslate), an Atom Shrinking Module (sticky piston) and an Atom Enlarging Module (piston), both around an eye of ender. The walls are also a building block you can break and reuse."
  ],
  "quest.0A2BE52F61AC0594.title": "Room sizes",
  "quest.0A2BE52F61AC0594.quest_desc": [
    "Walls, both modules and a core make the machine; the core sets the room: copper 3, iron 5, gold 7, diamond 9, obsidian 11, netherite 13, nether star 45, diamond hoe a 21x21 farm with grass. No machine recipes in JEI? An operator must enable the built-in templates (ops get a clickable warning), then restart."
  ],
  "quest.378FA233E5C9F039.title": "Personal Shrinking Device",
  "quest.378FA233E5C9F039.quest_desc": [
    "Use the PSD on a machine to shrink into its room; it has its own accessory slot. Inside there is no weather, beds do not work and the walls cannot be broken. A key under Controls quick-exits the room. Machines can hold machines, room inside room.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: the PSD needs a reinforced alloy (Act III)."
  ],
  "quest.078A57D9C7E6D9AD.title": "Working inside a room",
  "quest.078A57D9C7E6D9AD.quest_desc": [
    "Rooms live in their own dimension and load with the machine chunk outside. Plan how power and items get in: cross-dimension tools work well, such as Flux Networks, LaserIO Advanced Connectors or ender chests. Jade shows a machine's owner and bound room."
  ],
  "quest.1C8F40E049E50CFC.title": "Data Models",
  "quest.1C8F40E049E50CFC.quest_desc": [
    "Craft a Model Framework and right-click a mob with it: it attunes into a Data Model of that mob. One model per mob type; the model is what every other Hostile Neural Networks machine works with."
  ],
  "quest.3298A34ED1DAFBCA.title": "Deep Learner",
  "quest.3298A34ED1DAFBCA.quest_desc": [
    "Put models in the Deep Learner, worn as an accessory, and kill that mob yourself: each kill adds data, and the model climbs from Faulty to Basic, Advanced, Superior and Self Aware. A HUD shows the kills left for the next tier. In this pack Alt+U opens the Deep Learner."
  ],
  "quest.744919A3D068C9B6.title": "Simulation Chamber",
  "quest.744919A3D068C9B6.quest_desc": [
    "The Sim Chamber runs a model on FE and Prediction Matrices: each simulation gives a Generalized Prediction of the mob's world and, depending on the model's accuracy, a mob Prediction. It can run in Inference mode (outputs, no data) or Training mode (data, no outputs).",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: an Ecosystem Capsule (Act IV) is the chamber's core, in place of the obsidian."
  ],
  "quest.2DAC1FCED44B001F.title": "Loot Fabricator",
  "quest.2DAC1FCED44B001F.quest_desc": [
    "Turns Predictions into real drops, using FE. Pick which drop each prediction becomes, in fixed or queue mode; a Fabrication Directive copies those choices to other fabricators (right-click to copy, sneak-right-click to apply)."
  ],
  "quest.4E89E77C43C2662A.title": "Data Center",
  "quest.4E89E77C43C2662A.quest_desc": [
    "The top of the line runs up to 25 Self Aware models at once, one drop each per cycle. It sits in a 7x7x7 hollow shell: obsidian floor, black stained glass walls and ceiling, the controller facing out from the bottom wall. IO Ports replace shell blocks and cycle between Energy, Models, Inputs and Outputs with a right-click."
  ],
  "quest.43242F93257E8715.title": "Mastery: the compact workshop",
  "quest.43242F93257E8715.quest_desc": [
    "Fly in with an emerald jetpack, clear a site with a 7x7 Mining Gadget, and hide a simulation farm inside a Compact Machine, powered from outside through a cross-dimension link. That is a whole production line in one block."
  ],
  "chapter.2E9A7D72E0835EEA.title": "Immersive Aircraft",
  "chapter.2E9A7D72E0835EEA.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Airships, biplanes, a gyrodyne and more: parts, fuel, controls, repairs, upgrades and weapons."
  ],
  "quest.427571CE3B56C67C.title": "Seven flying machines",
  "quest.427571CE3B56C67C.quest_desc": [
    "All crafted from a handful of parts on a crafting table. They fly in any dimension by default, carry cargo, take upgrades and mount weapons. Pack pacing: the Engine needs a Power Regulator and the Gyrodyne a reinforced alloy (Act III), which covers every aircraft. A gifted aircraft flies normally."
  ],
  "quest.64316D614B1F2430.title": "Controls and keys",
  "quest.64316D614B1F2430.quest_desc": [
    "W and S push and pull the controls, A and D turn, Space climbs and Left Shift descends; B fires a rocket boost on aircraft with a booster slot. In this pack Dismount is F12 (R is taken): press it twice in the air to jump out.",
    "",
    "The camera switches to third person in an aircraft by default."
  ],
  "quest.3C52109D4DAAB402.title": "Hulls",
  "quest.3C52109D4DAAB402.quest_desc": [
    "Logs and iron ingots make the Hull, the frame of every aircraft. Most designs take two or more, and so does the Hull Reinforcement upgrade."
  ],
  "quest.72B3D7A1DFB7E1AB.title": "Sails and propellers",
  "quest.72B3D7A1DFB7E1AB.quest_desc": [
    "Sails are white carpet and string; propellers are iron bent into shape. The airship wants six sails, the biplane one propeller, the quadrocopter four."
  ],
  "quest.0C9B6B3192A484AE.title": "Boiler",
  "quest.0C9B6B3192A484AE.quest_desc": [
    "Copper around a furnace makes the Boiler, heart of the Engine. The fuel slot of each aircraft is its boiler: it burns normal furnace fuels, and blaze powder counts as a strong fuel."
  ],
  "quest.19E92EE086F5C840.title": "Engine",
  "quest.19E92EE086F5C840.quest_desc": [
    "Boiler, pistons, a blast furnace and cobblestone make the Engine for the airship, biplane and quadrocopter.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: the cobblestone on top is replaced by a Power Regulator (Act III). Everything else in the recipe is native."
  ],
  "quest.4A7E00C064077EA8.title": "Gyrodyne",
  "quest.4A7E00C064077EA8.quest_desc": [
    "A muscle-powered copter with no engine: two sails, two hulls and a propeller. Keep pushing forward on the ground until the rotor reaches minimum speed, then lift off. It burns your hunger, not fuel, so eat before a trip.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: a reinforced alloy (Act III) takes the lower sail's place."
  ],
  "quest.41571E5944B41C5F.title": "Airship",
  "quest.41571E5944B41C5F.quest_desc": [
    "Six sails, two hulls and an engine. Slow and forgiving: it climbs and descends straight up and down and holds position, with a weapon slot, three upgrade slots and a 16-slot hold. The best first aircraft."
  ],
  "quest.20D18291E169CAA8.title": "Biplane",
  "quest.20D18291E169CAA8.quest_desc": [
    "Three hulls, an engine and a propeller. Fast and reliable, but it needs a runway: speed up on flat ground before pulling up, and land the same way. It has a booster slot for rockets."
  ],
  "quest.3645241838AF3C28.title": "Quadrocopter",
  "quest.3645241838AF3C28.quest_desc": [
    "An engine, four propellers and bamboo. Slow and precise, it hovers and barely feels the wind: great for building high up, not for travel. It sips fuel."
  ],
  "quest.0527BDAA90FDB0EC.title": "Cargo Airship",
  "quest.0527BDAA90FDB0EC.quest_desc": [
    "An airship plus chests and a hull: extra boxed storage on both sides for moving a whole base, at the cost of more fuel and even less speed."
  ],
  "quest.3E5E43E5ED1910A7.title": "Bamboo Hopper",
  "quest.3E5E43E5ED1910A7.quest_desc": [
    "Built from two biplanes, five bamboo blocks, a hull and another engine. Three seats and pontoons let it land safely on water, with two weapon slots and a booster slot."
  ],
  "quest.70D6B624DE07D0C7.title": "Fuel and wind",
  "quest.70D6B624DE07D0C7.quest_desc": [
    "Put fuel in the boiler slot before takeoff; the hotbar gauge shows the engine. Aircraft warn when fuel runs low. Wind pushes you around, three times harder in rain or thunder; the Gyroscope upgrades cancel it.",
    "",
    "Upgrades change fuel use: the Eco Engine saves a lot, the Nether Engine and Steel Boiler burn more for more power."
  ],
  "quest.767DAAD2F5180B35.title": "Damage, repair and crashes",
  "quest.767DAAD2F5180B35.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a damaged aircraft to repair it a little each click, at the cost of some hunger. Crashes make a small explosion that breaks no blocks and starts no fires, and by default a crash cannot kill you.",
    "",
    "Breaking an aircraft returns it as an item: its upgrades stay inside, its cargo drops on the ground."
  ],
  "quest.0827E6F45D206DF5.title": "Engine upgrades",
  "quest.0827E6F45D206DF5.quest_desc": [
    "Upgrade slots accept parts that change stats: Sturdy Pipes (+10% power), Industrial Gears (-20% fuel), Steel Boiler (+25% power, +50% fuel), Eco Engine (-20% power, -75% fuel), Nether Engine (+40% power, +30% fuel) and the Enhanced Propeller (much less air friction).",
    "",
    "The tooltip of each upgrade lists its numbers."
  ],
  "quest.3591550FEC33CF17.title": "Gyroscopes and handling",
  "quest.3591550FEC33CF17.quest_desc": [
    "The Gyroscope removes wind and adds stability; the Advanced Gyroscope adds a mechanical dashboard and the Electronic Gyroscope a HUD. Hull Reinforcement doubles durability and the Improved Landing Gear gives 50% faster takeoff."
  ],
  "quest.5EB8D9EFE4993166.title": "Weapons",
  "quest.5EB8D9EFE4993166.quest_desc": [
    "Weapon slots take the Rotary Cannon (fires gunpowder), the Heavy Crossbow (arrows), the Bomb Bay (drops TNT that hurts but breaks no blocks) or the Telescope. Fire with the use key; by default weapons never destroy terrain."
  ],
  "quest.0337268EBFD86CD7.title": "Mastery: Warship",
  "quest.0337268EBFD86CD7.quest_desc": [
    "The Warship is built from a Cargo Airship plus sails, hulls, two engines and industrial gears: a slow flying fortress with three times the durability, several weapon and upgrade slots and a booster. Fit it with a gyroscope, reinforcement and your weapons of choice."
  ],
  "chapter.5AD31B22E0933A9F.title": "Integrated Dynamics and Tunnels",
  "chapter.5AD31B22E0933A9F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Menril, logic networks, readers, variable cards and operators, and Integrated Tunnels to move anything with logic filters."
  ],
  "quest.405EB0F2C544D3D5.title": "Logic instead of redstone",
  "quest.405EB0F2C544D3D5.quest_desc": [
    "Readers read values from the world, the Logic Programmer combines them with operators, writers act on the result. Integrated Tunnels uses the same networks to move items, fluids and energy with filters as smart as you like. Its book (book plus two crystallized menril chunks) has tutorials with rewards; craftable, not given on spawn."
  ],
  "quest.50FB10FD2141D419.title": "Menril trees",
  "quest.50FB10FD2141D419.quest_desc": [
    "Tall blue trees with glowing, edible berries: rare, but common in the Meneglin biome. Their wood holds Menril Resin, the base of almost everything. Plant saplings at home the moment you find one."
  ],
  "quest.3B0829A194600C5D.title": "Squeezer and Drying Basin",
  "quest.3B0829A194600C5D.quest_desc": [
    "Put a menril log in the Squeezer and jump on it until flat: resin flows out the sides into a Drying Basin, which makes Crystallized Menril. A redstone pulse resets the Squeezer; mechanical versions automate it. Never pour hot fluids into a basin."
  ],
  "quest.703F9772D06E2D30.title": "Menril in the Inventory Sensor",
  "quest.703F9772D06E2D30.quest_desc": [
    "Two Crystallized Menril Chunks go into the Inventory Sensor (Act III) with two LaserIO logic chips and a Routing Matrix. ID itself is not gated; a small menril farm covers everything."
  ],
  "quest.50DB3E215BD52AB5.title": "Logic cables",
  "quest.50DB3E215BD52AB5.quest_desc": [
    "A network is connected Logic Cables with parts on them. With the wrench, sneak-right-click removes, right-click disconnects. Facades hide cables behind any material."
  ],
  "quest.1F508FE56FB71B63.title": "Readers, cards and panels",
  "quest.1F508FE56FB71B63.quest_desc": [
    "Readers on cables read aspects of what they face: redstone, chest contents, the block or entity ahead. Bind an aspect to a Variable Card and a Display Panel shows its value. First tutorial: read a redstone torch and show it."
  ],
  "quest.5D3AA7B4C9C56A9A.title": "Logic Programmer and operators",
  "quest.5D3AA7B4C9C56A9A.quest_desc": [
    "Holds every operator: make static values or combine cards (Addition and friends) into a new card. Evaluation is lazy, so referenced cards must stay reachable: that is the Variable Store's job. Operators are values too: store them, partially apply them, pass them to filters."
  ],
  "quest.6F914BAD51E8EE43.title": "Value types",
  "quest.6F914BAD51E8EE43.quest_desc": [
    "Boolean, Integer, Long, Double, String, List, Operator, NBT, Block, Item, Entity, Fluid, Ingredients, Recipe. Integers span about plus or minus two billion, Longs far more; lists hold one type. Operators only take matching types: read the type colour."
  ],
  "quest.4FF178E723970DA5.title": "Writers",
  "quest.4FF178E723970DA5.quest_desc": [
    "Writers act on the world from a card: a Redstone Writer outputs the level a card holds. Reader, operator, writer: a logic gate of any complexity in three blocks."
  ],
  "quest.61DAEF084346B4B7.title": "Materializer, Proxy and recipes",
  "quest.61DAEF084346B4B7.quest_desc": [
    "The Materializer freezes a dynamic value into a static card; the Proxy adds indirection so values can change later. Machine Readers read recipes from blocks, and Recipe and Ingredients values work with them. NBT is the fallback."
  ],
  "quest.7F1E6CAD83572C63.title": "Integrated Tunnels",
  "quest.7F1E6CAD83572C63.quest_desc": [
    "Importers (blue) pull into the network, Exporters (orange) push out, Interfaces (white) are where it stores and takes, for items, fluids and energy, with priorities. A blank card means «move everything». Use logic as filter: «3 pickaxes under 10 durability into this chest every tick»."
  ],
  "quest.287131684A32618B.title": "World interaction and player simulation",
  "quest.287131684A32618B.quest_desc": [
    "World importers and exporters place and pick up items, fluids and blocks, break blocks (silk touch available) and talk to entity inventories. The Player Simulator clicks with any item. Breaker plus placer: a two-part farm with any filter."
  ],
  "quest.355F05E7E779D518.title": "Energy on the network",
  "quest.355F05E7E779D518.quest_desc": [
    "ID has its own Coal Generator and Energy Battery, and Tunnels moves energy with filtered importers, exporters and interfaces. One network can carry logic, items, fluids and power at once."
  ],
  "quest.4F02807EA82A8C59.title": "Challenges",
  "quest.4F02807EA82A8C59.quest_desc": [
    "The book ends with hintless challenges; every tutorial step grants an advancement and a small reward. Program misbehaving? Put its cards on Display Panels one by one until you find the wrong value."
  ],
  "quest.14EEA85DB5C4A668.title": "Mastery: a network that decides",
  "quest.14EEA85DB5C4A668.quest_desc": [
    "Watch a storage chest, decide with operators what is missing, and export exactly that from another inventory, without a speck of redstone dust. Same pattern for farms, sorting and machine control."
  ],
  "chapter.1BA01ED246964CAC.title": "LaserIO, Modular Routers and Flux",
  "chapter.1BA01ED246964CAC.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Card-driven laser networks, one-block routers with modules, and wireless energy with Flux Networks, in depth."
  ],
  "quest.35C219094495CADB.title": "Three compact logistics tools",
  "quest.35C219094495CADB.quest_desc": [
    "LaserIO moves items, fluids, energy, chemicals and redstone between machines with beams and cards; Modular Routers does almost anything with items from one block; Flux Networks sends FE without wires. Plain pipes (Pipez) live in the transport chapter."
  ],
  "quest.748A35F0C0CFD79B.title": "Logic Chips",
  "quest.748A35F0C0CFD79B.quest_desc": [
    "Every LaserIO item starts from a Logic Chip: craft the raw chip from clay, gold nuggets, a quartz block and redstone, then smelt it. Make a stack.",
    "",
    "In ENTRELUMEN, two logic chips also go into the Inventory Sensor, an Act III component."
  ],
  "quest.51B53009F045057E.title": "Laser Node and Laser Wrench",
  "quest.51B53009F045057E.quest_desc": [
    "The Laser Node touches your machines. Each of its six sides has a 3x3 grid for cards; right-click a side to open it, and use the top buttons to reach hidden sides. With the Laser Wrench, sneak and right-click one node, then right-click another to link them, up to 8 blocks apart.",
    "",
    "One node can serve several neighbours at once."
  ],
  "quest.002FECF554B908EC.title": "Connectors",
  "quest.002FECF554B908EC.quest_desc": [
    "Laser Connectors are cheap relay points to cover distance, each link again up to 8 blocks. Advanced Connectors pair with one other advanced connector at any distance, even across dimensions; the wrench shows its partner. They do not chunk-load: keep both ends loaded."
  ],
  "quest.2B8419E5F3058AE3.title": "Cards and modes",
  "quest.2B8419E5F3058AE3.quest_desc": [
    "Cards tell a node what to do with the neighbour: Item, Fluid, Energy, Chemical (Mekanism) and Redstone. Right-click a card to set its mode: Extract pulls out, Insert accepts, Stock keeps a filtered amount by pulling from inserters, and Sensor only watches and emits redstone.",
    "",
    "Cards only talk to cards on the same colour channel, so one network can run many routes."
  ],
  "quest.310F29B32CC27EAD.title": "Card settings",
  "quest.310F29B32CC27EAD.quest_desc": [
    "Sneaky picks which face of the neighbour the card works on: insert ore into the top of a furnace and fuel into the bottom from the same side. Priority orders inserters (higher first, otherwise nearest first). Round Robin spreads items evenly, and Enforced waits if one target is full. Exact only moves the full extract amount.",
    "",
    "Click values to change them; Shift is x10 and Ctrl is x64."
  ],
  "quest.0A991223C6FB52A7.title": "Filters",
  "quest.0A991223C6FB52A7.quest_desc": [
    "Filters go in cards: Basic (allow or deny listed items, optional NBT match), Counting (keep or leave a number, 1 to 4096), Tag, Mod and NBT filters. A counting filter on a Stock card keeps exactly that many in the target; with Regulate on, extras are pulled back out."
  ],
  "quest.6AD65369CE259224.title": "Overclockers",
  "quest.6AD65369CE259224.quest_desc": [
    "A plain item card moves 8 items every 20 ticks. Card Overclockers raise that: with 4, 64 items every tick. Fluid cards go from 5,000 mB per second up to 40,000 mB per tick. A node side runs only one card per tick; each Node Overclocker lets it run one more, up to all nine.",
    "",
    "Energy cards need no overclockers: they move up to 1,000,000 FE per tick, with a fill or leave-behind percentage."
  ],
  "quest.4BC75B98C5222905.title": "Redstone over lasers",
  "quest.4BC75B98C5222905.quest_desc": [
    "Redstone cards carry signals across the network on their own redstone channels: Input reads a lever or dust, Output emits weak or strong. Any card can obey a redstone channel (low or high), and a Sensor card lights one when the neighbour matches its filter, with And or Or logic."
  ],
  "quest.3F94E29FF26E96C2.title": "Card Holder and Card Cloner",
  "quest.3F94E29FF26E96C2.quest_desc": [
    "The Card Holder stacks cards with matching settings, filters and overclockers; sneak and right-click to make it pull them from your inventory automatically, and its contents show up when you open a node. The Card Cloner copies one card's settings and pastes them onto others, taking filters and overclockers from the holder."
  ],
  "quest.058BE65D29FE0DB7.title": "Modular Router",
  "quest.058BE65D29FE0DB7.quest_desc": [
    "A block with a one-stack buffer and nine module slots. Every router tick (once per second by default) it runs each module left to right on the buffer or the world around it. Pipes and hoppers can fill the buffer, and a comparator reads it.",
    "",
    "Blank Modules (paper, gold and redstone) start every module; two of them also go into the Handling Core, an Act III component."
  ],
  "quest.0DF16B8B6D8DC75E.title": "Sender and Puller",
  "quest.0DF16B8B6D8DC75E.quest_desc": [
    "Sender Mk1 pushes the buffer to an inventory in a straight line up to 8 blocks with clear sight. Mk2 reaches 24 blocks without sight (sneak-right-click the target with the module), and Mk3 reaches anywhere, any dimension, if the target is loaded. Pullers bring items into the buffer, Mk2 from up to 12 blocks away.",
    "",
    "Each module has nine filter slots and a direction relative to the router."
  ],
  "quest.062014D5E8DC4A34.title": "Working the world",
  "quest.062014D5E8DC4A34.quest_desc": [
    "Breaker, Placer, Vacuum and Activator modules let a router act on blocks and entities. The Breaker mines with the pickaxe it was crafted from, keeping its level and enchantments (Silk Touch, Fortune). The Vacuum grabs drops in a 13x13x13 area. The Activator right-clicks with the buffer item, even on entities, like milking or shearing."
  ],
  "quest.10A239B4537B4512.title": "Extruders, Player and Detector",
  "quest.10A239B4537B4512.quest_desc": [
    "Extruders push out a row of blocks on redstone and pull them back without it: drawbridges and hidden doors, 12 blocks long by default. The Player Module moves items to or from your own inventory, armour or ender chest from anywhere. The Detector emits redstone when the buffer matches its filter."
  ],
  "quest.54C9A1DC5FD165C8.title": "Upgrades and augments",
  "quest.54C9A1DC5FD165C8.quest_desc": [
    "Five router upgrade slots: Speed cuts 2 ticks per upgrade (down to 10 runs a second), Stack moves more per run and is kinder to the server, Energy adds 50,000 FE, Camouflage disguises, Muffler silences. Four augment slots per module: range, stack, redstone rule, regulator and more."
  ],
  "quest.7988B7B4D2D667BD.title": "Security and termination",
  "quest.7988B7B4D2D667BD.quest_desc": [
    "A Security Upgrade lets only listed players open the router, and makes the Placer, Breaker and Activator act as you instead of a nameless fake player: safer inside claims. A module's T button ends the router's run when that module did work, so a Void module for cobblestone can sit before a Sender for everything else."
  ],
  "quest.7681C3B3F5C1B7D3.title": "Flux Dust",
  "quest.7681C3B3F5C1B7D3.quest_desc": [
    "Flux Dust is made in the world: over bedrock (or a Flux Block), leave one block of air, then obsidian above it. Drop redstone into the gap and left-click the obsidian: the redstone turns into Flux Dust. Flux Dust, obsidian and an eye of ender make Flux Cores."
  ],
  "quest.27801123FEE6C86A.title": "Flux Plugs and Points",
  "quest.27801123FEE6C86A.quest_desc": [
    "A Flux Plug takes energy from the blocks it touches into a network; a Flux Point gives it out to the blocks it touches, anywhere the network reaches, across dimensions. Open any device to create a network or join one.",
    "",
    "ENTRELUMEN change: each Plug needs a reinforced alloy (Act III); a network carries nothing without one, so Points stay native."
  ],
  "quest.0745E3328F6CFACD.title": "Network settings",
  "quest.0745E3328F6CFACD.quest_desc": [
    "Each device has a priority, a transfer limit (or Bypass Limit), a Power Surge option for top priority, and optional chunk loading. Networks can be Public, Private or Encrypted with a password, and the members tab manages access. The Flux Configurator copies one device's settings onto others."
  ],
  "quest.5305E83D3AC47468.title": "Flux Storage",
  "quest.5305E83D3AC47468.quest_desc": [
    "Basic, Herculean and Gargantuan Flux Storage hold energy inside the network, each crafted from the one below. Put storage on the network to smooth out bursts from generators."
  ],
  "quest.48039F57E19CAEE5.title": "Flux Controller",
  "quest.48039F57E19CAEE5.quest_desc": [
    "The Flux Controller enables wireless charging: members of the network get items in their inventory charged. Toggle it in the Wireless Charging tab.",
    "",
    "The controller keeps its native recipe: a network needs a gated plug first."
  ],
  "quest.1A22FC3CCB620016.title": "Mastery: a quiet factory",
  "quest.1A22FC3CCB620016.quest_desc": [
    "Wire a machine room without a single pipe: nodes on every machine with Stock cards feeding them, a router sorting and voiding the outputs, and Flux Points powering it all from a distant generator room. Fewer blocks, fewer entities, fewer ticks wasted."
  ],
  "chapter.38AD653124CEAC3B.title": "Mekanism: energy and reactors",
  "chapter.38AD653124CEAC3B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Mekanism Generators from the first heat generator to fission, turbines, fusion and antimatter, plus how to store it all."
  ],
  "quest.4A4E430851F20CF4.title": "Power, Mekanism style",
  "quest.4A4E430851F20CF4.quest_desc": [
    "From day-one generators to base-powering reactors. Energy moves through Universal Cables and waits in Energy Cubes or an Induction Matrix. Start small, keep old generators as backup, and plan big reactors in EMI's multiblock planner."
  ],
  "quest.770AF573AE4A1192.title": "Heat Generator",
  "quest.770AF573AE4A1192.quest_desc": [
    "Burns lava or any fuel item. Pipe lava in and forget it: a Create Hose Pulley in a lava lake makes it endless."
  ],
  "quest.48EF67E0E00158F4.title": "Solar and wind",
  "quest.48EF67E0E00158F4.quest_desc": [
    "Solar Generators need daylight and open sky; the Advanced one catches more. Wind Generators produce more the higher you build them. No fuel, no babysitting: plant a field early."
  ],
  "quest.59101B3B1D85DE6B.title": "Bio Generator",
  "quest.59101B3B1D85DE6B.quest_desc": [
    "The Crusher turns crops, seeds, saplings, flowers and food into Bio Fuel for the Bio Generator. A farm feeding a crusher is renewable power, and bio fuel is also the base of ethene."
  ],
  "quest.1AD59FD5A21F356B.title": "Gas-Burning Generator",
  "quest.1AD59FD5A21F356B.quest_desc": [
    "Burns hydrogen and, much better, ethene: a Pressurized Reaction Chamber turns 2 bio fuel, 10 mB water and 100 mB hydrogen into 100 mB ethene and Substrate. Farm, separator and chamber: a compact fuel plant."
  ],
  "quest.483066BA7A7BDFE7.title": "Universal Cables and Energy Cubes",
  "quest.483066BA7A7BDFE7.quest_desc": [
    "Cables move FE and come in tiers; right-click placed cables with the next alloy to upgrade them. Cubes store energy, charge items and set which sides take or give. A cube by each generator group smooths day and night."
  ],
  "quest.19DD91D523871AD1.title": "Energized Induction Matrix",
  "quest.19DD91D523871AD1.quest_desc": [
    "A hollow box of Induction Casing and glass with Induction Ports; Cells inside add capacity, Providers add transfer rate. A configurator flips a port between input and output. The long-term battery; Extras adds higher tiers."
  ],
  "quest.108225E99DB836AD.title": "Plan multiblocks in EMI",
  "quest.108225E99DB836AD.quest_desc": [
    "Just Enough Mekanism Multiblocks plans any Mekanism structure in EMI: pick one, set its size, see the block cost, layout and stats (burn rate, steam flow, capacity). A turbine with wrong proportions will not even form, so plan first."
  ],
  "quest.5DEAF9CD61FFA814.title": "Heat as a resource",
  "quest.5DEAF9CD61FFA814.quest_desc": [
    "A Resistive Heater turns power into heat, a Fuelwood Heater burns items, Thermodynamic Conductors carry it. Heat drives the Thermoelectric Boiler. Keep heat blocks away from anything flammable."
  ],
  "quest.23D65931AD41ED7F.title": "Thermoelectric Boiler",
  "quest.23D65931AD41ED7F.quest_desc": [
    "Turns water into steam with Superheating Elements or hot coolant from fission. A full layer of Pressure Dispersers splits water and steam sections; valves are set to input, steam or coolant output. Its steam feeds a turbine."
  ],
  "quest.29569F80D701AD3D.title": "Industrial Turbine",
  "quest.29569F80D701AD3D.quest_desc": [
    "Odd width and length; rotors with blades in the middle, a Rotational Complex on top, a full layer of Pressure Dispersers around it, Electromagnetic Coils touching the complex, vents at or above it, Condensers above to return water. Feed it steam from a boiler or a water-cooled reactor."
  ],
  "quest.01F7BFEAFE162B95.title": "Fission fuel",
  "quest.01F7BFEAFE162B95.quest_desc": [
    "Uranium becomes Yellow Cake (enrichment), Uranium Oxide (oxidizer), Uranium Hexafluoride (infuser with hydrofluoric acid from fluorite and sulfuric acid) and finally Fissile Fuel (Isotopic Centrifuge). Fluorite sits deep: plan a steady supply."
  ],
  "quest.2C96C2EAAF41B7E4.title": "Fission Reactor",
  "quest.2C96C2EAAF41B7E4.quest_desc": [
    "Casing and glass around towers of Fuel Assemblies, each capped by a Control Rod. Ports switch with a configurator between input, coolant and waste. Water gives steam; sodium goes through a boiler. Start low, raise slowly, know where SCRAM is: past 100% damage it melts down."
  ],
  "quest.3D74EAF1AE047FEA.title": "Nuclear waste and radiation",
  "quest.3D74EAF1AE047FEA.quest_desc": [
    "Never let waste pile up: pipe it to a Radioactive Waste Barrel or process it into Plutonium and Polonium. A Logic Adapter can stop the reactor at a critical waste level. Geiger Counter for the area, Dosimeter for you, Hazmat Suit to survive leaks."
  ],
  "quest.00FC1E2FC7343444.title": "Fusion Reactor",
  "quest.00FC1E2FC7343444.quest_desc": [
    "Deuterium from heavy water (pump plus Filter Upgrade, then separator), tritium from lithium (Solar Neutron Activator), mixed into D-T fuel. A Hohlraum (gold dust infused with carbon) holding that fuel goes into the controller; charged lasers into the Laser Focus Matrix ignite it."
  ],
  "quest.2FEBB698F3A23BAD.title": "Supercritical Phase Shifter",
  "quest.2FEBB698F3A23BAD.quest_desc": [
    "Turns polonium into antimatter with enormous energy through Supercharged Coils on its ports. Antimatter feeds the Nucleosynthesizer and the MekaSuit's gravitational module. Build it only with a serious power plant behind."
  ],
  "quest.697731EB08867DF6.title": "Naquadah Reactor (Extras)",
  "quest.697731EB08867DF6.quest_desc": [
    "Its own casing, ports and radiation-proof glass, running on naquadah fuel from the Extras ore line. An optional late alternative to fusion; check the planner before building."
  ],
  "quest.01BB17F4F1378EE0.title": "Mekanism power in this pack",
  "quest.01BB17F4F1378EE0.quest_desc": [
    "Generators, matrix and reactors are native: no act component needed. Only the Creative Energy Cube costs Luminosities. The Energy chapter compares Mekanism with the other power mods."
  ],
  "quest.3CA9C31B0DCE2615.title": "Mastery: fusion",
  "quest.3CA9C31B0DCE2615.quest_desc": [
    "Fusion with a turbine on its steam and a matrix storing the output: energy stops being a problem. Keep the old fission reactor for plutonium and polonium; the SPS still needs them."
  ],
  "chapter.4C2044E7F6FFE914.title": "Mekanism: logistics",
  "chapter.4C2044E7F6FFE914.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Transmitters, sorting, QIO storage, teleporters, the Digital Miner and the addons for covers and routers."
  ],
  "quest.1E7FCDF8C67D46C9.title": "A transmitter for everything",
  "quest.1E7FCDF8C67D46C9.quest_desc": [
    "Logistical Transporters for items, Mechanical Pipes for fluids, Pressurized Tubes for chemicals, Universal Cables for energy, Thermodynamic Conductors for heat. All tiered, all upgradable in place with the next alloy."
  ],
  "quest.35CFDD95EF0BEBE4.title": "Logistical Transporter",
  "quest.35CFDD95EF0BEBE4.quest_desc": [
    "Pulls from inventories whose connection is set to pull (configurator) and delivers to the nearest inventory that accepts. The configurator colour-codes items so only matching paths take them. Diversion Transporters obey redstone; Restrictive ones are a last resort route."
  ],
  "quest.56242D5853E1D788.title": "Pipes, tubes and tanks",
  "quest.56242D5853E1D788.quest_desc": [
    "Pipes move fluids, Pressurized Tubes move chemicals, never mixed. Portable tanks carry them; a Dynamic Tank multiblock stores tons. The Electric Pump drains fluids (heavy water with a Filter Upgrade), the Fluidic Plenisher puts them back."
  ],
  "quest.58A15B3DB96171D5.title": "Logistical Sorter",
  "quest.58A15B3DB96171D5.quest_desc": [
    "Against an inventory, it pulls items matching its filters (item, tag or mod) into the transporter behind it, each filter with its own colour; unmatched items can leave with a default colour. One per loot chest keeps a base tidy without digital storage."
  ],
  "quest.7AD100EF8FCD9412.title": "Debugging a network",
  "quest.7AD100EF8FCD9412.quest_desc": [
    "The Network Reader shows what a transmitter network holds and moves. The configurator sets each side to normal, push, pull or none. Items bouncing back and forth? One side is pulling where it should push."
  ],
  "quest.66C520DFF400128D.title": "QIO: Quantum Item Orchestration",
  "quest.66C520DFF400128D.quest_desc": [
    "Mekanism's digital storage: a Drive Array holds QIO Drives (Drive, Hyper-Dense, Time-Dilating, Supermassive), and Dashboards, Importers, Exporters and Redstone Adapters reach it by frequency, no cables. The Portable Dashboard is a terminal in your pocket. Extras adds bigger drives."
  ],
  "quest.1979979E1A2C4484.title": "QIO or AE2?",
  "quest.1979979E1A2C4484.quest_desc": [
    "QIO has no channels or cables, but its first drive already wants Ultimate circuits. AE2 is cheaper to start and has deeper autocrafting. Bridges exist (Applied Mekanistics, RS Mekanism integration): pick one main system and let the others feed it."
  ],
  "quest.2F8F385F077C7A3E.title": "Teleporter",
  "quest.2F8F385F077C7A3E.quest_desc": [
    "A frame of Teleporter Frame blocks around an empty space with the Teleporter in it. Same frequency on two of them, walk through, pay energy per jump. The Portable Teleporter does it from your hand."
  ],
  "quest.7734F3CA01E08282.title": "Quantum Entangloporter",
  "quest.7734F3CA01E08282.quest_desc": [
    "Entangloporters on one frequency share items, fluids, chemicals, energy and heat instantly, at any distance and across dimensions. Configure sides like a machine. Power in, ores out, from any outpost."
  ],
  "quest.679EE6710CBD36EA.title": "Digital Miner",
  "quest.679EE6710CBD36EA.quest_desc": [
    "Mines the blocks you filter within a radius of up to 32, between the Y levels you set, into an inventory. Expensive (atomic alloy, a robit, a teleportation core) and power-hungry. Tag filters for ores; with Silk Touch and a good line, one miner feeds the base."
  ],
  "quest.2B9C871772346B23.title": "Robit and Chargepad",
  "quest.2B9C871772346B23.quest_desc": [
    "The Robit follows you, picks up items, crafts and smelts, and recharges on a Chargepad, which charges any mod's powered items while you stand on it. It is also a Digital Miner ingredient."
  ],
  "quest.72FDB9137F8338F4.title": "Mekanism Covers",
  "quest.72FDB9137F8338F4.quest_desc": [
    "Craft Empty Covers (osmium nuggets, sawdust, glass; four at a time) and combine one with a block to get a Cover of it. Covers hide transmitters behind the look of your walls: neat factories, cables still inside."
  ],
  "quest.69FAA53443B0B9B7.title": "Mekanistic Routers",
  "quest.69FAA53443B0B9B7.quest_desc": [
    "Chemical modules for Modular Routers: Mk1 moves chemicals to or from the block ahead, Mk2 reaches any nearby block, and the Refill Module tops up chemical items (like jetpacks) in your inventory wirelessly. The router needs a chemical container in its buffer."
  ],
  "quest.021E60BA01115D24.title": "Keeping machines running",
  "quest.021E60BA01115D24.quest_desc": [
    "Machines only work in loaded chunks. Mekanism has the Anchor Upgrade and the Dimensional Stabilizer; FTB Chunks lets your team force-load claimed chunks. Load only what must run alone: every chunk costs the server."
  ],
  "quest.30F0A34B1A356CFF.title": "Oredictionificator",
  "quest.30F0A34B1A356CFF.quest_desc": [
    "Converts items into the tag-equivalent item, say one mod's ingot into another's. Almost Unified already handles recipes; this cleans up drops and old chests. Filters go by tag."
  ],
  "quest.27D4F630282E2F33.title": "Mastery: miner to vault",
  "quest.27D4F630282E2F33.quest_desc": [
    "A Digital Miner in a mining area, an Entangloporter carrying its output home, a QIO system sorting it and your ore line processing it. A Portable Dashboard puts the whole base in your pocket."
  ],
  "chapter.36309EC497FB12EB.title": "Oritech",
  "chapter.36309EC497FB12EB.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Animated machines with cores and addons, lasers, gantry frames, drones, a modular reactor and a particle accelerator."
  ],
  "quest.2E2BEDE6BEB55268.title": "Big, animated machines",
  "quest.2E2BEDE6BEB55268.quest_desc": [
    "Oritech runs on RF (plain FE). Machines grow with cores and addons, lasers carry energy and dig, gantries farm and build, drones ship between bases, and a modular reactor and a particle accelerator crown it. The Oracle Index manual has a page for every block."
  ],
  "quest.21C03EBF4DEA19C6.title": "Nickel first",
  "quest.21C03EBF4DEA19C6.quest_desc": [
    "Copper, iron, coal and above all nickel for early machines and alloys; redstone, gold and diamonds soon after. Remember where amethyst geodes are: fluxite comes from them later."
  ],
  "quest.6D3692B4895FD225.title": "Basic Generator",
  "quest.6D3692B4895FD225.quest_desc": [
    "Nickel, copper, a furnace and two magnetic coils: 32 RF/t from furnace fuel. Build a few. Power is push-based: generators push into Energy Pipes (10,000 RF/t); a wrench cuts unwanted connections."
  ],
  "quest.13FF438B9DAC8414.title": "Pulverizer and Foundry",
  "quest.13FF438B9DAC8414.quest_desc": [
    "Steel, electrum and adamant can be hand-crafted, expensively. Move to a Pulverizer (ores and biomass to dust) and a Foundry (alloys, 3 machine cores) fast; they open biosteel, energite and duratium."
  ],
  "quest.35DBF6C8F461BD7E.title": "Machine cores",
  "quest.35DBF6C8F461BD7E.quest_desc": [
    "Bigger machines need cores in marked spots: right-click to highlight them, or click holding a core to place the next. Better cores raise quality (how many addons and extenders fit), not speed. No addons planned? Cheapest cores."
  ],
  "quest.257FB597393ED681.title": "Addons",
  "quest.257FB597393ED681.quest_desc": [
    "Speed, efficiency, capacitors, inventory proxies, fluid access, redstone, yield and more snap onto marked spots: blue means connected, pink means not. Extenders add spots up to the machine's quality. A Steam Boiler addon turns a generator into a steam maker."
  ],
  "quest.17BFEFFD52B91A0C.title": "Assembler, Centrifuge, Fragment Forge",
  "quest.17BFEFFD52B91A0C.quest_desc": [
    "The Assembler makes components better than hand crafting. The Fragment Forge breaks ores into clumps (feed it silk-touched blocks); the Centrifuge turns clumps into gems, more with water or acid. Nickel fragmenting is early platinum."
  ],
  "quest.4E8B29DF95E47ED3.title": "Enderic Laser and fluxite",
  "quest.4E8B29DF95E47ED3.quest_desc": [
    "Fires up to 128 blocks. Aim it with a Target Designator at amethyst clusters to harvest fluxite, gate to the strong machines. Lasers also power the Atomic Forge and Bedrock Extractor wirelessly."
  ],
  "quest.3BE889B5BCB922B9.title": "Atomic Forge",
  "quest.3BE889B5BCB922B9.quest_desc": [
    "Laser-powered only (pipes cannot connect), 8 machine cores. Advanced chips, reinforced deepslate, high-yield processing, and compatibility recipes for Mekanism circuits."
  ],
  "quest.04978122063C0015.title": "More generators",
  "quest.04978122063C0015.quest_desc": [
    "Lava, Fuel and Bio generators, a Big Solar Panel (32 RF/t in clear daylight) and the Steam Engine, fed by boiler-fitted generators, up to 50,000 RF/t. Oritech biofuel also super-heats a Create liquid burner."
  ],
  "quest.386CE7DAA46B48F5.title": "Pipes and drones",
  "quest.386CE7DAA46B48F5.quest_desc": [
    "Item pipes hold nothing: set one to extract from a neighbour, 8 items every 5 ticks. Drone Ports ship items and fluids to a port at least 50 blocks away, linked with a Target Designator: a chunk-friendly link between bases."
  ],
  "quest.2749BEE5AECFECFB.title": "Machine frames and gantries",
  "quest.2749BEE5AECFECFB.quest_desc": [
    "A rectangle of frame blocks (up to 64 long, empty inside) carries gantry machines: the Destroyer breaks, the Placer places, the Fertilizer grows. Farms and clearing without contraptions; the Tree Feller and Pump cover areas too."
  ],
  "quest.4365678511B2C10F.title": "Bedrock Extractor",
  "quest.4365678511B2C10F.quest_desc": [
    "26 cores, laser power, and it only works right above infinite resource nodes below bedrock (it scans 3x3). Pack change: it needs an ironwood ingot (Act IV), like every quarry."
  ],
  "quest.2C294F1441BCF3BB.title": "Exo suit and jetpacks",
  "quest.2C294F1441BCF3BB.quest_desc": [
    "The Exo Suit is early powered armour, one ability per piece. Jetpacks run on energy or turbofuel (Equipment Charger); the Exo Jetpack joins a jetpack and the Exo chestplate. Pack change: Jetpack needs a reinforced alloy (III), Exo Jetpack a zanite gemstone (IV), and all four jetpacks burn 2.5 times their native energy or fuel per tick."
  ],
  "quest.168FFC0A8124663A.title": "Arcane machines",
  "quest.168FFC0A8124663A.quest_desc": [
    "The Stabilized Enchanter picks the exact enchantment, paid in energy and helped by catalysts within 16 blocks. The Spawner Controller runs a spawner cage for drops. Pack change: the controller needs an ironwood ingot (IV)."
  ],
  "quest.59937063F0B18650.title": "Oritech reactor",
  "quest.59937063F0B18650.quest_desc": [
    "Up to 64 per side: walls on the edges, controller and energy ports (25,000 RF/t each) on the walls, fuel ports above the rods. Rods burn uranium or plutonium pellets; reflectors add efficiency; heat pipes, vents and ice-fed absorbers cool it. A rod over 2000 C too long melts down, and sirens warn first."
  ],
  "quest.26A7F7A273919745.title": "Particle accelerator",
  "quest.26A7F7A273919745.quest_desc": [
    "A ring of guides and motors: inject a particle, bring it up to speed, then inject a slow one into the same ring. Collision energy (sum of speeds) sets the result. Pack change: the controller needs an atomic alloy (V) and the Nether Star collision is removed."
  ],
  "quest.792CA8B0AABC4121.title": "Pack changes to Oritech",
  "quest.792CA8B0AABC4121.quest_desc": [
    "Jetpack (III), Exo Jetpack (IV), Bedrock Extractor (IV), Spawner Controller (IV), both nukes (ironwood, IV) and the accelerator controller (V) are gated; the Nether Star collision is gone. Everything else is native."
  ],
  "quest.19A9E13BBBEC2073.title": "Mastery: reactor to extractor",
  "quest.19A9E13BBBEC2073.quest_desc": [
    "A stable reactor feeding lasers that run an Atomic Forge and a Bedrock Extractor, with drones shipping it all home. Read the manual's reactor designs page before building big."
  ],
  "chapter.087AEC7F43E53ABA.title": "PneumaticCraft: Repressurized",
  "chapter.087AEC7F43E53ABA.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Compressed air as power, the Pressure Chamber, heat, oil, printed circuit boards, drones and logistics frames."
  ],
  "quest.51D2947340B730B4.title": "Running on air",
  "quest.51D2947340B730B4.quest_desc": [
    "Compressors make air (measured in bar), tubes carry it, machines spend it. Add real heat, crude oil, a chemistry line to plastic and circuit boards, and programmable drones. The manual (book plus compressed iron) unlocks pages with advancements. Its PCB goes into the Routing Matrix (III) and the Ark Bus (V)."
  ],
  "quest.3150D58D03E04401.title": "Compressed Iron: blow it up",
  "quest.3150D58D03E04401.quest_desc": [
    "No ores here. Throw iron ingots on the ground and blow them up with TNT: they become Compressed Iron, losing about 20%. The Pressure Chamber later does it without loss. Start with a stack of iron and a stack of stone."
  ],
  "quest.053308E13DBBF678.title": "How pressure works",
  "quest.053308E13DBBF678.quest_desc": [
    "Pressure is air divided by volume, minus one, in bar; air flows high to low. Open faces leak with a hiss: close them with the Pneumatic Wrench. Tier 1 machines resist 5 bar, tier 1.5 up to 10, tier 2 up to 20. Volume Upgrades add capacity."
  ],
  "quest.406D06BE3F1FCDC1.title": "Air Compressor and tubes",
  "quest.406D06BE3F1FCDC1.quest_desc": [
    "Burns any furnace fuel for a base 10 mL of air per tick (lava goes to the Liquid Compressor). Pressure Tubes carry air; a Pressure Gauge reads it. Other compressors: Flux (FE in, needs cooling), Thermal, Solar, Liquid, Advanced."
  ],
  "quest.34253C1A53D95911.title": "Pressure Chamber",
  "quest.34253C1A53D95911.quest_desc": [
    "A hollow 3x3x3 to 5x5x5 box of walls or glass, with a Valve for air and two Interfaces for items in and out. Under pressure it makes lossless Compressed Iron, etching acid, Empty PCBs and more. It stores a lot of air: a battery too."
  ],
  "quest.5326DE3052C2CB47.title": "Heat",
  "quest.5326DE3052C2CB47.quest_desc": [
    "Heat flows hot to cold, faster across big gaps and through conductive blocks like Compressed Iron Blocks. Lava, magma, ice and water are sources that change when drained. Heat Sinks cool, the Vortex Tube splits hot and cold. Some machines like heat, compressors and the dynamo hate it."
  ],
  "quest.721672145B1351AF.title": "Crude oil",
  "quest.721672145B1351AF.quest_desc": [
    "PneumaticCraft's only worldgen: oil lakes, mostly deep. A Seismic Sensor on the ground says if oil is below and how deep; a Gas Lift drills down and pumps it up. Oil becomes fuels, plastic and lubricant."
  ],
  "quest.5FA15976B9F5A7BA.title": "Refinery and plastic",
  "quest.5FA15976B9F5A7BA.quest_desc": [
    "The Refinery (controller plus 2 to 4 stacked outputs) needs 100 C or more; more outputs, more products. The Thermopneumatic Processing Plant turns LPG and coal, or biodiesel and charcoal, into molten plastic that hardens into sheets. No oil nearby? Biodiesel from yeast, vegetable oil and ethanol."
  ],
  "quest.31AD4839D991F0C3.title": "Printed Circuit Board",
  "quest.31AD4839D991F0C3.quest_desc": [
    "Empty PCB from the Pressure Chamber, exposed in a UV Light Box, etched in an Etching Tank, then crafted with capacitors and transistors. The UV box needs a PCB Blueprint, never crafted: trade for it via Amadron or a Mechanic villager. Failed boards go back to empty in a blast furnace."
  ],
  "quest.096DC7A2B6B67B2F.title": "PCBs in the act components",
  "quest.096DC7A2B6B67B2F.quest_desc": [
    "One PCB goes into the Routing Matrix (III), two into the Ark Bus (V); the mod itself is native, so start the plastic and PCB line early. The pack also fixed the manual clashing with Psi's book: both are craftable."
  ],
  "quest.4B1FD4C2C0FF7ED9.title": "Amadron and Mechanic villagers",
  "quest.4B1FD4C2C0FF7ED9.quest_desc": [
    "The Amadron Tablet orders drone deliveries, paid from a bound chest: things you cannot craft (PCB Blueprint, Assembly Programs), daily villager deals and player trades. Mechanic villagers live in their own houses; a Charging Station can turn a jobless villager into one."
  ],
  "quest.3ADE220C3D504D30.title": "Assembly System",
  "quest.3ADE220C3D504D30.quest_desc": [
    "Controller (the only part needing air), Platform, IO Units, Drill and Laser, side by side. Programs are traded, not crafted. The Laser program takes an Empty PCB straight to Unassembled, skipping UV and etching: the mass-production route."
  ],
  "quest.47774B423F345834.title": "Charging Station and upgrades",
  "quest.47774B423F345834.quest_desc": [
    "Pressurizes pneumatic items (usually to 10 bar) and installs upgrades: Volume, Speed, Dispenser, Inventory, Item Life, trackers and more; each GUI explains them. With a Dispenser Upgrade it recharges drones."
  ],
  "quest.21F5D15D3C5C324C.title": "Pneumatic Armor",
  "quest.21F5D15D3C5C324C.quest_desc": [
    "Barely better than iron until upgraded at the Charging Station: the helmet tracks mobs and blocks through walls, the boots cancel fall damage, give step assist and, with Jet Boots, flight (in this pack at 2.5 times the native air). The armour key (Ctrl+U in this pack) opens its settings."
  ],
  "quest.6C988EF917A96E05.title": "Drones",
  "quest.6C988EF917A96E05.quest_desc": [
    "Simple drones need no code: Collector (items to a chest, 17x17x17), Harvesting (give it a hoe to replant), Guard, Logistics. Programmable Drones run puzzle-piece programs. Low on air, they fly to a Charging Station with a Dispenser Upgrade within 80 blocks."
  ],
  "quest.747148527B77FFE1.title": "Programmer and Programmable Controller",
  "quest.747148527B77FFE1.quest_desc": [
    "Programs are puzzle-piece widgets (areas, conditions, dig, place, import, export and more; one manual page each). The Programmable Controller runs them with a non-entity mini-drone: no pathfinding, through walls, kinder to servers, more air. Prefer it for stationary jobs."
  ],
  "quest.14CC555DEE6D9EF0.title": "Logistics frames",
  "quest.14CC555DEE6D9EF0.quest_desc": [
    "Frames on chests and tanks say what to provide, store or request; Logistics Drones (33x33x33) or tubes with Logistics Modules move items and fluids between them. Factorio-style, on your existing inventories."
  ],
  "quest.25C690D3A3687FE0.title": "Handy machines",
  "quest.25C690D3A3687FE0.quest_desc": [
    "The Elevator lifts any entity, the Pneumatic Dynamo turns air into FE (keep it cool), Omnidirectional and Liquid Hoppers move things any direction, the Heat Frame smelts or freezes any inventory's contents, and the Security Station locks an area. The Jackhammer and Minigun run on air."
  ],
  "quest.7D3828A28FF6D5C5.title": "Mastery: a factory on air",
  "quest.7D3828A28FF6D5C5.quest_desc": [
    "An assembly line making PCBs, a refinery on a gas lift, a controller doing chores and jet boots on your feet. Keep PCBs flowing: the Ark Bus needs them later."
  ],
  "chapter.348CEA2D00B3DA83.title": "RFTools and XNet",
  "chapter.348CEA2D00B3DA83.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Machine frames and dimensional shards, power cells, crafters, screens, teleporters, the Builder, and XNet channel networks."
  ],
  "quest.05304B06AF7BC363.title": "RFTools as glue",
  "quest.05304B06AF7BC363.quest_desc": [
    "Base, Power, Utility and Builder, plus XNet: FE generation and storage, logic blocks, crafters, screens, teleporters, a shape-card Builder and channel logistics. Storage and Dimensions are left out on purpose (AE2 and the pack's own dimensions cover them). One shared manual."
  ],
  "quest.58B31E223A20F0D6.title": "Machine Frame and Dimensional Shards",
  "quest.58B31E223A20F0D6.quest_desc": [
    "The Machine Frame houses most machines; the Machine Base makes the quarter-block logic devices. Dimensional Shard ore (several dimensions, Fortune works) feeds advanced recipes and infusing. The Smart Wrench rotates, picks up and selects."
  ],
  "quest.29E9AAEA105FD7E2.title": "Machine Infuser",
  "quest.29E9AAEA105FD7E2.quest_desc": [
    "Feeds shards into a machine: most then use less power, some gain more (faster teleporters, longer screen range, stronger generators). Infuse whatever runs all day."
  ],
  "quest.7C066FE9FC7FCF26.title": "Coal Generator and Powercells",
  "quest.7C066FE9FC7FCF26.quest_desc": [
    "The Coal Generator burns coal or coal blocks into FE, free on purpose. Powercells store lots of FE and merge with neighbours of any tier; the Smart Wrench sets each side (blue in, yellow out). The Endergenic Generator is an ender-pearl timing puzzle for experts."
  ],
  "quest.45510A06967F9601.title": "Dimensional Cells",
  "quest.45510A06967F9601.quest_desc": [
    "Cells linked with a Powercell Card share FE without touching, across dimensions; remote draws cost a few percent, less when infused. Pack change: Simple and regular Dimensional Cells need a reinforced alloy (III); local Powercells stay the cheap option."
  ],
  "quest.36B12A0BD6F53671.title": "Crafter",
  "quest.36B12A0BD6F53671.quest_desc": [
    "Powered autocrafting: the top tier holds 8 recipes, 26 input and 4 output slots. R remembers a slot's item so it only accepts that, F forgets. Recipes live on Crafting Cards; it takes a Filter Module, and infusing cuts its power use."
  ],
  "quest.612F9FC41120325A.title": "Logic blocks and screens",
  "quest.612F9FC41120325A.quest_desc": [
    "Quarter-block timers, counters, sequencers, sensors, inventory checkers, analog and digit blocks, wireless redstone. Screens show energy, inventories and more through modules, powered by a Screen Controller (32x32x32); a Screen Link in a Tablet opens one remotely."
  ],
  "quest.181E685FFBFE7E7E.title": "Matter Transmitter and Receiver",
  "quest.181E685FFBFE7E7E.quest_desc": [
    "Stand on a Transmitter and jump to any Receiver, even in another dimension; a Dialing Device picks the destination. An underpowered receiver makes for a bad trip. Charged Porters teleport from your hand. Pack change: the Receiver needs a reinforced alloy (III); Porters only reach receivers, so they stay native."
  ],
  "quest.1C4C957B5C85CA8F.title": "Environmental Controller and Spawner",
  "quest.1C4C957B5C85CA8F.quest_desc": [
    "The Environmental Controller bathes an area in up to seven effect modules, more effects costing more power. The Spawner makes mobs from a filled syringe, FE and beamed materials. Pack change: Controller needs a reinforced alloy (III), Spawner an ironwood ingot (IV)."
  ],
  "quest.58DECA7D319F0107.title": "Builder and shape cards",
  "quest.58DECA7D319F0107.quest_desc": [
    "A Shape Card (box, sphere, cylinder, cone, torus, prism or scanned) with size, offset and fill tells the Builder what to build from supplied blocks; a Quarry Card makes it mine (Clear, Silk Touch, Fortune); Void, Liquid and Pump cards too. Pack change: Builder needs a Handling Core (III), Quarry Card two ironwood ingots (IV)."
  ],
  "quest.095CEC2B71BC1EB2.title": "Quarry etiquette",
  "quest.095CEC2B71BC1EB2.quest_desc": [
    "A quarry card empties huge volumes and backfills them unless you use a Clear variant. Run it in a JAMD mining dimension, not under your base or a village, and never in someone else's claim. It only works while its chunk is loaded."
  ],
  "quest.06141C8077AB2510.title": "XNet: controller, cables, connectors",
  "quest.06141C8077AB2510.quest_desc": [
    "Coloured cables (red, green, blue, yellow never connect to each other), connectors next to your blocks and one Controller. In it, add a channel (items, fluids, energy or logic) and connectors with side, priority, filter and speed. Pack change: the Controller needs a reinforced alloy (III)."
  ],
  "quest.4B7327FBE1FDB730.title": "XNet routers",
  "quest.4B7327FBE1FDB730.quest_desc": [
    "A Router links controller networks through routing cables: channels published on one side, consumed on the other. A Wireless Router does it without cables via an antenna on top (the dish has unlimited range at higher cost). Both routers keep their native recipes: they only work under a controller."
  ],
  "quest.7CF9EF22817C4CDF.title": "A useful XNet project",
  "quest.7CF9EF22817C4CDF.quest_desc": [
    "An energy channel plus a logic channel: a sensor watches a generator's buffer and feeds fuel only when it runs low, while an item channel ships output to the next workshop. One controller, items, fluids, FE and logic together."
  ],
  "quest.29B6F92F9CE9BAA0.title": "Mastery: the glue holds",
  "quest.29B6F92F9CE9BAA0.quest_desc": [
    "Powercells feeding the base, crafters on XNet, screens showing everything, a transmitter linking two bases and a Builder quarrying in the mining dimension."
  ],
  "chapter.4A93C950B465A2BB.title": "Refined Storage",
  "chapter.4A93C950B465A2BB.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The AE2 alternative: disks, grids and autocrafting with no channels. Same act, same components."
  ],
  "quest.26071B5D22707D62.title": "The other network",
  "quest.26071B5D22707D62.quest_desc": [
    "Refined Storage 2 does AE2's job with a simpler model: no channels, no meteorites, devices just touch the network. Optional: use it instead of AE2, or skip it. Pack change: Controller needs a Routing Matrix and Autocrafter a Handling Core, both Act III."
  ],
  "quest.092BCE5A62415FEB.title": "Quartz Enriched Iron and silicon",
  "quest.092BCE5A62415FEB.quest_desc": [
    "Three iron and one quartz make Quartz Enriched Iron; smelting quartz gives Silicon; eight QEI around stone make a Machine Casing. All plain crafting."
  ],
  "quest.05ADD56B9952F082.title": "Processors",
  "quest.05ADD56B9952F082.quest_desc": [
    "Binding (string, slime), silicon, redstone and iron, gold or diamond make Basic, Improved or Advanced raw processors: smelt to finish. Basic plus glowstone or quartz gives Construction and Destruction Cores. Most blocks want Advanced: save diamonds."
  ],
  "quest.0C90134B43428CA3.title": "Controller",
  "quest.0C90134B43428CA3.quest_desc": [
    "Powers the network with FE; several can share one network. Devices connect by touching or through cables; coloured cables only join their colour or grey, full blocks join any. Pack change: the silicon at the bottom becomes a Routing Matrix (Act III)."
  ],
  "quest.5382BA302E8991CE.title": "Disk Drive and disks",
  "quest.5382BA302E8991CE.quest_desc": [
    "Storage Disks hold 1k to 64k items (fluid disks in buckets), counting items, not types. Upgrade by crafting with a bigger part; an empty disk used in hand returns its part. Storage Blocks are the placeable version."
  ],
  "quest.2DF0680282D23B52.title": "Grids",
  "quest.2DF0680282D23B52.quest_desc": [
    "A Grid searches the whole network; with a crafting table it is a Crafting Grid, with a pattern a Pattern Grid. The Wireless Grid needs a Wireless Transmitter. The Portable Grid reads one disk with no network at all."
  ],
  "quest.4AF54AD3486EC50E.title": "Importer, Exporter, External Storage",
  "quest.4AF54AD3486EC50E.quest_desc": [
    "Importers pull in, Exporters push filtered resources out, External Storage adds any chest, drawer or tank with priority and filters. Upgrades: Speed, Stack, Regulator (export only while the target is below a set amount), Silk Touch, Fortune, Autocrafting."
  ],
  "quest.330E2F5809DE66F8.title": "Constructor, Destructor, Detector",
  "quest.330E2F5809DE66F8.quest_desc": [
    "Constructors place blocks from the network, Destructors break blocks into it (Silk Touch or Fortune upgrades), Detectors emit redstone by amount. A destructor on a cobble generator: infinite cobble."
  ],
  "quest.693470EAA0DF5046.title": "Autocrafter",
  "quest.693470EAA0DF5046.quest_desc": [
    "Pattern Grid patterns go into an Autocrafter facing a machine or station. Processing patterns list inputs out and outputs back; fuzzy mode accepts tag alternatives; higher priority wins. Pack change: a Handling Core (Act III) takes its machine casing's place."
  ],
  "quest.64046813EA62830E.title": "Autocrafting on demand",
  "quest.64046813EA62830E.quest_desc": [
    "An Autocrafting Upgrade in an Interface, Exporter or Constructor crafts whatever is missing. The Autocrafter Manager lists every pattern; the Autocrafting Monitor shows running jobs. Exporter plus Regulator plus Autocrafting keeps a chest topped up."
  ],
  "quest.1110515AD1564BE5.title": "Networks without cables",
  "quest.1110515AD1564BE5.quest_desc": [
    "A Network Transmitter and Receiver paired by a Network Card link a far section without cables. A Relay switches sections on or off and can expose only part of the network. The Security Manager with Security Cards sets permissions per player."
  ],
  "quest.25865080017091A2.title": "Chemicals in Refined Storage",
  "quest.25865080017091A2.quest_desc": [
    "The Mekanism integration adds Chemical Storage Disks and Blocks (64B to 8192B), so importers, exporters and grids handle chemicals, like Applied Mekanistics does for AE2. EMI moves recipes straight into grids."
  ],
  "quest.54732CCEAF78597A.title": "AE2 or Refined Storage?",
  "quest.54732CCEAF78597A.quest_desc": [
    "Same act, same bases. RS: no channels, disks count items, easy layout. AE2: channels to plan, but more addons here and the processors the Routing Matrix needs. Run both if you like, but keep one main storage."
  ],
  "quest.4E12666A1E451997.title": "Creative parts",
  "quest.4E12666A1E451997.quest_desc": [
    "The creative controller and disks have no survival recipe. The only pack gates are the Controller (Routing Matrix) and the Autocrafter (Handling Core). The Wrench rotates, and sneak-use dismantles."
  ],
  "quest.2184DCB320F1FED3.title": "Mastery: one search box",
  "quest.2184DCB320F1FED3.quest_desc": [
    "Controller, a wall of 64k disks, a crafting grid, a wireless grid and autocrafters feeding your machines. Moving to AE2 later? External Storage bridges the two while you migrate."
  ],
  "chapter.23EBFFCF7DB0326C.title": "Magic in ENTRELUMEN",
  "chapter.23EBFFCF7DB0326C.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Which schools open in each act, and the Atlas components that tie them together."
  ],
  "quest.64B2A5E5963EA9CE.title": "Many schools, no walls",
  "quest.64B2A5E5963EA9CE.quest_desc": [
    "You can play the whole story leaning on a few schools. What ties them together are the Atlas components, story items made from magic materials: every team touches Ars Nouveau, Occultism, Malum, EvilCraft and Nature's Aura at least once.",
    "",
    "Heliodor ran on light. You'll run on whatever works."
  ],
  "quest.37C01E0CCF31B45B.title": "Which school for what",
  "quest.37C01E0CCF31B45B.quest_desc": [
    "Fights: Iron's Spells. Utility and automation: Ars Nouveau. Working spirits: Occultism. Alchemical ores: Theurgy. Growing the world: Nature's Aura. Souls: Malum. Dark forging: Forbidden and Arcanus. Blood and brooms: EvilCraft. Relics: Reliquary. Programmed spells: Psi. Blood circles: Mahou Tsukai. Gear: Apotheosis.",
    "",
    "Master one or two; taste the rest."
  ],
  "quest.3F94947246CE6851.title": "Act I: the first sparks",
  "quest.3F94947246CE6851.quest_desc": [
    "No magic required yet, but doors are open: bookshelves take the table toward 30, Apotheosis starts at Haven, EvilCraft's dark ore shows up around redstone depth, and Artifacts turn up in chests.",
    "",
    "Stock up on books, lapis and gold."
  ],
  "quest.2C0E497095FC1CAA.title": "Act II: the magic act",
  "quest.2C0E497095FC1CAA.quest_desc": [
    "Most schools open: Ars, Occultism, Nature's Aura, Iron's Spells, Forbidden and Arcanus, Theurgy, the first relics and EvilCraft's blood. The table reaches 45. The story asks for Ars: the Living Matrix, delivered to «Living Workshop»."
  ],
  "quest.4051B723D469D474.title": "A Matrix for the Atlas",
  "quest.4051B723D469D474.quest_desc": [
    "Two magebloom fibers and two Source Gems in a cross around a Calibration Frame. Beyond the Act II delivery, Matrices go into the Propagation Core (Act III) and the Ecosystem Capsule (Act IV): a steady Ars workshop pays off for a long time."
  ],
  "quest.16714199FE6F628C.title": "Act III: deeper magic",
  "quest.16714199FE6F628C.quest_desc": [
    "Psi and Mahou Tsukai arrive. Put Occultism's spirits to work and start Malum's soul research: Act IV needs both. The table reaches 60, the first spawner augments appear, and the World Tier rises to Frontier, invaders included.",
    "",
    "Salvage the affix gear you don't use."
  ],
  "quest.3164104B39F3F774.title": "Act IV: voices and seals",
  "quest.3164104B39F3F774.quest_desc": [
    "Magic supplies two key components: the Spectral Lens and the Containment Seal. They unlock Theurgy's transmutation, the Eternal Stella, shelves up to 90, the Act IV augments and, with a Horizon Chart, the Rending Gale. World Tier: Ascent."
  ],
  "quest.157613639B482C59.title": "The Spectral Lens",
  "quest.157613639B482C59.quest_desc": [
    "An Occultism attuned crystal, two Malum arcane spirits, a Create precision mechanism and a Calibration Frame. Deliver one to «Voices in the Glass» and keep making them: the Seal, reinforced machines, shelves and the Arcane Module use it.",
    "",
    "Glass that hears what isn't said."
  ],
  "quest.51EE903C0C24FFF6.title": "Seal of the dark schools",
  "quest.51EE903C0C24FFF6.quest_desc": [
    "Two EvilCraft dark gems, two Malum Soulstained Steel and a Spectral Lens. Delivered to «A Vessel for Restless Memory», it gives your team an Altar of Time. It also gates the Eternal Stella, Theurgy's emitter, the fission reactor, the Burning augment and the Atlas Library."
  ],
  "quest.0690F6AE03FF5F8F.title": "Act V: the Ark",
  "quest.0690F6AE03FF5F8F.quest_desc": [
    "Two Ark pieces are magical: the Renewal Engine (Nature's Aura, farming and bees) and the Arcane Module (every dark school). The table reaches 100, the Atlas Library opens up, and at Summit tier Mythic loot and Godforged Pearls start to drop."
  ],
  "quest.523AB48D42660EA3.title": "An engine that grows gardens",
  "quest.523AB48D42660EA3.quest_desc": [
    "Two Ingots of the Skies, two imperium essences, two Ecosystem Capsules and two Propagation Cores. Deliver one to «Renewable Horizons»; more go into the Nature Module, Mekanism's SPS, the Mega pots and Act V augments.",
    "",
    "The gardens come back, one engine at a time."
  ],
  "quest.112D4E9BD5A29894.title": "The Arcane Module",
  "quest.112D4E9BD5A29894.quest_desc": [
    "Two Spectral Lenses, two Containment Seals, an iesnium ingot and the Wither's nether star. In a complete Ark it resets an item's anvil penalty for books and XP, keeping enchantments, affixes and sockets. Iesnium needs Occultism's infused pickaxe: plan ahead."
  ],
  "quest.318923AC1CC86BDE.title": "Act VI: light made solid",
  "quest.318923AC1CC86BDE.quest_desc": [
    "Solsticio's villagers sell six Luminosities, one per discipline; violet Arcane is magic's. They make the Luminous ingot and the creative items: the Source Jar for Ars, the Blood Drop for EvilCraft, the bookshelf for Create: Enchantment Industry. World Tier: Pinnacle."
  ],
  "quest.2E7C7D0C1E3A8844.title": "Where the magic keys went",
  "quest.2E7C7D0C1E3A8844.quest_desc": [
    "Ars radial: F6. Iron's wheel: the key left of 1, cast: Alt+Q. Psi: Alt+F. Mahou Tsukai's circle: Alt+M. Occultism's satchel: Insert, ender bag: O. Apotheosis: Ctrl+T World Tiers, Ctrl+O radial mining, Shift+T link item. All changeable under Controls."
  ],
  "quest.450143F1ED9D1D09.title": "Shortcuts the pack closed",
  "quest.450143F1ED9D1D09.quest_desc": [
    "Reliquary's Alkahestry Tome (item duplication) and its spawn-egg crafting, Apotheosis's spawner runes (copper augments replace them) and portable spawners. Everything else keeps its native recipe unless its chapter says otherwise.",
    "",
    "Every school keeps its place in line."
  ],
  "quest.5A233C6A570EB457.title": "Every school has a book",
  "quest.5A233C6A570EB457.quest_desc": [
    "Most guides craft from a book: Worn Notebook (Ars), Dictionary of Spirits (Occultism), Encyclopedia Arcana (Malum), Book of Natural Aura, Chronicle of Shadows (Apotheosis), Knowledge Compendium (Mahou Tsukai). EvilCraft's is chest loot, Psi's is cast onto a book, Reliquary uses EMI."
  ],
  "quest.60B4CFB438EA8E87.title": "Magic that belongs to the story",
  "quest.60B4CFB438EA8E87.quest_desc": [
    "Living Matrices from your Ars workshop, lenses and seals from the dark schools, a Renewal Engine that grows the world back and an Arcane Module that listens. Magic is half of what the Atlas asks for, and which half is yours to pick.",
    "",
    "The light came back. Part of it was yours."
  ],
  "chapter.352A5A2CBB626D18.title": "Apotheosis: Affixes and World Tiers",
  "chapter.352A5A2CBB626D18.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Rarities, gems, salvaging and reforging, invaders and World Tiers set by the story."
  ],
  "quest.7904F35EDB118489.title": "Loot with opinions",
  "quest.7904F35EDB118489.quest_desc": [
    "Affix gear drops everywhere, ranked Common to Mythic. Gems socket into it, tables salvage, reforge and augment it, and elites and invaders guard the best. Your World Tier sets how hard the world hits and how good the loot is, and here the story sets it.",
    "",
    "The sword you find may beat the one you made."
  ],
  "quest.7A5070A642F45370.title": "The story sets your tier",
  "quest.7A5070A642F45370.quest_desc": [
    "Haven, Frontier, Ascent, Summit, Pinnacle: each makes enemies stronger and rare loot commoner. You don't pick; when your team's campaign completes an act, everyone rises. Haven through Act II, then one tier per act up to Pinnacle in Act VI. It never goes down, even if you leave the team.",
    "",
    "The chat will say: «The story sets your World Tier to Frontier.»"
  ],
  "quest.19A3C2824330197A.title": "The tier screen",
  "quest.19A3C2824330197A.quest_desc": [
    "Ctrl+T opens it. Activating is disabled on purpose here, but Detailed Info shows each tier's buffs and the odds of every rarity and gem purity. Haven has no invaders and no Epic or Mythic items.",
    "",
    "Look, don't touch."
  ],
  "quest.3B2622C422A7A223.title": "Read the color",
  "quest.3B2622C422A7A223.quest_desc": [
    "Common: one or two stats. Uncommon: up to three, maybe a socket. Rare: a special effect joins in. Epic: up to four stats, two effects, two sockets. Mythic: two or three effects, up to three sockets, lots of durability. The name's color tells you at a glance."
  ],
  "quest.6CBF0EEB024203B7.title": "Apothic Attributes",
  "quest.6CBF0EEB024203B7.quest_desc": [
    "Affixes and gems work through attributes: crit chance and damage (past 100% you multi-crit), life steal, armor pierce, elemental damage, reach and more. An inventory button lists yours; hold Shift on one to see where each modifier comes from."
  ],
  "quest.01CA501717FC9BB8.title": "Salvage everything",
  "quest.01CA501717FC9BB8.quest_desc": [
    "It breaks affix gear into its rarity material, from Mysterious Scrap Metal (Common) up to Godforged Pearl (Mythic). They feed reforging and gems and, here, the Luminous ingot.",
    "",
    "One adventurer's junk is another's pearl."
  ],
  "quest.1AC33FE41F2CF11A.title": "Drop an anvil on it",
  "quest.1AC33FE41F2CF11A.quest_desc": [
    "The Salvaging Table needs gem dust, and dust comes from gems. The first time, crush a gem in the world by dropping an anvil on it; after that, the table does it. Gem dust also makes the slate behind every sigil.",
    "",
    "Crude, loud, effective."
  ],
  "quest.540189E6AF8A9257.title": "Reforging",
  "quest.540189E6AF8A9257.quest_desc": [
    "The Simple Reforging Table rerolls affixes up to Rare, even on plain gear: item in the middle, rarity material and Sigils of Rebirth around it. Three choices; the second and third cost double and triple. Upgrade it for Epic and up."
  ],
  "quest.4A5FBC9E2F7A3860.title": "Gems and sockets",
  "quest.4A5FBC9E2F7A3860.quest_desc": [
    "Gems come from chests and, rarely, mobs; real players and bosses get more, automation almost none. Purity runs Cracked to Perfect. Socket them at a smithing table; a Sigil of Socketing adds a socket, a Sigil of Withdrawal pulls every gem back out."
  ],
  "quest.2B16672990E6A285.title": "Cutting and the Gem Case",
  "quest.2B16672990E6A285.quest_desc": [
    "The Gem Cutting Table raises purity with a second gem of the same purity, dust and rarity materials. The Gem Case stores 32,000 of each gem and filters by what fits an item; infused, the House Fabergé case holds two billion.",
    "",
    "For the dragon in all of us."
  ],
  "quest.30179152BFACCA2A.title": "The Augmenting Table",
  "quest.30179152BFACCA2A.quest_desc": [
    "The endgame table edits one affix and leaves the rest alone: two Sigils of Enhancement raise it 25%, one rerolls it into another of the same type. Meant for Mythic, maybe Epic.",
    "",
    "Fine-tuning a legend."
  ],
  "quest.71BCDEB56D856B4E.title": "Invaders from the sky",
  "quest.71BCDEB56D856B4E.quest_desc": [
    "From Frontier on, an Invader may land with a bang, a chat message and a beacon beam, in full enchanted gear. It always drops one strong affix item carrying its name. Here at most one arrives every ten minutes, not every three.",
    "",
    "An event, not a chore."
  ],
  "quest.2BBA8EFEA68AF991.title": "Elites, cages and rogue spawners",
  "quest.2BBA8EFEA68AF991.quest_desc": [
    "Elites are empowered mobs that swap in unannounced and may drop affix gear. Invader dungeons hold a Caged Invader that wakes as you approach. Rogue Spawners sit alone in caves with a chest below: brutal ones slow and tough, swarm ones fast and many."
  ],
  "quest.008DCF98C026BD08.title": "Potion Charms",
  "quest.008DCF98C026BD08.quest_desc": [
    "Three potions of one type around blaze powder make a charm that outlasts all three. Enabled (it glows), from your inventory or charm slot it applies the effect a few seconds at a time, spending durability. An infusion makes it Unbreakable.",
    "",
    "The potion that never runs dry."
  ],
  "quest.2426B53E96944C95.title": "Three Apotheosis keys",
  "quest.2426B53E96944C95.quest_desc": [
    "Ctrl+T opens World Tiers. Ctrl+O cycles radial mining on Radial-affix tools. Shift+T over an item links it to chat. Apotheosis's own gear comparison is off, since Equipment Compare shows it on Shift."
  ],
  "quest.67A024413D93A15C.title": "Mythic gear",
  "quest.67A024413D93A15C.quest_desc": [
    "A Mythic weapon with three sockets of perfect gems, affixes pushed at the Augmenting Table and a tier that rose with every act. Keep salvaging what you outgrow: it all becomes material for the next step.",
    "",
    "Yesterday's legend is tomorrow's scrap metal."
  ],
  "chapter.23E6C27A76F2EC90.title": "Apothic Enchanting",
  "chapter.23E6C27A76F2EC90.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Eterna, Quanta and Arcana, the shelf ladder by act, infusion, tomes and the Atlas Library."
  ],
  "quest.7E61A14FE07F9DB9.title": "The table grows up",
  "quest.7E61A14FE07F9DB9.quest_desc": [
    "Shelves give three stats: Eterna (how high the table goes, up to 100), Quanta (how much results swing) and Arcana (rarer picks, and more of them). Special shelves add clues and filters. Here the ladder climbs by act, from 45 in Act II to 100 in Act V.",
    "",
    "Fifteen bookshelves were just the tutorial."
  ],
  "quest.071023362CD7F66D.title": "The Chronicle of Shadows",
  "quest.071023362CD7F66D.quest_desc": [
    "A book and a gold ingot: Apotheosis's guide to enchanting, affixes, spawners and potion charms. The table's own info screen is the other manual: put an item in and click the question mark at the top right."
  ],
  "quest.025856A8FAADDE9F.title": "Eterna, Quanta, Arcana",
  "quest.025856A8FAADDE9F.quest_desc": [
    "Each shelf adds Eterna only up to its own cap, so going higher needs better shelves. Quanta widens the random swing of power. Arcana tilts toward rare picks: 25% guarantees two enchantments, 75% three. Hover a shelf to see what it gives."
  ],
  "quest.1D8AB1AA11FFFBC3.title": "Level 45: fire or sea",
  "quest.1D8AB1AA11FFFBC3.quest_desc": [
    "Fifteen bookshelves still reach 30. For 45, Hellshelves (nether bricks, blaze rod) add Quanta, and Seashelves (prismarine, pufferfish) add Arcana. Skulls around the table add Quanta too.",
    "",
    "Pick a side: lava or brine."
  ],
  "quest.43344AD478B35363.title": "The Cartographer's Shelf",
  "quest.43344AD478B35363.quest_desc": [
    "Act II: four planks, two empty maps, two bookshelves and a Calibration Frame give two. Each adds 3 Eterna, up to level 40: a bridge between plain bookshelves and hellshelves.",
    "",
    "Made from what a mapmaker keeps on the desk."
  ],
  "quest.22E1C3ED5D785AC2.title": "Infusion and level 60",
  "quest.22E1C3ED5D785AC2.quest_desc": [
    "Crafting with the table: put in one item and, if the stats fall in the recipe's range, the third slot lights up. Hell and sea shelves infused at 45 Eterna and 30 Quanta reach 60. Some infusions also have a maximum: more isn't always better."
  ],
  "quest.46AB8401847D2569.title": "The Patina Shelf",
  "quest.46AB8401847D2569.quest_desc": [
    "Act III: four oxidized copper, four hellshelves and a Power Regulator give four. Each adds 4 Eterna up to level 60 and 12 Quanta; mix them with infused shelves to fill the ring faster.",
    "",
    "Copper gone green, the color of old Heliodor."
  ],
  "quest.4F4583C7325315E7.title": "Clues, stability, filters",
  "quest.4F4583C7325315E7.quest_desc": [
    "The Hellshelf of Sight adds a clue. The Bookshelf of Stability removes negative Quanta rolls. The Seashelf of Aquatic Filtration holds six single-enchantment books and bans them from the table. The Deepshelf of Arcane Treasures allows treasure enchantments, curses included."
  ],
  "quest.36A49169676E2BCE.title": "70 to 80: the deep shelves",
  "quest.36A49169676E2BCE.quest_desc": [
    "A Dormant Deepshelf infused at a level-60 table becomes a Deepshelf (up to 70); an echo shard or a soul lantern takes it to 75. The Sculkshelves (up to 80) need a Warden Tendril, and here two Act IV zanite gemstones too.",
    "",
    "The Warden doesn't lend. You take."
  ],
  "quest.0710D4AB14BD5B44.title": "The Lumen Shelf",
  "quest.0710D4AB14BD5B44.quest_desc": [
    "Act IV: glowstone, infused seashelves and a Spectral Lens give four. Each adds 7.5 Eterna up to 80, 15 Arcana and a clue: an easier road to 80 than hunting Wardens.",
    "",
    "Light, bottled for the bookcase."
  ],
  "quest.68EE07395D9794CA.title": "90 and 100: End shelves",
  "quest.68EE07395D9794CA.quest_desc": [
    "Infused dragon's breath makes the Endshelf (up to 90); one Draconic Endshelf, with a dragon head, lifts a table from 90 to 100. Here the Endshelf needs an Act IV zanite gemstone and the Draconic one two Act V Ingots of the Skies."
  ],
  "quest.4311A266E2FDCD0F.title": "The Horizon Shelf",
  "quest.4311A266E2FDCD0F.quest_desc": [
    "Act V: deepshelves, Horizon Charts, lumen shelves and an Ingot of the Skies give four. Each adds 12.5 Eterna up to 100, plus Quanta and Arcana, so the table reaches 100 without the draconic shelf.",
    "",
    "The last rung, and the view is worth it."
  ],
  "quest.296483B1183E3B16.title": "The ladder, act by act",
  "quest.296483B1183E3B16.quest_desc": [
    "Acts I–II: up to 45 (bookshelves, hell and sea shelves, cartographer). Act III: 60 to 65 (infused, patina). Acts III–IV: 70 to 80 (deep, sculk, lumen). Act IV: 90 (endshelves). Act V: 100 (draconic, horizon). Max enchantment levels stay Apothic's."
  ],
  "quest.60760C62C872171D.title": "Vanilla rules, bent",
  "quest.60760C62C872171D.quest_desc": [
    "Protection stacks with one specialized protection, Sharpness with one other damage enchantment. Tables and anvils charge exact XP, and «Too Expensive» is gone. Colored names mark Masterwork, Twisted (upside and downside) or Corrupted (costs health, counts as a curse)."
  ],
  "quest.5EA5741561913A04.title": "Tomes and the prismatic web",
  "quest.5EA5741561913A04.quest_desc": [
    "A Tome of Scrapping plus an item in an anvil destroys the item and gives a book with half its enchantments. Superior Scrapping takes them all; Extraction takes them all and keeps the item. A Prismatic Cobweb in the anvil removes every curse."
  ],
  "quest.758E6575C6681CC7.title": "Enchantment libraries",
  "quest.758E6575C6681CC7.quest_desc": [
    "The Enchantment Library stores enchantments as points: deposit books, click to pull a level. It holds up to XVI and never gives more than the highest level you deposited. Infused at 100 Eterna, it becomes the Library of Alexandria (XXXI), points included."
  ],
  "quest.034159BC81B6BB34.title": "The Atlas Library",
  "quest.034159BC81B6BB34.quest_desc": [
    "Act V: a Library of Alexandria between two Horizon Shelves, a Containment Seal above and below, and four Ingots of the Skies. It caps at XL, set by the Eterna around it (100 reaches 40), and writes any eligible enchantment, even never-deposited ones. Books pay into a pool of lumen: a deposit is worth at most half its cost, and each level up doubles the price. No curses."
  ],
  "quest.11BF9193B86B4311.title": "Atlas Library, by the numbers",
  "quest.11BF9193B86B4311.quest_desc": [
    "Hoppers and ME buses insert books; taking out is screen-only. Broken, it keeps the pool inside. Quick Charge and Lure stop at V. A Sharpness V book deposits 8 lumen and Sharpness X costs 512; Mending costs 10 and returns 2.",
    "",
    "A bank where interest is paid in levels."
  ],
  "quest.213870BB6F9F47F2.title": "The Ark forgets your anvil",
  "quest.213870BB6F9F47F2.quest_desc": [
    "Each anvil use doubles an item's prior-work penalty. In a complete Ark, the arcane module resets it to zero and keeps enchantments, curses, name, affixes and sockets: item in the main hand, plain books in the offhand. One book and five levels per past anvil use.",
    "",
    "A clean record, for a price."
  ],
  "quest.28822DE1AC98F8F1.title": "Level 100",
  "quest.28822DE1AC98F8F1.quest_desc": [
    "A table at 100 Eterna, Quanta and Arcana tuned to taste, filters for what you don't want, and an Atlas Library writing level XL books from a pool of lumen.",
    "",
    "Every act added a rung. You climbed them all."
  ],
  "chapter.4AF6456B9DBEF758.title": "Ars Nouveau I: Spellcraft",
  "chapter.4AF6456B9DBEF758.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Book, glyphs and grammar: from the first Projectile to the Archmage book."
  ],
  "quest.169396D3DE1B5E6B.title": "Magic you write",
  "quest.169396D3DE1B5E6B.quest_desc": [
    "Build spells from glyphs, cast them with mana, and later run machines, rituals and helpers on Source. The Act II Living Matrix needs magebloom and Source Gems, so some Ars is mandatory.",
    "",
    "Here, spelling mistakes tend to explode."
  ],
  "quest.2C02AB120B59CEC5.title": "The Worn Notebook",
  "quest.2C02AB120B59CEC5.quest_desc": [
    "A book and one lapis lazuli. It is Ars's own guide: every glyph, ritual, machine and creature, with its recipe. Everyone starts empty-handed here, so nobody hands it to you: craft it.",
    "",
    "Cheap, thorough, and it never says «I told you so»."
  ],
  "quest.15546909CB740D3E.title": "Four tools for one book",
  "quest.15546909CB740D3E.quest_desc": [
    "Shapeless: a book plus an iron shovel, pickaxe, axe and sword, and all four are consumed. It casts Tier 1 glyphs, keeps what you learn and holds your spell slots; every later upgrade keeps the glyphs.",
    "",
    "The blacksmith weeps. The scholar shrugs."
  ],
  "quest.0C1577A49BF96193.title": "C to write, right-click to cast",
  "quest.0C1577A49BF96193.quest_desc": [
    "Book in the hotbar, C opens spellcrafting: click glyphs into the bottom row, name it, save it to a slot; right-click casts. You start with Projectile, Touch, Self, Break and Harm. Slots switch on F6 here.",
    "",
    "First spell: Projectile, Break. Aim away from the house."
  ],
  "quest.73E32446AA1C3E4F.title": "Grammar with consequences",
  "quest.73E32446AA1C3E4F.quest_desc": [
    "One Form first (Projectile flies, Touch hits close, Self hits you), then Effects. An augment only changes the glyph to its left: Amplify harder, AOE wider, Extend Time longer. Book tier caps glyph tier: Novice 1, Mage 2, Archmage 3."
  ],
  "quest.2EBEB756212DF370.title": "Why hoarding glyphs pays",
  "quest.2EBEB756212DF370.quest_desc": [
    "A spell costs the sum of its glyphs and augments. Every glyph you learn adds max mana (15 by default) and some regen; book tiers, magic armor and trinkets add more.",
    "",
    "Even the glyph you never cast pays rent."
  ],
  "quest.379561AE02FBE13A.title": "Archwood in four colors",
  "quest.379561AE02FBE13A.quest_desc": [
    "Rare anywhere, everywhere in the Archwood Forest. Planks and slabs build the Scribe's Table and the jars; each log color is a ritual ingredient.",
    "",
    "Plant saplings at home: a grove at the door beats a weekly expedition."
  ],
  "quest.4F4C641A8B25C1DF.title": "A stick that finds geodes",
  "quest.4F4C641A8B25C1DF.quest_desc": [
    "Archwood planks and a gold ingot. Each use briefly highlights Budding Amethyst and nearby magic creatures, and it has limited uses. Geodes are the easy early amethyst, which the Imbuement Chamber turns into Source Gems (Ars II); Starbuncles show up too."
  ],
  "quest.259634AEB1E1C72A.title": "The Scribe's Table",
  "quest.259634AEB1E1C72A.quest_desc": [
    "Use your book on it, pick a glyph, drop in the listed items (it also pulls from adjacent inventories) and pay the XP; the glyph item teaches it. A Dominion Wand on the table turns auto-pull off.",
    "",
    "It eats whatever you drop. Don't drop dinner."
  ],
  "quest.1B497A4C308EA5AD.title": "Magelight, not torches",
  "quest.1B497A4C308EA5AD.quest_desc": [
    "A lantern and a torch. Cast on a block it leaves a permanent light; on yourself, Night Vision. Projectile + Conjure Magelight lights a cave from across the room; Amplify brightens, Dampen dims.",
    "",
    "The best torch is the one you don't have to carry."
  ],
  "quest.2413D4FAA7DEC70D.title": "Item Pickup: no loot in lava",
  "quest.2413D4FAA7DEC70D.quest_desc": [
    "Two hoppers. It pulls in the drops around where the spell lands. Put it after Break (Projectile, Break, Item Pickup) and the ore comes to you instead of taking a lava bath. AOE widens the radius."
  ],
  "quest.5C48B88C95EB53EF.title": "Amplify eats a diamond pick",
  "quest.5C48B88C95EB53EF.quest_desc": [
    "The table consumes a diamond pickaxe. After Break, Amplify raises the harvest level (Projectile, Break, Amplify mines diamond-tier ore); after Harm it adds damage. It stacks, and so does the mana cost.",
    "",
    "The pick dies so the spell can dig."
  ],
  "quest.5FB39D7422769D1D.title": "Sensitive: the fine print",
  "quest.5FB39D7422769D1D.quest_desc": [
    "Forms hit what they usually skip (Projectile hits grass, Touch hits fluids and air) and many effects change: Break shears, Ignite makes short Mage Fire that doesn't spread.",
    "",
    "If a spell acts weird, suspect Sensitive."
  ],
  "quest.5CA2AB5806697427.title": "A spell that digs for you",
  "quest.5CA2AB5806697427.quest_desc": [
    "Projectile, Break, Amplify, AOE, Item Pickup: a 3x3 face at range, up to diamond tier, drops collected. For ores add Extract (silk touch) or Luck (fortune) after Break, never both.",
    "",
    "Three good slots beat ten half-written ones."
  ],
  "quest.2493C7F684A71E4A.title": "Some glyphs want essences",
  "quest.2493C7F684A71E4A.quest_desc": [
    "Harm, Heal, Grow, Dispel, Smelt and more ask for an elemental essence at the Scribe's Table. Essences come from Source Gems in the Imbuement Chamber, with three items on pedestals around it (Ars II: Source).",
    "",
    "Same workshop, one room further in."
  ],
  "quest.4D872E563C2A08FE.title": "The Mage's Spell Book",
  "quest.4D872E563C2A08FE.quest_desc": [
    "Your Novice book plus obsidian, diamonds, quartz blocks and blaze rods; every glyph carries over. It unlocks Tier 2 (AOE, Extract, Luck, Heal…) and adds mana.",
    "",
    "Blaze rods mean the Nether first. Pack a lunch."
  ],
  "quest.4A5CA3AB42662843.title": "AOE: think in squares",
  "quest.4A5CA3AB42662843.quest_desc": [
    "One firework star (Tier 2). Each AOE after an effect widens the area around the target: one on Break mines 3x3, more grow the area and the cost. It also widens Item Pickup, Evaporate, Smelt and others."
  ],
  "quest.43D4ABD3B4D1EAA2.title": "Extract or Luck, never both",
  "quest.43D4ABD3B4D1EAA2.quest_desc": [
    "Extract (an emerald) makes Break act with silk touch; Luck (a rabbit's foot) adds drops to Break and Harm. Both are Tier 2, cost a little XP, and refuse to share a spell. Keep one mining slot with each and choose per ore."
  ],
  "quest.1B5711356EE9AFFF.title": "Wilden Chimera: bring Tier 2",
  "quest.1B5711356EE9AFFF.quest_desc": [
    "The Archmage book needs a Wilden Tribute from the Chimera. Craft the Summon Wilden tablet, then throw a Wilden Spike, Horn and Wing on the brazier before lighting it; Wilden in forests and cold biomes drop them.",
    "",
    "The summoning breaks blocks around it. Not in the garden."
  ],
  "quest.4138621CF1D1D61C.title": "The Archmage Spell Book",
  "quest.4138621CF1D1D61C.quest_desc": [
    "Your Mage's book, ender pearls, emeralds, a Totem of Undying, a Nether Star and a Wilden Tribute. It unlocks Tier 3: Blink, Burst, Wall, Lightning and more. Here the Nether Star only comes from the Wither: plan that fight."
  ],
  "quest.73F873CF3B844D0C.title": "Blink, and you're there",
  "quest.73F873CF3B844D0C.quest_desc": [
    "Self + Blink throws you forward; Projectile + Blink takes you where the bolt lands. With a written Warp Scroll in the offhand, Blink ships a creature to the scroll's spot.",
    "",
    "The Ars answer to legs, until you get wings."
  ],
  "quest.581AD0E934387194.title": "One diamond pick per team",
  "quest.581AD0E934387194.quest_desc": [
    "An Annotated Codex records every glyph you know, for XP per glyph (10 by default); another player uses it to learn them all. In co-op, one scribes the pricey glyphs, the rest copy.",
    "",
    "Amplify's diamond pick only dies once."
  ],
  "quest.64B9F129CADCE280.title": "Magic keys, moved",
  "quest.64B9F129CADCE280.quest_desc": [
    "Ars radial on F6; Iron's wheel on the key left of 1, cast Alt+Q; Psi Alt+F (C opens the Ars book even with Alt held); the crown's potion radial on 0; Mahou Tsukai Alt+M; Occultism bag O, satchel Insert. Your own rebinds are kept."
  ],
  "quest.0E2A82DAF269E3B0.title": "The Living Matrix",
  "quest.0E2A82DAF269E3B0.quest_desc": [
    "A cross: two Source Gems above and below, two magebloom fibers at the sides and a Calibration Frame in the middle, for «Living Workshop» (Act II). Magebloom and gems come from Ars II. Later components eat more Matrices, so keep the workshop running."
  ],
  "quest.771EBF275C8B2ED8.title": "A library in one book",
  "quest.771EBF275C8B2ED8.quest_desc": [
    "Archmage book, Tier 3 glyphs, working slots. A good benchmark: one slot to dig, one to light, one to move, one to fight, and one you invented.",
    "",
    "Next: Source, rituals, automation and the addons."
  ],
  "chapter.63373BA36912EC62.title": "Ars Nouveau II: Source",
  "chapter.63373BA36912EC62.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Imbuement, Source Gems, jars, Sourcelinks and the Enchanting Apparatus."
  ],
  "quest.5F43A0DE5096752B.title": "Source: what Ars runs on",
  "quest.5F43A0DE5096752B.quest_desc": [
    "Mana casts spells; Source runs blocks: it speeds up imbuing, pays for apparatus recipes and rituals, and feeds creatures and turrets. The chain ends in the Living Matrix.",
    "",
    "Mana is pocket money. Source pays the bills."
  ],
  "quest.46E0D864D0E37AEE.title": "Imbuement Chamber",
  "quest.46E0D864D0E37AEE.quest_desc": [
    "Put an item inside and it soaks up Source until it transforms. Alone it gathers a trickle; Source Jars within 2 blocks make it much faster. Side ingredients sit on Arcane Pedestals within 1 block and aren't consumed."
  ],
  "quest.620B3140D18DC266.title": "Eight Source Gems",
  "quest.620B3140D18DC266.quest_desc": [
    "Imbue an amethyst shard or lapis: 500 Source per gem. Almost every Ars recipe wants them and the Matrix takes two. A budding amethyst geode is the renewable supply.",
    "",
    "Purple is the color of «not enough yet»."
  ],
  "quest.7985E5BBF62B2095.title": "Source Jars",
  "quest.7985E5BBF62B2095.quest_desc": [
    "Archwood slabs top and bottom, glass on the sides. Jars store Source, and machines, rituals and creatures drink from the ones nearby. A comparator reads how full a jar is, and a broken jar keeps its Source inside.",
    "",
    "A piggy bank that glows."
  ],
  "quest.63936B61C6CCE928.title": "Sourcelinks: making Source",
  "quest.63936B61C6CCE928.quest_desc": [
    "The Agronomic Sourcelink turns crops and trees growing within 15 blocks into Source for jars within 5; magic plants count extra, bonemeal growth doesn't. Its siblings eat food (Mycelial), mob deaths (Vitalic), fuel (Volcanic) or potions (Alchemical)."
  ],
  "quest.0E9DF5090BA3B399.title": "The Volcanic link melts floors",
  "quest.0E9DF5090BA3B399.quest_desc": [
    "It burns fuel and pays best for archwood, Blazing Archwood above all. Its heat turns nearby stone into magma, then lava: build it on a floor you can lose, away from wood. The Mycelial link has its own habit: the ground below turns to mycelium."
  ],
  "quest.009AAD8E3CEA0FAE.title": "Berries that feed two links",
  "quest.009AAD8E3CEA0FAE.quest_desc": [
    "By an Agronomic link they count as magic plants; in a Mycelial link, berries and pie beat mundane food by far. Eating them restores mana, and a Starbuncle harvests them for you.",
    "",
    "A berry patch with no hands in it."
  ],
  "quest.3D5F2958796F6901.title": "Elemental essences",
  "quest.3D5F2958796F6901.quest_desc": [
    "A Source Gem in the chamber plus three items on pedestals, 2000 Source; each element has its trio (earth: iron ingot, seeds, dirt). Only the gem is spent, so leave the pedestals set. Essences unlock many glyphs, rituals and trinkets."
  ],
  "quest.6203913FCF726BDD.title": "Sourcestone and pedestals",
  "quest.6203913FCF726BDD.quest_desc": [
    "Eight stone around a Source Gem give eight Sourcestone; add gold nuggets and a gem for an Arcane Pedestal. Make four for side ingredients. Sourcestone also frames the Warp Portal and has stonecutter variants."
  ],
  "quest.47F1C61D11319558.title": "Arcane Core",
  "quest.47F1C61D11319558.quest_desc": [
    "Sourcestone around two gold ingots and a Source Gem. The Enchanting Apparatus only works with a core directly below it, so build them as one piece and leave room for pedestals around.",
    "",
    "Every altar needs a floor to stand on."
  ],
  "quest.70166A508E203421.title": "Enchanting Apparatus",
  "quest.70166A508E203421.quest_desc": [
    "It sits on the Arcane Core. Side ingredients on pedestals within 3 blocks, then use the central item on it; Source comes from nearby jars. Charms, armor, rings, the Dominion Wand and magebloom seeds are born here."
  ],
  "quest.4A9AE22AE00B592E.title": "Dominion Wand: the wiring",
  "quest.4A9AE22AE00B592E.quest_desc": [
    "Use it on a source, then on a target: jar to relay, Starbuncle to chest, Wixie to inventory. Sneak-use on a relay clears its links. Every Ars chapter from here uses it.",
    "",
    "Magic, with cable management."
  ],
  "quest.65604676A34768EC.title": "Relays: Source on the move",
  "quest.65604676A34768EC.quest_desc": [
    "Wand-link jar, relay, distant jar: up to 30 blocks per hop, and redstone stops it. Apparatus upgrades collect from or fill every jar within 5, split between many, or warp any distance, with loss past 30."
  ],
  "quest.5324A778EB9649C6.title": "Magebloom",
  "quest.5324A778EB9649C6.quest_desc": [
    "Any seeds ringed with four Source Gems in the apparatus become a Magebloom Seed. While it grows on farmland it adds extra Source to a nearby Agronomic link; replant what you harvest.",
    "",
    "A flower that pays for itself, then some."
  ],
  "quest.61BC93666A3CB4A1.title": "Sixteen Magebloom Fiber",
  "quest.61BC93666A3CB4A1.quest_desc": [
    "Each magebloom crafts into four fiber. It is Ars's cloth: Blank Parchment, Blank Thread, the Alteration Table, Sorcerer's robes and the Living Matrix. With fiber and gems, you hold every Ars ingredient of the Act II Atlas project."
  ],
  "quest.3F84D749D6ADB214.title": "Deliver the Living Matrix",
  "quest.3F84D749D6ADB214.quest_desc": [
    "Two Source Gems on the axis, two magebloom fibers at the sides and a Calibration Frame at the heart. Only the delivery at «Living Workshop» moves the story. Keep gems in stock: Acts III and IV ask for Matrices again.",
    "",
    "The first magic the Atlas asks for. Not the last."
  ],
  "quest.539A03F5CDA2B0CF.title": "Robes over plate",
  "quest.539A03F5CDA2B0CF.quest_desc": [
    "A golden armor piece plus four magebloom fiber in the apparatus: the Sorcerer's set, with mana regen and Thread slots. Least defence, best slots; Arcanist's and Battlemage's trade slots for defence.",
    "",
    "Pick by playstyle, not armor points."
  ],
  "quest.6600E7C12F5C6230.title": "Threads and the Alteration Table",
  "quest.6600E7C12F5C6230.quest_desc": [
    "Blank Thread becomes a perk thread in the apparatus (Repairing, Magic Capacity…). At the Alteration Table, armor on the stand, thread on the tablet. One thread per set, not per piece; armor tier upgrades add slots."
  ],
  "quest.75FDAE190AE176B9.title": "Rings and amulets",
  "quest.75FDAE190AE176B9.quest_desc": [
    "A Ring of Potential (iron nuggets around a gem) becomes a Ring of Lesser Discount in the apparatus: cheaper spells, a bit of mana. The Dull Trinket becomes a Mana Boost or Mana Regen amulet. Curios slots: they stack with armor."
  ],
  "quest.28007D969FECC081.title": "Enchanting without dice",
  "quest.28007D969FECC081.quest_desc": [
    "The apparatus applies vanilla enchantments one level at a time: tool in the center, items on pedestals, and each level needs the previous one (Smite 3 needs Smite 2). From 2,000 Source for level I to 9,000. Exact, no dice."
  ],
  "quest.0C57DF56701EAF4E.title": "The Creative Source Jar",
  "quest.0C57DF56701EAF4E.quest_desc": [
    "Not loot here: an endgame recipe with Nature and Arcane Luminosities (Solsticio, Act VI), a Nether Star, Source Gem Blocks, a Source Jar and a Renewal Engine (Act V).",
    "",
    "The bottomless jar waits at the end of the road."
  ],
  "quest.565C640EA8A5AA54.title": "Jars that stay full",
  "quest.565C640EA8A5AA54.quest_desc": [
    "Several Sourcelinks, a bank of jars, relays feeding the apparatus and chamber, magebloom around the Agronomic link. When jars stay full while you work, move on to rituals and creatures."
  ],
  "chapter.1E107E4CD0F954FB.title": "Ars Nouveau III: Rituals and Familiars",
  "chapter.1E107E4CD0F954FB.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The brazier, the most useful tablets, mob jars and companions bound to you."
  ],
  "quest.46A9A60C6D91E592.title": "Big, slow spells",
  "quest.46A9A60C6D91E592.quest_desc": [
    "A brazier casts rituals: weather, daylight, no spawns around the base, mobs into jars, crops harvested. Many drink Source from jars within 6 blocks. Familiars are small companions with passive bonuses.",
    "",
    "Spells too big for a book."
  ],
  "quest.2F3E42797FDBC5DD.title": "The Ritual Brazier",
  "quest.2F3E42797FDBC5DD.quest_desc": [
    "Shapeless: an Arcane Pedestal, a Source Gem Block and three gold ingots. A redstone signal stops the running ritual, which is how you pause long ones like Sanctuary or Harvest. Conjure Magelight lights it in your spell color, just for looks."
  ],
  "quest.350D28FB512A0937.title": "Tablet, augments, empty hand",
  "quest.350D28FB512A0937.quest_desc": [
    "Use the tablet on the brazier, throw any augment items on top, then start it with an empty hand; the tablet is spent and augments lock. Log color hints the theme: green grows, red burns, blue is water and sky, purple binds."
  ],
  "quest.68D703CB2F0A1672.title": "Sunrise, on demand",
  "quest.68D703CB2F0A1672.quest_desc": [
    "Sunrise makes it day; its twin Moonfall makes it night. Cheap and instant: the best way to learn the brazier loop.",
    "",
    "For once, the sun comes up when you say so."
  ],
  "quest.671E9DA04BF8532A.title": "Sanctuary: a quiet base",
  "quest.671E9DA04BF8532A.quest_desc": [
    "While it runs, no hostile mob spawns naturally within 32 blocks; each rotten flesh thrown in before starting adds a block, up to 128. It only charges Source when it actually blocks a spawn.",
    "",
    "As World Tiers climb, silence gets precious."
  ],
  "quest.3E586171800E29F1.title": "Harvest: crops, no hands",
  "quest.3E586171800E29F1.quest_desc": [
    "It harvests ripe crops around the brazier for a bit of Source each, into an adjacent inventory if there is one. Pair it with Overgrowth, but remember: bonemeal crops don't feed an Agronomic Sourcelink."
  ],
  "quest.6906CC2C09BAA8A8.title": "Scrying: see through stone",
  "quest.6906CC2C09BAA8A8.quest_desc": [
    "Throw in one block of what you're after before starting: for a while you see it through everything, white close, green medium, blue far. A Manipulation Essence stretches it to 15 minutes.",
    "",
    "Made for iesnium and soulstone hunts."
  ],
  "quest.225F391735441554.title": "Restoration: cheap cures",
  "quest.225F391735441554.quest_desc": [
    "A flourishing log, a golden apple and an abjuration essence. It heals the living nearby and hurts the undead over time. Zombie Villagers are cured instantly, and if you're close they give discounts: good trades, no weakness potions."
  ],
  "quest.718037DFEA5B61ED.title": "Containment: mobs in jars",
  "quest.718037DFEA5B61ED.quest_desc": [
    "Empty jars and the target within 3 blocks of the brazier, and in it goes; each capture after the first costs more Source. Jarred mobs keep living: eggs, wool, milk, trades. Dispel on the jar lets it out.",
    "",
    "A farm that fits on a shelf."
  ],
  "quest.75F78A67ECF0E466.title": "What a jar can do",
  "quest.75F78A67ECF0E466.quest_desc": [
    "A jarred villager trades and restocks; a piglin barters thrown gold; an allay stores items within 5 blocks in an adjacent inventory; a pufferfish emits redstone near mobs. A Drygmy counts jars as creatures: a compact drop farm."
  ],
  "quest.0F08A7BC7C4E9D3A.title": "Awakening: trees that walk",
  "quest.0F08A7BC7C4E9D3A.quest_desc": [
    "By an archwood trunk it makes a Weald Walker that guards the spot you set with the wand; by Budding Amethyst, an Amethyst Golem charm; with a book and quill, Bookwyrm charms. A fallen Walker becomes a Waddler that regrows.",
    "",
    "The gardener finally hires the garden."
  ],
  "quest.617FC8B4C2F0CBFD.title": "More rituals worth a tablet",
  "quest.617FC8B4C2F0CBFD.quest_desc": [
    "Cloudshaping sets the weather. Fertility breeds nearby animals. Disintegration kills monsters for double-XP gems, no drops. Burrowing digs to bedrock. Challenge starts a raid. Forestation, Flowering and Conjure Island reshape land."
  ],
  "quest.7C6D61C7BB2E7B53.title": "Flight that stays home",
  "quest.7C6D61C7BB2E7B53.quest_desc": [
    "Players near the brazier get creative-style flight when they jump, renewed while they stay, for Source each time. It builds, it doesn't travel: wander off and you fall. Portable flight waits for Act IV.",
    "",
    "Wings with a leash."
  ],
  "quest.7FF171DC9AFB1F3D.title": "Binding: your first familiar",
  "quest.7FF171DC9AFB1F3D.quest_desc": [
    "Run it next to a creature, a Starbuncle to start: it becomes a Bound Script that teaches you the familiar. Summon it from the book's Familiars tab; Familiar Sickness stops instant swaps.",
    "",
    "Friendship, with paperwork."
  ],
  "quest.7143B2456F90D31D.title": "Who does what",
  "quest.7143B2456F90D31D.quest_desc": [
    "Starbuncle: Speed II, gold nugget for a short gold Scrying. Bookwyrm: item and XP magnet. Drygmy: Earth spells, looting. Whirlisprig: cheaper Earth glyphs. Wixie: longer potions. Amethyst Golem: half knockback. Ars Elemental adds three more."
  ],
  "quest.4F5DCF26A1469A8E.title": "Familiars rent your mana",
  "quest.4F5DCF26A1469A8E.quest_desc": [
    "While out, a familiar reserves part of your max mana, so the bar looks shorter. One at a time: summoning another dismisses the first, and Dispel sends yours home. Bound Scripts are personal; each player runs their own Binding."
  ],
  "quest.44481184CD68D732.title": "Bookwyrm: the tidy one",
  "quest.44481184CD68D732.quest_desc": [
    "Summon a Bookwyrm from its charm (Awakening with a book and quill), run Binding beside it, learn the script. As a familiar it pulls items and XP within 5 blocks, but not what you throw. Take it mining; take the Starbuncle for surface speed."
  ],
  "quest.64C5DC7057974AC6.title": "Rituals at a distance",
  "quest.64C5DC7057974AC6.quest_desc": [
    "Three manipulation essences turn a brazier into a Relay in the apparatus. Wand-link them and the ritual acts around the relay, up to 15 blocks away, while Source is paid at home. Jars stay inside; Harvest works the field."
  ],
  "quest.55D479DF1EDD0846.title": "A ring of braziers",
  "quest.55D479DF1EDD0846.quest_desc": [
    "Sanctuary over the base, Harvest on the fields, a Containment bench and a Binding tablet ready for the next familiar. Next, the creatures you befriended go to work.",
    "",
    "A base that smells of incense and ozone."
  ],
  "chapter.7DA3D920791C4FD0.title": "Ars Nouveau IV: Automation",
  "chapter.7DA3D920791C4FD0.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Starbuncles, Drygmys, Whirlisprigs, Wixies, turrets and the Storage Lectern."
  ],
  "quest.7F26D4F81EA09940.title": "Creatures that do the chores",
  "quest.7F26D4F81EA09940.quest_desc": [
    "Starbuncles haul, Drygmys make drops without killing, Whirlisprigs grow, Wixies craft and brew, Amethyst Golems farm geodes, turrets cast on redstone. Most start as a token from a wild creature, made into a charm; all need Source nearby.",
    "",
    "The factory is alive, and expects a salary."
  ],
  "quest.6842698EBBA05998.title": "A Starbuncle Token",
  "quest.6842698EBBA05998.quest_desc": [
    "Starbuncles live in woods and flee from players, unless you hold a gold nugget. Let one take it: it vanishes and leaves a token. The Dowsing Rod or Sense Magic highlights magic creatures.",
    "",
    "The only employee paid up front."
  ],
  "quest.095EDA334AA7BB45.title": "Starbuncle Charm",
  "quest.095EDA334AA7BB45.quest_desc": [
    "Token in the apparatus, gold ingots on pedestals. Use the charm on the ground to summon it: it picks up nearby items and harvests ripe sourceberries. Dispel or death returns the charm, so you never lose one. Dye them by job."
  ],
  "quest.47DCEDEE953B0EDB.title": "Starbuncle routes",
  "quest.47DCEDEE953B0EDB.quest_desc": [
    "Dominion Wand: Starbuncle then chest, it delivers there; chest then Starbuncle, it takes from there. One can serve many chests; sneak-wand resets it. A charm used on a Starbuncle stacks them, and stacks carry more per trip."
  ],
  "quest.4BE4DD0664E13443.title": "Filters: Item Scrolls",
  "quest.4BE4DD0664E13443.quest_desc": [
    "Write items into an Allow scroll at the Scribe's Table (sneak-use them on it); a Starbuncle holding it moves only those, and Deny does the opposite. A scroll or single item in a frame on a chest filters every Starbuncle that uses it."
  ],
  "quest.786B44F172D40CA9.title": "Beds and shades",
  "quest.786B44F172D40CA9.quest_desc": [
    "A wand-bound Magebloom Bed gives idle Starbuncles a rest spot; redstone on it sends them all to sleep and pauses the line. Starbuncle Shades stop ground pickup and berry harvesting: route only.",
    "",
    "Sunglasses: the uniform of pure focus."
  ],
  "quest.62CD69998B3B9F95.title": "Drygmy: drops without killing",
  "quest.62CD69998B3B9F95.quest_desc": [
    "Throw a Wilden Horn near a wild Drygmy for its token; the charm on Mossy Cobblestone makes a henge. It yields drops and XP gems from creatures within 10 blocks, unharmed. More creatures and more variety, more output; jars count.",
    "",
    "A farm where nobody dies."
  ],
  "quest.701527690A16BF87.title": "Whirlisprig: a garden that pays",
  "quest.701527690A16BF87.quest_desc": [
    "Grow a tree next to a wild Whirlisprig for its token; the charm goes on a flower, with a chest beside it and Source nearby. It produces what grows within 10 blocks, but only when happy: quantity and variety. Moods update slowly."
  ],
  "quest.6D214A6A8D2A3D24.title": "Wixie: the crafting helper",
  "quest.6D214A6A8D2A3D24.quest_desc": [
    "Dispel a Witch at half health or less for the token; the charm on a cauldron makes a Wixie Cauldron. Show it an item: it crafts it from nearby inventories for a little Source; pedestals queue more, redstone stops it.",
    "",
    "A witch, reformed into middle management."
  ],
  "quest.6E9B8E04BACF9D1C.title": "Potions by the jar",
  "quest.6E9B8E04BACF9D1C.quest_desc": [
    "An empty Potion Jar by the cauldron, an Awkward Potion used on it, nether wart nearby: the Wixie brews three doses per craft and supplies the water. Sneak-wand a jar to lock its potion; a Starbuncle in a Wixie Hat moves potions."
  ],
  "quest.5F0C2EE9E724C72B.title": "Amethyst Golem",
  "quest.5F0C2EE9E724C72B.quest_desc": [
    "Wand the golem, then a block, to set its home. It turns amethyst blocks into budding ones, speeds growth, harvests clusters and stores the shards.",
    "",
    "Source Gems forever, from a rock with feelings."
  ],
  "quest.1AF787950B270CE0.title": "Spells on paper",
  "quest.1AF787950B270CE0.quest_desc": [
    "Blank Parchment on the Scribe's Table, select a slot as if to cast, sneak-use the book on the table. The parchment holds that spell and programs turrets, Runic Chalk and the Spell Sensor. A Manipulation Essence hides it from others."
  ],
  "quest.01C5F3CD9478E555.title": "Spell turrets",
  "quest.01C5F3CD9478E555.quest_desc": [
    "Load a written parchment: on redstone it casts like a dispenser, Touch or Projectile, paid from nearby jars; with an adjacent inventory, Item Pickup and Place Block work. The Enchanted Turret costs half.",
    "",
    "One-block farms and polite mob disposal."
  ],
  "quest.3B21E8052927B4E1.title": "A turret with a clock",
  "quest.3B21E8052927B4E1.quest_desc": [
    "It fires on its own, every second by default: right-click adds time, punch removes it, sneak steps by 10 seconds; 0 seconds or redstone stops it. Projectile, Touch, Sensitive and Redstone glyphs are free: only effects cost Source."
  ],
  "quest.496BD651BCA3D872.title": "Storage Lectern",
  "quest.496BD651BCA3D872.quest_desc": [
    "Wand-link inventories up to 30 blocks away, then view, sort and craft from all of them in one screen. Each Bookwyrm charm used on it links more, and named inventories become tabs.",
    "",
    "A library where the librarians have wings."
  ],
  "quest.2D28C08679B97E0A.title": "Repositories and the Catalog",
  "quest.2D28C08679B97E0A.quest_desc": [
    "A Repository holds a double chest and keeps its name when broken: easy tabs. A Repository Catalog exposes a whole chain of them to the lectern through one block, and it's kinder to the server than big chests."
  ],
  "quest.1022D6A130C47354.title": "Warp scrolls and portals",
  "quest.1022D6A130C47354.quest_desc": [
    "A Warp Scroll records a spot and takes you there once, same dimension. Thrown into a Sourcestone frame with a full jar nearby, it makes a permanent, free one-way portal. The Stabilized scroll is reusable and crosses dimensions."
  ],
  "quest.3533ACFFD34D8977.title": "No gates on the helpers",
  "quest.3533ACFFD34D8977.quest_desc": [
    "Every Ars charm, turret and the lectern keep native recipes. The only story gate in Ars is the Living Matrix delivery: automate as early as you like, since the Matrix wants the same workshop anyway."
  ],
  "quest.684E41AC69264217.title": "A factory that breathes",
  "quest.684E41AC69264217.quest_desc": [
    "Starbuncles feeding the lectern, a Wixie crafting on demand, a Drygmy henge ringed with jars, a Whirlisprig garden, a golem-tended geode and timer turrets on the boring jobs. The addons chapter plugs all of it into Create, AE2 and Occultism."
  ],
  "chapter.0831CF21ECDB3B76.title": "Ars Nouveau V: The Addons",
  "chapter.0831CF21ECDB3B76.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Elemental schools, Create and AE2 bridges, spirits in jars, charms and smarter Starbuncles."
  ],
  "quest.5DA041B573214448.title": "Nine addons, pick a few",
  "quest.5DA041B573214448.quest_desc": [
    "Nine addons plug Ars into elemental schools, extra glyphs, Create, Occultism, AE2 and fluid logistics. None is required by the story: pick the branches your base needs.",
    "",
    "A tree with nine branches, and you have two hands."
  ],
  "quest.4781668B662B5EB1.title": "Ars Elemental: the schools",
  "quest.4781668B662B5EB1.quest_desc": [
    "Most glyphs belong to a school, from Fire to Anima, and gear attuned to one boosts or discounts its glyphs. Some base glyphs change too: Crush processes items with Sensitive, Ignite melts ice, summoned lightning spares items."
  ],
  "quest.0475CD3D25414D31.title": "Pick an element",
  "quest.0475CD3D25414D31.quest_desc": [
    "An amethyst shard imbued with three essences of one element and three gold (5,000 Source). As a curio it boosts its school, weakens the other elements and bends some glyphs: with Fire, Ignite adds Magic Burn.",
    "",
    "Loyalty has perks."
  ],
  "quest.380894BB2C2418A4.title": "Mark of Mastery",
  "quest.380894BB2C2418A4.quest_desc": [
    "A Wilden Tribute imbued with all eight essences gives five Marks. A Mark turns a Lesser Focus into a full one, or a tier-3 Ars armor piece into an elemental one (with netherite). A full elemental set soaks its element's damage and turns some into mana."
  ],
  "quest.4372B3A3FBF3073E.title": "A pouch for trinkets",
  "quest.4372B3A3FBF3073E.quest_desc": [
    "Magebloom fiber around a chest. It holds magic trinkets and opens with its own key (Alt+Insert here) from the hotbar or a curio slot; it upgrades into the bigger, dyeable Spellcaster Bag.",
    "",
    "For mages who lose rings in their pockets."
  ],
  "quest.11F6F626EEDE0091.title": "Not Enough Glyphs",
  "quest.11F6F626EEDE0091.quest_desc": [
    "More glyphs for the same table. Best of them: contingencies that fire a stored spell when the target teleports, falls, dies, heals, burns or drops low; and Propagate Plane, which spreads the rest of the spell flat.",
    "",
    "If-then, in spell form."
  ],
  "quest.0EACFC65D758ED00.title": "Source Motor: magic to shafts",
  "quest.0EACFC65D758ED00.quest_desc": [
    "Imbue a Create precision mechanism with amethyst and Source Gems, then build the Motor with brass and cogwheels. It turns jar Source into rotation at the speed you set, and stops when the jar runs dry: fuel, not free power."
  ],
  "quest.646DFC08E02887AB.title": "Create recipes, cast",
  "quest.646DFC08E02887AB.quest_desc": [
    "Glyphs that run Create recipes on dropped items: Obliterate crushes, Press, Fuse mixes, Polish, Carve, Pack, and Whirl washes, smokes, smelts or haunts by the next glyph. On a Timer Turret over a hopper: a Create machine running on Source."
  ],
  "quest.228526A103C7AB08.title": "Starbuncles on Create",
  "quest.228526A103C7AB08.quest_desc": [
    "A Starbuncle charm plus a water wheel makes a Starbuncle Wheel: small rotation, faster with a gold block in front. Ars blocks also work on moving contraptions, and potions pipe into Create tanks.",
    "",
    "A hamster wheel with better PR."
  ],
  "quest.6644EE1A37239BF7.title": "Spirits in jars",
  "quest.6644EE1A37239BF7.quest_desc": [
    "Catch an Occultism worker (Foliot Crusher, Janitor) in a Containment Jar: it keeps working and never decays. It grabs matching items in 7x7 around the jar, and hoppers, pipes and Starbuncles can feed it. One input per insert, no duplication."
  ],
  "quest.40CDC45F6A9D87D8.title": "Attuned gems, no diamond",
  "quest.40CDC45F6A9D87D8.quest_desc": [
    "An apparatus route to Occultism's Spirit Attuned Gem: a Source Gem with three essences, 500 Source, no diamond burned in spirit fire. Four attuned gems make the crystal of the Spectral Lens."
  ],
  "quest.3F58A364F4327BC3.title": "The apparatus on autopilot",
  "quest.3F58A364F4327BC3.quest_desc": [
    "Sneak-use a Wixie Charm on an Enchanting Apparatus. Show it the result item, like a Wixie Cauldron, and the Wixie fills the pedestals from nearby inventories and runs the recipe. Essences, charms and threads by the dozen, without you standing there."
  ],
  "quest.67984B072FE95817.title": "Charms with charges",
  "quest.67984B072FE95817.quest_desc": [
    "Curios with charges, made in the apparatus around a bottle. Second Wind saves you from a fatal hit; Featherlight catches you after 3 blocks of falling; others cover night vision, fire, water, powder snow, the void and the Warden's boom. Recharge in the Imbuement Chamber."
  ],
  "quest.2D79F650880F3F27.title": "Remote access",
  "quest.2D79F650880F3F27.quest_desc": [
    "The Ender Source Jar shares one pool across every copy. The Warp Index opens your Storage Lectern from anywhere in the dimension; the Stabilized one crosses dimensions. The Advanced Dominion Wand links many blocks at once."
  ],
  "quest.41F688C7F615FBD7.title": "Spawner yes, chunkloader no",
  "quest.41F688C7F615FBD7.quest_desc": [
    "The Source Spawner spawns whatever sits in nearby Containment Jars, for Source per mob. It's native, so mind the server. The Ritual of Arcane Permanence stays disabled: chunk loading belongs to FTB Chunks."
  ],
  "quest.4F9CD649FCDDC520.title": "Logic glyphs, far links",
  "quest.4F9CD649FCDDC520.quest_desc": [
    "Logic glyphs (height filters, Not, Or, Xor, Random) and Precise Delay. Blocks: the Scryer's Linkage lets machines reach a far linked block; the Warping Spell Prism sends a spell anywhere, even another dimension; the Remote does wand work at range."
  ],
  "quest.73D9F01382DCC7E0.title": "A lag alarm",
  "quest.73D9F01382DCC7E0.quest_desc": [
    "With a comparator, its signal rises as the world approaches lag. Wire it to Starbuncle beds, turrets or braziers and your farms switch off when the server struggles.",
    "",
    "On a shared server, a small act of love."
  ],
  "quest.4266D0AE6FBF7F11.title": "Source in AE2",
  "quest.4266D0AE6FBF7F11.quest_desc": [
    "With AE2 (Act III), store Source as a resource: Source Storage Cells, the ME Source Jar and the ME Source Converter, which turns Source into AE energy. When the jar runs dry, the network shuts down: a bridge, not a generator."
  ],
  "quest.7069913D5208B8FC.title": "Starbuncles with tanks",
  "quest.7069913D5208B8FC.quest_desc": [
    "A Fluid Jar holds 16 buckets. Accessories change a Starbuncle's job: the Starbucket moves fluids, the StarbAttery FE, the Starballoon Mekanism chemicals, all routed with the wand. The Fluid Sourcelink burns fluids into Source."
  ],
  "quest.459528C6934BB218.title": "Two recipes, one pedestal",
  "quest.459528C6934BB218.quest_desc": [
    "When two apparatus or imbuement recipes share inputs, Ars Polymorphia lets Polymorph show a button to choose the output. If the apparatus hands you a surprise, check the selector before blaming the pedestals."
  ],
  "quest.5EF4707344BC23D8.title": "Ars, wired into everything",
  "quest.5EF4707344BC23D8.quest_desc": [
    "Source Motors spinning Create shafts, spirits working in jars, a Wixie running the apparatus, Source in AE2, Starbuncles hauling fluids and power. The magic road goes on with Occultism, Malum and the rest; «Magic in ENTRELUMEN» has the map."
  ],
  "chapter.764474727FAF4C24.title": "EvilCraft: Blood Magic",
  "chapter.764474727FAF4C24.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Dark gems, blood extraction, the Blood Infuser, brooms and vengeance spirits."
  ],
  "quest.6FB6533026337171.title": "Blood, with machines",
  "quest.6FB6533026337171.quest_desc": [
    "Mine dark gems, collect blood from the fallen and feed it to machines that infuse items, repair tools, lift curses, fly brooms and trap spirits. It all works early; the story needs two dark gems for the Act IV Containment Seal.",
    "",
    "Squeamish? Try Nature's Aura."
  ],
  "quest.385FA6C934E3365F.title": "Origins of Darkness",
  "quest.385FA6C934E3365F.quest_desc": [
    "Loot, not a recipe: about one chest in five in villages, dungeons, mineshafts, temples, igloos, fortresses and ancient cities carries it. A diary in two ages, with clickable recipes.",
    "",
    "Someone else's diary. Read it anyway."
  ],
  "quest.7043B42051E1F0E1.title": "Dark gems",
  "quest.7043B42051E1F0E1.quest_desc": [
    "Dark Ore sits mostly around redstone depth and needs an iron pickaxe; Fortune adds Crushed Dark Gem. Keep a stack: gems build spikes, tanks and bricks, and two go into the Containment Seal.",
    "",
    "The darkest thing you'll mine on purpose."
  ],
  "quest.063626A177E886C8.title": "Blood Extractor",
  "quest.063626A177E886C8.quest_desc": [
    "In your inventory it fills when you kill certain creatures; sneak-use it on Blood Stains, left where things fell to their death. Right-click pours a bucket. Combine extractors, or add Dark Tanks, in a grid for capacity."
  ],
  "quest.439881AF0DC88B9D.title": "Dark Tank",
  "quest.439881AF0DC88B9D.quest_desc": [
    "About sixteen buckets, carried in your inventory; tanks merged in a grid grow without spilling. Right-click a placed tank to open a drain below it; sneak-use in the air to top up what you hold."
  ],
  "quest.7CDFDBE98EC4294D.title": "Dark Power Gems",
  "quest.7CDFDBE98EC4294D.quest_desc": [
    "Toss a dark gem into a blood pool of at least five source blocks: it becomes a Dark Power Gem. Once by hand; later the Infuser does it cheaper. Hardened blood shards around a power gem make the Blood Infusion Core.",
    "",
    "A pool party nobody wants to attend."
  ],
  "quest.76FA8595F2D5755E.title": "Blood Infuser",
  "quest.76FA8595F2D5755E.quest_desc": [
    "It fills blood containers and infuses items: cheaper Dark Power Gems, Blooks (books with blood), undead saplings and more; redstone pauses it. Promises of Tenacity, Velocity and Productivity upgrade capacity, speed and blood cost."
  ],
  "quest.7E2465162DFCD0F3.title": "Blood Chest",
  "quest.7E2465162DFCD0F3.quest_desc": [
    "It slowly repairs tools inside, using blood. The catch: now and then a tool picks up a bad effect, like Curse of Breaking, which the Purifier removes.",
    "",
    "Free repairs, fine print included."
  ],
  "quest.6D0085AFA7386179.title": "Purifier",
  "quest.6D0085AFA7386179.quest_desc": [
    "With a bucket of blood it strips bad effects from a tool. Full, with a Blook, it moves a random enchantment from an item onto the book, for three buckets. One of several ways to move enchantments, with Apothic's extraction tome."
  ],
  "quest.3235317897092347.title": "Pedestals and spiked plates",
  "quest.3235317897092347.quest_desc": [
    "A Sanguinary Pedestal pulls blood from nearby stains into adjacent tanks; a Spiked Plate on top adds the blood of whatever it kills. Mobs dropped onto plates over pedestals: the classic blood farm.",
    "",
    "Grim, efficient, and quiet."
  ],
  "quest.351C2326640B6B1B.title": "Dark Temples and weather",
  "quest.351C2326640B6B1B.quest_desc": [
    "A Weather Container thrown into a Dark Temple's core absorbs the weather; throw it again to release it. The temple's Environmental Accumulators empower items with lightning, but slowly wear down its biome. The Sanguinary Accumulator does it at home, on blood."
  ],
  "quest.0DE1D4B13C0A2DA2.title": "Vengeance spirits",
  "quest.0DE1D4B13C0A2DA2.quest_desc": [
    "Kills leave a fading aura. A Vengeance Ring shows it and taps its power, but angers the spirits, who chase you. A Vengeance Focus freezes them for a Box of Eternal Closure; the piercing one kills them for loot.",
    "",
    "They remember you. Specifically you."
  ],
  "quest.09F4B8C1E0773233.title": "Spirit Furnace",
  "quest.09F4B8C1E0773233.quest_desc": [
    "A cube of blood-infused Dark Bricks around a hollow sized for the mob, one Spirit Furnace in the wall. Load a Box of Eternal Closure with a spirit: the furnace revives and cooks it for drops, at a steep blood cost. A zombie needs a 3x4 shell."
  ],
  "quest.06763A6655A282B2.title": "Spirits into spawn eggs",
  "quest.06763A6655A282B2.quest_desc": [
    "The Spirit Reanimator pours a captured spirit and a lot of blood into an egg: a spawn egg. The spirit is spent; some mobs refuse. Reliquary's spawn-egg crafting is removed here, but this route is native. Spawners can't be moved with Silk Touch."
  ],
  "quest.711D75049FB2E851.title": "The Broom",
  "quest.711D75049FB2E851.quest_desc": [
    "Three parts combined in a grid: Rod, Brush and Cap. A material on each part (bone, blaze rod, feathers, diamonds, skulls) changes base stats, and modifiers like speed, levitation or flame are added for good. Keep it full of blood or it crawls.",
    "",
    "Witch-grade transport, blood-grade fuel."
  ],
  "quest.27FFB9FB26490BDB.title": "The broom flies first",
  "quest.27FFB9FB26490BDB.quest_desc": [
    "The broom isn't staged: real flight for blood and dark gems. The rest is: basic jetpacks wait for the Act III Power Regulator, and the Rending Gale, Exo Jetpack, Gravichestplate and Just Dire Things' flight upgrade for the Act IV Horizon Chart."
  ],
  "quest.0E305F7EF8D735F8.title": "Blood-powered tools",
  "quest.0E305F7EF8D735F8.quest_desc": [
    "The Blood Pearl of Teleportation is a reusable ender pearl paid in blood; the Mace of Distortion knocks back everything around you; the Necromancer Staff raises zombies against your target. Maces and staff need Empowered Inverted Potentia, charged by lightning."
  ],
  "quest.2B529AB6EBE14361.title": "Full moon over the village",
  "quest.2B529AB6EBE14361.quest_desc": [
    "Some villages hide a werewolf: a villager oddly keen on dark gems who turns into a tall wolf on full-moon nights. A tough fight that drops Werewolf Fur, bones and flesh.",
    "",
    "The quiet neighbor was never that quiet."
  ],
  "quest.56A5B35F99624D2A.title": "The Containment Seal",
  "quest.56A5B35F99624D2A.quest_desc": [
    "Two dark gems, two Soulstained Steel and a Spectral Lens, for «A Vessel for Restless Memory» in Act IV. It gates Theurgy's sulfuric emitter, the Eternal Stella, the fission reactor, burning augments and the Atlas Library.",
    "",
    "What the dark schools make, together."
  ],
  "quest.4AD07AAD58C2D981.title": "A blood engine",
  "quest.4AD07AAD58C2D981.quest_desc": [
    "Spiked plates feeding pedestals and tanks, an infuser with promises, a purifier cleaning tools, a broom overhead and a spirit furnace humming. Malum, Occultism and EvilCraft: the dark schools behind Act IV.",
    "",
    "Every fight is fuel now."
  ],
  "chapter.0F7AE372F9CD1DF7.title": "Forbidden and Arcanus",
  "chapter.0F7AE372F9CD1DF7.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Arcane crystal, the Clibano, the Hephaestus Forge, its four essences and item modifiers."
  ],
  "quest.358A3821475C5EDC.title": "Dark magic as a trade",
  "quest.358A3821475C5EDC.quest_desc": [
    "Mine arcane crystal and darkstone, build the Clibano (a furnace for alloys and extra ore) and the Hephaestus Forge, whose essence-fed rituals forge relics, armor and tool modifiers. No guidebook: EMI has tabs for both.",
    "",
    "The smith's apron is black for a reason."
  ],
  "quest.4FC309242490B654.title": "Arcane crystal",
  "quest.4FC309242490B654.quest_desc": [
    "Fortune works on the ore. Smelt ore for crystals and a crystal for Arcane Crystal Dust; a blast furnace does both faster. Keep both: crystals upgrade the forge, dust goes into almost everything else."
  ],
  "quest.338375EA7163146B.title": "Darkstone by the ton",
  "quest.338375EA7163146B.quest_desc": [
    "Darkstone generates underground and polishes into bricks, tiles and chiseled variants. The Clibano takes 26 blocks and the Hephaestus Forge more than 60, pedestals aside.",
    "",
    "Bring a bigger pickaxe. And a bigger chest."
  ],
  "quest.5693E18BB2B40839.title": "Mundabitur Dust",
  "quest.5693E18BB2B40839.quest_desc": [
    "The mod's activator: use it on a finished structure to turn it into the Clibano or the Hephaestus Forge. Deorum and Quantum Cores eat it too.",
    "",
    "Pixie dust, if pixies were into metallurgy."
  ],
  "quest.3C32648DA7CFCF15.title": "Deorum",
  "quest.3C32648DA7CFCF15.quest_desc": [
    "Gold, Mundabitur Dust, arcane crystal dust and charcoal. Its nuggets gild the chiseled darkstone the forge needs; ingots make lanterns, chains, the Golden Dragon Scale and the tier 3 upgrade.",
    "",
    "Gold that went to finishing school."
  ],
  "quest.2591D00C81AFB14D.title": "The Clibano",
  "quest.2591D00C81AFB14D.quest_desc": [
    "A Clibano Core inside a darkstone shell with an empty center; Mundabitur Dust on the core wakes it up. A faster blast furnace for ores, raw metals, arcane crystal and runic stone: an Act II ore line that needs no power."
  ],
  "quest.3B69EC6CAD40801E.title": "Soul fire and residues",
  "quest.3B69EC6CAD40801E.quest_desc": [
    "Souls give soul fire (about 1.5x faster), Enchanted Souls enchanted fire (about 2.5x), and both leave residues: nine iron residues make an iron block. An Artisan Relic from village smith chests unlocks alloys like Obsidiansteel."
  ],
  "quest.1B60A5EE34117ECD.title": "Blacksmith Gavel",
  "quest.1B60A5EE34117ECD.quest_desc": [
    "Shape clay into a Gavel Head and make a gavel from stone to netherite. Every forge ritual starts with a gavel strike, and mining ore with one can double the drops.",
    "",
    "A hammer that thinks it's a judge. Order in the forge."
  ],
  "quest.253FE16B6D4A2791.title": "The Hephaestus Forge",
  "quest.253FE16B6D4A2791.quest_desc": [
    "Build the base in the wiki's pattern (48 Polished, 9 Gilded Chiseled and 4 Chiseled Arcane darkstone), put a smithing table on the central gilded block and sneak-use Mundabitur Dust on it: corrupted lightning makes the forge. Ritual ingredients go on Darkstone Pedestals around it, the main one in the forge.",
    "",
    "Stand back when the lightning comes."
  ],
  "quest.20379F2B379281E0.title": "Four essences",
  "quest.20379F2B379281E0.quest_desc": [
    "Rituals spend four essences. Aureal: bottles or an Arcane Crystal Obelisk. Souls: a Soul Extractor on soul sand. Blood: hurt creatures near the forge. Experience: Xpetrified Orbs, bottles o' enchanting or enchanted tools, whose enchantments melt down. Higher tiers store more."
  ],
  "quest.6488F327A9FE403D.title": "Forge tiers",
  "quest.6488F327A9FE403D.quest_desc": [
    "Each upgrade needs exactly the previous tier. Tier 2 wants Spawner Scrap (spawners broken without Silk Touch); 3, Deorum; 4, Stellarite (Stella Arcanum ore) and Runes; 5, sculk catalysts, Dark Nether Stars and Dragon Scales (the dragon, End Cities). EMI has each recipe."
  ],
  "quest.6653C2EF87A62B16.title": "Relics in the forge",
  "quest.6653C2EF87A62B16.quest_desc": [
    "Enhancer slots open with tiers. Crimson Stone halves souls; Crescent Moon trims aureal by time of day; Artisan Relic saves XP. Elementarium (jungle temples, pyramids, ocean ruins) enables the prisms; the Pacts, celestial and cursed items. EMI shows which ritual needs which."
  ],
  "quest.6CA12743B44C426C.title": "Modifiers: tools that cheat",
  "quest.6CA12743B44C426C.quest_desc": [
    "Applied at a Smithing Table with the Apply Modifier template. Smelter Prism: tools smelt what they mine. Sea Prism: Aquatic helmets. Ferrognetic Mixture: Magnetized boots. Soul Binding Crystal: kept on death. Eternal Stella: never breaks. Each modifier excludes some enchantments."
  ],
  "quest.312349D84B6E290C.title": "The Eternal Stella",
  "quest.312349D84B6E290C.quest_desc": [
    "A tier 3 ritual with a diamond, three Xpetrified Orbs, Stellarite and essences, and here an Act IV Containment Seal too. The Eternal modifier makes a tool unbreakable, so it sits with late-game power.",
    "",
    "Forever has a price. It's in Act IV."
  ],
  "quest.74A847173675E8AB.title": "Xpetrified Orbs, a mystery",
  "quest.74A847173675E8AB.quest_desc": [
    "Each holds 91 experience essence, and the Eternal Stella needs three. The mod's wiki says the Black Hole block makes them from nearby XP orbs, but no recipe in the pack's data creates that block: check EMI before counting on them.",
    "",
    "Even the wiki shrugs."
  ],
  "quest.44D5BD1787A15336.title": "Draco Arcanus and Tyr",
  "quest.44D5BD1787A15336.quest_desc": [
    "Tier 2 forges Draco Arcanus from netherite pieces, Dragon Scales and Obsidiansteel; tier 4 turns it into Tyr with Aquatic and Golden scales, at a far higher essence cost. Scales come from the Ender Dragon: Act V gear.",
    "",
    "Dress like the thing you killed."
  ],
  "quest.4D06EC892DA23352.title": "Quantum Catcher",
  "quest.4D06EC892DA23352.quest_desc": [
    "It captures a creature and releases it elsewhere; a tier 4 ritual with a Nether Star makes the Boss Catcher. Spawners can't be Silk-Touched here, so moving mobs is how farms get rearranged.",
    "",
    "A moving van for villagers."
  ],
  "quest.63CB6C45914A7709.title": "Odds and ends",
  "quest.63CB6C45914A7709.quest_desc": [
    "Edelwood trees give planks, sticks and a wooden bucket, and their logs smelt into Dark Matter. Bats drop wings for Bat Soup; endermen drop pearl fragments. Magical Farmland has its own crop-doubling rule.",
    "",
    "Bat soup: for the brave, or the lost."
  ],
  "quest.5CA11C0E042C3532.title": "A master smith",
  "quest.5CA11C0E042C3532.quest_desc": [
    "A tier 5 forge, tools that never break, smelt their own ore and stay with you on death, and Tyr on your back. Pair modifiers with Apotheosis affixes; when anvil costs climb too high, the Ark's arcane module resets them."
  ],
  "chapter.4571B8DFF90ABA38.title": "Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks",
  "chapter.4571B8DFF90ABA38.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Scrolls, spell books, inks and the Arcane Anvil: the pack's combat magic."
  ],
  "quest.1588F3F9DFC9186D.title": "Magic that wins fights",
  "quest.1588F3F9DFC9186D.quest_desc": [
    "Spells come on scrolls, go into a spell book and cast from a hotkey with your own mana. Nine schools, each with spells, gear and a focus. Its structures dot the world, each guarded by a mage who won't like you.",
    "",
    "Bring a spare hat."
  ],
  "quest.310C86E24A1949F0.title": "Don't read that scroll",
  "quest.310C86E24A1949F0.quest_desc": [
    "Scrolls come from chests and spellcasting mobs. Using one casts its spell once, free, and destroys it. Better: inscribe it into a spell book and cast it forever. Scrolls have levels, like enchanted books.",
    "",
    "The urge to read it is strong. Resist."
  ],
  "quest.5B5796E05B4E5718.title": "A spell book",
  "quest.5B5796E05B4E5718.quest_desc": [
    "The Flimsy Journal (copper ingots, string, paper) or the Ironbound Tome (chains, leather, paper). Each tier adds slots and often bonuses. It goes in the Spell Book curio slot, and its rarity caps which scrolls the Inscription Table will accept."
  ],
  "quest.5300AB8C0C6E4322.title": "Inscription Table",
  "quest.5300AB8C0C6E4322.quest_desc": [
    "A book on wooden slabs and fences. Put in your spell book and a scroll to inscribe the spell; take the scroll back out and it's uninscribed, free to trade or upgrade.",
    "",
    "The spell moves in; the scroll moves on."
  ],
  "quest.0F2BD1F9BD1B43E6.title": "The wheel, then Alt+Q",
  "quest.0F2BD1F9BD1B43E6.quest_desc": [
    "Hold the wheel key (here the one left of 1, grave accent on US keyboards), pick a spell, press cast (Alt+Q). Fifteen quick-cast slots come unbound: assign your favorites. Iron's mana is separate from Ars's."
  ],
  "quest.2DA843F392A3C84D.title": "Arcane Essence",
  "quest.2DA843F392A3C84D.quest_desc": [
    "Drops from magic structures and spellcasting mobs. With leather armor it makes the Wandering Magician set, early extra mana; eight around wool make Arcane Cloth for robes, eight around an ingot an Arcane Ingot for orbs. Raids are the only bulk source."
  ],
  "quest.0672E75E2444ABC8.title": "A staff for the wizard look",
  "quest.0672E75E2444ABC8.quest_desc": [
    "The Graybeard Staff casts your active spell on right-click and adds passive bonuses; the Artificer's Cane is the stylish option. Rarer ones: the frosted staff comes in pieces, the Blood Staff only from its undead owner.",
    "",
    "The beard is optional."
  ],
  "quest.16AAAB0D7E1898FC.title": "Nine schools, nine foci",
  "quest.16AAAB0D7E1898FC.quest_desc": [
    "Each school has a crafting focus: blaze rod (Fire), Frozen Bone (Ice), Bottle o' Lightning filled at a charged creeper (Lightning), Divine Pearl (Holy), ender pearl, Blood Vial from mobs cooked in a cauldron (Blood), emerald, poisonous potato. Eldritch spells come from restored manuscripts."
  ],
  "quest.63517637E8CE5A1E.title": "Scroll Forge",
  "quest.63517637E8CE5A1E.quest_desc": [
    "Once you reach the Nether. It makes scrolls from ink, paper and a focus: the ink sets rarity and level, the focus the school. Common ink drops from mobs and chests; rare and epic from spellcasters and magic chests.",
    "",
    "Goodbye, loot lottery."
  ],
  "quest.685ED6CB1E5B9681.title": "Alchemist Cauldron",
  "quest.685ED6CB1E5B9681.quest_desc": [
    "It brews ink upward, a quarter of the volume per step: common plus copper is uncommon, then iron, gold and amethyst up to legendary. Bottles fill and empty it. It also recycles scrolls into ink, brews elixirs and makes Blood Vials."
  ],
  "quest.597CF7E4B465F18F.title": "Bigger books",
  "quest.597CF7E4B465F18F.quest_desc": [
    "The Apprentice's and Enchanted spell books hold more spells; both need hoglin Hogskin. Others hide in the world. Unique books like the Necronomicon carry fixed spells you level up at the Arcane Anvil.",
    "",
    "More pages, more trouble."
  ],
  "quest.241F2B077C534AE0.title": "Runes and school armor",
  "quest.241F2B077C534AE0.quest_desc": [
    "Blank Runestones come from magic structures; eight of a school's focus around one make its rune (eight blaze rods, a Fire Rune). School armor is Arcane Cloth plus that rune and boosts its school: specialize, or mix pieces."
  ],
  "quest.49A652D6796F6545.title": "Arcane Anvil",
  "quest.49A652D6796F6545.quest_desc": [
    "Ink of the next rarity levels a scroll up, a higher scroll raises a unique book's locked spell, weapons get imbued with spells, and upgrade orbs go on armor and books.",
    "",
    "The mod's most expensive furniture, and worth it."
  ],
  "quest.4843FD54806C56BA.title": "Mithril and upgrade orbs",
  "quest.4843FD54806C56BA.quest_desc": [
    "Mithril ore is rare, below Y -38, never touching air, and needs a netherite pick. Cinder Essence drops from Ancient Knights, woken by breaking armor piles in the Nether. An orb ringed with eight runes of one attribute grows gear past crafting."
  ],
  "quest.122E552959C3FE9C.title": "Mages and bosses",
  "quest.122E552959C3FE9C.quest_desc": [
    "Class mages always drop their school's rune. The Dead King guards the Necronomicon and the Blood Staff; the dragon drops Dragonskin; Ancient Cities hide the Ruined Book. All optional, and the best source of epic and legendary ink."
  ],
  "quest.4E40FFE6E511D3CC.title": "Spell books with affixes",
  "quest.4E40FFE6E511D3CC.quest_desc": [
    "Iron's registers Apotheosis affixes: books and armor can roll «Intelligent» (max mana), swords «Mana-tapped» (mana regen), plus the usual stat affixes. A looted book may arrive with extra bonuses, and rarity climbs with the World Tier."
  ],
  "quest.6AD961EF77B52800.title": "Iron's Gems 'n Jewelry",
  "quest.6AD961EF77B52800.quest_desc": [
    "A Jewelcrafting Station and its guide, «Jewelcrafting and You». Rings and amulets come from patterns: some unlocked from the start, others from chest scrolls or Jeweler villagers. The primary part sets the quality.",
    "",
    "Bling, with stats."
  ],
  "quest.5E4295CD5E030CFF.title": "No gates on Iron's",
  "quest.5E4295CD5E030CFF.quest_desc": [
    "Nothing is staged: inks, the forge, the cauldron and the anvil keep the mod's own rarity pacing. Raid its structures in Act II for essence, scrolls and the first runestones.",
    "",
    "The mages were here first. Knock anyway."
  ],
  "quest.6095C571C61BE84F.title": "A battle mage",
  "quest.6095C571C61BE84F.quest_desc": [
    "A book of leveled spells, school armor with orbs, affinity rings and a staff for quick casts. The Ancient Codex (netherite, a Ruined Book, Arcane Cloth, a Blood Vial, a Bottle o' Lightning) is the best craftable book.",
    "",
    "The bosses of other worlds are waiting."
  ],
  "chapter.26A82B73436021A2.title": "Nature's Aura",
  "chapter.26A82B73436021A2.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Gold leaf, the Ritual of the Forest, the Natural Altar and the Offering to the Gods."
  ],
  "quest.09484EBB494EFD55.title": "The world is a battery",
  "quest.09484EBB494EFD55.quest_desc": [
    "Devices drain aura, plants refill it. Drain too much and grass rots, breathing hurts and, at worst, the ground explodes; keep it high and plants grow faster. The Act V Renewal Engine needs two Ingots of the Skies from this mod.",
    "",
    "Heliodor built gardens. This is how you pay them back."
  ],
  "quest.441C4201C1880A9C.title": "The Book of Natural Aura",
  "quest.441C4201C1880A9C.quest_desc": [
    "Two paper, leather and a sapling, shapeless. Its chapters unlock with the mod's advancements: red icons are new chapters, orange ones your next research step. The front page links to the advancement tab, the clearest view of your progress."
  ],
  "quest.61D7D048F05DA8C6.title": "Gold that grows on trees",
  "quest.61D7D048F05DA8C6.quest_desc": [
    "Place Brilliant Fiber among a tree's leaves and, over time, it turns them into Gold Leaf. Crushed, it becomes Gold Powder, the chalk of the Ritual of the Forest.",
    "",
    "Finally, money that grows on trees."
  ],
  "quest.23D456E8D1488BBE.title": "The Ritual of the Forest",
  "quest.23D456E8D1488BBE.quest_desc": [
    "Draw the pattern in Gold Powder as the book shows, set Wooden Stands with the ingredients around it and plant the sapling in the middle (oak for early recipes). When it grows, by time or bonemeal, the tree is consumed and the result appears. Only stands with ingredients are needed.",
    "",
    "A tree gives its life for your recipe. Say thanks."
  ],
  "quest.0E8C5FBA5BEA7FEB.title": "Bottled air",
  "quest.0E8C5FBA5BEA7FEB.quest_desc": [
    "Use a Bottle and Cork on the air to collect aura: sunlight in the Overworld, ghosts in the Nether, darkness in the End. Aura Blooms and Cacti are gentle early spots, and dispensers fill bottles for you.",
    "",
    "The only souvenir that's literally air."
  ],
  "quest.10FCA52E96462BEC.title": "Tokens of emotion",
  "quest.10FCA52E96462BEC.quest_desc": [
    "Carved figurines of aura and feeling that build most devices, two per ritual. Joy takes cheerful things, Fear Nether aura and bones, Sorrow a ghast tear, Anger magma and blaze powder. Fear and Sorrow together unlock the Offering Table."
  ],
  "quest.45D368FDE6DD8769.title": "The Natural Altar",
  "quest.45D368FDE6DD8769.quest_desc": [
    "Made by ritual, then built as a multiblock of Golden Stone Bricks. It drains nearby aura only until the area is empty, so it can't do real harm. Iron on it becomes Infused Iron; gold, Tainted Gold, more slowly."
  ],
  "quest.1ABA937F5A5951D2.title": "The Environmental Eye",
  "quest.1ABA937F5A5951D2.quest_desc": [
    "In your hotbar it shows the aura stored in what you look at and the saturation around you; half full is normal. The Environmental Ocular doubles the range and lists active imbalance effects from anywhere in the inventory.",
    "",
    "Never garden blind."
  ],
  "quest.116B803C6C4E8D37.title": "Too little, too much",
  "quest.116B803C6C4E8D37.quest_desc": [
    "Low aura: grass and leaves rot, creatures struggle to breathe and heal, and at the extreme the surface explodes. High aura (about three quarters of the Eye's bar): crops grow in spurts. An Aura Imbalance Ward shuts a draining device off while aura is low."
  ],
  "quest.7447D8C94CD8B600.title": "Making aura",
  "quest.7447D8C94CD8B600.quest_desc": [
    "Ancient Trees restore aura as their leaves die. The Herbivorous Absorber eats nearby flowers but tires of the same one: feed it about six kinds. The Canopy Diminisher turns big-oak growth into aura. The Creational Catalyst lifts the generators' cap."
  ],
  "quest.3A31B8FDDFF83B8B.title": "Altar catalysts",
  "quest.3A31B8FDDFF83B8B.quest_desc": [
    "A catalyst on one of the altar's lower bricks adds recipes. Transmutation (needs an Ingot of the Skies): charcoal to coal, sand to soul sand, Dragon's Breath from End aura. Crumbling: bones to bone meal, cobblestone to sand."
  ],
  "quest.08001C294EFA9C63.title": "Offering to the Gods",
  "quest.08001C294EFA9C63.quest_desc": [
    "Build the Offering Table and ring it with flowers as the book shows. Put Infused Iron in its bowl and throw a Spirit of Calling nearby: with luck, Ingots of the Skies rain down. Tainted Gold as the offering yields more.",
    "",
    "When the gods pay, they pay in metal."
  ],
  "quest.5C61FC7DC4A15D47.title": "The Renewal Engine",
  "quest.5C61FC7DC4A15D47.quest_desc": [
    "Two Ingots of the Skies, two imperium essences, two Ecosystem Capsules and two Propagation Cores, for «Renewable Horizons» in Act V. It then feeds the Ark's nature module, Mekanism's SPS and the Mega pots.",
    "",
    "Keep the offering table busy."
  ],
  "quest.4057018AB5A21247.title": "Botanist and Skyseeker gear",
  "quest.4057018AB5A21247.quest_desc": [
    "Infused Iron tools garden as they work: mossy blocks, spreading grass, seeds from the hoe; an Aura Cache repairs them. Sky ingot gear sends drops to your inventory, fells small trees at once and tills wide.",
    "",
    "Tools with a green thumb."
  ],
  "quest.3D990502C6760FA3.title": "World Eye and the Aura Forge",
  "quest.3D990502C6760FA3.quest_desc": [
    "The World Eye keeps an area loaded for a little aura, radius set by redstone up to about 30 blocks; go easy on shared servers. The Energetic Aura Forge turns surplus aura into Forge Energy."
  ],
  "quest.0A7328CE39A59CC0.title": "A balanced grove",
  "quest.0A7328CE39A59CC0.quest_desc": [
    "Ancient Trees and flower absorbers keeping aura high, an altar with its catalysts, an Offering Table raining sky ingots and an Eye always on you.",
    "",
    "If the base looks greener than the day you arrived, you're doing it right."
  ],
  "chapter.3D66BA95CC40B62F.title": "Occultism I: The Summoner's Craft",
  "chapter.3D66BA95CC40B62F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Spiritfire, chalk, pentacles and bound books, up to iesnium and the attuned crystal."
  ],
  "quest.1F5FC18D82DB781E.title": "Bargains with spirits",
  "quest.1F5FC18D82DB781E.quest_desc": [
    "Chalk pentacles, offerings in bowls, spirits from the Otherworld: Foliot, Djinni, Afrit, Marid, weakest to strongest. Bound, they crush ore, haul, mine and run storage. The story needs a Spirit Attuned Crystal (Act IV) and iesnium (Act V).",
    "",
    "Read the contract. Then read it again."
  ],
  "quest.55F0051E7C82041E.title": "Demon's Dream",
  "quest.55F0051E7C82041E.quest_desc": [
    "Break grass until Demon's Dream Seeds drop and plant a few. The fruit lights spiritfire, heals spirits and familiars, and compresses into an essence. All of Occultism starts here.",
    "",
    "Grandma's garden, if grandma summoned demons."
  ],
  "quest.7823312EBC3C6871.title": "The Dictionary of Spirits",
  "quest.7823312EBC3C6871.quest_desc": [
    "Seeds and a book. Guide and tool at once: crafted with a Book of Binding it writes a spirit's name in, and it's never used up. Each ritual previews its pentacle, and you can anchor the preview in the world to trace it."
  ],
  "quest.4EF837799172E91F.title": "The Third Eye",
  "quest.4EF837799172E91F.quest_desc": [
    "Eat a Demon's Dream Fruit: with luck, Third Eye shows where the Otherworld overlaps ours and lets you harvest those blocks while it lasts. The compressed essence lasts longer, with side effects.",
    "",
    "Side effects include enlightenment."
  ],
  "quest.0E09EEC04A2E0A79.title": "Spiritfire",
  "quest.0E09EEC04A2E0A79.quest_desc": [
    "Throw a Demon's Dream Fruit on the ground and light it: spiritfire doesn't hurt the living and converts items instead of burning them. Andesite becomes Otherstone, a diamond an attuned gem, a book a Taboo Book.",
    "",
    "A bonfire with a customs office."
  ],
  "quest.1C3EF3482F1256F9.title": "Bowls for the offerings",
  "quest.1C3EF3482F1256F9.quest_desc": [
    "The Golden Ritual Bowl sits at the center of every pentacle and starts the ritual when you use the activation item on it. Plain Sacrificial Bowls hold the ingredients, anywhere within 8 blocks horizontally."
  ],
  "quest.4B35F393DC92C7AA.title": "White chalk",
  "quest.4B35F393DC92C7AA.quest_desc": [
    "Burnt Otherstone plus Otherworld ashes make Impure White Chalk; purify it in spiritfire. Right-click draws; clicking again only changes the doodle, since color and position are all that count. A Chalk Brush wipes marks."
  ],
  "quest.1C93C34CD1BCA38E.title": "Candles and tallow",
  "quest.1C93C34CD1BCA38E.quest_desc": [
    "A Butcher Knife gets Tallow from pigs, cows and sheep; string over tallow makes a Large Candle. Almost every pentacle wants candles, and any candle works. Large Candles also count as bookshelves for enchanting.",
    "",
    "Ambience is a technical requirement."
  ],
  "quest.6517C4129FA2CD9B.title": "A book with a name in it",
  "quest.6517C4129FA2CD9B.quest_desc": [
    "Crafted with the Dictionary, a Book of Binding gets a spirit's name and becomes a ritual's activation item. The dye sets the tier: blue Foliot, purple Djinni, yellow Afrit, green Marid. A chiseled bookshelf sneak-used with the Dictionary binds six at once."
  ],
  "quest.1CA9462AE1EC919A.title": "First ritual: a Foliot Crusher",
  "quest.1CA9462AE1EC919A.quest_desc": [
    "Draw Aviar's Circle around the golden bowl in white chalk, put an iron, gold, copper and silver ingot in four bowls, and use the bound Foliot book; purple particles mean it's working. The crusher turns each dropped ore into two dusts (Djinni three, Afrit four, Marid six).",
    "",
    "Ore doubling, with a pulse."
  ],
  "quest.0F3A72F66AD6AC52.title": "Any silver will do",
  "quest.0F3A72F66AD6AC52.quest_desc": [
    "Almost Unified merges duplicate metals by tag: recipes take any silver and output the pack's preferred one. If EMI shows a different ingot than yours, that's expected; rituals check the tag, not the mod."
  ],
  "quest.0A1B2A6A83AAAF8F.title": "Grey smoke: it's waiting",
  "quest.0A1B2A6A83AAAF8F.quest_desc": [
    "Grey particles and nothing consumed: the ritual wants an item used within 16 blocks, or a sacrifice killed by a player within 8 (machine kills don't count). A hopper can start rituals, but familiars then come out untamed."
  ],
  "quest.195DB7C39D08F1A7.title": "Divination Rod",
  "quest.195DB7C39D08F1A7.quest_desc": [
    "Sneak-use it on a block to attune it (andesite finds Otherstone, netherrack iesnium ore), then hold right-click: the nearest match is outlined through walls. Theurgy adds rods for ordinary ores.",
    "",
    "Dowsing, with better eyesight."
  ],
  "quest.63C6B6180B77CA54.title": "Yellow chalk: possession",
  "quest.63C6B6180B77CA54.quest_desc": [
    "Each chalk color opens a ritual type, and yellow is possession. It needs glowstone and gold dust from any crusher: Foliot, Create or Mekanism. The Dictionary's Pentacles section is the roadmap; follow its unlocked entries in order."
  ],
  "quest.4E9DB6E8CEC581C6.title": "End stone without the End",
  "quest.4E9DB6E8CEC581C6.quest_desc": [
    "Hedyrin's Lure plus dirt and stone in the bowls and the Foliot book: a Possessed Endermite that drops end stone often, which purple chalk needs long before the End. Possessed mobs hit harder but drop rare loot far more."
  ],
  "quest.5ECD62C10AC28D2B.title": "Purple chalk: infusion",
  "quest.5ECD62C10AC28D2B.quest_desc": [
    "Purple binds a spirit into an object, drawn on Eziveus' Spectral Compulsion. It opens Foliot infusions: goggle lenses, the Surprisingly Substantial Satchel, the storage actuator base and Research Fragment Dust.",
    "",
    "Put a Foliot in it. It'll work harder."
  ],
  "quest.360C63CD62EEDB62.title": "Otherworld Goggles",
  "quest.360C63CD62EEDB62.quest_desc": [
    "Infused lenses in a Lens Frame, plus leather. Permanent Third Eye, even for iesnium ore, but no harvesting: that takes an Infused or Iesnium Pickaxe.",
    "",
    "The summoner's rite of passage, with prescription."
  ],
  "quest.2FDA25063F13E2DD.title": "Light gray and lime: a Djinni",
  "quest.2FDA25063F13E2DD.quest_desc": [
    "Light gray chalk is a stronger base that replaces white almost everywhere. Lime needs Research Fragment Dust, a Foliot infusion. Djinni pentacles also want skeleton skulls; draw them once and each higher tier upgrades the same drawing."
  ],
  "quest.4DD282FC85BCA251.title": "A pickaxe with a Djinni inside",
  "quest.4DD282FC85BCA251.quest_desc": [
    "Three attuned gems make a Pickaxe Head; infuse it with a Djinni on Strigeor's Higher Binding. It mines Tier 2 Otherworld ore like iesnium, but barely lasts: get your first iesnium and make a real pick.",
    "",
    "The Djinni did not sign up for this."
  ],
  "quest.3E8773D95C626DDC.title": "Iesnium",
  "quest.3E8773D95C626DDC.quest_desc": [
    "The ore looks like netherrack: find it with the netherrack-attuned rod and mine it with the Infused Pickaxe. Raw iesnium smelts into ingots and takes Fortune. Three ingots make an Iesnium Pickaxe; lamps, the mineshaft and the Ark's arcane module want the rest."
  ],
  "quest.2C1E92621CCD380C.title": "Afrit Essence: a bad idea",
  "quest.2C1E92621CCD380C.quest_desc": [
    "Red chalk needs Afrit Essence, and the only source is an Afrit summoned unbound and killed. Its pentacle wants gray and orange chalk and a Spirit Attuned Crystal. Unbound spirits attack everything: far from home, good armor, potions.",
    "",
    "You called it. It's your problem now."
  ],
  "quest.36C42226788C6281.title": "The Spirit Attuned Crystal",
  "quest.36C42226788C6281.quest_desc": [
    "Four Spirit Attuned Gems: diamonds through spiritfire, or Ars Ocultas's apparatus route. It stabilizes advanced pentacles and is Occultism's share of the Act IV Spectral Lens. Make it early and the lens only waits on Malum."
  ],
  "quest.57D4D0D6C014C7D4.title": "Satchels, bags and keys",
  "quest.57D4D0D6C014C7D4.quest_desc": [
    "The ender bag opens with O and the satchel with Insert. Ritual Satchels carry chalk, candles and crystals and place a previewed pentacle for you, block by block or all at once.",
    "",
    "Pentacles to go."
  ],
  "quest.5CB156A16604FA31.title": "Malum mends your chalk",
  "quest.5CB156A16604FA31.quest_desc": [
    "Malum's Repair Pylon restores Occultism chalk with arcane spirits. Those four recipes failed to load upstream on 1.21.1; the pack ships fixed copies with the same materials. Once you run Malum, it's the cheapest way to keep colored chalk alive."
  ],
  "quest.21E542A0FB078F6A.title": "A summoner's circle",
  "quest.21E542A0FB078F6A.quest_desc": [
    "Foliot and Djinni pentacles, bound books, eyes and a pick for the Otherworld, iesnium in the chest. Next: miners in a pocket dimension, magic storage and familiars.",
    "",
    "The spirits have signed. Now they clock in."
  ],
  "chapter.3B13A4C4EA11278B.title": "Reliquary: Monster Relics",
  "chapter.3B13A4C4EA11278B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Mob drops, the Void Tear, pedestals, the handgun, charms and the Rending Gale."
  ],
  "quest.131C52EB72D74003.title": "Relics from monsters",
  "quest.131C52EB72D74003.quest_desc": [
    "Rare monster parts become relics: a bottomless Void Tear, a magnet coin, an XP medallion, a handgun, charms that make one mob ignore you, pedestals that run items. No book: EMI's info tab is the manual.",
    "",
    "Every monster carries a souvenir."
  ],
  "quest.4046BADD160B83AA.title": "One trophy per monster",
  "quest.4046BADD160B83AA.quest_desc": [
    "Each monster has its part: Zombie Heart, Rib Bone, Chelicerae (spider), Catalyzing Gland (creeper), Nebulous Heart (enderman), Witch Hat, Eye of the Storm (charged creeper) and more. Player kills only, about 2% base; Looting raises it."
  ],
  "quest.75974F7E0E2DE9B1.title": "Severing and the Magicbane",
  "quest.75974F7E0E2DE9B1.quest_desc": [
    "Severing, a rare sword enchantment up to V, rolls its own much better chance for these drops, separate from Looting: two tries per kill. The Magicbane is a fragile athame with better odds, and its enchantments add damage."
  ],
  "quest.67E629F9FB07CC3A.title": "Spare parts, recycled",
  "quest.67E629F9FB07CC3A.quest_desc": [
    "Mob drops uncraft into vanilla items: a Rib Bone gives five bones, a Nebulous Heart three ender pearls, and so on. Nothing goes to waste. The only one removed here: spawn eggs from charm fragments."
  ],
  "quest.1602FCCE67071632.title": "The Void Tear",
  "quest.1602FCCE67071632.quest_desc": [
    "It swallows the item you carry most of, in near-unlimited amounts. Sneak-right-click to vacuum that item; right-click a chest to give or take; sneak-scroll changes how much it leaves you. It's also the heart of many relics.",
    "",
    "A pocket with no bottom. Finally."
  ],
  "quest.3F66B42978A29BEB.title": "Coin of Fortune",
  "quest.3F66B42978A29BEB.quest_desc": [
    "It pulls items and XP orbs from about five blocks around; sneak-right-click toggles it, and holding right-click roughly triples the range. On a pedestal it collects into adjacent containers.",
    "",
    "Heads you win. Tails you also win."
  ],
  "quest.6B7CA145EEF35E33.title": "A bank for your XP",
  "quest.6B7CA145EEF35E33.quest_desc": [
    "The Hero's Medallion stores your XP while active and returns it level by level on right-click. On a pedestal it repairs Mending items nearby. The Infernal Tear burns one item type from your inventory into XP.",
    "",
    "A savings account that levels up."
  ],
  "quest.0D1D01C3A723C11C.title": "Pain for hunger",
  "quest.0D1D01C3A723C11C.quest_desc": [
    "The Emperor's Chalice is an endless water bucket; aimed at nothing, you drink and trade health for hunger. The Infernal Chalice carries lava and turns fire damage into hunger, as the Kraken Shell does with drowning.",
    "",
    "Everything costs a sandwich."
  ],
  "quest.3D7F21C902B6A1AC.title": "Feathers that cheat death",
  "quest.3D7F21C902B6A1AC.quest_desc": [
    "The Angelic Feather turns fall damage into hunger. An Angelheart Vial shatters just before you'd die and saves you. Three vials and a feather make the Phoenix Down: full-health revival, then back to being a feather.",
    "",
    "Death, postponed."
  ],
  "quest.704767047C143491.title": "Ender Staff and Wraith Node",
  "quest.704767047C143491.quest_desc": [
    "Charge it with ender pearls; it throws pearls that don't hurt you, far and straight in long-cast mode. Bound to a Wraith Node, holding right-click takes you back there for pearls, same dimension only."
  ],
  "quest.47B3F1FBA7A0719F.title": "Harvest Rod and lily pads",
  "quest.47B3F1FBA7A0719F.quest_desc": [
    "The Harvest Rod stores bone meal and seeds, with three modes: fertilize, plant or unbreakable hoe, over an area while you hold right-click. The Lilypad of Fertility speeds nearby crops, and several stack.",
    "",
    "Farming, in bulk."
  ],
  "quest.1F2BD5D642D742F3.title": "Never place a torch again",
  "quest.1F2BD5D642D742F3.quest_desc": [
    "The Sojourner's Staff holds 1,500 torches and places them up to 30 blocks away. The Lantern of Paranoia places torches by itself wherever monsters could spawn. The Interdiction Torch pushes creatures away.",
    "",
    "Paranoid, and right."
  ],
  "quest.399F5E31880D8EC7.title": "The Hunter's Handgun",
  "quest.399F5E31880D8EC7.quest_desc": [
    "Barrel, grip and hammer assemblies. Right-click fires; hold to reload from magazines. Bullets range from neutral to exorcism, ender (piercing, seeking), buster (TNT-sized) and storm. Recoil, reload and fire rate improve with your XP level, up to 20.",
    "",
    "Magic, with a trigger."
  ],
  "quest.5211737DB3C3FFAB.title": "Peace treaties with mobs",
  "quest.5211737DB3C3FFAB.quest_desc": [
    "Six Charm Fragments of a mob, with leather and string, make a Charm: that mob ignores you even if you hit it. Killing it wears the charm down; its drops repair it. The Charm Belt holds them all.",
    "",
    "Diplomacy, one species at a time."
  ],
  "quest.2DF1BCA7D91D6E9F.title": "Pedestals that work",
  "quest.2DF1BCA7D91D6E9F.quest_desc": [
    "It runs the item on top: the coin collects, the medallion repairs, a sword attacks mobs in range (not bosses, pets or babies), a bucket milks, shears shear, a rod fishes. Switch it on by hand, with redstone, or from another pedestal."
  ],
  "quest.42624A1953E3F0E1.title": "Altar of Light",
  "quest.42624A1953E3F0E1.quest_desc": [
    "Feed it redstone until it activates, and after a while a glowstone block appears on top; it needs direct sunlight. Its partner, the Alkahestry Tome, is removed here, but the altar works alone.",
    "",
    "Photosynthesis for rocks."
  ],
  "quest.4CB4E091ADE69433.title": "Witherless Rose",
  "quest.4CB4E091ADE69433.quest_desc": [
    "Four nether stars, four fertile essences and a rose bush: while it's in your inventory, wither can't touch you. Stars only come from the Wither here, so it's a late, deliberate buy.",
    "",
    "Kill four Withers to stop fearing the fifth."
  ],
  "quest.3AE6FEA5D618D686.title": "The Rending Gale",
  "quest.3AE6FEA5D618D686.quest_desc": [
    "It flies you where you point, pushes or pulls creatures and calls lightning in storms; charge it with feathers. No fall protection, but pointing down and holding cancels the fall. Here its recipe takes an Act IV zanite gemstone.",
    "",
    "Your own private storm."
  ],
  "quest.09A09F5AB3BF9AE8.title": "What the pack took away",
  "quest.09A09F5AB3BF9AE8.quest_desc": [
    "The Alkahestry Tome and its recipes are gone: charged with redstone, it duplicated iron, gold, diamonds and even nether stars. Spawn eggs from charm fragments are gone too, to keep mob farms staged.",
    "",
    "No free diamonds. Sorry."
  ],
  "quest.632F3641C05B1EF2.title": "A hall of relics",
  "quest.632F3641C05B1EF2.quest_desc": [
    "A Void Tear that never fills, a coin and a medallion working on pedestals, a charm belt keeping the dangerous ones polite and, from Act IV, the Rending Gale overhead. Every drop has a use; hunting pays.",
    "",
    "The monsters funded your museum."
  ],
  "chapter.01D252FF0982B5FE.title": "Theurgy: Spagyrics",
  "chapter.01D252FF0982B5FE.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Salt, sulfur and mercury: triple your ores, then learn to transform matter."
  ],
  "quest.083771EBDC43B500.title": "Alchemy, with lab coats",
  "quest.083771EBDC43B500.quest_desc": [
    "Every item is Salt (body), Sulfur (soul) and Mercury (energy). Split and recombine them and one raw ore becomes three ingots; later, one material becomes another. Refining is free from Act II; transmutation waits for Act IV.",
    "",
    "It insists it's science. Humor it."
  ],
  "quest.73C3DD49C2314F5A.title": "The Hermetica",
  "quest.73C3DD49C2314F5A.quest_desc": [
    "A book and two sand. Theurgy's guide walks the processes in order, with the machines each step needs. Occultism's Dictionary links to it for Theurgy's divination rods, which find the ordinary ores Occultism's rod ignores."
  ],
  "quest.09B46C72FEF179E8.title": "A rod for ordinary ores",
  "quest.09B46C72FEF179E8.quest_desc": [
    "Shift-click a block to attune the Glass Divination Rod, hold right-click, and it points to the nearest match: iron, coal and other common ores. Gold and diamonds need the Iron and Diamond rods; sulfur-made rods come pre-attuned."
  ],
  "quest.45B1C0CCAB3365E4.title": "Pyromantic Braziers",
  "quest.45B1C0CCAB3365E4.quest_desc": [
    "Make four. Every heated apparatus sits on one and burns the fuel you give it, by hand or hopper: the calcination oven, the liquefaction cauldron, the distiller and the incubator.",
    "",
    "Alchemy starts with a good fire."
  ],
  "quest.5E1BACB0C941F280.title": "Salt: the body",
  "quest.5E1BACB0C941F280.quest_desc": [
    "A Calcination Oven on a brazier. Right-click it with minerals (ores, raw metals, even stone, sand and dirt) for Alchemical Salt; an empty hand takes it out. Mineral Salt is the body of every refined metal, and dirt is renewable."
  ],
  "quest.7038E75724D0B7B7.title": "Sal Ammoniac: the solvent",
  "quest.7038E75724D0B7B7.quest_desc": [
    "An Accumulator on top of its Tank; pour in up to ten water buckets and wait. A Sal Ammoniac Crystal found while mining speeds it up a lot. The solvent strips salt and mercury and leaves the sulfur."
  ],
  "quest.00239A02D0B8CA69.title": "Sulfur: the multiplier",
  "quest.00239A02D0B8CA69.quest_desc": [
    "A Liquefaction Cauldron on a brazier, filled with Sal Ammoniac. Right-click it with a raw metal or ore: several Alchemical Sulfurs come out, and that's where the multiplication happens.",
    "",
    "The soul of an ingot, in powder."
  ],
  "quest.3A0E5E4FB37C3C75.title": "Mercury: the energy",
  "quest.3A0E5E4FB37C3C75.quest_desc": [
    "A Mercury Distiller on a brazier eats almost anything, crops, food, ores, stone, glass, and distills Mercury Shards; valuable, refined items give more. Mercury recombines items and also powers the Mercury Catalyst and Theurgy's item logistics."
  ],
  "quest.7E37B0C668398893.title": "Three ingots from one",
  "quest.7E37B0C668398893.quest_desc": [
    "The Incubator with its Mercury, Salt and Sulfur vessels around it. Fill each, heat it, take the result: one raw iron gives three ingots. That's why Theurgy belongs in an Act II base.",
    "",
    "Body, soul and spark, back together."
  ],
  "quest.2362DF329027AE22.title": "No more feeding the fire",
  "quest.2362DF329027AE22.quest_desc": [
    "All apparatus share rules: an empty hand takes output first, then input; an item in hand goes in; fluid containers fill or drain. Hoppers and pipes do the same. The Caloric Flux Emitter heats from a distance with no fuel."
  ],
  "quest.2970F8DD054660BA.title": "Mercurial logistics",
  "quest.2970F8DD054660BA.quest_desc": [
    "Mercurial Extractors and Inserters move items over Copper Wire, set with the Mercurial Wand; list and attribute filters pick what moves. The extractor with a list filter is the best way to pull items out of Occultism's storage."
  ],
  "quest.1EF21A76A090EE96.title": "Mercury Catalyst",
  "quest.1EF21A76A090EE96.quest_desc": [
    "Feed it Mercury Shards and it slowly turns them into Mercury Flux, the raw energy flux emitters use. A redstone signal stops output, not conversion. Flux is what drives the Reformation Array later."
  ],
  "quest.30885D7DF78DB6DA.title": "Niter: the idea of a thing",
  "quest.30885D7DF78DB6DA.quest_desc": [
    "Sulfur resists change, so it becomes Niter: the idea of a material rather than the material. Reformation swaps sulfurs of one type and tier, Transmutation changes type (about two metals per gem), Exaltation changes tier (four to one).",
    "",
    "Philosophy you can smelt."
  ],
  "quest.7AFB72ECB64931DE.title": "The Sulfuric Flux Emitter",
  "quest.7AFB72ECB64931DE.quest_desc": [
    "Reformation needs this emitter, and here its recipe takes an Act IV Containment Seal. So every transformation is Act IV, while ore tripling stays free from Act II."
  ],
  "quest.60577799DFED02A7.title": "The Reformation Array",
  "quest.60577799DFED02A7.quest_desc": [
    "No fixed shape: a Target Pedestal (the sulfur you want more of), Source Pedestals (sulfurs to consume) and a Result Pedestal within a few blocks, wand-linked to the emitter, which runs on mercury flux.",
    "",
    "Alchemy that needs furniture arranged just so."
  ],
  "quest.22AECFBCC6A23EE3.title": "Fermentation and Digestion",
  "quest.22AECFBCC6A23EE3.quest_desc": [
    "The Fermentation Vat turns sulfur into niter with crops; the Digestion Vat moves niter between tiers, with purified gold as catalyst. Both work only closed and take input only open: redstone automates them.",
    "",
    "A brewery with a PhD."
  ],
  "quest.6104E3D2E6C0C579.title": "Why transmutation waits",
  "quest.6104E3D2E6C0C579.quest_desc": [
    "Reformation, transmutation and exaltation together replicate almost any material, so the pack ties them to the Containment Seal like other replication tools. Refine ores from day one; save transmutation for what you can't mine."
  ],
  "quest.4297D7DC09942CDB.title": "The alchemist's laboratory",
  "quest.4297D7DC09942CDB.quest_desc": [
    "A heated line tripling every raw metal, flux feeding a reformation array, vats climbing tiers, mercurial wire carrying it all. The magic answer to Mekanism's ore processing, no electricity needed."
  ],
  "chapter.7A8CF776A4A9F342.title": "Mahou Tsukai",
  "chapter.7A8CF776A4A9F342.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Blood circles, powdered catalysts, scrolls, the Fae and Caliburn."
  ],
  "quest.0FA522C681794545.title": "Circles drawn in blood",
  "quest.0FA522C681794545.quest_desc": [
    "Draw circles in your own blood, grind gems and metals into catalysts and put three on a circle to make a spell: one that stays on the floor, or a scroll. No machines, no tiers; mana grows with use.",
    "",
    "Bring bandages."
  ],
  "quest.595636BCD5A9064E.title": "Knowledge Compendium",
  "quest.595636BCD5A9064E.quest_desc": [
    "Red dye, paper and leather. It lists every spell by category, with its cost and whether it needs a cloth. EMI shows each spell's circle and scroll recipe: search the spell's name to see its three catalysts."
  ],
  "quest.0859CF3B84289FA9.title": "First blood",
  "quest.0859CF3B84289FA9.quest_desc": [
    "Take some damage and right away press Draw Mahoujin (Alt+M here): a blood circle appears and a mana bar shows on screen. Rather not jump off things? The Dagger hurts you on purpose.",
    "",
    "The first cut is the deepest. The first voluntary one."
  ],
  "quest.5CDFF2165D9D638C.title": "Mana is a muscle",
  "quest.5CDFF2165D9D638C.quest_desc": [
    "Max mana grows as you spend it. It regenerates slowly, faster on a full stomach, and sleep restores a big chunk: sleep often. Standing near a leyline or leypoint speeds regen further.",
    "",
    "The only gym where naps count as training."
  ],
  "quest.44720A1D5EEEF884.title": "Powdered catalysts",
  "quest.44720A1D5EEEF884.quest_desc": [
    "A Hammer crushes one powder per catalyst; a Mortar and Pestle, two. One per school: iron (Boundaries), ender pearl (Displacement), diamond (Projection), emerald (Exchange), gold (Mystic), quartz (Intelligence), eye of ender (Mystic Eyes)."
  ],
  "quest.4C1CB94C2C87E21C.title": "The mortar pays for itself",
  "quest.4C1CB94C2C87E21C.quest_desc": [
    "Four diamonds, and from then on every catalyst you crush gives double, diamonds and emeralds included. If you'll cast more than a handful of spells, build it early.",
    "",
    "The best investment advice you'll get in this pack."
  ],
  "quest.6592F31DF7E45E78.title": "Circle or scroll",
  "quest.6592F31DF7E45E78.quest_desc": [
    "A spell takes mana, a blood circle and three powders right-clicked onto it. Lay a Spell Cloth first and draw on top, and it comes out as a portable scroll; without the cloth, it stays as a circle on the floor. The book says which spells need cloth."
  ],
  "quest.1A487DE58D0BAD17.title": "Projection and Strengthening",
  "quest.1A487DE58D0BAD17.quest_desc": [
    "Projection copies the tool or weapon you look at, with limited durability. Strengthening makes your first hotbar item briefly unbreakable, stronger and faster. Strengthened items unlock several legendary weapons.",
    "",
    "A sword out of thin air. Literally."
  ],
  "quest.2980EF2C6FEB6D5B.title": "Boundaries",
  "quest.2980EF2C6FEB6D5B.quest_desc": [
    "Circles that act on the area around them and drain mana at a fixed rate: Alarm, Gravity, Drain Life and more. Right-click toggles them, redstone inverts them, and a comparator reads their state (the Alarm gives 15 when it detects something)."
  ],
  "quest.555113334FA34893.title": "Attuned gems",
  "quest.555113334FA34893.quest_desc": [
    "An Attuner (gold and lapis) plus a diamond or an emerald makes an Attuned Gem. Right-click with it in hand to store mana; spells draw from any attuned gem you carry. A spare tank for long casts, before you have circuits."
  ],
  "quest.6E69EB7DC94BE8E5.title": "Leylines and the Fae",
  "quest.6E69EB7DC94BE8E5.quest_desc": [
    "Fay Sight reveals leylines and the Fae. Leylines raise mana regen and even boost an elytra flying along them. The Fae drop Fae Essence, which places circles anyone can use: ideal for automating scrolls.",
    "",
    "The world has veins. Now you can see them."
  ],
  "quest.6713F22CD30C7F75.title": "Mana Circuits",
  "quest.6713F22CD30C7F75.quest_desc": [
    "A Mana Circuit stores mana you can draw on nearby. The first to right-click owns it: right-click deposits, sneak toggles, Fae Essence shares it. The Magitech version skips the Fae. Kodoku worms and written works can feed circuits."
  ],
  "quest.52951C5E08145F8D.title": "The Mystic Code",
  "quest.52951C5E08145F8D.quest_desc": [
    "It holds three stacks of scrolls: sneak-right-click opens it, its key switches scrolls, right-click casts. The First Sorcery variant wears out but reuses scrolls instead of burning them.",
    "",
    "A wizard's holster."
  ],
  "quest.42CD70A6B27D9F8B.title": "Swaps, scrying, familiars",
  "quest.42CD70A6B27D9F8B.quest_desc": [
    "Equivalent Displacement circles pair up anywhere, even across dimensions, and swap only when both have something on top. Summon Familiar sends a scout that reports players, mobs and blocks and keeps its area loaded; hand it a block to hunt just that."
  ],
  "quest.6CBDD65A4899ED9C.title": "Kodoku worms",
  "quest.6CBDD65A4899ED9C.quest_desc": [
    "It feeds on conflict: each time a monster kills something, its value grows by one plus the victim's. Put a hungry worm on a strong specimen, kill it, pick the worm back up. Burned near circuits it makes mana; carried, it shields you from sympathetic magic.",
    "",
    "The food chain, bottled."
  ],
  "quest.609BD579C2FEF1AF.title": "A sword from the lake",
  "quest.609BD579C2FEF1AF.quest_desc": [
    "The Power Consolidation circle grows a lake, mana per step. Once full, throw in an enchanted sword to receive Caliburn: its damage plus a bonus for enchantments, holier ones counting more. Undead flee it; a lance becomes Rhongomyniad.",
    "",
    "The lady of the lake takes swords, not requests."
  ],
  "quest.17D803A7819F2A32.title": "Weapons you earn",
  "quest.17D803A7819F2A32.quest_desc": [
    "Some weapons are feats, not recipes. Nobu appears when a strengthened bow hits an enemy 200 blocks away; Replica wants a block with a strengthened shield under stacked defensive spells. EMI shows each condition as a special recipe.",
    "",
    "Morgan's is cruel on purpose."
  ],
  "quest.60C225AB0B544AE1.title": "Big spells, big bills",
  "quest.60C225AB0B544AE1.quest_desc": [
    "Treasury Projection throws weapons from your inventory, bags and ender chest; Rho Aias bounces mobs and deletes projectiles. Late spells like these charge per use or per weapon: carry attuned gems or stay near circuits.",
    "",
    "No casting on credit."
  ],
  "quest.68924C9E1161B371.title": "Mahou keys",
  "quest.68924C9E1161B371.quest_desc": [
    "Draw Mahoujin is Alt+M here (plain M is a JourneyMap waypoint; Ctrl+M and Shift+M toggle magnets) and Selective Displacement is Ctrl+H. The Mystic Code, Nobu and settings keys keep their defaults. Nothing in Mahou Tsukai needs an Atlas component."
  ],
  "quest.5DE51A3BBD3C868B.title": "A true mahoutsukai",
  "quest.5DE51A3BBD3C868B.quest_desc": [
    "Mana trained by use, a mortar full of powders, circuits fed by the Fae, Caliburn in hand and a Mystic Code loaded. Keep experimenting and chase the book's secret hints.",
    "",
    "No tiers, no ceiling. Just you and a lot of blood."
  ],
  "chapter.6016EB06EA820BF3.title": "Malum: Soul Research",
  "chapter.6016EB06EA820BF3.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Scythes, spirit crystals, the Spirit Altar, soul-touched metals and totem rites."
  ],
  "quest.34CEB9CA120B9540.title": "The magic of souls",
  "quest.34CEB9CA120B9540.quest_desc": [
    "Kill with a scythe and souls shatter into spirit crystals; infuse them at a Spirit Altar into metals, trinkets, armor and totems. Act IV needs Arcane Spirits and Soulstained Steel, so start in Act III.",
    "",
    "Soul research. Ethics committee pending."
  ],
  "quest.581C01A7948EB423.title": "Soulstone",
  "quest.581C01A7948EB423.quest_desc": [
    "Mine Soulstone ore underground and smelt it: two Refined Soulstone per raw piece. The scythe, the altar, the Encyclopedia and every Soulstained Steel ingot (four each) eat it.",
    "",
    "It looks boring until refined. Like most scholars."
  ],
  "quest.2CB3D5EEC792BEB2.title": "Encyclopedia Arcana",
  "quest.2CB3D5EEC792BEB2.quest_desc": [
    "A book and a Refined Soulstone. Malum's guide, written as a researcher's notes: each entry shows its infusion with the spirits and extra items it needs. The entries form a tree; the top branches are the path that matters first."
  ],
  "quest.0699DB3FC29CDC66.title": "Crude Scythe",
  "quest.0699DB3FC29CDC66.quest_desc": [
    "Creatures killed with it shatter into spirit crystals that fly to you. Weaker than a sword but it sweeps wide; Spirit Plunder drops more spirits for a bit of durability.",
    "",
    "The harvest is not wheat."
  ],
  "quest.639E0711137A795A.title": "Eight kinds of spirit",
  "quest.639E0711137A795A.quest_desc": [
    "Each mob gives its own: Sacred from passive animals, Wicked from hostiles, Arcane from witches, skeletons and blazes; Earthen, Infernal, Aerial, Aqueous and Eldritch from zombies, creepers, chickens, drowned and endermen. Get eight Arcane first."
  ],
  "quest.4FB4904FC059FA41.title": "Soulwoven Pouch",
  "quest.4FB4904FC059FA41.quest_desc": [
    "Spirits clutter the inventory fast. The Soulwoven Pouch (string and spirit-infused silk) picks up spirit crystals by itself. Fed rot, it becomes the Ravenous Pouch, which snatches anything matching what it holds."
  ],
  "quest.26F8A7D4DA540396.title": "Runewood",
  "quest.26F8A7D4DA540396.quest_desc": [
    "Orange-yellow leaves in open plains. Strip a sappy log and bottle Runic Sap: a healing drink, and sapballs replace slimeballs in most recipes. Smelted runewood gives Arcane Charcoal, which outlasts normal charcoal."
  ],
  "quest.5B96C1F2F831C4BE.title": "Spirit Altar",
  "quest.5B96C1F2F831C4BE.quest_desc": [
    "Item on the altar, its spirits inside, extra ingredients on runewood pedestals within 4 blocks. Spirits flow in and the extras are pulled one by one; obelisks speed it up later.",
    "",
    "Slow on purpose. The soul doesn't rush."
  ],
  "quest.0F75CFDAF88DDB4D.title": "First infusion: Hex Ash",
  "quest.0F75CFDAF88DDB4D.quest_desc": [
    "Gunpowder plus one Arcane Spirit. The altar's first product, and a common extra ingredient: totem bases, the crucible, impetus, the steel scythe. Make a stack while you learn the altar's rhythm."
  ],
  "quest.6B389E759EB3AD28.title": "Hallowed Gold and jars",
  "quest.6B389E759EB3AD28.quest_desc": [
    "A gold ingot with Sacred and Arcane spirits and quartz on pedestals: Hallowed Gold, the ideal spirit conductor. Hallowed gold over glass makes Spirit Jars, each holding a near-infinite amount of one spirit: one per type by the altar."
  ],
  "quest.5168CEF9792AB068.title": "Soulstained Steel",
  "quest.5168CEF9792AB068.quest_desc": [
    "An iron ingot with Wicked, Earthen and Arcane spirits and four Refined Soulstone on pedestals. Make at least two for the Act IV Containment Seal; zombies and witches cover almost every spirit.",
    "",
    "Steel that hits the soul, not the armor."
  ],
  "quest.6BA85AC9B81751C1.title": "Soulstained gear",
  "quest.6BA85AC9B81751C1.quest_desc": [
    "The altar upgrades the Crude Scythe with Soulstained Steel and spirits, enchantments kept. Soulstained armor carries Soul Ward, a recharging barrier that absorbs part of the damage.",
    "",
    "Metal that bites back, dressed as armor."
  ],
  "quest.029C950DD37077D3.title": "Tainted and Twisted Rock",
  "quest.029C950DD37077D3.quest_desc": [
    "Sixteen stone with Sacred and Arcane spirits give Tainted Rock; with Wicked and Arcane, Twisted Rock. Tainted dissipates nearby magic, Twisted pushes it away. The Spirit Crucible takes eight of each."
  ],
  "quest.3A6925EFDA62BD58.title": "Spirit Crucible",
  "quest.3A6925EFDA62BD58.quest_desc": [
    "Fed an Alchemical Impetus and spirits, it focuses them into redstone, glowstone, gunpowder, quartz, amethyst or prismarine. Metal impetuses make nodes worth two thirds of an ingot. The impetus wears with each cycle.",
    "",
    "Slow, but it beats mining."
  ],
  "quest.0292DE93381C1030.title": "Totems and spirit rites",
  "quest.0292DE93381C1030.quest_desc": [
    "Engrave spirits into runewood logs and stack them on a Totem Base in the right order: the totem performs a rite, like healing, harming, Stone Ward, speed, faster-growing animals or a locus that smelts blocks. An axe strips a wrong rune."
  ],
  "quest.1E5BF251F3080AFD.title": "Blight: keep it fenced",
  "quest.1E5BF251F3080AFD.quest_desc": [
    "The Undirected Rite scars a totem into Soulwood, which changes every rite. Soulwood trees spread Blight and corrupt the ground: experiment far from farms and builds.",
    "",
    "It starts as one tree. It never ends as one tree."
  ],
  "quest.5DB4B6324C23E1DD.title": "Obelisks",
  "quest.5DB4B6324C23E1DD.quest_desc": [
    "Up to four Runewood Obelisks near the altar each speed infusion by a quarter. A Brilliant Obelisk counts as five bookshelves for enchanting. Brilliance is solid experience, found as ore where a soul faded into stone."
  ],
  "quest.5E5D469EB7EAF98D.title": "Rings, belts and runes",
  "quest.5E5D469EB7EAF98D.quest_desc": [
    "An infused Gilded Ring becomes the Ring of Curative Talent (heals as you collect spirits) or of Manaweaving (faster Soul Ward); the Belt of the Prospector adds Avarice, a kind of fortune. Later, runes on a brooch end the jewelry swapping."
  ],
  "quest.3CB2F87E38786E69.title": "Repair Pylon",
  "quest.3CB2F87E38786E69.quest_desc": [
    "Fed spirits and the right repair material, it mends an item on a nearby pedestal or stand without XP: about half the durability, three quarters for spirit gear. Occultism's four chalk repairs work here at their original costs."
  ],
  "quest.1B30DDEA4B287B48.title": "Recipes that now load",
  "quest.1B30DDEA4B287B48.quest_desc": [
    "Create milling of Grim Talc works here: bone meal plus a chance of yellow dye. The four Occultism chalk repairs load with their original costs. Malum's repair recipes for The Undergarden are disabled.",
    "",
    "A few bugs, exorcised."
  ],
  "quest.288073C2EAA54A10.title": "Spirits for the Lens",
  "quest.288073C2EAA54A10.quest_desc": [
    "The Act IV Spectral Lens takes two Arcane Spirits, plus an Occultism crystal, a Create precision mechanism and a Calibration Frame, for «Voices in the Glass». Keep a jar of Arcane: the Seal and the Ark's module want more lenses."
  ],
  "quest.2D93ECBE7A5490E5.title": "A soul workshop",
  "quest.2D93ECBE7A5490E5.quest_desc": [
    "An altar sped by obelisks, a wall of spirit jars, a crucible turning souls into metal, totems blessing the base, Soulstained gear on your back. Spirits also feed the Lens, Occultism's chalk and your enchanting table.",
    "",
    "Patience, and a steady supply of souls."
  ],
  "chapter.099A3C8886D50AB9.title": "Occultism II: Spirits at Work",
  "chapter.099A3C8886D50AB9.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Workers, miners in a pocket dimension, magic storage, familiars and master tools."
  ],
  "quest.2375A818765DD8FC.title": "Spirits on the payroll",
  "quest.2375A818765DD8FC.quest_desc": [
    "Workers that sort, carry, smelt and crush; miners in a pocket dimension; storage that grows with rituals; familiars. Most need Djinni rituals. By default only trader, time and weather spirits decay.",
    "",
    "No unions in the Otherworld. Yet."
  ],
  "quest.353FC9B6E478C883.title": "Foliot Transporter",
  "quest.353FC9B6E478C883.quest_desc": [
    "The ritual also drops its Book of Calling. Sneak-use the book on the source inventory, then on the target: it moves everything between them, machines and other spirits included.",
    "",
    "A hopper line without the hoppers."
  ],
  "quest.5D6A2910F50F7AD3.title": "Foliot Janitor",
  "quest.5D6A2910F50F7AD3.quest_desc": [
    "It picks up dropped items into the inventory bound with its book. Trap: it starts in allow mode and only grabs what's listed, so open the book (right-click the air) and set the list. Janitor plus Transporter around a Crusher: the classic loop."
  ],
  "quest.2113321E34D6AB18.title": "Books of Calling and lamps",
  "quest.2113321E34D6AB18.quest_desc": [
    "A Book of Calling runs one worker: right-click the air to configure, sneak-use a block to apply, sneak-use the spirit to capture or release it. Lost it? Craft another and sneak-use it on the spirit. A Magic Lamp carries a worker safe from decay."
  ],
  "quest.4A60EF2567A10FC6.title": "A Djinni with a watch",
  "quest.4A60EF2567A10FC6.quest_desc": [
    "A Djinni called with a torch, a sapling, wheat and yellow dye makes it day, then leaves; gunpowder, rotten flesh, a bone and black dye make it night. One change, and it's gone. Cheaper than waiting when a ritual or hunt needs a certain hour."
  ],
  "quest.125BACA6BF18264C.title": "Dimensional Mineshaft",
  "quest.125BACA6BF18264C.quest_desc": [
    "A Djinni holds a portal too small for people, and miner spirits go through to an empty mining dimension. Miner lamp in the top slot, ores out the bottom; it discards what it can't store, so drain it.",
    "",
    "Mining without the commute."
  ],
  "quest.2CDF4CFA614E7F02.title": "Miner Foliot",
  "quest.2CDF4CFA614E7F02.quest_desc": [
    "It mines slowly and returns everything, stone included. The lamp wears out and the spirit goes home. A comparator reads fill and lamp durability; redstone pauses the shaft."
  ],
  "quest.70071D10FE1B5D24.title": "Ore Miner Djinni",
  "quest.70071D10FE1B5D24.quest_desc": [
    "A Djinni upgrade of the Foliot's lamp: it skips stone and returns only ores, faster, but wears its lamp quickly. The Afrit adds deepslate ores; the Marid finds the rarest, ancient debris and iesnium included, and is an Act V project."
  ],
  "quest.1E82438707E4EBB5.title": "What the miners won't find",
  "quest.1E82438707E4EBB5.quest_desc": [
    "Miners pull from ore tags, and Create: New Age's thorium has none here: the thorium reactor needs real mining. Efficiency speeds miners, Fortune adds results, Silk Touch multiplies them, Unbreaking and Mending spare the lamp."
  ],
  "quest.212D8FE4CBAB4DA8.title": "One huge chest",
  "quest.212D8FE4CBAB4DA8.quest_desc": [
    "A Djinni-made crystal matrix crafted onto a Foliot-made base: the Dimensional Storage Actuator. 128 item types, 256,000 items; broken, it keeps everything inside like a shulker box. Damaged or enchanted variants take a type each."
  ],
  "quest.4AAF6194A6D896F8.title": "Stabilizers: more room",
  "quest.4AAF6194A6D896F8.quest_desc": [
    "Rituals take a stabilizer from Tier 0 up to Tier 5. Point them at the matrix (one block above the actuator), up to 5 blocks away in a straight line. Breaking one to upgrade loses nothing; new items just wait for room."
  ],
  "quest.2CB1AAE292F36D40.title": "Remotes and wormholes",
  "quest.2CB1AAE292F36D40.quest_desc": [
    "A Stable Wormhole is another access point; the Storage Accessor opens it from your hand. Hoppers and pipes work, but pulling items out is the costly part: Transporter spirits or Theurgy's extractor with a list filter beat slot-scanning pipes."
  ],
  "quest.43B08A1E3138F0D9.title": "Familiars",
  "quest.43B08A1E3138F0D9.quest_desc": [
    "Spirits in animal bodies that follow you with buffs; some fight. Start the ritual by hand or they come out untamed; Demon's Dream fruit heals them. Cheap first picks: the Greedy Familiar grabs items, the Deer gives speed and jump.",
    "",
    "A pet with a résumé."
  ],
  "quest.4A0440E2A68B91C9.title": "A familiar for every job",
  "quest.4A0440E2A68B91C9.quest_desc": [
    "Bat: night vision. Beaver: fells small trees. Cthulhu: water breathing. Devil: fire resistance. Drikwing: multi-jump. Blacksmith: repairs gear as you pick up stone and upgrades familiars for iron. Fairy: keeps familiars alive. Guardian: gives a limb so you don't die."
  ],
  "quest.14809600791FA54B.title": "Soul Gems",
  "quest.14809600791FA54B.quest_desc": [
    "A Fragile Soul Gem (Foliot infusion) carries one creature; the full one is a Djinni infusion. Right-click to capture, again to release; bosses refuse. It moves animals and villagers, and feeds the Familiar Ring and the Battlefield."
  ],
  "quest.7D62DC89A1D57289.title": "Familiar Ring",
  "quest.7D62DC89A1D57289.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a tamed familiar with it and wear it as a curio: the effect stays, the creature doesn't follow. Whoever releases it becomes its master, so familiars can be traded. A ringed Greedy Familiar widens your own pickup range."
  ],
  "quest.5CEE9965BE070ED8.title": "Dimensional Battlefield",
  "quest.5CEE9965BE070ED8.quest_desc": [
    "An Afrit infusion opens an arena. Feed it a creature in a soul gem, a weapon for the Afrit and spiritual fuel: it clones the creature and kills it for loot. A Trinity Gem even allows possessed mobs and bosses.",
    "",
    "A mob farm with no mobs in your yard."
  ],
  "quest.7DC606A8388E92A2.title": "Spirit Grindstone",
  "quest.7DC606A8388E92A2.quest_desc": [
    "It removes only curses, keeps every other enchantment, refunds the curses' experience and repairs better when combining. The other way to lift curses is Apothic Enchanting's prismatic web in an anvil."
  ],
  "quest.177EAD9F1FA367B4.title": "Iesnium Anvil",
  "quest.177EAD9F1FA367B4.quest_desc": [
    "A Marid infusion on a pentacle of many chalks and a wither skull. It never breaks, pushes an enchantment one level past max, pays half the shown cost and raises the cap. It doesn't reset prior work; the Ark's arcane module does.",
    "",
    "The summoner's summit, Act V."
  ],
  "quest.11A513C5F99884D1.title": "The Wild Hunt",
  "quest.11A513C5F99884D1.quest_desc": [
    "Marid pentacles want wither skeleton skulls. The Wild Hunt, started with a skeleton skull on Osorin's Unbound Calling, calls Greater Spirits shaped like wither skeletons, nearly invulnerable until their minions fall. They drop skulls, rudely."
  ],
  "quest.53DE6B143EACBE84.title": "Iesnium for the Ark",
  "quest.53DE6B143EACBE84.quest_desc": [
    "The Ark's Arcane Module (Act V) takes two Spectral Lenses, two Containment Seals, an iesnium ingot and a nether star. In a complete Ark it resets a worn item's prior-work penalty, keeping enchantments, affixes and sockets.",
    "",
    "Where arcane materials become Ark hardware."
  ],
  "quest.7983A45463227146.title": "A house full of spirits",
  "quest.7983A45463227146.quest_desc": [
    "Miners in the shaft, a stabilized actuator holding the base, workers hauling and sweeping, a ring on your finger, an iesnium anvil in the forge. Next on the arcane road: Malum, whose spirits finish the Spectral Lens."
  ],
  "chapter.330F418E7969E977.title": "Psi: Programmable Spells",
  "chapter.330F418E7969E977.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The CAD, the Spell Programmer, bullets, psimetal and the Exosuit."
  ],
  "quest.31660A2849BD9384.title": "Spells you program",
  "quest.31660A2849BD9384.quest_desc": [
    "Build a Casting Assistant Device (CAD), write spells on a 9x9 grid of small pieces, copy them into Spell Bullets and cast. All of Psi is Act III here: the CAD Assembler needs a Power Regulator.",
    "",
    "Terra's kind of magic: a machine you teach to think."
  ],
  "quest.7D362F3E6640B2DF.title": "CAD Assembler",
  "quest.7D362F3E6640B2DF.quest_desc": [
    "Iron, a piston and a Power Regulator (Act III). It builds a CAD from its components and loads Spell Bullets into it, and into Psimetal tools and armor. No Assembler, no CAD, no spell: this is where Psi really starts."
  ],
  "quest.24BA6CEFF3600962.title": "A bare CAD makes Psidust",
  "quest.24BA6CEFF3600962.quest_desc": [
    "An Iron CAD Assembly alone in the Assembler is a bare CAD. It can't cast spells, but drop redstone dust, point the empty CAD at it and right-click: the redstone becomes Psidust, the base of every early part.",
    "",
    "Step one of magic: redstone, but spicier."
  ],
  "quest.377B938ABA847AB6.title": "Core, Socket and Bullets",
  "quest.377B938ABA847AB6.quest_desc": [
    "A casting CAD needs an Assembly, a Core and a Socket, all from iron and psidust; bullets too. A bare CAD in a crafting grid gives the Assembly back. A Battery is worth it; a Colorizer only changes colors."
  ],
  "quest.336C46A2C862033C.title": "The Spell Programmer",
  "quest.336C46A2C862033C.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a cell and type to search pieces; left-click a piece to point its inputs at neighbors. When the corner X turns into a check, the spell compiles. The book's tutorials teach the whole system in order.",
    "",
    "First program: «hello, world». Second: «hello, crater»."
  ],
  "quest.349FE8F901DFB239.title": "Load and fire",
  "quest.349FE8F901DFB239.quest_desc": [
    "Use a bullet on the Programmer to copy the spell, then load it into the CAD at the Assembler. Hold the Psi key (Alt+F here) to pick it on the radial and right-click. Sneak-use the CAD on the Programmer to refresh the loaded bullet."
  ],
  "quest.1A449BEF14F33074.title": "Five numbers to respect",
  "quest.1A449BEF14F33074.quest_desc": [
    "The Core caps Complexity and Projection, the Assembly Potency, the Socket spell size. Cost comes from your Psi energy; overdraw and the rest comes out of your health, and the CAD shuts down until you refill. Tricks reach 32 blocks at most.",
    "",
    "A Battery is cheaper than a funeral."
  ],
  "quest.49C120F578144C3E.title": "One CAD per mage",
  "quest.49C120F578144C3E.quest_desc": [
    "Carry a single CAD. Two or more in your inventory interfere and every spell shorts out; the book calls it cast jamming. Spares go in a chest.",
    "",
    "Two radios on the same frequency. Same result."
  ],
  "quest.66787E7A0B61BE71.title": "Psimetal",
  "quest.66787E7A0B61BE71.quest_desc": [
    "Cast Trick: Infusion near gold ingots on the ground and they become Psimetal: better cores, sockets and batteries, the Psimetal Assembly, drives, tools and armor. It also upgrades a Gold CAD Assembly lying there.",
    "",
    "Alchemy, compiled."
  ],
  "quest.1E8264AB0191DD07.title": "Bullet types",
  "quest.1E8264AB0191DD07.quest_desc": [
    "One extra ingredient sets the bullet type: arrow Projectile, string Loopcast (four times a second while held), snowball Circle, gunpowder Grenade, redstone Charge (waits for a Detonator), button Mine. Each type multiplies the cost and moves the focal point."
  ],
  "quest.2BAA9AA5501D9B58.title": "Better cores and sockets",
  "quest.2BAA9AA5501D9B58.quest_desc": [
    "Psimetal shell, and the dust inside picks the model. Redstone: Overclocked Core (double Complexity) and Signaling Socket (six bullets). Glowstone: Conductive Core (four tricks at once) and Large Socket (eight bullets). The Psimetal Assembly adds Potency."
  ],
  "quest.6089239E241C601C.title": "Psigems",
  "quest.6089239E241C601C.quest_desc": [
    "With a Psimetal Assembly, cast Trick: Greater Infusion near diamonds on the ground: they become Psigems, for the top cores and sockets, Psimetal tools and the Exosuit.",
    "",
    "Diamonds, but with opinions."
  ],
  "quest.7E7538E140C58749.title": "Psigem cores need a Matrix",
  "quest.7E7538E140C58749.quest_desc": [
    "The Hyperclocked Core (double a Conductive's Complexity) and the Radiative Core (seven tricks at once) keep their native recipes, psimetal and psigems: the CAD Assembler already makes Psi an Act III mod."
  ],
  "quest.4E1D12B86BB751F6.title": "Ebony and Ivory",
  "quest.4E1D12B86BB751F6.quest_desc": [
    "In the End only: cast Trick: Ebony and Ivory (Psimetal Assembly needed) near coal and nether quartz on the ground. Coat psimetal with the results for the top Assemblies: Ebony takes more Potency, Ivory is more efficient.",
    "",
    "In perfect harmony, far from home."
  ],
  "quest.51AA960E129CC4FD.title": "Tools that cast",
  "quest.51AA960E129CC4FD.quest_desc": [
    "About diamond grade. They cast their selected spell every time they break a block (the sword on every hit), hold three bullets and repair with spare Psi. A pickaxe that also breaks the blocks around the one you mined is a classic."
  ],
  "quest.52A72E20AF458775.title": "The Psimetal Exosuit",
  "quest.52A72E20AF458775.quest_desc": [
    "Each piece holds three bullets and fires on its own trigger: the Helmet on its Sensor (light, heat, water…), the Chestplate when you're hit, the Leggings every tick, the Boots when you jump. A bit better than iron, self-repairing.",
    "",
    "Armor with reflexes."
  ],
  "quest.4621F69AC863F5AC.title": "A spell library",
  "quest.4621F69AC863F5AC.quest_desc": [
    "A Spell Drive stores one spell: sneak-use it on the Programmer to save, again to load. A Vector Ruler stores a position or offset your spells can read.",
    "",
    "Version control, the magical kind."
  ],
  "quest.1F1890606B8EECB9.title": "Alt+F and the missing book",
  "quest.1F1890606B8EECB9.quest_desc": [
    "Psi's master key moves from C to Alt+F here: C saves hotbars and opens the Ars book even with Alt held. With no CAD in hand it opens the Encyclopaedia Psionica. Psi's book as an item: drop a plain book and cast at it with a CAD."
  ],
  "quest.7B2642782F246FD0.title": "A spellslinger",
  "quest.7B2642782F246FD0.quest_desc": [
    "A psigem-core CAD, an Exosuit that reacts by itself, tools that cast as they work and a drive full of spells you wrote. The only ceiling is your ingenuity: compress, chain tricks, share spells with friends.",
    "",
    "The grid is small. What fits in it is not."
  ],
  "chapter.78BEECFE74B3285C.title": "Spawners and Augments",
  "chapter.78BEECFE74B3285C.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Spawner stats, the sixteen copper augments by act, no Silk Touch and Capturing."
  ],
  "quest.46B4B2355B6D1190.title": "Spawners you tune in place",
  "quest.46B4B2355B6D1190.quest_desc": [
    "Every spawner has stats (delay, count, range…) you can change where it stands, using sixteen copper Augments built on Atlas components, one set per act from III to V. Apotheosis's runes are removed, and spawners can't be picked up.",
    "",
    "You don't move the spawner. You move in."
  ],
  "quest.2FA66A984D5CBF5F.title": "What a spawner knows",
  "quest.2FA66A984D5CBF5F.quest_desc": [
    "It waits between Min and Max Spawn Delay, tries Spawn Count mobs at once, stops at Max Entities nearby, runs only with a player in Activation Range and spawns within Spawn Range. Switches include No AI, Silent, Youthful, Redstone Control and Echoing (extra loot)."
  ],
  "quest.3604CB1267C1BCF1.title": "Spawners stay put",
  "quest.3604CB1267C1BCF1.quest_desc": [
    "Silk Touch can't lift spawners here: portable spawners would bring mob farms ahead of the Act IV routes. Build the farm around the spawner you found, or leave it be.",
    "",
    "Location, location, location."
  ],
  "quest.323AF494EF14AD45.title": "Applying an augment",
  "quest.323AF494EF14AD45.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click the spawner with an augment: it's spent and the stat moves one fixed step, up to a cap (Multitude: +2 Spawn Count, up to 16). EMI lists every step and cap. Mistake? Nether quartz in the offhand plus the same augment reverses a step."
  ],
  "quest.1130D1DBD5D17857.title": "Copper medallions",
  "quest.1130D1DBD5D17857.quest_desc": [
    "A small copper medallion: the classic core for the stat in the middle (sugar for speed, a clock for delay), an Atlas component on top and three copper sheets. The component sets the act and stands in for Apotheosis's gem dust and rarity materials."
  ],
  "quest.1CEB5CEB62360BE4.title": "Act III: speed and reach",
  "quest.1CEB5CEB62360BE4.quest_desc": [
    "Quickening lowers Min Delay 10 ticks and Hastening Max Delay 20, both down to 20. Spread adds 2 Spawn Range (up to 32); Reach adds 4 Activation Range (up to 48). Lower both delays: if max drops below min, min wins."
  ],
  "quest.527B9F06CC766C21.title": "Act III: silent and youthful",
  "quest.527B9F06CC766C21.quest_desc": [
    "Silent mutes the spawned mobs, a mercy next to your base. Youthful spawns babies whenever the mob has them. Both are switches: one augment is enough.",
    "",
    "Peace and quiet, and tiny zombies."
  ],
  "quest.2F85F12146928AC0.title": "Act IV: more, and weaker",
  "quest.2F85F12146928AC0.quest_desc": [
    "Multitude adds 2 Spawn Count (up to 16) and Crowd 2 Max Entities (up to 32). Debilitating cuts Initial Health by 5%, down to 20%; Burning sets mobs on fire. Raise Max Entities with Spawn Count, or the spawner stops once the room fills."
  ],
  "quest.23901202F94D30E8.title": "Act V: the full farm",
  "quest.23901202F94D30E8.quest_desc": [
    "Echoing adds a level of extra loot, up to 3. Defiant ignores spawn conditions; Twilight ignores light, pointless once conditions are ignored. Solitude runs with nobody near, Stupor spawns mobs without AI, Control waits for redstone.",
    "",
    "The farm, finished."
  ],
  "quest.1D36BEF7A5EA2A67.title": "No AI, no lag",
  "quest.1D36BEF7A5EA2A67.quest_desc": [
    "For any big farm, add Stupor: mobs without AI float in place doing nothing, which cuts server load a lot and makes them easy to handle; they can still be pushed. Add Control to switch it all off with a lever.",
    "",
    "The politest mobs in the pack."
  ],
  "quest.4A3E617E34F69B7F.title": "No runes here",
  "quest.4A3E617E34F69B7F.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis 8.7 swapped Apothic Spawners' modifiers for spawner and tier-upgrade runes. The pack removes them all and puts the full modifier set on its copper augments: one route. Spawner chains still drop but craft nothing."
  ],
  "quest.7DFEB61C03844351.title": "Capturing and spawn eggs",
  "quest.7DFEB61C03844351.quest_desc": [
    "A spawn egg changes a spawner's mob. Capturing, a sword enchantment, gives a 0.5% chance per level for the mob to drop its egg (the book says 0.4%; the pack's config sets 0.5%). EvilCraft's Spirit Reanimator also makes eggs, for a lot of blood."
  ],
  "quest.482C3406948169E0.title": "Where spawners hide",
  "quest.482C3406948169E0.quest_desc": [
    "Vanilla dungeons, mineshafts and fortresses have them; Apotheosis adds Rogue Spawners in caves, each with a chest hidden below. Since none can be moved, scout a few before sinking augments into one."
  ],
  "quest.161AAF92BC2C0056.title": "A tuned spawner",
  "quest.161AAF92BC2C0056.quest_desc": [
    "Sixteen mobs every second, no AI, no noise, maximum Echoing and a lever to stop it all: a machine built over three acts. Fabric for speed, crystal for numbers, sands for the finishing touches.",
    "",
    "The dungeon works for you now."
  ],
  "chapter.5EEA4B45009E12E6.title": "Explore without getting lost",
  "chapter.5EEA4B45009E12E6.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Compass, Atlas, maps, locators and waystones: which one to reach for."
  ],
  "quest.2B106DDD74F05ABD.title": "Always know the next step",
  "quest.2B106DDD74F05ABD.quest_desc": [
    "Three layers keep you oriented: the Heliodor Compass says where the story goes next, the Living Atlas says what to deliver, and maps, locators and waystones get you there and back.",
    "",
    "The story never asks you to walk thousands of blocks or fly a jetpack."
  ],
  "quest.3963A066C717E409.title": "The Heliodor Compass",
  "quest.3963A066C717E409.quest_desc": [
    "Take it from the pedestal in your start ruin, one per player and world, and carry it a moment to attune it. It points to whatever the story needs next and turns on its own when your team gets there.",
    "",
    "Colors, states and route: The Heliodor Compass chapter."
  ],
  "quest.561896BFDF3BEFF6.title": "Reading the needle",
  "quest.561896BFDF3BEFF6.quest_desc": [
    "The needle's color names the target's world. Grey means there is nothing to point at: nothing within 1,500 blocks, a goal from a later act, or nothing left. Hover it and the tooltip spells out the state.",
    "",
    "The full legend is in The Heliodor Compass chapter."
  ],
  "quest.28F6CDF826378F45.title": "The compass follows the team",
  "quest.28F6CDF826378F45.quest_desc": [
    "It works per FTB team: everyone sees the same objective, and whatever any member completes counts for all. Places found by any team are remembered by the world.",
    "",
    "More in The Heliodor Compass chapter."
  ],
  "quest.2DF6858601AF0E06.title": "Do not lose it",
  "quest.2DF6858601AF0E06.quest_desc": [
    "The pedestal gives one compass per player and no recipe makes another. A Soulbound rune from Tombstone's Book of Soulbound keeps it on you when you die.",
    "",
    "Or leave it at home once you know the way. It will not sulk."
  ],
  "quest.7BF4FFF84427DFBB.title": "The Living Atlas",
  "quest.7BF4FFF84427DFBB.quest_desc": [
    "A book and a copper ingot. It takes each act's deliveries, keeps the lore fragments and the compass page, and never delivers anything by accident: delivering is always a button.",
    "",
    "How it works: The Living Atlas chapter."
  ],
  "quest.1F9F7B401D29563A.title": "The Survey Station",
  "quest.1F9F7B401D29563A.quest_desc": [
    "A movable bookmark: use a plain compass on it and the compass points to the station, like a lodestone; with an empty hand it opens the Atlas.",
    "",
    "Put one at your base and carry the bound compass on expeditions: an arrow home that does not need a map."
  ],
  "quest.3015B662CC892ACD.title": "Your map: JourneyMap",
  "quest.3015B662CC892ACD.quest_desc": [
    "It remembers everything you have seen and marks where you die; &eJ&r opens the full map and &eM&r drops a waypoint where you stand. Mark every ruin and portal you want to find again.",
    "",
    "Views, keys and death points: the Travel chapter."
  ],
  "quest.09CC6C35446FD380.title": "Waystones as anchors",
  "quest.09CC6C35446FD380.quest_desc": [
    "Every waystone you activate becomes a destination and, by default, a JourneyMap waypoint. Plant one next to everything that matters: your base, each Heliodor ruin, each portal.",
    "",
    "Costs, scrolls and building your own: the Travel chapter."
  ],
  "quest.0B70E5F10FB1C6D9.title": "Explorer's Compass",
  "quest.0B70E5F10FB1C6D9.quest_desc": [
    "A compass ringed by cobwebs and cracked stone bricks. Right-click to pick any structure, vanilla or modded; it finds the nearest, points at it and shows the distance.",
    "",
    "Made for side trips. The story never needs it."
  ],
  "quest.1595C7F7FF1FE7A5.title": "Nature's Compass",
  "quest.1595C7F7FF1FE7A5.quest_desc": [
    "A compass ringed by saplings and logs finds the nearest biome you choose, with its climate: a Solsticio native's biome, a mushroom island, the Aether's cloud biomes.",
    "",
    "Both locator compasses are repaired by crafting them with a plain compass."
  ],
  "quest.5D02424D936F2EF9.title": "Maps that lead somewhere",
  "quest.5D02424D936F2EF9.quest_desc": [
    "Cartographers sell ocean, woodland and trial maps (ocean maps also find YUNG's monuments), Repurposed Structures adds maps to some trades, Dungeons and Taverns taverns sell maps to their dungeons, and the Twilight Forest has magic, maze and ore maps.",
    "",
    "The maps you fill yourself look great framed on a wall."
  ],
  "quest.52E2B71D1CE5C3B2.title": "The Ark's chart room",
  "quest.52E2B71D1CE5C3B2.quest_desc": [
    "From act V, the Ark's Exploration Module merges maps: hold a filled map, use the module, and it absorbs the explored detail of your other maps of the same area, even one already framed on a wall. Nothing is consumed.",
    "",
    "Five field maps in, one overview out."
  ],
  "quest.7766CF40B9EB3115.title": "Special locators",
  "quest.7766CF40B9EB3115.quest_desc": [
    "Eyes of Ender find the stronghold (YUNG's version), Cataclysm's eyes one boss arena each, and Eternal Starlight's Seeking Eyes aim with a locator item in the other hand. Twilight magic maps chart the forest, the recovery compass points to your last death, and a lodestone or a Survey Station anchors any compass."
  ],
  "quest.0C32CBED1669E8DF.title": "Solsticio's cartographer",
  "quest.0C32CBED1669E8DF.quest_desc": [
    "In act VI, Rumbo sells survey maps that chart the nearest monument, trial chamber, jungle temple, swamp hut, buried treasure, mansion or ancient city under the Overworld sky, plus locator compasses, a spyglass and a lodestone.",
    "",
    "Memoria, the curator, sells Heliodor lore books and every pottery sherd."
  ],
  "quest.383C1B79AE356FE3.title": "A routine that never fails",
  "quest.383C1B79AE356FE3.quest_desc": [
    "Before each trip: check the compass and the Atlas, mark your base waystone, pack a Return Scroll, a bound compass and a sleeping bag. On arrival, place a waystone and a waypoint. If you die, follow the Death waypoint to your grave.",
    "",
    "Boring? Yes. Dying far from home is worse."
  ],
  "quest.47008CA35EB7072E.title": "Map, compass, way home",
  "quest.47008CA35EB7072E.quest_desc": [
    "A compass for the story, an Atlas for the why, a map for the where and a waystone for the way back.",
    "",
    "Heliodor lost its way once. You do not have to."
  ],
  "chapter.6701A0A9BE8B444F.title": "The Otherside and the mining worlds",
  "chapter.6701A0A9BE8B444F.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Deeper and Darker's sculk dimension below the ancient cities, and JAMD's disposable mining dimensions."
  ],
  "quest.1D8476E08D24EE0A.title": "Worlds below",
  "quest.1D8476E08D24EE0A.quest_desc": [
    "Two more dimensions live under your feet: the Otherside, Deeper and Darker's dark sculk world beyond the ancient cities, with the Warden's best gear; and JAMD's flat, ore-rich mining worlds, opened with act components, so you can dig without scarring home.",
    "",
    "Neither is part of the story. Both make the rest easier."
  ],
  "quest.268BE62D8492E76E.title": "A Metropolis of Restless Souls",
  "quest.268BE62D8492E76E.quest_desc": [
    "Find an ancient city in the Deep Dark. Sculk sensors and shriekers call the Warden: sneak, avoid stepping on sculk, and muffle your steps with wool.",
    "",
    "Deeper and Darker adds Warden Carapaces and the Warden upgrade template to their loot. Worth the whispering."
  ],
  "quest.766213489C04EA8E.title": "The Heart of the Deep",
  "quest.766213489C04EA8E.quest_desc": [
    "Slay the Warden and take its heart (Phantom Thief): with Deeper and Darker it drops a Heart of the Deep and Warden Carapaces. It is the hardest vanilla creature, so bring a plan (ranged damage, strong armor, potions) or come back later.",
    "",
    "The heart opens the way to the Otherside."
  ],
  "quest.064BBB48B3503996.title": "Below the Bedrock",
  "quest.064BBB48B3503996.quest_desc": [
    "Use the Heart of the Deep on an ancient city's portal frame to open the way to the Otherside: dark, hostile and full of sculk creatures. Bring light, food and a way back.",
    "",
    "Exploring every Otherside biome is Echolocation; killing one of each sculk monster, Sculk Slayer."
  ],
  "quest.0139E5BED18C0C11.title": "Abyssal Descent",
  "quest.0139E5BED18C0C11.quest_desc": [
    "Ancient temples hide deep in the Otherside with its rarest loot, including the Sonorous Staff (Noise Complaint), which fires sonic blasts like the Warden's; Reverberation and Volume enchantments improve it.",
    "",
    "Finally, a weapon that is also a noise complaint."
  ],
  "quest.0C808CA553F23E84.title": "Cover Me with Sculk",
  "quest.0C808CA553F23E84.quest_desc": [
    "Two upgrade paths: Resonarium plates turn iron gear into Resonarium, and Reinforced Echo Shards (Sculk Engineer) plus the Warden template turn netherite gear into Warden gear. A full Warden set earns Cover Me with Sculk.",
    "",
    "Sculk Smite adds damage against sculk mobs and the Warden."
  ],
  "quest.322768E7F9B343C6.title": "Sculk gadgets",
  "quest.322768E7F9B343C6.quest_desc": [
    "The Sculk Transmitter (Remote Storage) links to a container and opens it from far away. Soul Elytra have a boost on a cooldown.",
    "",
    "Their keys moved here to &eAlt+B&r (boost) and &eAlt+N&r (transmitter), off the backpack and Ultimine keys."
  ],
  "quest.706A01ED65FEE247.title": "A mining portal (act II)",
  "quest.706A01ED65FEE247.quest_desc": [
    "JAMD's Mining Portal leads to a separate mining dimension, so your home world stays intact. Here it takes seven obsidian, a diamond pickaxe and a Calibration Frame, the act II component.",
    "",
    "Place it, step in, and come back through the portal on the other side."
  ],
  "quest.5C93958CD8D9B795.title": "To Infinity and Underground",
  "quest.5C93958CD8D9B795.quest_desc": [
    "Enter the Mining dimension and dig freely: it exists to be dug up. Bring torches, and mark your portal on JourneyMap before wandering off.",
    "",
    "Its ores feed your processing lines, and Ultimine and the pack's mining gadgets are right at home here."
  ],
  "quest.39444A8C452B5290.title": "Nether and End portals (act IV)",
  "quest.39444A8C452B5290.quest_desc": [
    "The Nether Mining Portal takes seven Nether bricks, a netherite pickaxe and a Containment Seal; the End one seven End stone, a diamond pickaxe and a Horizon Chart, both act IV components.",
    "",
    "Nether and End blocks and ores, minus the parts of those dimensions that want you dead."
  ],
  "quest.290EE2DE0AFF78E4.title": "Nether Mining",
  "quest.290EE2DE0AFF78E4.quest_desc": [
    "Visit the Nether Mining dimension through its portal. Pack as you would for the real Nether: fire resistance and a way home.",
    "",
    "Safer than the original. Not safe."
  ],
  "quest.08D53AB973F79599.title": "How these fit in ENTRELUMEN",
  "quest.08D53AB973F79599.quest_desc": [
    "The Otherside is optional and native, with the Warden's heart as its key. JAMD portals are staged with act components (Calibration Frame in II, Containment Seal and Horizon Chart in IV); the rest of their recipes is the mod's own.",
    "",
    "The Undergarden, the other underground dimension, has its own chapter."
  ],
  "quest.5F16E45ACDCAF7F7.title": "End Mining",
  "quest.5F16E45ACDCAF7F7.quest_desc": [
    "End stone and End materials without endermen breathing down your neck.",
    "",
    "A good stop before building an End base."
  ],
  "quest.0C70A64FFF7EB727.title": "Echoes to spare",
  "quest.0C70A64FFF7EB727.quest_desc": [
    "Echo shards from ancient cities become Reinforced Echo Shards, the core of Warden gear.",
    "",
    "They are also a luxury trade: Solsticio's rarities dealer sells them from act III."
  ],
  "quest.0A744E5120330A73.title": "Deeper than deep",
  "quest.0A744E5120330A73.quest_desc": [
    "You stole the Warden's heart, crossed below the bedrock and opened portals to worlds made for digging.",
    "",
    "The deep is no longer a place to fear. Only a place to mine."
  ],
  "chapter.6EDF48A8FC48C541.title": "Weapons and armor by act",
  "chapter.6EDF48A8FC48C541.chapter_subtitle": [
    "What to wear and wield in each act, and where it comes from."
  ],
  "quest.068B39AFC641D9DE.title": "Gear follows the story",
  "quest.068B39AFC641D9DE.quest_desc": [
    "For each act, the gear worth having and where it drops. The world gets tougher as the story advances, and the best set in the pack, Luminous, only appears in act VI.",
    "",
    "None of it is mandatory. Dress for your own style."
  ],
  "quest.3FDA107F53BB433C.title": "The story sets the difficulty",
  "quest.3FDA107F53BB433C.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis World Tiers rise when your team completes an act and never drop: Haven for acts I and II, then Frontier, Ascent, Summit and Pinnacle. Higher tiers mean tougher monsters and better loot.",
    "",
    "The whole ladder, invaders included: the World Tiers chapter."
  ],
  "quest.23CAAA5BB61ABC15.title": "Affix loot: colors and salvage",
  "quest.23CAAA5BB61ABC15.quest_desc": [
    "Apotheosis gear drops with a rarity color, Common to Mythic, and random affixes; hover to read them. Break what you will not wear at a &eSalvaging Table&r for rarity materials, which upgrade gems at the Gem Cutting Table and pay the Augmenting Table.",
    "",
    "Smithing keeps affixes: an Epic diamond sword stays Epic as netherite, and as Luminous."
  ],
  "quest.6D553D7AA84D7933.title": "Test your damage",
  "quest.6D553D7AA84D7933.quest_desc": [
    "Before a boss, compare weapons on a &eTarget Dummy&r: it shows each hit's damage and never dies. Equipment Compare sets what you hold beside what you wear, Overloaded Armor Bar keeps armor above 20 readable, and AttributeFix lifts the vanilla armor cap.",
    "",
    "The dummy does not judge. Much."
  ],
  "quest.7B66E584AE08E8C5.title": "Act I: iron and a shield",
  "quest.7B66E584AE08E8C5.quest_desc": [
    "A full iron set, a shield (it stops creeper blasts and arrows) and a bow. Watch for the camouflaged biome creepers and wildlife that bites; dungeon loot can already beat crafted iron.",
    "",
    "The tier is Haven: no invaders yet. Enjoy it while it lasts."
  ],
  "quest.5DCF5003DE90D8A8.title": "Act II: diamond and a big axe",
  "quest.5DCF5003DE90D8A8.quest_desc": [
    "Enchanted diamond gear, from the table or Apotheosis shelves, carries you through act II. The best early prize is optional: Mowzie's Ferrous Wroughtnaut guards the Axe of a Thousand Metals and the Wrought Helm, both unbreakable.",
    "",
    "He is slow. He is not gentle."
  ],
  "quest.77D4B4D620982CB6.title": "Act III: Twilight and Undergarden",
  "quest.77D4B4D620982CB6.quest_desc": [
    "Two armories open.\n- Twilight: Naga armor, Ironwood, Steeleaf, Knightmetal (bonus against armor), Fiery gear (auto-smelting pickaxe, burning armor) and Phantom armor, never lost on death.\n- Undergarden: Cloggrum, then Froststeel (slows), Utherium (1.5× against Rotspawn) and Forgotten tools.",
    "",
    "The tier rises to Frontier, and invaders appear."
  ],
  "quest.224722532A1DBC7C.title": "Netherite: the base of it all",
  "quest.224722532A1DBC7C.quest_desc": [
    "Ancient debris, netherite scrap and an upgrade template from a bastion turn diamond into netherite. Keep those pieces: Cataclysm's Ignitium and Cursium upgrades and ENTRELUMEN's Luminous gear are all smithed on top of netherite.",
    "",
    "In Solsticio, the smith sells the upgrade template from act IV on."
  ],
  "quest.66BCFEB62531D362.title": "Act IV: sky gear and boss loot",
  "quest.66BCFEB62531D362.quest_desc": [
    "- Aether: Gravitite (high jump, no fall damage), Valkyrie (short flight), Phoenix and Obsidian armor; Deep Aether adds Skyjade and Stratus.\n- Cataclysm: Ignitium (from Ignis) and Cursium (from Maledictus) upgrade netherite, plus unique weapons.\n- Eternal Starlight: Unrealium and boss weapons.",
    "",
    "Aether set bonuses need the matching gloves. The tier rises to Ascent."
  ],
  "quest.646ACD59C4D7C3BE.title": "Act V: space suits",
  "quest.646ACD59C4D7C3BE.quest_desc": [
    "Venus and Mercury need Ad Astra's Netherite Space Suit (fire resistance, oxygen), and the Jet Suit adds flight. Tech mods bring their own top armor, like the MekaSuit and Modern Industrialization's quantum suit.",
    "",
    "The tier rises to Summit, where Mythic loot appears: salvaging it is the only source of the Godforged Pearl."
  ],
  "quest.31F1025C6342BEC4.title": "Act VI: Luminous gear",
  "quest.31F1025C6342BEC4.quest_desc": [
    "The best set in the pack: netherite pieces upgraded with a Luminous Ingot and a nether star. It never breaks, repairs itself in light, and the full set flies.",
    "",
    "Recipe, stats and tricks: the Luminosities and Luminous Gear chapter."
  ],
  "quest.5B6C3F10776C0B4F.title": "Ranged options along the way",
  "quest.5B6C3F10776C0B4F.quest_desc": [
    "A well-enchanted bow ages well, and each dimension adds its own: the Aether's dart shooters (darts ignore gravity) and Phoenix Bow, Twilight's Triple and Seeker bows from the Snow Queen, the Undergarden Slingshot, Cataclysm's Cursed Bow and Astrape, Eternal Starlight's crystal crossbow and Moonring Bow, and Mowzie's blowgun with poison darts."
  ],
  "quest.1420E6D2867191CA.title": "Staying alive",
  "quest.1420E6D2867191CA.quest_desc": [
    "Run-savers: the Totem of Undying (evokers), Friends and Foes' Totems of Freezing and Illusion (below half health), Twilight's Charms of Life and Keeping, the Cursium chestplate (one revive), Aether Life Shards (up to 10 extra hearts) and, in this pack, buffs for varied food and leftover saturation.",
    "",
    "Dying is optional. Mostly."
  ],
  "quest.5361C7F7A2A980B5.title": "Keep your look",
  "quest.5361C7F7A2A980B5.quest_desc": [
    "Cosmetic Armor Reworked adds cosmetic slots: wear the protection you need and show the armor you like. Armor trims work on any armor with the vanilla tags, and Solsticio's smith sells all eighteen templates.",
    "",
    "Saving the world is no excuse to dress badly."
  ],
  "quest.37575A687460FCA9.title": "Dressed in light",
  "quest.37575A687460FCA9.quest_desc": [
    "From iron to Luminous, every dimension left something on your belt.",
    "",
    "The last set is not about numbers: it is Heliodor's light, forged with respect this time."
  ],
  "chapter.6CB674C10F6F716D.title": "Accessories and artifacts",
  "chapter.6CB674C10F6F716D.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Curios slots, the Artifacts you find while exploring and the Aether's own accessory menu."
  ],
  "quest.44730CF39368B534.title": "Extra slots, extra powers",
  "quest.44730CF39368B534.quest_desc": [
    "Most mods hang accessories on Curios slots (head, necklace, belt, hands, feet, back and more), the Aether keeps its own menu, and Eternal Starlight's are fused into your gear. The richest source is the Artifacts mod: uncraftable trinkets found while exploring.",
    "",
    "Armor keeps you alive; trinkets make it interesting."
  ],
  "quest.56867C76555F0B5F.title": "Open the Curios inventory",
  "quest.56867C76555F0B5F.quest_desc": [
    "&eG&r, or the Curios button in your inventory, opens the slots. Each slot can hide its item visually, and Artifacts adds cosmetic slots to show one trinket while wearing another.",
    "",
    "If something does not fit, it belongs to another slot: hover the slot to read its name."
  ],
  "quest.6AFD3B81196BB353.title": "Find an Artifact",
  "quest.6AFD3B81196BB353.quest_desc": [
    "Artifacts are never crafted. They hide in the loot of mineshafts, dungeons, temples, strongholds, fortresses, bastions, End and ancient cities, shipwrecks, buried treasure, outposts, igloos, ruined portals and village chests, plus suspicious sand and gravel; YUNG's rebuilt structures count too.",
    "",
    "Your first one earns Amateur Archaeologist."
  ],
  "quest.6C0D53F0E5B344E2.title": "Campsites and Mimics",
  "quest.6C0D53F0E5B344E2.quest_desc": [
    "Artifacts adds small underground campsites with supply barrels and a tool chest. Some of those chests are Mimics that jump and bite when opened; kill one for Chest Slayer, since every Mimic drops an artifact. Lootr keeps structure loot per player, so each teammate rolls their own.",
    "",
    "If the chest has teeth, it has loot."
  ],
  "quest.10DCD6E41BA4EB13.title": "Artifacts for moving",
  "quest.10DCD6E41BA4EB13.quest_desc": [
    "Cloud in a Bottle double-jumps, Bunny Hoppers jump higher and land softer, Running Shoes sprint faster and step higher, Aqua-Dashers run across fluids, Flippers swim much faster, Snowshoes walk on powder snow, Steadfast Spikes shrug off knockback and ice, and the Helium Flamingo \"swims\" through the air for a while."
  ],
  "quest.5D491DCB10C0BB73.title": "Artifacts for mining and looting",
  "quest.5D491DCB10C0BB73.quest_desc": [
    "Digging Claws mine faster and at a higher base tier, even bare-handed; the Pickaxe Heater smelts ores as you mine; the Lucky Scarf adds Fortune and the Superstitious Hat Looting; the Universal Attractor pulls nearby items; Night Vision Goggles see in the dark; the Onion Ring gives Haste after eating; the Golden Hook adds creature experience."
  ],
  "quest.6AC851742C49051F.title": "Artifacts for fighting",
  "quest.6AC851742C49051F.quest_desc": [
    "The Power Glove adds damage, Feral Claws attack speed and the Pocket Piston knockback. The Vampiric Glove heals on melee hits, the Fire Gauntlet burns and the Withered Bracelet may inflict Wither. The Crystal Heart adds max health, the Cross Necklace longer invincibility, the Panic Necklace speed when hurt, and Thorn, Flame and Shock Pendants hit back."
  ],
  "quest.75F48F47F46DCE94.title": "Artifacts that save you",
  "quest.75F48F47F46DCE94.quest_desc": [
    "The Chorus Totem may teleport you away from a fatal hit (with a cooldown), the Obsidian Skull grants fire resistance after a burn, Strider Shoes ignore hot floors, the Antidote Vessel shortens bad effects, the Snorkel and the Charm of Sinking handle water, Kitty Slippers keep creepers and phantoms away, and the Umbrella slows falls and blocks like a shield."
  ],
  "quest.0DF1D75734FC4CE0.title": "Everyday artifacts",
  "quest.0DF1D75734FC4CE0.quest_desc": [
    "Villager Hat: better trades, handy before Solsticio. Angler's Hat: more Luck of the Sea and Lure. Cowboy Hat: faster mounts. Drinking hats: eat and drink faster. Rooted Boots: hunger refills on grass. Warp Drive: ender pearls cost hunger instead of pearls. Charm of Shrinking: go tiny. Scarf of Invisibility: go unseen."
  ],
  "quest.0CF6BCA100209E87.title": "Adventurous Eater",
  "quest.0CF6BCA100209E87.quest_desc": [
    "The Everlasting Beef and the Eternal Steak are food that never runs out, each with a cooldown. Eat one for Adventurous Eater.",
    "",
    "This pack rewards variety: an endless steak is a safety net, not a diet."
  ],
  "quest.1F729E92C66954CF.title": "Toggles and keys",
  "quest.1F729E92C66954CF.quest_desc": [
    "The Universal Attractor, Night Vision Goggles, Scarf of Invisibility, Charms of Shrinking and Sinking and the Helium Flamingo's flight can be switched on and off; their keys are in Controls, under Artifacts.",
    "",
    "Turn the attractor off at home, unless you enjoy collecting every dropped seed."
  ],
  "quest.6ED869120880E115.title": "The Aether accessory menu",
  "quest.6ED869120880E115.quest_desc": [
    "The Aether has its own screen (&eI&r, or its inventory button) for rings, a pendant, gloves, a cape, a shield and more. Highlights: Zanite rings and pendants (faster mining for a while) and Ice ones (walk on water and lava), the Regeneration Stone, the Iron Bubble, the Invisibility Cloak, and Deep Aether's Cloud Cape (double jump) and Aercloud Necklace."
  ],
  "quest.4E0B57BF283905C8.title": "Terra's Arm",
  "quest.4E0B57BF283905C8.quest_desc": [
    "ENTRELUMEN's own accessory: Terra's cyborg arm, worn in a Curios hands slot for extra block reach. The Atlas gives it when act II closes, and the sunken workshop ruin keeps one in a chest.",
    "",
    "Everything else: the Terra's Arm chapter."
  ],
  "quest.434AD099488E169B.title": "Starlight goes inside your gear",
  "quest.434AD099488E169B.quest_desc": [
    "Eternal Starlight's accessories are not worn: each one combines into a specific kind of equipment, like items into a bundle, and the gear gains its effect. How many fit depends on the gear's accessory slots.",
    "",
    "The Glimmering Tablet says how to get each one."
  ],
  "quest.0A8B8F620E1A4BED.title": "Accessories in this pack",
  "quest.0A8B8F620E1A4BED.quest_desc": [
    "Curios and the Aether's Accessories run side by side. Artifacts registers its slots and cosmetic slots in Curios, and Cataclysm, Occultism, Industrial Foregoing and Sophisticated Backpacks use Curios slots too (a backpack goes on your back).",
    "",
    "Iron's Gems and Jewelry makes rings and amulets at a jeweller's bench; it has its own chapter."
  ],
  "quest.68A75072CA987105.title": "A full set of trinkets",
  "quest.68A75072CA987105.quest_desc": [
    "Every slot filled with something that suits you: a jump, a heal, a magnet, a lucky scarf.",
    "",
    "That is how two players in the same armor end up playing completely different games."
  ],
  "chapter.7B3D8EAE5467125E.title": "Creatures of the world",
  "chapter.7B3D8EAE5467125E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Friends and Foes, Naturalist, Creeper Overhaul and Enderman Overhaul: who helps, who bites."
  ],
  "quest.1428DDF847B60627.title": "A livelier world",
  "quest.1428DDF847B60627.quest_desc": [
    "From the first night: Friends and Foes brings vanilla-style mobs and golems, Naturalist fills biomes with real-world wildlife, and Creeper Overhaul and Enderman Overhaul give creepers and endermen a variant per biome. None is gated.",
    "",
    "Some help, some bite, and a few do both depending on your manners."
  ],
  "quest.5B073D11A6FC1137.title": "A copper golem",
  "quest.5B073D11A6FC1137.quest_desc": [
    "A block of copper, a carved pumpkin and a lightning rod on top build a Copper Golem (Off you go); any oxidation stage works, waxed or not. It wanders looking for copper buttons and presses them.",
    "",
    "A small, living redstone clock. Heliodor would approve of the copper."
  ],
  "quest.57FA2F4D749C9AB2.title": "A Glare in the dark",
  "quest.57FA2F4D749C9AB2.quest_desc": [
    "Glares are small, grumpy moss creatures from lush caves. Tame one with glow berries (Grumpy and Cute) and it leads you to dark spots where monsters could spawn.",
    "",
    "A torch-placement consultant that works for berries."
  ],
  "quest.51525F2225F81724.title": "Crab claw: longer reach",
  "quest.51525F2225F81724.quest_desc": [
    "Beach crabs drop Crab Claws, which brew the Potion of Reaching: longer range for placing and breaking blocks, great for building.",
    "",
    "Moobloom cows grow buttercups on their backs; shear one for MooBoom!"
  ],
  "quest.473AD09B7CEAB75C.title": "Hide and seek with a Rascal",
  "quest.473AD09B7CEAB75C.quest_desc": [
    "Rascals are shy creatures hiding in mineshafts. Find one and it runs to hide again; find it three times (Hide and Seek) and it rewards you, sometimes with ores or a pickaxe.",
    "",
    "The most harmless thing in any mineshaft."
  ],
  "quest.2769E179BE1CCD4C.title": "The illager magicians",
  "quest.2769E179BE1CCD4C.quest_desc": [
    "The Iceologer throws ice from its cabin; the Illusioner, in shacks and training grounds, copies himself. Kill both plus an Evoker for The Magicians.",
    "",
    "Each drops a totem that triggers below half health: the Totem of Freezing and the Totem of Illusion."
  ],
  "quest.715470BADBA985D5.title": "The Wildfire",
  "quest.715470BADBA985D5.quest_desc": [
    "The Nether's Citadel (A fortress? No, a citadel!) is guarded by the Wildfire, a blaze-like boss, and its barrels hold diamond gear.",
    "",
    "The Wildfire drops Crown Fragments; enough of them make the Wildfire Crown (Who's da New King of Nether?)."
  ],
  "quest.58D1BA3AF7E9C073.title": "Friends and Foes, the rest",
  "quest.58D1BA3AF7E9C073.quest_desc": [
    "The Tuff Golem (tuff, wool, a carved pumpkin) holds an item for you. The Mauler is a biting ambush predator (It Bites). The Beekeeper is a villager profession, with beehives for every wood (Be Keeper). Zombie horse traps are the skeleton trap with zombie riders (Riders On The Storm)."
  ],
  "quest.11386129FAD7C940.title": "Naturalist: wildlife",
  "quest.11386129FAD7C940.quest_desc": [
    "Real-world animals in fitting biomes: bears, deer, boars, lions, zebras, giraffes, elephants, rhinos, hippos, alligators, komodo dragons, snakes, scorpions, sharks, whales, birds, butterflies, fireflies and more.",
    "",
    "Honeycomb for a Bear, melon for a Hippo, a map read on a Giraffe: three advancements."
  ],
  "quest.25F90752659FC778.title": "The Capture Net",
  "quest.25F90752659FC778.quest_desc": [
    "Bamboo and string. It catches small creatures (butterflies, caterpillars, snails and the like) as items to release elsewhere: decorate, breed, fill a greenhouse.",
    "",
    "Fish and small water creatures still go in buckets."
  ],
  "quest.5E9E708CBED4A95A.title": "What wildlife gives",
  "quest.5E9E708CBED4A95A.quest_desc": [
    "Hide smelts into leather and makes a Knapsack; Glow Goop, from glow berries, turns arrows spectral; duck eggs work in cakes and pumpkin pie; and new meats and fish cook the usual way. Naturalist also brews Antivenom and Forest Dasher potions: EMI shows how.",
    "",
    "More variety for a pack that rewards eating well."
  ],
  "quest.66132E311AD3BBD4.title": "Wildlife that bites back",
  "quest.66132E311AD3BBD4.quest_desc": [
    "Early on, respect alligators in swamps and rivers, sharks and piranhas in water, desert and jungle scorpions, snakes, and big cats like lions and tigers. Rhinos charge and break some blocks.",
    "",
    "Keep your distance from anything large until you have armor. Especially the rhino."
  ],
  "quest.3F178A29219B7BE0.title": "Creepers in camouflage",
  "quest.3F178A29219B7BE0.quest_desc": [
    "Creeper Overhaul gives most biomes their own creeper, textured to blend in: jungle, bamboo, desert, badlands, hills, savanna, mushroom, swamp, dripstone, cave, dark oak, spruce, beach, snowy, ocean and birch.",
    "",
    "The hiss is your best warning. In caves and forests, listen before you look."
  ],
  "quest.56E3082B5DAADD68.title": "Endermen for every biome",
  "quest.56E3082B5DAADD68.quest_desc": [
    "Enderman Overhaul adds an enderman for badlands, caves, coral, crimson, dark oak, desert, End, End islands, flower fields, ice spikes, mushroom, Nether wastes, savanna, snow, soul sand valley, swamp, warped and windswept hills. Some hit harder than vanilla; cave ones can drop ores and emeralds.",
    "",
    "Their drops are worth the hunt."
  ],
  "quest.46128FFEEEFDAAD4.title": "A hood against stares",
  "quest.46128FFEEEFDAAD4.quest_desc": [
    "Badlands, savanna and snowy endermen can drop hoods. Wear one and you can look endermen in the eye without angering them.",
    "",
    "A carved pumpkin, minus the pumpkin on your face."
  ],
  "quest.3252F91E012FD964.title": "Special pearls",
  "quest.3252F91E012FD964.quest_desc": [
    "Each biome enderman drops its own pearl: Bubble (coral) flies straight, Icy (ice spikes, snow) freezes, Crimson and Warped grant Strength II and Resistance II on teleport, Soul (soul sand valley) moves a bound creature, Summoner (swamp, windswept hills) teleports nearby targets, Corrupted (End) sends targets anywhere and Ancient (End islands) summons an allied enderman."
  ],
  "quest.6B546E821D9A722C.title": "Corrupted gear",
  "quest.6B546E821D9A722C.quest_desc": [
    "End endermen drop Corrupted Pearls and Enderman Teeth. Two teeth on a stick make the Corrupted Blade, which teleports what it hits; the Corrupted Shield teleports whoever hits you.",
    "",
    "Any special pearl crafts back into a plain ender pearl if you need one."
  ],
  "quest.3267C60676392C44.title": "How these fit in ENTRELUMEN",
  "quest.3267C60676392C44.quest_desc": [
    "All four mods are native, with no recipe changes, and live in the world from act I. Their meats, fish and berries add food variety, which the pack rewards. Carry On can lift some animals but never bosses or protected entities, and Friends and Foes structures keep per-player loot through Lootr."
  ],
  "quest.65D3528A8F5F856A.title": "Naturalist's notebook",
  "quest.65D3528A8F5F856A.quest_desc": [
    "Working golems, a Glare that finds dark corners, a crab claw for reach, totems from illager magicians, a hood against endermen and a pocketful of odd pearls.",
    "",
    "The living world is on your side now. Mostly."
  ],
  "chapter.66656B710E644D7B.title": "Death without stress: Tombstone",
  "chapter.66656B710E644D7B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "What happens when you die, how to get your things back and how to die less."
  ],
  "quest.5B2E78124626820D.title": "Death is a detour",
  "quest.5B2E78124626820D.quest_desc": [
    "Tombstone is the pack's only death-recovery mod, on purpose. When you die, your items go into a grave on the spot and you respawn with a Grave Key and a brief Ghostly Shape that keeps creatures off you. With default settings, nothing is lost.",
    "",
    "A grave with your things, no stress. Death here is paperwork."
  ],
  "quest.00B31EEBD396DE86.title": "The Grave Key",
  "quest.00B31EEBD396DE86.quest_desc": [
    "In the same dimension, the key shows your grave from a distance. Walk back and right-click the grave, or sneak over it, to get everything back.",
    "",
    "Items lying a few blocks from your death go into the grave too, and dying again before you recover it adds to the same grave instead of making another."
  ],
  "quest.313E939E0182E31D.title": "Find it on the map",
  "quest.313E939E0182E31D.quest_desc": [
    "JourneyMap drops a Death waypoint where you fall: follow its beam, and let a Return Scroll or a nearby waystone save most of the walk.",
    "",
    "In the Aether, falling off an island drops you into the Overworld instead of killing you; your grave, if any, stays where you actually died."
  ],
  "quest.3882431F9809F0FC.title": "A key that teleports",
  "quest.3882431F9809F0FC.quest_desc": [
    "An enchanted Grave Key lets you hold right-click to teleport straight to your grave. Enchant it by crafting it with an ender pearl, or with a soul haunting a decorative grave; sometimes it comes enchanted already.",
    "",
    "The trip caps Ghostly Shape at 10 seconds, so land ready to fight."
  ],
  "quest.104A12BF2CCE58CC.title": "Grave Dust",
  "quest.104A12BF2CCE58CC.quest_desc": [
    "Undead drop it, and cats sometimes bring it as a morning gift. It is the base of almost everything Tombstone crafts: marble, decorative graves, scrolls, tablets, books and the Ankh.",
    "",
    "Keep a stack. Your cat is doing its best."
  ],
  "quest.7C5F2A452A57289E.title": "Soulbound: keep it on death",
  "quest.7C5F2A452A57289E.quest_desc": [
    "A Book of Soulbound (book, diamond, lapis and grave dust) puts a Soulbound rune on a non-stackable item, which then stays in your inventory when you die. Use it on a soul-haunted decorative grave, book in the offhand and item in the main hand.",
    "",
    "Start with your pickaxe and your Heliodor Compass."
  ],
  "quest.30CFA1170E3DD6BA.title": "Decorative graves and souls",
  "quest.30CFA1170E3DD6BA.quest_desc": [
    "Marble (stone and grave dust, tinted with lapis, emerald, red sand or bone meal) crafts decorative graves. At night they smoke, and sometimes a soul haunts one: that soul powers Tombstone's magic.",
    "",
    "Do not overuse one grave: too much corruption makes it a Screaming Grave that throws bones and refuses rituals until it calms down. Relatable."
  ],
  "quest.691F4A212F9F9496.title": "Tablets: home and recall",
  "quest.691F4A212F9F9496.quest_desc": [
    "From a Strange Tablet (marble and grave dust) come travel tablets, charged on a soul-haunted grave: Home takes you to your respawn point, Recall to a memorized place, Assistance toward another player. Ancient versions bring nearby creatures along.",
    "",
    "Lost Tablets found in the world lead somewhere far away."
  ],
  "quest.34A8C9D3EA1C3B96.title": "Scrolls and books",
  "quest.34A8C9D3EA1C3B96.quest_desc": [
    "Strange Scrolls become magic scrolls with one extra ingredient: Knowledge (stores your experience, with a loss), Feather Fall, Aquatic Life, Frost and Lightning Resistance, Reach, True Sight, Preservation and more.",
    "",
    "Tombstone's books repair, disenchant, recycle or move enchantments. EMI has every recipe."
  ],
  "quest.766C9D99AAF5C9E3.title": "The Ankh of Prayer",
  "quest.766C9D99AAF5C9E3.quest_desc": [
    "The Ankh (gold, a stick and grave dust) lets you pray at decorative graves, with a cooldown, for Knowledge of Death. Knowledge buys perks: Memento Mori cuts experience lost on death by 20% per level, up to 100%, and Jailer raises the chance of a pre-enchanted Grave Key by 20% per level.",
    "",
    "Pray a little. Die a lot less."
  ],
  "quest.133E7F3115F3B234.title": "Other ways to keep your things",
  "quest.133E7F3115F3B234.quest_desc": [
    "Twilight's Charms of Keeping save armor, hotbar or everything, and Phantom armor is never lost. Charms of Life, the Totem of Undying and Friends and Foes' totems stop the death itself, Cataclysm's Cursium chestplate revives you once, and Tombstone's Receptacle of Soul and Voodoo Poppet can prevent one too."
  ],
  "quest.69A50A20C65D42DD.title": "For the server owner",
  "quest.69A50A20C65D42DD.quest_desc": [
    "Operators have /tbshowlastgrave (where a player's last grave is), /tbteleport death (your last death spot) and /tbrecovery (save and restore player backups).",
    "",
    "The pack keeps Tombstone's defaults: no random item loss, graves fill up instead of multiplying, and a grave from player-versus-player death stays unlocked."
  ],
  "quest.20F71F03CB9DD338.title": "Knowledge of Death",
  "quest.20F71F03CB9DD338.quest_desc": [
    "A key that teleports, soulbound tools, tablets home and a few perks from the Ankh: death is now an inconvenience, not a disaster.",
    "",
    "Go take the risks the story asks for."
  ],
  "quest.4F8FE857899146D4.title": "A Voodoo Poppet",
  "quest.4F8FE857899146D4.quest_desc": [
    "Leather, string, a clay ball, a dead bush and grave dust. Enchant it on a soul-haunted grave and it saves you from your next death (Not Today, Grim Reaper); the Witch Doctor perk may let you keep it afterwards.",
    "",
    "One active poppet is cheap insurance before a boss."
  ],
  "quest.6175649F4EB8ECBF.title": "Bring your pet back",
  "quest.6175649F4EB8ECBF.quest_desc": [
    "A Receptacle of Familiar (iron, a ghast tear and an impregnated diamond) captures a pet's soul when it dies, with what it carried. Carry it while the soul slowly recovers on some of your vital essence, then use it on a soul-haunted grave to revive your familiar (Bound Forever).",
    "",
    "Nobody gets left behind. Not even the parrot."
  ],
  "chapter.71AA5DE361B1FD32.title": "Structures and loot",
  "chapter.71AA5DE361B1FD32.chapter_subtitle": [
    "What each structure mod adds, what is worth looting and why every player gets their own chest."
  ],
  "quest.745231331921FF54.title": "A world full of places",
  "quest.745231331921FF54.quest_desc": [
    "One answer per role: YUNG's mods replace vanilla dungeons, mineshafts, temples, witch huts, monuments, fortresses, strongholds and the End island instead of adding a second set, and Repurposed Structures, Dungeons and Taverns, Towns and Towers, Explorify and Hellish Trials fill in around them.",
    "",
    "Structures only appear in newly generated chunks."
  ],
  "quest.74D96402A467B05B.title": "Lootr: a chest for each player",
  "quest.74D96402A467B05B.quest_desc": [
    "Structure chests, barrels, shulkers, minecarts, item frames, decorated pots and even suspicious sand and gravel become Lootr containers: each player opens their own copy. Arriving second is never a waste.",
    "",
    "Breaking one takes sneaking and removes it for everyone. Your first one earns 'X' Marks the Spot."
  ],
  "quest.296E4C9B99FD4B9E.title": "Loot collector",
  "quest.296E4C9B99FD4B9E.quest_desc": [
    "Lootr counts what you open: 10, 25, 50 and 100 containers each earn an advancement, and there is a Centennial Trophy for the most dedicated. Brushing every kind of Lootr suspicious block is Brush It Off.",
    "",
    "Carry On cannot lift Lootr containers, spawners, trial spawners or vaults in this pack."
  ],
  "quest.3F33812A507EFF11.title": "YUNG's: dungeons, mines and huts",
  "quest.3F33812A507EFF11.quest_desc": [
    "Better Dungeons gives skeleton, spider and zombie dungeons real layouts; Better Mineshafts styles them by biome, a good early source of ore and rails; Better Witch Huts adds swamp and cave huts; YUNG's Extras scatters wells and ruins.",
    "",
    "They keep vanilla chest tables, so Artifacts and other mods still add their loot."
  ],
  "quest.6033524BE932FAA1.title": "YUNG's: temples with puzzles",
  "quest.6033524BE932FAA1.quest_desc": [
    "Better Desert Temples are puzzle temples that apply Mining Fatigue while you are inside, so digging around the rooms is not the answer. Better Jungle Temples are trapped and many-roomed.",
    "",
    "Bring a brush: desert structures and trail ruins hide suspicious sand, and the pack's archaeology viewer shows what each one can give."
  ],
  "quest.38DDCCC783CF1767.title": "YUNG's: the big ones",
  "quest.38DDCCC783CF1767.quest_desc": [
    "Better Ocean Monuments, Nether Fortresses, Strongholds and End Island rebuild the big vanilla structures under new IDs: locate them as betteroceanmonuments:ocean_monument, betterfortresses:fortress or betterstrongholds:stronghold. Eyes of Ender and ocean explorer maps still find them.",
    "",
    "The Heliodor Compass uses these same structures in acts III and V."
  ],
  "quest.29F5F44DF6356939.title": "Repurposed Structures",
  "quest.29F5F44DF6356939.quest_desc": [
    "Vanilla structures re-imagined for other biomes and dimensions: mansions in seven styles, biome mineshafts, outposts, pyramids, igloos, ruins, shipwrecks and witch huts, Nether and End strongholds, crimson, warped, mushroom and ocean villages, and ancient cities in the End, the Nether and the ocean.",
    "",
    "Each group has its own advancement."
  ],
  "quest.4D4B19A26212780C.title": "Repurposed: the unusual ones",
  "quest.4D4B19A26212780C.quest_desc": [
    "Some have no vanilla twin: the Jungle Fortress, the Underground Bastion, the Overworld City in the sky, the Nether City and the End-themed Ruined Portal. Dangerous and well stocked.",
    "",
    "Its villager maps say \"Locating... (Do not buy this map until finished)\" while they search. Believe them."
  ],
  "quest.77AC4F74AE0AED43.title": "Find a tavern",
  "quest.77AC4F74AE0AED43.quest_desc": [
    "Dungeons and Taverns builds taverns in many wood styles across the Overworld: a safe place to rest, trade and hear about adventures (Safe Haven), and its cartographer sells maps to the mod's dungeons.",
    "",
    "Two hidden DnT advancements do not load in 1.21.1 and are disabled, so the quest trader has one trade fewer than upstream."
  ],
  "quest.6CD7B0207C292C8D.title": "Dungeons and Taverns mini-bosses",
  "quest.6CD7B0207C292C8D.quest_desc": [
    "Several DnT structures hide a boss room behind keys found inside: the Lone Citadel (a frozen breeze), the Toxic Lair (the Spider Queen), the underwater Trident Trial Monument (an Ancient Guardian) and the End Castle (a haunting phantom). Beating each once is Dungeon Master.",
    "",
    "Shrines are combat trials in five tiers."
  ],
  "quest.324E7D8B1ED78009.title": "Illagers and witches",
  "quest.324E7D8B1ED78009.quest_desc": [
    "DnT adds a whole illager and witch network: manors, hideouts and camps, witch villas, swamp villages, the Badlands Miner Outpost and more; visiting them all is The Ill Manored.",
    "",
    "Its loot hides treasure-only enchantments: Traveler (faster sprint, step-up), Outreach (longer block reach), Photosynthesis (repairs in sunlight) and Illager's Bane."
  ],
  "quest.7949A648A9538C15.title": "Towns and Towers",
  "quest.7949A648A9538C15.quest_desc": [
    "Villages and pillager outposts get a style for almost every biome, plus rare exclusives (Iberian, Mediterranean, Nilotic, Rustic, Swedish and Tudor), a Piglin village and a wandering trader camp.",
    "",
    "More villages, more trades, more spots for a waystone."
  ],
  "quest.41C40BD2B08166F8.title": "Explorify: small stops",
  "quest.41C40BD2B08166F8.quest_desc": [
    "Small vanilla-style places everywhere: campsites, farmsteads, watchtowers, guide posts, supply caches for each forest type, desert shrines, a badlands pyramid, a mausoleum, dark forest settlements, mangrove huts, ruins and even an End shipwreck.",
    "",
    "Open the supply caches in your first days."
  ],
  "quest.7D9A441741BA22FB.title": "Hellish Trials",
  "quest.7D9A441741BA22FB.quest_desc": [
    "Trial chambers in the Nether, with trial spawners and vaults like the Overworld ones.",
    "",
    "Bring fire resistance and a way back. Especially the way back."
  ],
  "quest.283F099B40C6AFCA.title": "Trial chambers and vaults",
  "quest.283F099B40C6AFCA.quest_desc": [
    "Trial chambers are an act I stop: the compass leads you to one until your team reaches First Signal. Beat the trial spawners, collect trial keys and open the vaults (Under Lock and Key).",
    "",
    "Vaults, like Lootr containers, reward each player separately."
  ],
  "quest.7DB4E463C1F1E87E.title": "How to find them",
  "quest.7DB4E463C1F1E87E.quest_desc": [
    "From cheapest to most specific: explore (most are common near villages and rivers), the Explorer's Compass, villager and tavern maps, special locators (Cataclysm eyes, Eternal Starlight Seeking Eyes, Twilight magic maps) and, in act VI, Solsticio's cartographer.",
    "",
    "The tools themselves: the Explore Without Getting Lost chapter."
  ],
  "quest.1C01894D54875656.title": "Worldgen and performance",
  "quest.1C01894D54875656.quest_desc": [
    "Measured on a dedicated server, new Overworld chunks generate noticeably slower than vanilla, mostly because of the whole batch (ores, crops, fauna) rather than one structure mod. Existing chunks are unaffected.",
    "",
    "On a modest PC, explore at a steady pace instead of flying over new land at full speed, and let the world catch up."
  ],
  "quest.698FE5ED4BE18AB2.title": "Cartographer of ruins",
  "quest.698FE5ED4BE18AB2.quest_desc": [
    "Temples solved, fortresses cleared, taverns visited and a hundred Lootr chests opened.",
    "",
    "Somewhere among them Heliodor left its own ruins, and the compass knows which ones matter."
  ],
  "chapter.0D797BF58DA82A00.title": "Travel: waystones, maps and vehicles",
  "chapter.0D797BF58DA82A00.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Get anywhere and back: JourneyMap, the Waystones network, beds on the road and aircraft."
  ],
  "quest.5ED3EEFF545DFC0B.title": "Walking it twice is optional",
  "quest.5ED3EEFF545DFC0B.quest_desc": [
    "The toolkit: JourneyMap for maps and waypoints, Waystones for fast travel between places you have visited, Comforts for sleeping away from home and, from act III, aircraft and late-game teleports.",
    "",
    "The compass says where. This is about getting there, and back in time for dinner."
  ],
  "quest.14793195884A6FFF.title": "JourneyMap: open the map",
  "quest.14793195884A6FFF.quest_desc": [
    "It draws the world as you explore: a minimap in the corner and a full map on &eJ&r, with day, night, topography, biome and cave views; underground it switches to caves on its own.",
    "",
    "FTB Chunks' minimap is off so the two do not overlap; FTB Chunks stays for claims (&eK&r)."
  ],
  "quest.214D3B0E22D5020A.title": "Waypoints and death points",
  "quest.214D3B0E22D5020A.quest_desc": [
    "&eM&r makes a waypoint where you stand; &eB&r on the full map makes one at the cursor (both moved off the backpack key). Waypoints show a beam in the world and can be shared.",
    "",
    "A Death waypoint marks where you fell and leads straight back to your Tombstone grave."
  ],
  "quest.11D3557EB07DBDD1.title": "Find a waystone",
  "quest.11D3557EB07DBDD1.quest_desc": [
    "Waystones spawn in the wild, roughly every 25 chunks in the biome's style, and in some villages. Right-click one to activate it for yourself: from then on it is in your destination list and, by default, on your JourneyMap.",
    "",
    "A glowing stone in the middle of nowhere is always worth the detour."
  ],
  "quest.48B1F5AEFE7478C8.title": "A Warp Stone",
  "quest.48B1F5AEFE7478C8.quest_desc": [
    "An ender pearl, amethyst shards and an emerald. Hold right-click to open your list of activated waystones from anywhere; each use costs durability.",
    "",
    "It is also the heart of every waystone you build."
  ],
  "quest.3B12191E4646294F.title": "Your own waystone",
  "quest.3B12191E4646294F.quest_desc": [
    "Stone bricks, obsidian and a Warp Stone, in mossy, sandy, deepslate, blackstone, Nether, End, purpur, prismarine and mud brick styles. Put one at your base, at each camp and at every structure you will revisit.",
    "",
    "Only the owner can edit a placed waystone, and Carry On cannot move it."
  ],
  "quest.6AC8F125761802DA.title": "What a warp costs",
  "quest.6AC8F125761802DA.quest_desc": [
    "Warps cost experience: within a dimension the cost grows with distance, between dimensions it is flat and higher, capped either way. Warps to global waystones and from warp plates are free.",
    "",
    "Leashed animals come along; pets stay home. Keep some levels in reserve before a long trip."
  ],
  "quest.243D9C659D4F16E0.title": "Scrolls: one-way tickets",
  "quest.243D9C659D4F16E0.quest_desc": [
    "Single use: the &eReturn Scroll&r takes you to your nearest activated waystone, the &eWarp Scroll&r opens the destination list once, a &eBlank Scroll&r used on a waystone becomes a Bound Scroll to it (a gift for a friend who has never been there), and the &ePortal Scroll&r opens a temporary Warp Portal.",
    "",
    "Never leave home without a Return Scroll."
  ],
  "quest.51955BCEF229BF86.title": "Sharestones and warp plates",
  "quest.51955BCEF229BF86.quest_desc": [
    "Sharestones come in sixteen colors, each linking to every other of its color and shared by everyone: perfect for a team network. Warp Plates pair up with shards: step on one, appear on the other, for free.",
    "",
    "Portstones are waystones you can leave from but never arrive at. One-way doors."
  ],
  "quest.0BA11AB7D4F5E416.title": "Solsticio joins the network",
  "quest.0BA11AB7D4F5E416.quest_desc": [
    "When the Town Hall portal opens in act VI, a global Solsticio waystone appears there, so any waystone can reach the city.",
    "",
    "Until then, keep a waystone near your Ark: act V is the busiest act for travel."
  ],
  "quest.1176F66E03A9338E.title": "A bed for the road",
  "quest.1176F66E03A9338E.quest_desc": [
    "A &eSleeping Bag&r skips the night away from home without moving your respawn; crouch to place it. &eHammocks&r hang between two Rope and Nail blocks and let you sleep through the day.",
    "",
    "Your spawn stays at base while you camp at the edge of the map."
  ],
  "quest.39BDBAC06BA5F7D3.title": "Small travel fixes",
  "quest.39BDBAC06BA5F7D3.quest_desc": [
    "Jump Boat lets a boat hop onto the shore instead of getting stuck or breaking. Fireproof Boats adds crimson and warped boats that survive lava like their planks. Nether Portal Fix links return portals to the one you came from, so two bases never share a Nether exit by accident."
  ],
  "quest.487E9F0D517D781D.title": "Aircraft (act III)",
  "quest.487E9F0D517D781D.quest_desc": [
    "Immersive Aircraft builds airships, biplanes, quadrocopters and gyrodynes. Here the engine needs a Power Regulator and the gyrodyne a reinforced alloy, both act III; the rest is the mod's own, with no pack gates on fuel or repairs.",
    "",
    "Dismount moved to &eF12&r. Mind the landing."
  ],
  "quest.77A8A9F84C5EA7C9.title": "Late-game teleports",
  "quest.77A8A9F84C5EA7C9.quest_desc": [
    "Ender IO's Travel Anchor and Staff of Travelling take an act III reinforced alloy, and Tombstone's tablets take you home or to a memorized place.",
    "",
    "Pick one system for your base network and keep it simple. Three half-built networks add up to zero."
  ],
  "quest.18E4ED0DBED8F947.title": "Always a way back",
  "quest.18E4ED0DBED8F947.quest_desc": [
    "A map that remembers, a waypoint on every find, a waystone network, a scroll in your pocket and a bed on your back.",
    "",
    "Getting lost is now a choice."
  ],
  "chapter.2141D3453BBA64F0.title": "The Nether and the End",
  "chapter.2141D3453BBA64F0.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Two vanilla dimensions, rebuilt and crowded: what changes, what to look for and how to survive."
  ],
  "quest.03CC695E3623C8E5.title": "Familiar places, new rules",
  "quest.03CC695E3623C8E5.quest_desc": [
    "Both dimensions are far busier than vanilla: YUNG's rebuilds the big structures, Repurposed Structures, Dungeons and Taverns, Cataclysm, Friends and Foes and Hellish Trials add many more, and Enderman Overhaul fills them with biome endermen.",
    "",
    "The compass sends you to a Nether fortress in act III and to the End in act V."
  ],
  "quest.5A8E9C6BA67CBFA4.title": "We Need to Go Deeper",
  "quest.5A8E9C6BA67CBFA4.quest_desc": [
    "Build an obsidian frame and light it; Nether Portal Fix links the return portal to the one you came from.",
    "",
    "Pack fire resistance, one piece of gold armor (piglins leave you alone), blocks to bridge and something to put out fires. The Nether does not do second chances."
  ],
  "quest.653E3DFA0A5DA6FE.title": "A blaze rod from a fortress",
  "quest.653E3DFA0A5DA6FE.quest_desc": [
    "YUNG's Better Nether Fortresses makes them larger and themed. In act III the compass points to one and counts it done as soon as someone on your team carries a Blaze Rod.",
    "",
    "Blaze rods feed brewing, Powah and many mid-game recipes, and wither skeletons here drop the skulls for the Wither."
  ],
  "quest.6C2CB59EB7AB9359.title": "Crossing lava seas",
  "quest.6C2CB59EB7AB9359.quest_desc": [
    "Fireproof Boats adds crimson and warped boats that survive lava like their planks: cross lava oceans and scout the shores.",
    "",
    "Or go vanilla: saddle a strider and steer it with a warped fungus on a stick. Slower, but it has personality."
  ],
  "quest.0905D2D4B1D95BDF.title": "What else lives in the Nether",
  "quest.0905D2D4B1D95BDF.quest_desc": [
    "Dungeons and Taverns adds Nether Keeps (with their own key), ports, skeleton towers and camps, and piglin camps, hamlets and donjons. Repurposed Structures adds Nether cities, underground bastions, strongholds, pyramids, mineshafts, temples and crimson or warped villages. Add Hellish Trials' chambers, the Citadel of the Wildfire (Friends and Foes) and the Burning Arena and Soul Forge (Cataclysm)."
  ],
  "quest.76C7A1F4CEEEEE65.title": "Concrete Halls",
  "quest.76C7A1F4CEEEEE65.quest_desc": [
    "Find a Dungeons and Taverns Nether Keep for Concrete Halls. Keeps and ports are skeleton strongholds; exploring every skeleton camp, tower, port, fortress and keep is Skull Collector.",
    "",
    "Bathing in powder snow inside a keep is its own advancement, Cool Off. Somebody had a fun afternoon designing that."
  ],
  "quest.2A4135289353D989.title": "Bastions and piglins",
  "quest.2A4135289353D989.quest_desc": [
    "Bastion remnants hold gold and netherite upgrade templates, with ancient debris nearby. Wear gold, do not open chests in sight of piglins, and watch for Piglin Brutes, which ignore gold entirely.",
    "",
    "Dungeons and Taverns adds four more piglin places, for Hog Hunt."
  ],
  "quest.50763FDA378A360C.title": "Hidden in the Depths",
  "quest.50763FDA378A360C.quest_desc": [
    "Ancient debris hides low in the Nether and shrugs off explosions. Mine it with a diamond pickaxe, smelt it into scrap and combine with gold into netherite ingots.",
    "",
    "Keep your netherite gear: it is the base for Cataclysm's Ignitium and Cursium and for Luminous gear."
  ],
  "quest.4394BC17C2F2C3BE.title": "Nether endermen and food",
  "quest.4394BC17C2F2C3BE.quest_desc": [
    "Enderman Overhaul gives each Nether biome its own enderman: crimson ones drop pearls that grant Strength on teleport, warped ones Resistance, and soul sand valley ones a pearl that teleports a bound creature.",
    "",
    "My Nether's Delight adds Nether cooking to Farmer's Delight: more variety for the pack's food system."
  ],
  "quest.6F418FFE86CB3ACD.title": "The stronghold",
  "quest.6F418FFE86CB3ACD.quest_desc": [
    "Eyes of Ender lead to the stronghold, rebuilt by YUNG's Better Strongholds. In act V the compass counts it done when your team reaches the End.",
    "",
    "Bring spare eyes. They break at the worst moment."
  ],
  "quest.5DC959C522847AC4.title": "The End",
  "quest.5DC959C522847AC4.quest_desc": [
    "YUNG's Better End Island rebuilds the central island and the Dragon arena; the fight itself is in the bosses chapter. After the Dragon, throw an ender pearl into an End Gateway to reach the outer islands (Remote Getaway)."
  ],
  "quest.108AAEC672725EF9.title": "The City at the End of the Game",
  "quest.108AAEC672725EF9.quest_desc": [
    "End cities rise on the outer islands, guarded by Shulkers whose Levitation can kill you when it wears off: carry slow falling or a water bucket. Their ships hide Elytra, and their chests hold good enchanted gear.",
    "",
    "Look up before you look down."
  ],
  "quest.2DB3986BA317369E.title": "The busy outer End",
  "quest.2DB3986BA317369E.quest_desc": [
    "Dungeons and Taverns adds the End Castle (a haunting boss), the End Lighthouse and lone ships; Repurposed Structures, End outposts, mineshafts, shipwrecks, pyramids, strongholds and an ancient city; Explorify, a shipwreck; Cataclysm, the Ruined Citadel and its Ender Guardian. Enderman Overhaul's End endermen drop Corrupted and Ancient Pearls, and End's Delight cooks it all."
  ],
  "quest.09764E768DB75F4F.title": "The Light at the End of the Game",
  "quest.09764E768DB75F4F.quest_desc": [
    "Find a Dungeons and Taverns End Lighthouse: a fitting landmark for a pack about light, and a good spot for a waystone before exploring further.",
    "",
    "Even at the end of the world, someone left a light on."
  ],
  "quest.6771B1C3C9DED3B8.title": "Waystones in other dimensions",
  "quest.6771B1C3C9DED3B8.quest_desc": [
    "Build a Nether waystone (red Nether bricks) and an End one (End stone bricks) near each portal. Warping between dimensions costs a flat amount of experience and saves the portal walk every time.",
    "",
    "Wild waystones also generate in the Nether and the End."
  ],
  "quest.0A003066AB308EE3.title": "What ENTRELUMEN changes here",
  "quest.0A003066AB308EE3.quest_desc": [
    "The compass visits a YUNG's fortress in act III (carry a blaze rod) and, in act V, the ocean monument, the stronghold and the End (kill the Dragon). The Wither is the only nether star source.",
    "",
    "Dungeons and Taverns adds fortresses, ports and towers to the Nether, and the pack's measurements flag them as worth watching on a modest PC."
  ],
  "quest.5DEB6F3020339532.title": "Both ends of the world",
  "quest.5DEB6F3020339532.quest_desc": [
    "Fortresses, bastions and keeps below; cities, lighthouses and citadels beyond the void.",
    "",
    "You have seen both ends of the world. Heliodor is somewhere in between."
  ],
  "chapter.15E243BD7219AC6D.title": "The Twilight Forest",
  "chapter.15E243BD7219AC6D.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A forest of locked biomes: each boss lifts a curse and opens the next one."
  ],
  "quest.7BAACB5DDB46EED3.title": "Where the light never arrives",
  "quest.7BAACB5DDB46EED3.quest_desc": [
    "A dimension of endless dusk built as a chain of bosses: most biomes are cursed (darkness, mosquitoes, blizzards, heat, acid rain), and each curse lifts when you beat the boss feeding it. The mod's advancements tab is the progression map.",
    "",
    "The compass sends you here in act III. Heliodor's gardeners called this forest \"the rehearsal\"."
  ],
  "quest.0EA44BF18B7729BC.title": "A pool, flowers and a diamond",
  "quest.0EA44BF18B7729BC.quest_desc": [
    "Dig a pool of water (2×2 is classic) edged with grass or dirt, put a plant on every border block (flowers, grass, ferns, mushrooms) and throw a diamond in. Lightning strikes and the water becomes a portal, which works both ways afterwards.",
    "",
    "The lightning sets things on fire: build it well away from your wooden house."
  ],
  "quest.7FC4E052AE4B63B7.title": "Into the Twilight Forest",
  "quest.7FC4E052AE4B63B7.quest_desc": [
    "It is dark even at noon and mobs spawn more than you expect: bring light. Fireflies and cicadas are harmless ambience, and you can jar them as lamps.",
    "",
    "Your team's first visit records the milestone the act IV Atlas asks for, even if you come during act III."
  ],
  "quest.74502BCE49B10400.title": "Locked biomes, explorer's notes",
  "quest.74502BCE49B10400.quest_desc": [
    "Walk into a biome you have not earned and a \"Biome Locked!\" toast appears while its curse gets to work. Boss structures have unbreakable walls, so no tunnel skips a lock.",
    "",
    "Arrive early and the mod hands you an explorer's notebook: it says which creature feeds the curse and where to find it."
  ],
  "quest.7212AD2EC72A656F.title": "The Naga",
  "quest.7212AD2EC72A656F.quest_desc": [
    "A huge serpent coiled around its stone courtyard. It charges in straight lines: sidestep, hit the head, and fight in the open.",
    "",
    "It drops Naga Scales and its trophy, into a chest as bosses do here. A scale is the key to the Lich Tower's barrier (Time To Even The Scales), and scales make the Naga chestplate and leggings."
  ],
  "quest.2343281F0BF397DB.title": "Naga armor",
  "quest.2343281F0BF397DB.quest_desc": [
    "The Naga chestplate and leggings are a solid step above iron for the early forest, and Twilight gear may come pre-enchanted (the tooltip shows it).",
    "",
    "Do not spend every scale: keep one for the Lich Tower."
  ],
  "quest.4946C8BB9106BD4D.title": "The Twilight Lich",
  "quest.4946C8BB9106BD4D.quest_desc": [
    "He waits atop his pointy tower, throwing bolts, some explosive, and calling minions: bring a bow, food and good armor.",
    "",
    "Beating him and taking a scepter lifts three curses at once, the Swamp's mosquitoes, the Dark Forest's blindness and the Snowy Forest's chill (Bring Out Your Dead), and the forest branches into three paths in any order."
  ],
  "quest.6139B043AA702225.title": "The four scepters",
  "quest.6139B043AA702225.quest_desc": [
    "The Lich's loot rolls one of four: Twilight (damaging pearls), Life Draining (steals health), Zombie (a loyal zombie) and Fortification (a shield). Each has limited charges; Renewal recharges them from your inventory.",
    "",
    "All four is By Our Powers Combined!, which means more than one Lich."
  ],
  "quest.1BC244DB1E06B5D7.title": "The Labyrinth and the Minoshroom",
  "quest.1BC244DB1E06B5D7.quest_desc": [
    "Under the Swamp lie labyrinths full of Minotaurs, and the Minoshroom guards the vault. It drops Meef Stroganoff, which acclimatizes you to the Fire Swamp's heat (Mighty Stroganoff), a diamond Minotaur axe and its trophy.",
    "",
    "Minotaurs drop the Maze Map Focus, key to the Maze Map and the Uncrafting Table."
  ],
  "quest.282914EAB0C2CF9C.title": "The Hydra",
  "quest.282914EAB0C2CF9C.quest_desc": [
    "A many-headed beast in the Fire Swamp that breathes fire and lobs mortars. Hit its heads when they come close; fire resistance helps a lot.",
    "",
    "It drops Fiery Blood, Hydra Chops and its trophy (Hydra Slayer). Fiery Blood and an iron ingot make a Fiery Ingot."
  ],
  "quest.7C2E55F2F5F32A25.title": "Fiery gear",
  "quest.7C2E55F2F5F32A25.quest_desc": [
    "A Fiery Ingot (Fiery Blood or Fiery Tears plus iron) makes Fiery tools, which auto-smelt what you mine, and Fiery armor, which burns attackers. Hold a Fiery tool with a Fiery armor piece in your inventory for Gallons of Blood and Tears.",
    "",
    "The Fiery Pickaxe is an auto-smelter, very early."
  ],
  "quest.4698EBAFF4445D37.title": "A trophy on the pedestal",
  "quest.4698EBAFF4445D37.quest_desc": [
    "The Dark Forest hides the Knight Stronghold, full of goblin knights. Deep inside, place any boss trophy (the Naga's works) on the Trophy Pedestal to claim your title and open the main stronghold (Trophied Champion).",
    "",
    "Goblin knights drop Armor Shards; nine make a cluster that smelts into Knightmetal."
  ],
  "quest.3F2B34D964E4C5A9.title": "The Knight Phantoms",
  "quest.3F2B34D964E4C5A9.quest_desc": [
    "They fight as a group in the stronghold's tomb. Settling them all is Carminite Acclimation, after which the Dark Tower's carminite devices obey you.",
    "",
    "They drop Knightmetal tools and Phantom armor; the Phantom helmet and chestplate are never lost on death. Perfect for dangerous trips."
  ],
  "quest.076AE29C59A9324D.title": "Knightmetal",
  "quest.076AE29C59A9324D.quest_desc": [
    "Knightmetal swords and pickaxes deal extra damage to armored targets, the axe to unarmored ones, and a Knightmetal block hurts whatever touches it.",
    "",
    "It also makes the Block and Chain, a heavy flail for people who solve problems directly."
  ],
  "quest.1921A9F593AFFAC9.title": "The Ghast Trap",
  "quest.1921A9F593AFFAC9.quest_desc": [
    "The Dark Tower is a vertical carminite puzzle: vanishing and reappearing blocks, and doors opened by a Tower Key. At the top, kill the Carminite Ghastlings around a Ghast Trap and activate it to drag the Ur-Ghast from the sky (Something Strange in Towerwood).",
    "",
    "Towerwood Borers drop Borer Essence; with a ghast tear and redstone it makes Carminite."
  ],
  "quest.2DE150A68B058983.title": "The Ur-Ghast",
  "quest.2DE150A68B058983.quest_desc": [
    "Trapped, it fights in its room atop the tower, crying fire and shooting fireballs: bring fire resistance and a bow.",
    "",
    "It drops Fiery Tears, Carminite and its trophy (Tears of Fire). The tears make Fiery Ingots just like Fiery Blood."
  ],
  "quest.40852BEC9F8AF9D4.title": "The Alpha Yeti",
  "quest.40852BEC9F8AF9D4.quest_desc": [
    "The Alpha Yeti feeds the Snowy Forest's blizzard from a cave full of yetis, throwing Ice Bombs and dropping ice from the ceiling.",
    "",
    "Its fur keeps you safe from the Glacier's cold (Alpha Fur). Regular yetis and winter wolves drop Arctic Fur for dyeable Arctic armor."
  ],
  "quest.5E27FBC034C96D9A.title": "The Snow Queen",
  "quest.5E27FBC034C96D9A.quest_desc": [
    "Atop the Glacier stands the Aurora Palace, and on its roof the Snow Queen: ice cores, falling ice and Snow Guardians. Keep moving and keep your distance.",
    "",
    "She drops the Triple Bow or the Seeker Bow, plus her trophy (Clear Skies)."
  ],
  "quest.363D1E6BBE352CC4.title": "Ultimate Showdown",
  "quest.363D1E6BBE352CC4.quest_desc": [
    "With the Hydra, the Ur-Ghast and the Snow Queen down, the acid rain over the Highlands stops (Ultimate Showdown): the three branches meet.",
    "",
    "The Highlands are the last region: troll caves, giants in the clouds and the Final Castle on the plateau."
  ],
  "quest.1983173282DF3813.title": "Jack and the Beanstalk",
  "quest.1983173282DF3813.quest_desc": [
    "Highland trolls drop Magic Beans. Use one on the glowing Uberous Soil below the clouds and a beanstalk grows up to them (Jack and the Beanstalk).",
    "",
    "Up there, Giant Miners carry the Giant's Pickaxe, which breaks the troll caves' giant blocks (I'm on Cloud Nine)."
  ],
  "quest.305E00B5ADF67301.title": "The Lamp of Cinders",
  "quest.305E00B5ADF67301.quest_desc": [
    "Behind the giant blocks lies a vault with the Lamp of Cinders, which burns away the thorn barriers to the plateau (I Wish For More Burning).",
    "",
    "That is as far as the mod goes: the Final Castle is unfinished, and reaching it shows End of Progression and a note from the authors."
  ],
  "quest.7A964152B947BDAF.title": "Ironwood",
  "quest.7A964152B947BDAF.quest_desc": [
    "Liveroot, raw iron and a gold nugget make Raw Ironwood; smelt it into an Ironwood Ingot. Liveroot comes from Liveroot blocks among underground roots, and from chests.",
    "",
    "Here the Ironwood Ingot is also the act IV component of Powah's niotic capacitor."
  ],
  "quest.55D0B07C36817F68.title": "Hollow Hills",
  "quest.55D0B07C36817F68.quest_desc": [
    "Mounds in the forest are Hollow Hills, caves full of ore, spawners and Redcaps; beating a Redcap in a small one is The Boots Are Mine!",
    "",
    "Their chests hold Steeleaf, the Ore Magnet (pulls ore out of rock), Transformation Powder (turns creatures into others) and Charms of Life."
  ],
  "quest.258FDDFEE1E8F9DE.title": "Charms: life and keeping",
  "quest.258FDDFEE1E8F9DE.quest_desc": [
    "A Charm of Life saves you from one deadly blow and is used up. A Charm of Keeping keeps part of your inventory on death: tier I armor and held items, II adds the hotbar, III everything. Four of a tier craft the next.",
    "",
    "Phantom armor is never lost either; for the rest, the Tombstone chapter."
  ],
  "quest.0C4CE938F64896BA.title": "Magic maps",
  "quest.0C4CE938F64896BA.quest_desc": [
    "Hunt the local wildlife (The Silence of the Forest), then craft a Magic Map Focus from a Raven Feather, glowstone dust and Torchberries from cave ceilings. The Magic Map shows the forest's biomes and landmarks at a glance.",
    "",
    "A Maze Map Focus gives the Maze Map, and later comes the Ore Map."
  ],
  "quest.2F31C4287AA428C1.title": "The Uncrafting Table",
  "quest.2F31C4287AA428C1.quest_desc": [
    "A crafting table and a Maze Map Focus. It breaks crafted items back into ingredients, or repairs them, for experience; banned items say so.",
    "",
    "Uncrafting an Uncrafting Table is an advancement (A Step too Far). Of course it is."
  ],
  "quest.24460174056CB15A.title": "The Questing Ram",
  "quest.24460174056CB15A.quest_desc": [
    "A Quest Grove hides a strange, colourful ram missing wool of several colours. Bring it what it lacks, one by one (Consummate Baaahs): the reward is worth the errand, and there is a trophy.",
    "",
    "A good detour while you are still looking for the Naga."
  ],
  "quest.039C50EEE3A8B7EC.title": "Trophies and team fights",
  "quest.039C50EEE3A8B7EC.quest_desc": [
    "Every boss drops a trophy head for decoration, and one of them opens the Knight Stronghold.",
    "",
    "The pack keeps the mod's group defaults: boss loot drops into a chest, and the multiplayer adjuster is off, so bosses do not scale with more players. Bring friends, they will not make it harder."
  ],
  "quest.0D69862767E638BA.title": "What changes in the forest",
  "quest.0D69862767E638BA.quest_desc": [
    "The compass points here in act III, then to the Naga Courtyard; the Lich Tower follows in act IV. Your team's first arrival counts for act IV. Ironwood is the act IV component of Powah's niotic capacitor, Twilight's Flavor and Delight adds cooking, Carry On refuses bosses and their spawners, and the Traveller's Belt swaps on &e;&r instead of V."
  ],
  "quest.514F42EDF180AD10.title": "Eating at eternal sundown",
  "quest.514F42EDF180AD10.quest_desc": [
    "Venison from deer, Meef from Minotaurs, Hydra Chops and the odd cake called Experiment 115; eating every Twilight-exclusive food is We Dine At Eternal Sundown.",
    "",
    "It matters here: the pack rewards variety, and leftover saturation becomes random buffs."
  ],
  "quest.545788B47FC5D0BF.title": "The forest is quiet",
  "quest.545788B47FC5D0BF.quest_desc": [
    "Naga, Lich, Minoshroom, Hydra, Knight Phantoms, Ur-Ghast, Alpha Yeti and Snow Queen: every curse lifted, plus Ironwood, Steeleaf, Knightmetal, Fiery Ingots and Carminite for the rest of the pack.",
    "",
    "Juan used to call this place a rehearsal. You just passed it."
  ],
  "chapter.452B4A2E808E616E.title": "The Undergarden",
  "chapter.452B4A2E808E616E.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A hostile world below the world: its own ores, the Rotspawn plague and the Forgotten."
  ],
  "quest.0244990CBBDEA01A.title": "The forgotten land below",
  "quest.0244990CBBDEA01A.quest_desc": [
    "An underground dimension with its own stones (Depthrock, Shiverstone, Tremblecrust, Dreadrock), its own ores (Cloggrum, Froststeel, Utherium, Regalium, Rogdorium) and fauna from harmless to nasty. Optional: no story step or compass target needs it.",
    "",
    "It opens in act III, because the Catalyst that lights its portal takes a Routing Matrix."
  ],
  "quest.1BD7823BF183F956.title": "The Catalyst",
  "quest.1BD7823BF183F956.quest_desc": [
    "Here it is 4 copper ingots, 3 stones, an ender pearl and a Routing Matrix in the top middle slot, and it is not consumed on use.",
    "",
    "The Crumbling Catalyst (Cloggrum, Depthrock and a Forgotten Nugget) wears out with use: a spare for later, since you must have been down there to craft it."
  ],
  "quest.56473A0DAA1097B3.title": "A stone-brick portal",
  "quest.56473A0DAA1097B3.quest_desc": [
    "Build a Nether-portal-shaped frame of stone bricks (mossy, cracked and chiseled count), deepslate bricks or tiles, or polished deepslate, and use the Catalyst inside. It only works in the Overworld and the Undergarden.",
    "",
    "You arrive underground in the dark: bring torches, food and a pickaxe, and mark the portal before wandering off."
  ],
  "quest.1EF964F39F27AEC6.title": "Rotspawn and the infection",
  "quest.1EF964F39F27AEC6.quest_desc": [
    "The Rotspawn (Rotling, Rotwalker, Rotbeast, Rotbelcher) are the local plague. Fighting them and walking infected areas fills the Utheric Infection meter, which can kill you.",
    "",
    "Eat Rogdorium (or a nugget) or get Purity to hold it back (A Much Needed Antidote). Rotspawn drop Utheric Shards; one on a stick is a Shard Torch that hurts nearby Rotspawn."
  ],
  "quest.7A5577FC60DD8C3A.title": "A Shard Torch",
  "quest.7A5577FC60DD8C3A.quest_desc": [
    "A Utheric Shard on a stick (Warding Device). Place a few around your landing point to keep Rotspawn away.",
    "",
    "Its magic can hurt you too if you stand beside it while fleeing something. Torches, it turns out, have opinions."
  ],
  "quest.68C302C8CB5FA6FF.title": "Who lives down here",
  "quest.68C302C8CB5FA6FF.quest_desc": [
    "Not everything bites: Scintlings are harmless and leave slowing goo (killing one earns a guilty advancement), Gloompers, Dwellers and Mogs are passive or neutral, and Gwiblings are fish for your bucket. Watch for Brutes, Nargoyles, Munchers and Rotspawn.",
    "",
    "Stoneborn trade (Interdimensional Business). Denizens live in camps; break their campfire and the whole camp turns on you."
  ],
  "quest.64BB6C9B5B694154.title": "Deep extraction",
  "quest.64BB6C9B5B694154.quest_desc": [
    "Cloggrum is the common, iron-like metal; Froststeel comes from Shiverstone in cold biomes; Utherium is a crystal; Regalium a precious gem; and Rogdorium hides in Dreadrock at the very bottom. All carry the usual c: tags, so other mods' machines process them.",
    "",
    "One block of every ore is Collector's Edition."
  ],
  "quest.08116F2B51A7FD13.title": "Cloggrum gear",
  "quest.08116F2B51A7FD13.quest_desc": [
    "Smelt raw Cloggrum into tools and armor. A full suit is Cover Me in Coprolites, and Cloggrum boots ignore Scintling goo.",
    "",
    "Keep the tools: the Forgotten upgrade later turns them into the best gear down here."
  ],
  "quest.2BCA276FF34515F9.title": "Froststeel and Utherium",
  "quest.2BCA276FF34515F9.quest_desc": [
    "Froststeel weapons slow what they hit; Utherium weapons deal 1.5× damage to Rotspawn, the natural answer to the Infected Depths.",
    "",
    "The Undergarden also brews Brittleness (more damage the more armor the victim wears), Featherweight (more knockback) and Virulent Resistance."
  ],
  "quest.5243B599FDF23D62.title": "The Slingshot",
  "quest.5243B599FDF23D62.quest_desc": [
    "Craft one (Your New Best Friend) and fire Depthrock Pebbles, dropped by Mogs and Stoneborn; Goo Balls, Rotten Blisterberries (they explode) and even Gronglets also work, each with an advancement.",
    "",
    "Ricochet bounces shots off walls, and Self Sling fires you instead: a cheap way across a gap, if you trust your aim."
  ],
  "quest.6F9634CD107335CC.title": "Underground food",
  "quest.6F9634CD107335CC.quest_desc": [
    "Pick an Underbean Bush (Glorious Beans!), plant Gloomgourd seeds (Purple Pumpkins) and hunt Dwellers and Gloompers for meat. Blisterberries are food too, but rotten ones are ammo, not dinner.",
    "",
    "Every new dish counts toward ENTRELUMEN's food variety."
  ],
  "quest.2E81A1F973314EFF.title": "Forgotten Halls",
  "quest.2E81A1F973314EFF.quest_desc": [
    "Catacombs are ruined Depthrock halls whose chests hold Cloggrum and Froststeel nuggets, Regalium, Utheric Shards and the Forgotten upgrade template.",
    "",
    "The Forgotten guard them, and some carry a Cloggrum Battleaxe you can pry from their hands (Cold Dead Hands)."
  ],
  "quest.43D1DB8A024E10C7.title": "The Forgotten Guardian",
  "quest.43D1DB8A024E10C7.quest_desc": [
    "The Undergarden's heavy hitter, found in the Catacombs. Beating it is Decommissioned and it drops Forgotten Nuggets.",
    "",
    "Nine nuggets make a Forgotten Ingot (What Now Is), this dimension's endgame metal."
  ],
  "quest.5EE9D31CF36D4673.title": "Forgotten Arsenal",
  "quest.5EE9D31CF36D4673.quest_desc": [
    "At a smithing table, the Forgotten template and a Forgotten Ingot upgrade a Cloggrum tool or weapon. Forgotten tools mine Undergarden blocks 1.5× faster, and Forgotten weapons deal 1.5× damage to non-boss Undergarden mobs.",
    "",
    "Only Forgotten tools break Dreadrock, the barrier at the bottom."
  ],
  "quest.0E7DE09D7A18EDF9.title": "A Forgotten Minion",
  "quest.0E7DE09D7A18EDF9.quest_desc": [
    "Put a Carved Gloomgourd on a Block of Forgotten Metal, golem-style, and you get a Forgotten Minion that shoots hostile creatures (Buildin' a Sentry).",
    "",
    "A good guard for a base down here. It does not ask for wages."
  ],
  "quest.1075165C09B99F54.title": "Into the Depths",
  "quest.1075165C09B99F54.quest_desc": [
    "Break through the Dreadrock barrier with a Forgotten pickaxe to reach the Depths: Rogdorium, Dreadrock Utherium, Denizen camps and the Infected Depths, where the infection is at its worst.",
    "",
    "Pack Rogdorium to eat and Utherium weapons for the Rotspawn."
  ],
  "quest.7DB1066C527E1A9F.title": "The Infuser",
  "quest.7DB1066C527E1A9F.quest_desc": [
    "Dreadrock, a Utheric Cluster (9 shards) and Rogdorium. Fuelled with Rogdorium or Utherium, it purifies and converts: a Utheric Cluster into a Utherium Crystal, an Ancient Root into a Denizen Totem, and it infuses armor.",
    "",
    "EMI lists every Infusing recipe."
  ],
  "quest.04E5B17B3C7E2EFC.title": "Meeting the locals",
  "quest.04E5B17B3C7E2EFC.quest_desc": [
    "Denizen camps sit around a campfire in the Depths. Their camps hold Ancient Roots, Denizen Masks and totems, and a Mysterious Mask from a Denizen is One of Us.",
    "",
    "Leave the campfire alone. They are very attached to it."
  ],
  "quest.5DD3FBB588B8A96D.title": "Subterranean Cartographer",
  "quest.5DD3FBB588B8A96D.quest_desc": [
    "Visit every Undergarden biome: Smogstem and Wigglewood forests, mushroom bogs, the Frostfields, dead and ancient seas, the Smog Spires and more; the Forgotten Field and the Depths count too.",
    "",
    "JourneyMap keeps mapping down here, and waypoints are your best defence against getting lost."
  ],
  "quest.6D7F3B5108B92223.title": "What changes down here",
  "quest.6D7F3B5108B92223.quest_desc": [
    "The Catalyst takes a Routing Matrix, so the dimension opens in act III, and nothing in the story asks for it. Its ores keep their c: tags for other mods' processing. A few upstream compatibility recipes that do not load in 1.21.1 (Malum repairs for its tools) are disabled, and its Delight addon was left out to keep the pack lean."
  ],
  "quest.2A574F05F7829F64.title": "Master of the underground",
  "quest.2A574F05F7829F64.quest_desc": [
    "You lit the portal, survived the infection, beat the Forgotten Guardian and broke into the Depths.",
    "",
    "The Undergarden is now a mine you control: Regalium and Utherium for trade and gear, Froststeel and Cloggrum by the ton."
  ],
  "chapter.44444DD14A3061C3.title": "Eternal Starlight",
  "chapter.44444DD14A3061C3.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A night that never ends, meteor showers and the machines of a lost civilization."
  ],
  "quest.1E64401CFF4C70E1.title": "Sky of a million stars",
  "quest.1E64401CFF4C70E1.quest_desc": [
    "A dimension under an eternal starry night, left by the Starlighters, whose golems and machines still guard their ruins, with its own biomes, ores, crops, meteor showers and bosses.",
    "",
    "It belongs to act IV, the Observatory's act, through a Horizon Chart in the Orb of Prophecy. Optional for the story."
  ],
  "quest.57487D350C886A96.title": "The portal ruins",
  "quest.57487D350C886A96.quest_desc": [
    "Small portal ruins dot the Overworld (common, cold, desert, forest and jungle): a Chiseled Voidstone frame and the spawner of their guardian, the Gatekeeper. Spread out but not rare; the Explorer's Compass finds them.",
    "",
    "Talk to the Gatekeeper first. He trades, answers questions and accepts challenges."
  ],
  "quest.2193C7A643FCA2F9.title": "The Gatekeeper's trial",
  "quest.2193C7A643FCA2F9.quest_desc": [
    "Pick Challenge and confirm: he is a duelist who parries and throws fireballs (Duke it out!). He only trades with the proven: beat him, or have killed the Ender Dragon.",
    "",
    "The first win drops the Glimmering Tablet and an Orb of Prophecy, with a chance of a Glistering weapon and a music disc."
  ],
  "quest.09AFA411E26E9BD2.title": "The Orb of Prophecy",
  "quest.09AFA411E26E9BD2.quest_desc": [
    "Use it on a ruin's Chiseled Voidstone frame to open the portal. The first comes from the Gatekeeper; spares here take blue starlight crystal shards, glass and a Horizon Chart (act IV), and the shards grow in the dimension itself.",
    "",
    "It is also your spellbook: it holds crests and casts them with mana crystals. Switch crest with &eH&r."
  ],
  "quest.6857CE79DA16E994.title": "Into the Starlight dimension",
  "quest.6857CE79DA16E994.quest_desc": [
    "Cross the portal (Sky of a Million Stars). It is always night: bring light and expect monsters, and open the Glimmering Tablet often as it fills in.",
    "",
    "In the pack's server measurements this was the costliest dimension to generate. Explore at walking pace, especially on a modest PC."
  ],
  "quest.1D265267129434E6.title": "Seeking Eyes",
  "quest.1D265267129434E6.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Starlight Flowers around an ender pearl make 16 Seeking Eyes (Guided by Starlight). Thrown, one flies toward ruins with powerful creatures.",
    "",
    "Aim it with a locator item in the other hand: redstone or Golem Steel for the Golem Forge, cave moss and similar plants for the Cursed Garden."
  ],
  "quest.71928319D4A2D4B1.title": "The Golem Forge",
  "quest.71928319D4A2D4B1.quest_desc": [
    "A large underground ruin (Cradle of Legion) with Freezes, ancient cooling machines, and two bosses: the Starlight Golem and the Permafrost.",
    "",
    "Cold-proof armor helps against the Freezes. Dress warmly for the machine room."
  ],
  "quest.633C1F8E3CE415A8.title": "The Starlight Golem",
  "quest.633C1F8E3CE415A8.quest_desc": [
    "It does not move, and its armor shrugs off attacks. When it stops to absorb energy, shut down the Energy Blocks feeding it and its armor drops for a while (The Backstabber); a Frozen Tube thrown at it triggers that sooner (Chill Out, Buddy!).",
    "",
    "Beating it is Ancient Wisdom and yields Golem Steel."
  ],
  "quest.29268E6B61BB234A.title": "The Permafrost",
  "quest.29268E6B61BB234A.quest_desc": [
    "The Starlighters fused several Freezes into one thermal regulator: it spits frost and spreads freezing clouds. Beating it is Winter is Leaving.",
    "",
    "The oldest air conditioner in the game, and the angriest."
  ],
  "quest.5131C5A8261FB584.title": "The Lunar Monstrosity",
  "quest.5131C5A8261FB584.quest_desc": [
    "A plant in the Cursed Garden that fed on prisoners' souls. Its skin cuts all damage unless it is burning or stunned: set it alight (Burn it to the Ground) and strike then. It burrows after you, and Tangled Skulls explode when killed.",
    "",
    "Beating it is Through the Thorns; it drops the Moonring Bow and opens the Crescent Spear and Unrealium armor."
  ],
  "quest.16FDCDD39224D764.title": "Stepping into the Unseen",
  "quest.16FDCDD39224D764.quest_desc": [
    "A full set of Unrealium armor is the dimension's top gear and earns Stepping into the Unseen.",
    "",
    "EMI shows the recipes and the boss materials they need. Budget a few rematches."
  ],
  "quest.09A9D7E845A30DD2.title": "Wish upon a star",
  "quest.09A9D7E845A30DD2.quest_desc": [
    "Meteor showers cross the night sky: dodge the big ones, then check the craters for Raw Aethersent and other ores. Creteors can crawl out of large impacts, and their hide is a crafting material.",
    "",
    "An Aethersent Ingot is Gift from the Sky, and an Aetherstrike Rocket calls a shower whenever you like."
  ],
  "quest.53B40E460A2787F6.title": "Starlit materials",
  "quest.53B40E460A2787F6.quest_desc": [
    "Starlit Diamonds, Deepsilver (ore in stone, ice and Nightfall mud), Glacite shards in the Permafrost Forest, Thioquartz on the Ether River banks, Stellagmite underground (it melts in lava) and Amaramber from stripped Torreya logs, each with an advancement.",
    "",
    "Deepsilver matters in the Dark Swamp: Stranghouls fear silver."
  ],
  "quest.17F178E61BD3E14C.title": "Stranghouls",
  "quest.17F178E61BD3E14C.quest_desc": [
    "Feral but clever humanoids of the Dark Swamp: they hunt (Even Death May Die), barter and fear silver. A bowl of Pungency Stew hires one for a day (Anyone Can Cook).",
    "",
    "The Seeds Launcher, a weapon that fires any seed, only comes from bartering with them."
  ],
  "quest.0A6E97F5DECA4E45.title": "The Crystallized Desert",
  "quest.0A6E97F5DECA4E45.quest_desc": [
    "Blue starlight crystals, Crinoa seeds and Thirst Walkers (Castle of Glass). Kill a Thirst Walker or block its attack for a Tooth of Hunger: it crafts the Dagger of Hunger, which sharpens as it feeds, and the Crystalborn Catalyst, a redstone machine that \"infests\" its surroundings to gather resources.",
    "",
    "Crystallized Moths can be tamed with enough meat."
  ],
  "quest.6D6AE7D888D9F568.title": "Accessories in your gear",
  "quest.6D6AE7D888D9F568.quest_desc": [
    "Starlight accessories are combined into a specific kind of equipment, like items into a bundle, rather than worn. The Glimmering Tablet says how to get each one: the Butterfly Wings Amulet by throwing any accessory into the Ether, the Pearl Necklace by fishing over the Abyss.",
    "",
    "More on how they fit: the Accessories chapter."
  ],
  "quest.57DCFA1F9F867EC1.title": "Eating under the stars",
  "quest.57DCFA1F9F867EC1.quest_desc": [
    "Bouldershroom Stew lets you climb any wall (Nimble as a Squirrel), Silver Pungency Fruit gives Numbness, which delays damage rather than stopping it (I've Become so Numb), and Nocturnal Millet's seeds hide in Thioquartz along the Ether River.",
    "",
    "It all counts toward ENTRELUMEN's food variety."
  ],
  "quest.5246BBF74C2B6819.title": "Hammers, scythes and bombs",
  "quest.5246BBF74C2B6819.quest_desc": [
    "Hammers with a special attack on a full-strength critical hit (The Hammer of Justice), scythes (CHAOS, CHAOS), crystal greatswords and crossbows, Glacite arrows, and Tear and Frozen Bombs to throw.",
    "",
    "Unrealium and the boss weapons top the list."
  ],
  "quest.146B68A60537D26F.title": "Starlight Explorer",
  "quest.146B68A60537D26F.quest_desc": [
    "Visit every biome: the Starlight, Dense, Scarlet, Torreya and Permafrost forests, the Dark Swamp, the Crystallized Desert, the Solaris Isles, the Ether and Shimmer rivers, the seas and the Abyss.",
    "",
    "A long trip: combine it with the materials hunt."
  ],
  "quest.4B2D5F060CEA8A5A.title": "What ENTRELUMEN changes here",
  "quest.4B2D5F060CEA8A5A.quest_desc": [
    "The Orb of Prophecy recipe takes a Horizon Chart, though the Gatekeeper still drops one on your first win. The guidebook is never handed out on join: you earn the Glimmering Tablet from him. Carry On cannot lift the Starlight Portal, the crest key is &eH&r, and this is the costliest dimension to generate, so explore calmly."
  ],
  "quest.401F3C6F1B4BD6FE.title": "The Starlighters' heir",
  "quest.401F3C6F1B4BD6FE.quest_desc": [
    "You passed the Gatekeeper, crossed into the eternal night, silenced the Starlight Golem and burned the Lunar Monstrosity. Golem Steel, Aethersent, Unrealium, crests and spells are yours.",
    "",
    "Another civilization that played with light and machines. Heliodor was not the only one."
  ],
  "chapter.6EE4C13B1B5A28DC.title": "L_Ender's Cataclysm",
  "chapter.6EE4C13B1B5A28DC.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Eight arena bosses across three dimensions, each with a structure, a key and a weapon."
  ],
  "quest.64975244823C07C4.title": "Optional giants",
  "quest.64975244823C07C4.quest_desc": [
    "Big boss structures: the Ancient Factory, Cursed Pyramid, Frosted Prison, Sunken City and Acropolis in the Overworld, the Burning Arena and Soul Forge in the Nether, the Ruined Citadel in the End. Each boss drops a unique weapon or material and a music disc.",
    "",
    "No act needs them. Come when your gear is ready, not when your pride is."
  ],
  "quest.0CDA886D408DA541.title": "Eyes that find arenas",
  "quest.0CDA886D408DA541.quest_desc": [
    "Each structure has its own eye, crafted around an Eye of Ender, that flies to the nearest one like an ender eye to a stronghold: Mech (Factory), Desert (Pyramid), Curse (Prison), Abyss (Sunken City), Storm (Acropolis), Flame (Burning Arena), Monstrous (Soul Forge) and Void (Ruined Citadel).",
    "",
    "EMI has the recipes; all vanilla materials."
  ],
  "quest.6E4573618DC54B72.title": "The Cursed Pyramid",
  "quest.6E4573618DC54B72.quest_desc": [
    "A desert pyramid full of poison dart traps (Desert Pyramid Revamped). Its prize is buried: brush the suspicious sand inside for the Necklace of the Desert. An Eye of Desert finds it faster.",
    "",
    "As the necklace's tooltip hints, it can wake something up. It will."
  ],
  "quest.78546A4B9B108D1B.title": "The Ancient Remnant",
  "quest.78546A4B9B108D1B.quest_desc": [
    "Wake it in the pyramid and knock it down (Death Finds a Way); it fights with sandstorms and brute force.",
    "",
    "It drops a Remnant Skull (summons a Modern Remnant you tame with a Sniffer Egg), Sandstorm in a Bottle (two orbiting sandstorms) and a Block of Ancient Metal."
  ],
  "quest.4C7FF27418A7D8F5.title": "The Ancient Factory",
  "quest.4C7FF27418A7D8F5.quest_desc": [
    "Buried underground and far apart from each other (Out-of-Place), guarded by machines, with the Harbinger asleep at its heart.",
    "",
    "An Eye of Mech (Eye of Ender, iron and a redstone block) points the way."
  ],
  "quest.18D815D26CB453DD.title": "The Harbinger",
  "quest.18D815D26CB453DD.quest_desc": [
    "A war machine you wake with a nether star (The Thing of Ancient Civilization). The Wither is the only star source here, so fight the Wither first. It fires missiles and a death laser.",
    "",
    "It drops a Block of Witherite; its ingots make the Mechanical Fusion Anvil, the Laser Gatling, the Meat Shredder and the Wither Assault Shoulder Weapon."
  ],
  "quest.2EB85A616616FC85.title": "The Frosted Prison",
  "quest.2EB85A616616FC85.quest_desc": [
    "On snowy plains (Jail of Cold). Its Door of Seal only opens with a Strange Key, dropped by the Aptrgangr along with Black Steel.",
    "",
    "Inside waits the Cursed Tombstone. Too early and it only says \"Its power is still weak\"; when ready, it lights up and Maledictus rises."
  ],
  "quest.52BC12CEDD020F1B.title": "Maledictus",
  "quest.52BC12CEDD020F1B.quest_desc": [
    "The prison's cursed warlord (Crusade Against Curse) drops Cursium Ingots. With its template, netherite armor becomes Cursium: the helmet shows creatures through walls, the chestplate revives you once at 5 health (then a long debuff), the leggings sometimes dodge and the boots soften falls and back-step.",
    "",
    "The Cursed Bow fires phantom arrows."
  ],
  "quest.218996A57FF6A475.title": "The Sunken City",
  "quest.218996A57FF6A475.quest_desc": [
    "Deep in the ocean (Sunken in the Sea), with the Altar of Abyss. Summon its boss with an Abyssal Sacrifice: a nautilus shell, a heart of the sea, crystallized coral, an Athame and blocks of diamond, emerald, iron, gold and amethyst.",
    "",
    "Bring water breathing or the Aether's Iron Bubble."
  ],
  "quest.769A2395F35EC1DB.title": "The Leviathan",
  "quest.769A2395F35EC1DB.quest_desc": [
    "A multidimensional predator that fights underwater (A Multidimensional Predator). It drops the Tidal Claws (right-click grapples, left-click lashes a tentacle) and an Abyssal Egg.",
    "",
    "After it dies, Coral Golems start appearing in the ocean. The sea noticed."
  ],
  "quest.2DC24D7A21183977.title": "The Acropolis",
  "quest.2DC24D7A21183977.quest_desc": [
    "It rises over warm oceans (Why in the Sky?). Its sea creatures drop Lacrima, and the Clawdian (Not so Shrimple Now) also a Chitin Claw.",
    "",
    "An Eye of Storm (prismarine, diamonds, a lightning rod and a water bucket around an Eye of Ender) leads there."
  ],
  "quest.6B5403BBFAF47AC5.title": "Scylla, the Storm Empress",
  "quest.6B5403BBFAF47AC5.quest_desc": [
    "She rules the Acropolis (The Calm after the Storm) and drops Essence of the Storm and Lacrima. The essence crafts Astrape, whose right-click throws a lightning spear, and Ceraunus, a throwable anchor that summons waves when used sneaking."
  ],
  "quest.75BDA8800F4E0BEF.title": "The Burning Arena",
  "quest.75BDA8800F4E0BEF.quest_desc": [
    "In the Nether Wastes (A Massive Arena), with the Altar of Fire. Its Ignited Revenants drop Burning Ashes (Imperfect thing), or craft ashes from four Dying Embers.",
    "",
    "Place Burning Ashes on the altar to summon Ignis."
  ],
  "quest.412A7A62CD34F63A.title": "Ignis",
  "quest.412A7A62CD34F63A.quest_desc": [
    "A burning knight with a shield (The Extinguished Fire); fire resistance is mandatory. It drops Ignitium Ingots: the upgrade turns netherite armor into Ignitium (the chestplate combines with an elytra, the boots walk on lava) and crafts the Bulwark of the Flame and the Blazing Grips.",
    "",
    "After Ignis falls, Ignited Berserkers wake in Nether fortresses."
  ],
  "quest.583916C2A54A3B6A.title": "The Soul Forge",
  "quest.583916C2A54A3B6A.quest_desc": [
    "It hides in crimson and warped forests, soul sand valleys and wastes (Where the Monstrous be Forged), home of the Netherite Monstrosity.",
    "",
    "An Eye of Monstrous (blackstone, netherite scrap, a lava bucket and an Eye of Ender) points to it."
  ],
  "quest.507AEE61E72A81D7.title": "The Netherite Monstrosity",
  "quest.507AEE61E72A81D7.quest_desc": [
    "The Nether's giant war machine (The Broken Nether's Warmachine). It drops the Infernal Forge (a pickaxe with right-click area damage), a Lava Power Cell and a Monstrous Horn.",
    "",
    "Smith the horn onto a netherite helmet for the Monstrous Helm: it knocks back nearby enemies and raises defense below half health."
  ],
  "quest.3AD88921A7247356.title": "The Ruined Citadel",
  "quest.3AD88921A7247356.quest_desc": [
    "On the outer End highlands and midlands (Another Stronghold?!), patrolled by Ender Golems that drop Void Cores, which summon Void Runes (Palette Swap).",
    "",
    "An Eye of Void (End stone bricks, purpur and a shulker shell around an Eye of Ender) finds it. You need the End, so act V at the earliest."
  ],
  "quest.587DF57B0258B9AC.title": "The Ender Guardian",
  "quest.587DF57B0258B9AC.quest_desc": [
    "It commands the Citadel (Wasn't that a Shulker?) and drops the Gauntlet of Guard, whose right-click pulls creatures toward you.",
    "",
    "Useful, and deeply rude to anything you use it on."
  ],
  "quest.4CD300D0AC1CBA75.title": "Smaller finds",
  "quest.4CD300D0AC1CBA75.quest_desc": [
    "Amethyst Nests hide Amethyst Crabs, whose blessed meat protects against darkness and abyssal effects, and abandoned spires, temples, villages and desert sites dot the world with loot and traps.",
    "",
    "Good practice before the arenas."
  ],
  "quest.134981EE21C9111A.title": "Before any Cataclysm fight",
  "quest.134981EE21C9111A.quest_desc": [
    "These bosses telegraph long attack patterns: watch one full cycle before committing. Bring fire resistance or water breathing as needed, a Charm of Keeping or Phantom armor, a Tombstone plan, and a bed or waystone near the arena.",
    "",
    "Bosses cannot be lifted with Carry On, and their altars cannot be moved."
  ],
  "quest.7D3F711B7A5C58B5.title": "What ENTRELUMEN changes",
  "quest.7D3F711B7A5C58B5.quest_desc": [
    "No act, Atlas project or compass stop needs Cataclysm. The Wither is the only nether star source, which matters for the Harbinger. Armor ability keys moved off V and C: &eAlt+J&r ability, &eAlt+K&r helmet, &eAlt+L&r chestplate, &eAlt+I&r boots. Carry On refuses Cataclysm entities and altars, and structures only appear in new chunks."
  ],
  "quest.2E15E4E5C60FFCDF.title": "The Cataclysmfarer",
  "quest.2E15E4E5C60FFCDF.quest_desc": [
    "Defeat every Cataclysm boss for The Cataclysmfarer and its music disc.",
    "",
    "The hardest optional challenge in this family, and pure bragging rights: the story never asks for it."
  ],
  "chapter.515F02D1F755FA13.title": "The Aether and Deep Aether",
  "chapter.515F02D1F755FA13.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Floating islands, three dungeons and the Sun Spirit: the sky where act IV ends."
  ],
  "quest.07164C544A900A0B.title": "The sky above Heliodor",
  "quest.07164C544A900A0B.quest_desc": [
    "Floating islands with their own ores, tools and mounts, and three boss dungeons: Bronze, Silver and Gold. It belongs to act IV: the compass leads you through the dungeons, and the Sun Spirit at the end of the Gold one closes the act.",
    "",
    "Nothing locks the portal, so you can go earlier. Deep Aether adds biomes, Skyjade, Stratus and a Brass Dungeon."
  ],
  "quest.42F9D9395A6E191A.title": "A glowstone frame",
  "quest.42F9D9395A6E191A.quest_desc": [
    "Ten glowstone blocks (four dust each) in a Nether-portal-shaped frame, inside at least 2 wide and 3 tall, corners optional. Pour a water bucket in and it becomes an Aether portal. The pack turns off the free portal frame item, so this is the way up.",
    "",
    "Place the water carefully: a misclick breaks the frame you just built."
  ],
  "quest.2D510131BF5A8D84.title": "Hostile Paradise",
  "quest.2D510131BF5A8D84.quest_desc": [
    "Your first arrival brings a Book of Lore and a Golden Parachute; put any item in the book to read what it does. Days last three times longer, and eternal daylight holds while the Sun Spirit lives.",
    "",
    "Your team's first visit records the act IV milestone, even if you come early."
  ],
  "quest.6833E110D55B57C8.title": "Falling is not the end",
  "quest.6833E110D55B57C8.quest_desc": [
    "Fall out of the Aether and you land back in the Overworld instead of dying. Parachutes open by themselves when you drop off an island: a Cold Parachute (4 Cold Aerclouds) lasts one use, a Golden one 20.",
    "",
    "White Cold Aerclouds cancel fall damage, Blue ones bounce you high. Carry spare blocks for bridges."
  ],
  "quest.55968319FACF3C73.title": "What pushes you off",
  "quest.55968319FACF3C73.quest_desc": [
    "Most Aether deaths are falls, not fights: Zephyrs' knockback snowballs, slippery Quicksoil on island edges, Blue Aerclouds launching you, Chest Mimics in the Bronze and Silver dungeons, and deep shafts in the ground.",
    "",
    "Fight with your back to the island's centre, never to the edge."
  ],
  "quest.184C5196748CB082.title": "A quiet garden",
  "quest.184C5196748CB082.quest_desc": [
    "A Swet Banner stops Swets from appearing around it (Get Off My Lawn!), and a flower on Enchanted Aether Grass keeps Aechor Plants from spawning there (Tending The Garden).",
    "",
    "Skyroot beds set your respawn up here during the day, and vanilla beds do not explode here either."
  ],
  "quest.4F2B4AEB1BDA3011.title": "Aether tools for Aether blocks",
  "quest.4F2B4AEB1BDA3011.quest_desc": [
    "Start with a Skyroot pickaxe, then Holystone. Outside tools mine Aether blocks slower, on purpose.",
    "",
    "Skyroot tools double drops of Holystone, Ambrosium, Aether dirt and logs, and the Skyroot sword doubles mob drops; Holystone tools randomly drop Ambrosium Shards as you work."
  ],
  "quest.6F240D5A235EA0B5.title": "Ambrosium, the sky's coal",
  "quest.6F240D5A235EA0B5.quest_desc": [
    "The most common Aether ore. Its shards fuel the Altar, make Ambrosium Torches (light, and the Incubator's fuel) and heal half a heart when eaten; a Skyroot pickaxe doubles them.",
    "",
    "Hoard early: every Altar enchantment and repair burns shards."
  ],
  "quest.18F6BB6F5F90C589.title": "Zanite gets better as it wears",
  "quest.18F6BB6F5F90C589.quest_desc": [
    "A stone-tier pickaxe mines it. Zanite armor protects like iron, but its tools and sword grow stronger as they lose durability, the sword from iron damage up to double; repairing resets them, so repair late.",
    "",
    "Here a Zanite Gemstone is also the act IV component of the Iron Jetpacks elite coil."
  ],
  "quest.14968BF98158D2B0.title": "Gloves complete the set",
  "quest.14968BF98158D2B0.quest_desc": [
    "Aether armor has a fifth piece: set bonuses only work with the matching gloves (Gravitite's jump, Valkyrie flight, Phoenix fire immunity, Neptune swimming). There are gloves for vanilla armors too.",
    "",
    "Gloves, rings, pendants, capes and shields go in the accessory menu on &eI&r."
  ],
  "quest.03FC782CF49140C2.title": "Aether poison and its cure",
  "quest.03FC782CF49140C2.quest_desc": [
    "Aechor Plants and poison darts cause Inebriation: damage over time and random stumbling, lovely near an edge. Cure it with a White Apple from Crystal Trees or a Skyroot Remedy Bucket, enchanted from a Poison Bucket at the Altar, which also grants immunity for a while.",
    "",
    "Aechor petals are baby Moas' favourite food."
  ],
  "quest.3B595FC78D380340.title": "The Altar: ambrosium magic",
  "quest.3B595FC78D380340.quest_desc": [
    "Eight Holystone around a Zanite Gemstone, fuelled with Ambrosium. Its \"enchanting\" converts: Gravitite Ore into Enchanted Gravitite, Blue Berries into Enchanted Berries, Holystone into a Healing Stone, Poison Bucket into Remedy, Quicksoil into its glass, a music disc into its blue version.",
    "",
    "It also repairs, which matters for Zanite and Gravitite gear. EMI lists every recipe."
  ],
  "quest.71B9F0B85C252B0F.title": "The Freezer and icy jewelry",
  "quest.71B9F0B85C252B0F.quest_desc": [
    "Holystone, an Icestone and Skyroot planks, fuelled with Icestone. It freezes Aerclouds, water buckets and accessories: an iron or gold ring or pendant becomes an Ice one that freezes water and lava under your feet (Cool Jewelery!).",
    "",
    "A placed Icestone freezes nearby water and turns lava to obsidian: a cheap panic button."
  ],
  "quest.157454C8A47D5E06.title": "A Moa egg",
  "quest.157454C8A47D5E06.quest_desc": [
    "Moas lay eggs now and then, and Silver Dungeon chests hold some too. Blue Moas give 3 mid-air jumps, White 4, and the rare Black Moa 8: the best island-hopper there is.",
    "",
    "Hatching needs an Incubator. Step one is an egg in your hand."
  ],
  "quest.7358AEF66888973E.title": "Incubate and raise it",
  "quest.7358AEF66888973E.quest_desc": [
    "An Incubator (Holystone around an Ambrosium Torch) hatches the egg on Ambrosium Torch fuel, slowly (... Until They Hatch!). Feed the chick Aechor Petals until it grows, then ride it (Let's Fly! needs a Black Moa).",
    "",
    "A Nature Staff makes a tamed Moa sit and stay; Moas take saddles and, with Deep Aether, Skyjade armor."
  ],
  "quest.008596E65CFB1CEE.title": "Gravitite, the floating ore",
  "quest.008596E65CFB1CEE.quest_desc": [
    "The rarest Aether ore floats up when nothing is above it: mine from below or cover it first. Enchant it at the Altar for the Aether's best tools and armor.",
    "",
    "Gravitite tools lift blocks with right-click and the pickaxe mines any ore; the full set with gloves jumps much higher and ignores fall damage. The best insurance up here."
  ],
  "quest.0D4FDE9B09C3C886.title": "Bronze Dungeon: the Slider",
  "quest.0D4FDE9B09C3C886.quest_desc": [
    "Carved Stone halls with a Chest Mimic or two. The Slider, a sliding stone block, crushes you against the walls and only takes damage from pickaxes; a sword does nothing, and the game says so.",
    "",
    "Its Bronze Key opens the treasure: the Hammer of Kingbdogz, the Valkyrie Lance (long reach), Sentry Boots (no fall damage) and more."
  ],
  "quest.50470D5C8C86C94D.title": "Ten Victory Medals",
  "quest.50470D5C8C86C94D.quest_desc": [
    "The Silver Dungeon is a Valkyrie sanctuary. Its lesser Valkyries teleport, hit hard and drop a Victory Medal each, and the Queen will not fight until you bring ten.",
    "",
    "The Angelic Stone walls stay unbreakable until she falls, and some blocks are traps. Collect first, then knock."
  ],
  "quest.48C59C6D4759C71F.title": "Silver Dungeon: the Queen",
  "quest.48C59C6D4759C71F.quest_desc": [
    "Hand the Queen ten medals and strike when she says she is ready; she flies and teleports, so the Lance's reach helps. Her Silver Key opens a chest with Valkyrie gear (full set with gloves: short flight) and treasures like the Regeneration Stone, the Invisibility Cloak (toggle on &eHome&r here) and the Holy or Lightning Sword."
  ],
  "quest.05E67C9013A9B189.title": "Gold Dungeon: the Sun Spirit",
  "quest.05E67C9013A9B189.quest_desc": [
    "Hellfire Stone walls, unbreakable until the boss dies. The Sun Spirit ignores normal hits: knock one of its ice crystals back at it and, only while it is frozen, your weapons hurt. It also calls Fire Minions, so bring fire protection.",
    "",
    "It always drops the Gold Key and the Sun Altar, and here it gives back the Heart of Heliodor it had confiscated, closing act IV."
  ],
  "quest.3BB24EE38039A313.title": "Phoenix turns to obsidian",
  "quest.3BB24EE38039A313.quest_desc": [
    "The treasure holds Phoenix armor (full set with gloves: fire immunity and lava swimming) and Life Shards, and with Deep Aether always the Stratus template.",
    "",
    "Stand in water long enough in Phoenix armor and it becomes Obsidian armor, stronger than diamond and obtainable no other way. Decide which one you want before going for a swim."
  ],
  "quest.7D711A8074032A49.title": "A permanent heart",
  "quest.7D711A8074032A49.quest_desc": [
    "Life Shards from the Gold Dungeon treasure each grant a permanent extra heart, up to the mod's limit of 10 per player, which the pack keeps.",
    "",
    "In a team, share them: every player has their own cap."
  ],
  "quest.15FAE0E455CA7991.title": "Night returns to the Aether",
  "quest.15FAE0E455CA7991.quest_desc": [
    "With the Sun Spirit gone, the eternal day ends and a normal cycle begins, three times longer than the surface's. The Sun Altar it dropped sets the Aether's time of day; on a server anyone can use it unless an operator enables its whitelist.",
    "",
    "Now you can finally sleep up here: A Well Earned Rest."
  ],
  "quest.09480F82FCA889E5.title": "Deep Aether: more sky",
  "quest.09480F82FCA889E5.quest_desc": [
    "Same dimension, same portal, more of it: Aerglow Forests, Golden Heights and Grove, the Yagroot Swamp, Aerlavender Fields and high Cloud biomes, plus new woods, Quails, Aerglow Fish and a Brass Dungeon with its own boss.",
    "",
    "Its tips show in light blue among the Aether ones."
  ],
  "quest.1E7AA1B9A19FBDC5.title": "Aether Explorer",
  "quest.1E7AA1B9A19FBDC5.quest_desc": [
    "Walk all ten biomes the advancement lists. The Cloud biomes float highest and hold the Brass Dungeon, so the trip doubles as scouting.",
    "",
    "Nature's Compass finds Aether biomes by name if you get tired of looking."
  ],
  "quest.0CD74F73BE883B6B.title": "Skyjade: strong, then fragile",
  "quest.0CD74F73BE883B6B.quest_desc": [
    "Skyjade needs an iron-tier pickaxe. Its gear is Zanite in reverse: it starts above diamond (the sword at netherite damage) and weakens as it wears, so keep it repaired.",
    "",
    "It also makes Moa armor, a shield, lanterns and chains, and goes into the Combiner and the Stratus Ingot."
  ],
  "quest.15B2CFFE81FDD257.title": "The Combiner",
  "quest.15B2CFFE81FDD257.quest_desc": [
    "Skyroot planks, Holystone, Skyjade and an Ambrosium Shard, or find one in a Brass Dungeon. It combines Golden Amber, Frozen Goldenleaf Berries and a third item into Deep Aether goods; EMI lists every Combining recipe.",
    "",
    "Goldenleaf Berries grow on Golden Vines from Quicksoil, and the frozen ones are what it wants."
  ],
  "quest.78E2FDDEBE4738FF.title": "Purple magic",
  "quest.78E2FDDEBE4738FF.quest_desc": [
    "Deep Aether makes Aether poison a bucketable fluid. Items thrown in are transformed: Altar-made blocks and items lose their enchantment, and Squashes turn purple (Purple Magic).",
    "",
    "Water and poison make Aersmog, a venomous cloud block. Antidotes, from Venomites' Bio Crystals, grant Remedy."
  ],
  "quest.12D8D2165B156844.title": "Brass Dungeon: Eye of the Storm",
  "quest.12D8D2165B156844.quest_desc": [
    "It spawns only in Cloud and Overgrown Cloud biomes, from about height 184 up: bring parachutes, Gravitite or a Moa. Its boss hides in a whirlwind, and the game hints you should hit the wind.",
    "",
    "The Brass Key opens a Cloud Cape (double jump), an Aercloud Necklace (stand on clouds and powder snow) or a glove-reach book, plus knockback-proof Stormforged armor."
  ],
  "quest.6E067188FF68A39A.title": "A Stratus Ingot",
  "quest.6E067188FF68A39A.quest_desc": [
    "The step past Gravitite: enchant Sterling Aerclouds from near the build limit into Chromatic Aerclouds, then craft 5 of them with Enchanted Gravitite, a Zanite Gemstone, an Ambrosium Shard and Skyjade.",
    "",
    "The Stratus template from the Gold Dungeon upgrades Gravitite gear at a smithing table, and the full set adds a dash to Gravitite's jump on &eAlt+G&r."
  ],
  "quest.609F33918E4CE5DF.title": "Flawless: no-hit trophies",
  "quest.609F33918E4CE5DF.quest_desc": [
    "Beat the Slider without taking a hit for a Slider Eye (a ground slam on &eShift+H&r), the Valkyrie Queen for a Medal of Honor (resistance against unholy mobs), the Sun Spirit for a Sun Core, which makes the Afterburner flamethrower.",
    "",
    "Every Aether boss flawless is Champion Of The Aether. Pure bragging rights."
  ],
  "quest.1B7D3535D683B41C.title": "What changes up here",
  "quest.1B7D3535D683B41C.quest_desc": [
    "No free portal frame on world creation, so you build the glowstone one; the entry gift stays. Carry On cannot lift Treasure Chests, Mimics or bosses. The Zanite Gemstone gates the Iron Jetpacks elite coil in act IV, and Aether's Delight adds cooking. Keys: accessories &eI&r, invisibility &eHome&r, Stratus dash &eAlt+G&r, Slider Eye &eShift+H&r."
  ],
  "quest.342AE474AB81ED04.title": "The compass in the sky",
  "quest.342AE474AB81ED04.quest_desc": [
    "In act IV it lists the Aether, then the Bronze, Silver and Gold dungeons. From the Overworld the needle rests gold; inside the Aether it points at the nearest known dungeon.",
    "",
    "How far it looks and what grey means: The Heliodor Compass chapter."
  ],
  "quest.4EE142A746000BC9.title": "Master of the sky",
  "quest.4EE142A746000BC9.quest_desc": [
    "Gravitite for safe falls, a Black Moa for travel, Ice accessories for lava, Stratus for the dash and the Sun Altar to pick day or night.",
    "",
    "For the story, what matters is what the Sun Spirit carried. From now on, the Atlas speaks clearly."
  ],
  "chapter.2347B543172CE0D8.title": "The Bumblezone",
  "chapter.2347B543172CE0D8.chapter_subtitle": [
    "A dimension inside a beehive: honey, wrath, a Bee Queen with her own quest line and ancient sanctums."
  ],
  "quest.5D9195CF9044684B.title": "Where Juan's bees came from",
  "quest.5D9195CF9044684B.quest_desc": [
    "A dimension of honeycomb, bees, honey and odd structures. It belongs to act IV: the compass points there, and anyone on your team arriving records the milestone the act IV Atlas asks for.",
    "",
    "The story says Juan's bees came from here and Heliodor signed a treaty with them. The bees remember how you treat them."
  ],
  "quest.7F28E1B8F31E6ADD.title": "A pearl into a beehive",
  "quest.7F28E1B8F31E6ADD.quest_desc": [
    "Throw an ender pearl at an Overworld bee nest or beehive and you land in the Bumblezone (Beenderman Intrusion!); a piston pushing you into a nest works too.",
    "",
    "To leave, go below the floor or above the ceiling: you teleport out instead of dying (Dive Bombing Exit). Beds work here and set your respawn without exploding."
  ],
  "quest.425D89601FD767DC.title": "Wrath of the Hive",
  "quest.425D89601FD767DC.quest_desc": [
    "Hit a bee or take honey carelessly and you get Wrath of the Hive: every bee nearby hunts you, and hitting one makes it worse (NOT THE BEEEEEES!!!). Feeding the swarm may calm it, if you last.",
    "",
    "Feeding bees or brood blocks gives the opposite, Protection of the Hive: safe honey and bees on your side."
  ],
  "quest.3159CA3F1D7126D2.title": "Winning favors",
  "quest.3159CA3F1D7126D2.quest_desc": [
    "Feed a Honeycomb Brood Block or a bee until you get Protection of the Hive (Winning Favors), then collect honey from a filled porous honeycomb or mine a honey block while protected (No more Wrath! Only friendship!).",
    "",
    "That is the safe way to farm the Bumblezone. The other way is also a way, briefly."
  ],
  "quest.44F6D70D92566D98.title": "A bucket of honey",
  "quest.44F6D70D92566D98.quest_desc": [
    "Honey is a fluid here: fill a bucket (MOAR HONEEEEY!!!). It grows baby bees instantly, makes adults fall in love and grows larvae in brood blocks (Bee Farmer).",
    "",
    "Honey crystals and sticky residue are the other local materials; keep the fragile crystal blocks with Silk Touch."
  ],
  "quest.3D2652F97EBFEB82.title": "The Honey Compass",
  "quest.3D2652F97EBFEB82.quest_desc": [
    "Craft or find a Honey Compass (Is this even still a compass..?) and turn on its tracking (Dora the Beexplorer). Rare ones from structure cocoons point to a Throne Pillar, seat of the Bee Queen (Off to see the Queen!).",
    "",
    "Honey Cocoons are the dimension's loot containers; Silk Touch takes them whole."
  ],
  "quest.1C5656CBC74B525B.title": "The Bee Queen",
  "quest.1C5656CBC74B525B.quest_desc": [
    "Enter a Throne Pillar (Royal Presence) to meet her. She trades, and she starts The Queen's Desire, a line of advancements paid in Royal Jelly: breed bees, craft nests, pollinate, kill spiders, silverfish and endermites, save stingerless bees and more.",
    "",
    "Finish them all and talk to her again for the Essence of the Bees (Journey's End)."
  ],
  "quest.00BEE638ED279EBC.title": "Trading with a queen",
  "quest.00BEE638ED279EBC.quest_desc": [
    "The Queen takes many items for Bumblezone goods, and some bonus trades rotate over time. She is also the source of Windy Air, a placeable jet stream (Placeable Jetstreams!).",
    "",
    "Trading with her 128 times is Crazy Trader. The title is earned."
  ],
  "quest.56F766EC2A7BB911.title": "Essence of the Bees",
  "quest.56F766EC2A7BB911.quest_desc": [
    "It opens the six Sempiternal Sanctums (Ancient Origins), one per color, each with its own event and essence: Raging (red, Strength from kills), Knowing (purple, highlights mobs), Calming (blue, calm out of combat), Life (green, heals allies and grows crops), Radiance (yellow, sun mends armor) and Continuity (white, respawn instead of dying)."
  ],
  "quest.5D89181441024606.title": "Solar powered",
  "quest.5D89181441024606.quest_desc": [
    "Beat the yellow Sempiternal Sanctum for the Essence of Radiance (Solar Powered): sunlight mends your armor and grants benefits.",
    "",
    "In a pack about light, it is the essence Heliodor would have picked."
  ],
  "quest.5D23AB3A8AD69B98.title": "A flying mount",
  "quest.5D23AB3A8AD69B98.quest_desc": [
    "Beehemoths are giant bees. Tame one with honey buckets and saddle it for a flying mount (Bee Movie But It's 300% Larger), then keep befriending it for maximum friendship.",
    "",
    "One of the few ways to fly this early without a jetpack."
  ],
  "quest.38A8AD749EA449E6.title": "The Bee Warrior",
  "quest.38A8AD749EA449E6.quest_desc": [
    "Bee armor has tricks: the Stingless Bee Helmet highlights bees, the Bumble Bee Chestplate buzzes, Honey Bee Leggings gather pollen and Carpenter Bee Boots burrow and cling to walls. Flower Headwear keeps the Cell Maze calm.",
    "",
    "The Stinger Spear can be thrown and, with Neurotoxin, paralyzes. Full set plus spear: The Bee Warrior Rises!"
  ],
  "quest.532097AFB2E17182.title": "The Crystalline Flower",
  "quest.532097AFB2E17182.quest_desc": [
    "Bumblezone's own enchanting: feed it items and experience until it grows (CONSUME CONSUME CONSUME), then right-click it to put enchantments on books (Choosing Wisely).",
    "",
    "A flower with an appetite and taste."
  ],
  "quest.1F3224E60E1C6A3C.title": "Places inside the hive",
  "quest.1F3224E60E1C6A3C.quest_desc": [
    "Cell Mazes (Wrath inside unless you wear Flower Headwear), hanging gardens, honey fountains, hive temples, a honey slime ranch, a pirate ship, a subway, battle cubes, candle parkour and the Throne Pillars.",
    "",
    "Entering them all is Sightbee-er; finding every biome is Beeography. The puns are not ours."
  ],
  "quest.47C889B23C8B0BAB.title": "Bumblezone in ENTRELUMEN",
  "quest.47C889B23C8B0BAB.quest_desc": [
    "The act IV compass points here and advances when your team arrives, and an earlier arrival still counts for the Atlas. Nothing gates the entry: a pearl and a bee nest are enough. The Queen's rewards are the mod's own and the story needs none of them.",
    "",
    "Juan's side of the story treats the bees as allies. Wrath is the price of forgetting that."
  ],
  "quest.0141D5FD03C6F696.title": "Keeper of the treaty",
  "quest.0141D5FD03C6F696.quest_desc": [
    "You entered through a beehive, won the bees' favor, served the Queen and walked the Sempiternal Sanctums.",
    "",
    "Heliodor's treaty with the bees still holds, and now your name is on it."
  ],
  "chapter.2B47486A10736E41.title": "Ad Astra: rockets and planets",
  "chapter.2B47486A10736E41.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Steel, oxygen and fuel: from the first launch to another solar system."
  ],
  "quest.4B444004D4ACED14.title": "Beyond the sky",
  "quest.4B444004D4ACED14.quest_desc": [
    "Rockets, space suits, oxygen machines and worlds: the Moon, Mars, Venus, Mercury, their orbits and Glacio in another solar system. Each rocket tier unlocks a planet whose metal builds the next rocket: steel, Desh, Ostrum, Calorite.",
    "",
    "Space opens in act V: the NASA Workbench needs an atomic alloy. Steel, energy, oil and oxygen can be ready before."
  ],
  "quest.6CD31724A52E8A85.title": "The Astrodux",
  "quest.6CD31724A52E8A85.quest_desc": [
    "Ad Astra's own guide: a book ringed by iron ingots and blue dye. Its chapters walk the same route with recipes and pictures.",
    "",
    "Nobody hands out books on join here, so craft it yourself."
  ],
  "quest.20AAB21A1B32374E.title": "Carbon Footprint",
  "quest.20AAB21A1B32374E.quest_desc": [
    "Ad Astra machines run on FE. Its Coal Generator burns wood or coal, and any other mod's FE generator works too; Solar Panels produce more, especially near the sun and in orbit.",
    "",
    "The Etrionic Capacitor is a portable battery for machines and your inventory."
  ],
  "quest.6126FC516BA3CEB6.title": "Plates and steel",
  "quest.6126FC516BA3CEB6.quest_desc": [
    "The Compressor presses ingots and blocks into plates, used almost everywhere (Under Pressure). The Etrionic Blast Furnace blasts four slots at once, and in alloying mode turns one iron plus one coal into a Steel Ingot (Smart Blasting).",
    "",
    "Steel builds the first rocket, the suit and the launch pad."
  ],
  "quest.4D9B26FD92C13E4D.title": "Ocean Cleanup",
  "quest.4D9B26FD92C13E4D.quest_desc": [
    "Oil wells spout over ocean biomes in the Overworld: fill buckets there. Oil does not renew, and a Moon round trip burns six buckets of fuel, so collect plenty.",
    "",
    "A powered Fuel Refinery turns oil into rocket fuel."
  ],
  "quest.6D6B547743F538B7.title": "Refined fuel",
  "quest.6D6B547743F538B7.quest_desc": [
    "Oil in the refinery's left slot, fuel out. Three buckets launch the rocket and three more bring you back, all stored in the rocket's own inventory.",
    "",
    "Mars has a better option waiting: Cryo Fuel."
  ],
  "quest.1D2D65C4B7DDAB39.title": "Astronaut",
  "quest.1D2D65C4B7DDAB39.quest_desc": [
    "The full suit (helmet, suit, pants, boots) takes steel plates, wool, a glass pane for the helmet, and a gas tank and oxygen gear for the suit. It stores oxygen; without it the Moon kills you fast.",
    "",
    "The pocket TI-69 shows local oxygen, temperature and gravity. Check it before taking your helmet off."
  ],
  "quest.15752BDB4F142178.title": "Oxygen from water",
  "quest.15752BDB4F142178.quest_desc": [
    "An Oxygen Loader turns water in its left tank into oxygen for your suit and Gas Tanks; holding right-click with a full tank shares it into your inventory, armor first.",
    "",
    "Bring more oxygen than you think. The first trip is always the one that goes wrong."
  ],
  "quest.4B7A356D731AFC7A.title": "The NASA Workbench",
  "quest.4B7A356D731AFC7A.quest_desc": [
    "Every rocket is assembled here (Rocket Science): nose cone, fins, tanks and engine. Its recipe carries an atomic alloy in the top middle slot, so space opens with act V; the rest is steel plates, iron rods, steel blocks, a crafting table and redstone torches."
  ],
  "quest.55E62F8CB61E0090.title": "Baby's First Rocket",
  "quest.55E62F8CB61E0090.quest_desc": [
    "Nose cone, six steel blocks, four fins, two steel tanks and a steel engine. Place it on a Launch Pad (steel plates and rods); a redstone-powered pad launches it once fueled.",
    "",
    "Shift-right-click the rocket to open its inventory and load fuel."
  ],
  "quest.3E1882A814C9C57A.title": "The pre-launch checklist",
  "quest.3E1882A814C9C57A.quest_desc": [
    "Forget one item and you may live on the Moon now. Before jumping in: 3 buckets of fuel in the tank slot, 3 more plus a Launch Pad in the rocket inventory for the return; a full, charged suit and spare Gas Tanks; food, weapons, tools; and soul torches or glowstone, since normal torches go out without oxygen."
  ],
  "quest.1C874811C4A21BF4.title": "One Small Step",
  "quest.1C874811C4A21BF4.quest_desc": [
    "The Moon has no oxygen and is freezing: water freezes, torches break, plants die. Desh, the next metal, waits underground.",
    "",
    "To go home, Shift-right-click the lander to take back rocket, fuel and pad, punch the lander away, set up the pad, place and fuel the rocket and jump."
  ],
  "quest.38C048D4BF0517BC.title": "Lunarians and their traders",
  "quest.38C048D4BF0517BC.quest_desc": [
    "Big underground villages on the Moon house Lunarians, alien villagers who need no oxygen and trade planet materials, suits and oxygen gear. Their wandering traders visit every moon and planet with launch pads, oxygen, fuel, soul torches and water, for emeralds from space structures.",
    "",
    "If a trip goes wrong, one of them is your ticket home."
  ],
  "quest.71161BAE92ED02FC.title": "A room with air",
  "quest.71161BAE92ED02FC.quest_desc": [
    "The Oxygen Distributor fills a sealed room (Take a Deep Breath): feed it water nonstop from a Water Pump on an infinite source, power both, and press \"show\" to see the covered area.",
    "",
    "Cables and pipes leak, so use their duct blocks; 3×3 Sliding Doors seal and make good airlocks. The Gravity Normalizer does the same for gravity, 0 to 2 g."
  ],
  "quest.4BA52976F8727EBB.title": "Space stations",
  "quest.4BA52976F8727EBB.quest_desc": [
    "From the planet screen, build a station in any moon or planet's orbit if you carry the listed materials; nobody else can build in the same spot. Orbit is where Solar Panels shine brightest.",
    "",
    "In zero gravity you float without friction; the Zip Gun burns oxygen to push you around (Unconventional Flight)."
  ],
  "quest.47E25D6FB6A4DA3D.title": "Desh and the Tier 2 Rocket",
  "quest.47E25D6FB6A4DA3D.quest_desc": [
    "Moon Desh makes advanced machines, cables faster than steel, station parts and the Tier 2 Rocket, built like the first with Desh instead of steel (The Next Step).",
    "",
    "Moon cheese is real here. It has its own advancement."
  ],
  "quest.4ECC630DC8A5BE32.title": "A rover",
  "quest.4ECC630DC8A5BE32.quest_desc": [
    "A fast land vehicle for rough terrain: two seats, 16 storage slots, fuel in its left slot, and it hurts what it runs over. Its built-in radio plays real internet stations; open it with &eAlt+R&r here.",
    "",
    "The standalone Radio block is craftable too (DJ)."
  ],
  "quest.290170B66C86597D.title": "The Martian",
  "quest.290170B66C86597D.quest_desc": [
    "The Tier 2 Rocket reaches Mars, home of Ostrum: stronger space armor, better machines and the heat-proof Tier 3 Rocket. The polar caps also hold Ice Shard ore, the base of Cryo Fuel.",
    "",
    "As always, keep a spare pad and fuel for the way back."
  ],
  "quest.7FFBC1246DFE1803.title": "Cryo Fuel",
  "quest.7FFBC1246DFE1803.quest_desc": [
    "The Cryo Freezer turns Ice Shards (ore on the Moon, Mars and Glacio) into 25 mB of Cryo Fuel each; ice, packed ice and blue ice work too. It is about three times as efficient: one bucket per launch, two for a round trip.",
    "",
    "Poured out, it hurts like lava and freezes water. Handle with gloves."
  ],
  "quest.6164BA6BB34CC619.title": "Doom Slayer",
  "quest.6164BA6BB34CC619.quest_desc": [
    "Venus and Mercury burn a normal suit's wearer in seconds. The Netherite Space Suit adds permanent fire resistance and more protection: craft the full set before the Tier 3 Rocket takes you there.",
    "",
    "Sunscreen, but metal."
  ],
  "quest.7866F9F2E4D6B118.title": "The hot planets",
  "quest.7866F9F2E4D6B118.quest_desc": [
    "With the Tier 3 Rocket and the netherite suit, visit Venus (Venusian) and Mercury (Quite the Sun Tan) for Calorite, the metal of the Tier 4 Rocket.",
    "",
    "Solar Panels on Mercury, so close to the sun, produce the most. Heliodor would have loved it there."
  ],
  "quest.647B411C0A583890.title": "Rocket Man",
  "quest.647B411C0A583890.quest_desc": [
    "The Jet Suit upgrades the netherite suit with more protection, more oxygen and flight: jump to rise, jump and sprint to boost like a rocket-powered elytra. It runs on energy, charged at an Energizer; in this pack flight costs 2.5 times as much.",
    "",
    "Toggle its flight with &eCtrl+F4&r in this pack."
  ],
  "quest.4C18B1FEA4AF14BB.title": "Interstellar",
  "quest.4C18B1FEA4AF14BB.quest_desc": [
    "Calorite builds the Tier 4 Rocket, the only one that leaves the solar system (To Infinity and Beyond). First stop in Proxima Centauri: Glacio, brutally cold but breathable, so the helmet can come off (Interstellar).",
    "",
    "The Astrodux says it plainly: Ad Astra's progression ends here, for now."
  ],
  "quest.7A8C4395D7991615.title": "What changes in space",
  "quest.7A8C4395D7991615.quest_desc": [
    "The NASA Workbench needs an atomic alloy, so rockets and planets open during act V; everything before it can be prepared earlier. Ad Astra's old-format compatibility recipes with Create, Mekanism and Immersive Engineering do not load in 1.21.1 and are disabled, and its metals join Almost Unified. Keys: radio &eAlt+R&r, suit flight &eCtrl+F4&r."
  ],
  "quest.1B63ACCAD2B87970.title": "Ad astra",
  "quest.1B63ACCAD2B87970.quest_desc": [
    "From a coal generator to another star: steel, Desh, Ostrum and Calorite, rooms full of air and stations in orbit.",
    "",
    "Heliodor looked at the sky through a telescope. You went."
  ],
  "chapter.7D2C7B91D8E8EE7B.title": "Bosses: vanilla and Mowzie's",
  "chapter.7D2C7B91D8E8EE7B.chapter_subtitle": [
    "The Wither, the Dragon and the Elder Guardian as materials, plus Mowzie's optional mini-bosses."
  ],
  "quest.435A3AA816CEBEC3.title": "Materials, not milestones",
  "quest.435A3AA816CEBEC3.quest_desc": [
    "The Wither, the Ender Dragon and the Elder Guardian matter for their drops: nether stars, dragon hearts and wet sponges feed Luminous gear and act VI's creative items. The compass passes their lairs in act V.",
    "",
    "Mowzie's Mobs adds optional mini-bosses with unique weapons for acts II to IV. None of them closes an act; all of them hit hard."
  ],
  "quest.528E49AE28EBD771.title": "Three wither skeleton skulls",
  "quest.528E49AE28EBD771.quest_desc": [
    "Wither skeletons live in Nether fortresses, rebuilt larger by YUNG's. Skulls are a rare drop, so Looting helps a lot.",
    "",
    "Four soul sand or soul soil blocks in a T, three skulls on top: that is the Wither. Do it far from home."
  ],
  "quest.617F3D63E49031FA.title": "The Wither",
  "quest.617F3D63E49031FA.quest_desc": [
    "Summon it far from your base: it breaks blocks and explodes on spawn. Bring healing, milk for the Wither effect and a strong bow or a Smite sword. It drops a nether star.",
    "",
    "Here it is the only star source: the pack removed Modern Industrialization's implosion, Oritech's particle collision and Reliquary's alkahestry recipes."
  ],
  "quest.1CC6054DE3D91DA9.title": "What a nether star is for",
  "quest.1CC6054DE3D91DA9.quest_desc": [
    "Each Luminous piece uses one as its smithing template (nine for a set), several creative items ask for one, and so do beacons, Cataclysm's Harbinger and many high-tier recipes: &eU&r on the star in EMI lists them all.",
    "",
    "Tired of farming? Train a Hostile Neural Networks Wither model and simulate stars; the Simulation Chamber is an act IV machine here."
  ],
  "quest.321C015FCBE1CF65.title": "The monument and the wet sponge",
  "quest.321C015FCBE1CF65.quest_desc": [
    "YUNG's rebuilds ocean monuments, still guarded by Elder Guardians and their Mining Fatigue. In act V the compass counts one done when someone carries a wet sponge, which also goes into the creative fluid tanks.",
    "",
    "Bring water breathing and Respiration or Depth Strider; the Aether's Neptune armor and Iron Bubble shine here."
  ],
  "quest.6D96F605B73EC48A.title": "Eye Spy: the stronghold",
  "quest.6D96F605B73EC48A.quest_desc": [
    "Eyes of Ender still lead to the stronghold, rebuilt larger by YUNG's Better Strongholds. Follow one for Eye Spy. It is an act V compass stop, done when your team reaches the End.",
    "",
    "Bring spare eyes: some break on the way, always the one you needed."
  ],
  "quest.1367C89E923AF6CB.title": "The End",
  "quest.1367C89E923AF6CB.quest_desc": [
    "YUNG's Better End Island rebuilds the central island and the Dragon's arena, with its own towers and spawn platform. Your team's first arrival is an act V milestone.",
    "",
    "Bring blocks, a bow, slow falling or a water bucket, and a pumpkin on your head if you would rather not argue with every enderman."
  ],
  "quest.7D5F1D9C8CD14406.title": "Free the End",
  "quest.7D5F1D9C8CD14406.quest_desc": [
    "Break the End Crystals on the towers first (arrows, or climb to the caged ones), then hit the Dragon when it perches. Killing it completes the act V compass stop.",
    "",
    "It drops a pile of experience, the Dragon Egg, the gateway to the outer islands and, with Draconic Evolution, a Dragon Heart for act VI's creative energy items."
  ],
  "quest.58072A51FC29378C.title": "Bottled dragon's breath",
  "quest.58072A51FC29378C.quest_desc": [
    "During the fight the Dragon breathes a purple cloud: catch it in empty bottles (You Need a Mint). It makes lingering potions and shows up in several mod recipes.",
    "",
    "Need more? Four End Crystals on the exit portal bring the Dragon back (The End... Again...)."
  ],
  "quest.20DDBA794FE6B671.title": "Wings from an End city",
  "quest.20DDBA794FE6B671.quest_desc": [
    "The exit gateway leads to the outer islands, where End city ships hide Elytra (Sky's the Limit), guarded by Shulkers whose shells make shulker boxes.",
    "",
    "Solsticio's rarities dealer also sells Elytra, but only from act VI."
  ],
  "quest.2A5ED82F67EC1780.title": "The Warden: avoid, do not farm",
  "quest.2A5ED82F67EC1780.quest_desc": [
    "Sculk Shriekers summon it from the Deep Dark. It is blind, tracks vibrations and smell, and hits harder than almost anything: sneak, muffle steps with wool, and distract it with snowballs or arrows (Sneak 100).",
    "",
    "Ancient cities hold echo shards and Swift Sneak books, and Deeper and Darker adds a way into the Otherside."
  ],
  "quest.243E8667C02EA066.title": "Mowzie's Mobs",
  "quest.243E8667C02EA066.quest_desc": [
    "A handful of detailed creatures and four headline mini-bosses in a natural difficulty chain: the Ferrous Wroughtnaut underground, the Frostmaw in the cold, Tongbi the Sculptor in the mountains and Umvuthi the Sunbird with its tribe.",
    "",
    "Optional, acts II to IV here, and their prizes never break. Worth the detour."
  ],
  "quest.1F8C4C21E5A2D724.title": "The Ferrous Wroughtnaut",
  "quest.1F8C4C21E5A2D724.quest_desc": [
    "An armored giant asleep in a Wrought Chamber, roughly between Y 20 and Y 50. Dodge its huge axe, wait for the swing to end and hit its exposed back (Just a Flesh Wound).",
    "",
    "Prize: the unbreakable Axe of a Thousand Metals (right-click sweeps an arc, sneak-right-click sends a shockwave) and the unbreakable Wrought Helm."
  ],
  "quest.6FA6B0CE78579892.title": "The Frostmaw",
  "quest.6FA6B0CE78579892.quest_desc": [
    "A huge ice ape asleep in cold biomes (Rude Awakening is killing it). It freezes you in place; fire damage breaks Frozen early.",
    "",
    "It carries an Ice Crystal that channels an icy whirlwind and recharges in your inventory. You can steal it instead of fighting (Big Brain Time). The ape will not be pleased."
  ],
  "quest.36297A349942A165.title": "Tongbi, the Sculptor",
  "quest.36297A349942A165.quest_desc": [
    "He waits in a mountain monastery. Give him a Bluff Rod, from a Bluff, to start his test: climb the course he raises and right-click him at the top in time, without placing or breaking blocks, teleporting or flying (You Must Believe).",
    "",
    "Passing earns the Earthrend Gauntlet: throw boulders, tunnel and ride pillars of earth. Geomancer robes and beads boost it."
  ],
  "quest.74055B78138FF495.title": "Umvuthi, the Sunbird",
  "quest.74055B78138FF495.quest_desc": [
    "Umvuthi rules a grove guarded by masked Umvuthana. Beat a Raptor for a mask (Masquerade), then fight the Sunbird (Praise the Sun).",
    "",
    "It drops the unbreakable Sol Visage: wear it and right-click another mask to summon followers. The six masks give Strength, Speed, Haste, Resistance, Jump Boost or Health Boost."
  ],
  "quest.3C3360B975FDD608.title": "Heliomancer",
  "quest.3C3360B975FDD608.quest_desc": [
    "Sneak into a grove wearing a mask (Birds of a Feather) and Umvuthi may grant the Sun's Blessing (Heliomancer). With an empty hand: Sunstrike, Solar Flare, Solar Beam and Supernova, paid in blessing time that only starts counting when you use one; the Sunbird refills it for free later.",
    "",
    "Sun magic in a pack about Heliodor's light. Of course."
  ],
  "quest.5F3E5D75317D70D9.title": "The Grottol",
  "quest.5F3E5D75317D70D9.quest_desc": [
    "Diamond-crusted cave critters that flee on sight. Kill one with a Fortune pickaxe for extra diamonds (Double Or Nothing!), or with Silk Touch to capture it whole (You're Coming With Me).",
    "",
    "It is a rock with legs and a diamond problem."
  ],
  "quest.2F3AD185B74C7469.title": "The flying Naga",
  "quest.2F3AD185B74C7469.quest_desc": [
    "Not the Twilight one: Mowzie's Naga is a winged sea serpent that spits poison (Wingin' It). Its Naga Fang brews Poison Resistance, makes the Naga Fang Dagger (poison, double damage from behind) and makes darts for the Blowgun."
  ],
  "quest.7C0A20130CB7B6F9.title": "Smaller creatures",
  "quest.7C0A20130CB7B6F9.quest_desc": [
    "Foliaaths are carnivorous plants; their seed grows a pet if you feed it meat for two days. Lanterns drift at night and drop Luminous Jelly (brief night vision). Elokosa Howlers drop moon paws that inflict Weakness, Slowness, Mining Fatigue, Fragility or Eclipse on nearby mobs."
  ],
  "quest.4D9BB6756E65D6DE.title": "What ENTRELUMEN changes",
  "quest.4D9BB6756E65D6DE.quest_desc": [
    "The Wither is the only nether star source, and Hostile Neural Networks can simulate it once trained. YUNG's replaces fortresses, monuments, strongholds and the End island, so their /locate IDs change (for example betterstrongholds:stronghold). Carry On refuses the Wither, the Elder Guardian, the Warden, the Dragon and Mowzie's bosses.",
    "",
    "Nice try, though."
  ],
  "quest.45C9342D1E83A92F.title": "Trophy wall",
  "quest.45C9342D1E83A92F.quest_desc": [
    "Nether star, wet sponge, dragon's breath and Elytra from the vanilla bosses; an axe, a helm, a crystal, a gauntlet and the blessing of the sun from Mowzie's.",
    "",
    "None of it was required. All of it makes the rest easier."
  ],
  "chapter.0EF22D195361F538.title": "The Sun of Heliodor",
  "chapter.0EF22D195361F538.chapter_subtitle": [
    "Six acts under one sun."
  ],
